window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y2v2-index"]=[{"i":"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p6-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka amasawa-ichika","q":"amasawa ichika amasawa  white room prologue  her pov  in her own voice she explains she is a fifth generation white room student  that she has always been compared to the fourth generation  god  ayanokoji kiyotaka and found wanting  and that she worships only hatred  not him  she watched him through a visiting room and shivered at his figure  this is amasawa s interior monologue  her pov  no spoken line is quoted  driven by hatred rather than worship   she refuses to revere ayanokoji and treats him as her enemy  the obstacle to her being recognized as the white room s success story  to prove ayanokoji is not number one and to be recognized by the organization as the true success  the opportunity comes now that he has refused to return to the restarted white room  the fourth generation  god  she has been measured against her whole life  she has resolved to bury him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p6-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html#sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p6-1\">Amasawa: White Room prologue (her POV)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.6–10<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In her own voice she explains she is a fifth-generation White Room student, that she has always been compared to the fourth-generation “god” Ayanokōji Kiyotaka and found wanting, and that she worships only hatred, not him; she watched him through a visiting room and shivered at his figure.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> This is Amasawa&#x27;s interior monologue (her POV); no spoken line is quoted.<span class=\"pg\">p.6–10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Driven by hatred rather than worship — she refuses to revere Ayanokōji and treats him as her enemy, the obstacle to her being recognized as the White Room&#x27;s success story.<span class=\"pg\">p.6–10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> To prove Ayanokōji is not number one and to be recognized by the organization as the true success; the opportunity comes now that he has refused to return to the restarted White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.6–10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The fourth-generation “god” she has been measured against her whole life; she has resolved to bury him.<span class=\"pg\">p.6–10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p69-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"inner","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka prologue  the white room pov the unnamed white room 5th generation student s monologue from a 1st year advanced nurturing classroom  the 4th generation held as the unreachable model  the students made to worship him  and the narrator s own  worship free hatred that kept him in the white room   ayanokouji kiyotaka was much better than you a year ago    the instructor s cold words  recalled  an off page speaker  the instructor   i needed to prove that ayanokouji kiyotaka wasn t number one by all means necessary  i had to be recognized by that organization as the true success story  the organization s true goal was mass production  not producing number 1 individuals  failures were of no value  so recognition as the true success story or elimination as a failure were the only ends  he resolves to bury the 4th generation  god  he learns that ayanokoji broke orders by refusing to return to the restarted white room   the first chance to contact the target  killing him is floated as one way to solve the problem  his name is invoked throughout  he never enters the scene  not a presence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1\">Prologue: The White Room POV<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.6–10<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The unnamed White Room 5th-generation student&#x27;s monologue from a 1st-year Advanced Nurturing classroom: the 4th generation held as the unreachable model, the students made to worship him, and the narrator&#x27;s own “worship”-free hatred that kept him in the White Room.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I needed to prove that Ayanokouji Kiyotaka wasn’t number one by all means necessary. I had to be recognized by that organization as the true success story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Ayanokouji Kiyotaka was much better than you a year ago” — the instructor&#x27;s cold words, recalled; an off-page speaker (the instructor).<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The organization&#x27;s true goal was mass production, not producing number-1 individuals; failures were of no value, so recognition as the true success story or elimination as a failure were the only ends; he resolves to bury the 4th-generation “god”.<span class=\"pg\">p.8–10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He learns that Ayanokōji broke orders by refusing to return to the restarted White Room — the first chance to contact the target; killing him is floated as one way to solve the problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> His name is invoked throughout; he never enters the scene; not a presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.6–10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p12-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka coverage note  passing mentions his name invoked in the classroom speculation  ayanokouji kiyotaka  not on the page   the only one in the class that had achieved a perfect score was ayanokouji himself   ayanokouji got a perfect score  which should be impossible  ishizaki s goal on page  to invite ayanokouji kun before anyone else could  his name is invoked in amasawa s monologue  she tails karuizawa in hopes of getting him to let her in the room   the fact he wasn t a normal student was something i knew even before he got that perfect score in maths  tsubaki s interior monologue  she tails him to the convenience store","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p12-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–352<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> His name invoked in the classroom speculation (“Ayanokouji Kiyotaka”); not on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The only one in the class that had achieved a perfect score was Ayanokouji himself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ayanokouji got a perfect score, which should be impossible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Ishizaki’s goal on page: to invite Ayanokouji-kun before anyone else could.<span class=\"pg\">p.342–344<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> His name is invoked in Amasawa’s monologue; she tails Karuizawa in hopes of getting him to let her in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.346–347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The fact he wasn’t a normal student was something I knew even before he got that perfect score in maths.”<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Tsubaki’s interior monologue: she tails him to the convenience store.<span class=\"pg\">p.351–353<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1\">← Before: Prologue: The White Room POV<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\">→ After: After Tsukishiro&#x27;s office; Chabashira waits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae coverage note  passing mentions  chabashira had called him away and he had gone off somewhere  so he resorted to waiting in the classroom for him to return   in stark contrast to the overjoyed chabashira  his expression was somewhat resentful   yes  although i tried to confirm it with chabashira sensei tactfully  she didn t show signs she knew about it   shortly after  i could hear chabashira and kouenji from around the corner   chabashira  presumably standing face to face with kouenji  waited for his question   chabashira to leave  in a bit  the sound of her footsteps disappeared   as she entered the classroom  chabashira s natural expression turned serious  and the atmosphere grew heavy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–139<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira had called him away and he had gone off somewhere, so he resorted to waiting in the classroom for him to return.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In stark contrast to the overjoyed Chabashira, his expression was somewhat resentful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Yes. Although I tried to confirm it with Chabashira-sensei tactfully, she didn’t show signs she knew about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Shortly after, I could hear Chabashira and Kouenji from around the corner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira, presumably standing face to face with Kouenji, waited for his question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira to leave. In a bit, the sound of her footsteps disappeared.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “As she entered the classroom, Chabashira’s natural expression turned serious, and the atmosphere grew heavy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\">→ After: Chabashira waits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko sakura-airi miyake-akito hasebe-haruka","q":"hasebe haruka haruka watches the uproar in the front of the classroom with yukimura  sakura and akito  she is closest to his panic  sighs as she looks out at the may sky   can you calm down a little  it hasn t even been 5 minutes since kiyopon left  he was called out by the teacher  right  it s going to be a while   was the question that hard  she thought about it all over again   how had the situation become like this   and decides to stay and talk with yukimura about it  miyake packs his archery club things and she and sakura see him off the turbulent classroom  outspoken  observant  steady  she reads the attributes of the perfect score uproar faster than her classmates and chooses patience over panic  her closest counterpart in the room  she keeps him anchored  she watches with her  sees him off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html#sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p12-1\">Haruka watches the uproar<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the front of the classroom with Yukimura, Sakura and Akito; she is closest to his panic; sighs as she looks out at the May sky. Miyake packs his archery-club things and she and Sakura see him off the turbulent classroom.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “Can you calm down a little? It hasn’t even been 5 minutes since Kiyopon left. He was called out by the teacher, right? It’s going to be a while.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “Was the question that hard?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She thought about it all over again — how had the situation become like this — and decides to stay and talk with Yukimura about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Outspoken, observant, steady; she reads the attributes of the perfect-score uproar faster than her classmates and chooses patience over panic.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Her closest counterpart in the room; she keeps him anchored.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She watches with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Sees him off.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p39-1\">→ After: Haruka mediates and manages<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu coverage note  passing mentions  shared token  every page in this range contains the token  horikita  most often referring to horikita suzune  the sister  manabu himself  identified by name on pages 56  72  73  75  76  77  80  83  271  274  276  277  281  288  289  291  348  carries his own rows above  every other page hit is suzune s name and is recorded on horikita suzune md  the locator s hit set is not a name disambiguation tool  the triage is line by line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p12-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions (shared token)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–350<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Every page in this range contains the token &quot;Horikita&quot;, most often referring to Horikita Suzune (the sister). Manabu himself, identified by name on pages 56, 72, 73, 75, 76, 77, 80, 83, 271, 274, 276, 277, 281, 288, 289, 291, 348, carries his own rows above; every other page hit is Suzune&#x27;s name and is recorded on horikita-suzune.md. The locator&#x27;s hit set is not a name-disambiguation tool; the triage is line-by-line.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–350<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p56-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions (Manabu)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune coverage note  passing mentions  suzune  yukimura gave up waiting for ayanokoji after school because of horikita s appearance  after that  i tried to call horikita  right now  horikita seemed like the most helpful person to resolve the situation   ayanokoji s narration   i ll thank horikita and yosuke another day  they might have understood what i intended  as horikita was the first to leave  the print debates how horikita handled it being easier to pin blame on him than to be honest   kept as printed   and based on what horikita said  you ll continue to hold back after this  right   yeah  i m serious  until i heard horikita s explanation  i was determined to leave because i didn t think kiyotaka could be trusted at all  suzune s name    because of suzune s strategy  right    sudo s question   well  you two have been close ever since school started    sudo s assumption   even carefully selected people such as horikita s older brother  horikita manabu  who had studied martial arts   and there were things he could see only because of his fondness for horikita  he considered asking horikita to force sudo s mouth shut about it  and would have asked horikita to tell sudo to keep quiet   you and suzune  we re not dating    sudo s question  supported manabu and had been scheming  he discovered that manabu s sister horikita was going to join the student council  so he might have wanted to take some kind of action   horikita  or is it one of the boys  as i thought of this  i confirmed who the visitor was through the peephole   horikita told me to keep an eye out on your actions  we don t know how kouenji will act  she said   horikita san and her class are also rapidly gaining strength  in terms of individual strength  some of them wouldn t lose to anyone in the other classes   and then  the leader who brought them together and led them forward  horikita san  she has both excellent academic and physical abilities  and has recently joined the student council   that s right  partnerships can t last forever   a cooperative relationship between classes isn t a bad thing  in fact  didn t you have a similar relationship with horikita san of class d when you were 1st years    sakayanagi   in fact  the reason why ichinose and horikita s class ceased their hostility towards each other  was because of the huge difference in class points   but if you and i group up  horikita san and ryuuen kun might also group up   however  both ryuuen kun and horikita san are formidable opponents   considering horikita had ayanokouji behind her  the battle was never going to be easy   graduated from the same junior high school as horikita and kushida   it would be harder to eliminate an underclassman compared to horikita and i   horikita san and youself are no exception to this   horikita had already joined the student council  but even after that  she couldn t provide me with any new information   i m referring to horikita suzune  who just joined the student council   you wanted horikita manabu s sister to join the student council to monitor nagumo  right    kiriyama   unless horikita thinks nagumo s an obstacle   nagumo was more or less aware of what i d been doing with horikitasenpai   it was just a prettier excuse to keep horikita and i out of his way   he was worried that horikita and i would say something unnecessary   when horikita joined the student council  she was supposed to be introduced to the other members later on  but you came early  vice president  i know the reason for that   someone who wasn t interested in both horikita senpai or i  would be interested in ayanokouji   you and horikita  are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class s groups   our first choice of student to invite wasn t sakayanagi san  ichinose san or even horikita san  i and ishizaki kun both shared this sentiment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p12-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions (Suzune)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–342<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>37 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Yukimura gave up waiting for Ayanokōji after school because of Horikita’s appearance.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> After that, I tried to call Horikita… Right now, Horikita seemed like the most helpful person to resolve the situation — Ayanokōji’s narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’ll thank Horikita and Yosuke another day. They might have understood what I intended, as Horikita was the first to leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> The print debates how Horikita handled it being easier to pin blame on him than to be honest — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “And based on what Horikita said, you’ll continue to hold back after this, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Yeah, I’m serious. Until I heard Horikita’s explanation, I was determined to leave because I didn’t think Kiyotaka could be trusted at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Suzune’s name — “because of Suzune’s strategy, right?” — Sudō’s question.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Well, you two have been close ever since school started.” — Sudō’s assumption.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Even carefully selected people such as Horikita’s older brother, Horikita Manabu, who had studied martial arts…”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “And there were things he could see only because of his fondness for Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> He considered asking Horikita to force Sudō&#x27;s mouth shut about it… and would have asked Horikita to tell Sudō to keep quiet.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You and Suzune… We’re not dating.” — Sudō’s question.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> supported Manabu and had been scheming… he discovered that Manabu’s sister Horikita was going to join the student council, so he might have wanted to take some kind of action.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita? Or is it one of the boys? As I thought of this, I confirmed who the visitor was through the peephole.”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita told me to keep an eye out on your actions. We don’t know how Kouenji will act, she said.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita-san and her class are also rapidly gaining strength. In terms of individual strength, some of them wouldn’t lose to anyone in the other classes…”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “And then, the leader who brought them together and led them forward, Horikita-san. She has both excellent academic and physical abilities, and has recently joined the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That’s right… partnerships can’t last forever.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “A cooperative relationship between classes isn’t a bad thing. In fact, didn’t you have a similar relationship with Horikita-san of Class D when you were 1st years?” — Sakayanagi.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In fact, the reason why Ichinose and Horikita’s class ceased their hostility towards each other, was because of the huge difference in class points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But if you and I group up, Horikita-san and Ryuuen-kun might also group up…”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “However, both Ryuuen-kun and Horikita-san are formidable opponents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Considering Horikita had Ayanokouji behind her, the battle was never going to be easy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “graduated from the same junior high school as Horikita and Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It would be harder to eliminate an underclassman compared to Horikita and I.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita-san and youself are no exception to this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita had already joined the student council, but even after that, she couldn’t provide me with any new information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’m referring to Horikita Suzune, who just joined the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You wanted Horikita Manabu’s sister to join the student council to monitor Nagumo, right?” — Kiriyama.<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Unless Horikita thinks Nagumo’s an obstacle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo was more or less aware of what I’d been doing with Horikitasenpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It was just a prettier excuse to keep Horikita and I out of his way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “He was worried that Horikita and I would say something unnecessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “When Horikita joined the student council, she was supposed to be introduced to the other members later on, but you came early, Vice President. I know the reason for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “someone who wasn’t interested in both Horikita-senpai or I, would be interested in Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You and Horikita, are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class’s groups?”<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “our first choice of student to invite wasn’t Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san or even Horikita-san. I and Ishizaki-kun both shared this sentiment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.342<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p22-1\">→ After: She sits through the uproar without a word<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito miyake shakes off the tension sits with yukimura  haruka and sakura up front  the classroom heavy with speculation over the math score  packs up his archery club things ahead of the others and leaves the turbulent classroom  seen off by sakura and haruka  more than half the class stays behind after him  mentioned by name in keisei s worry about who else doesn t know  akito is assumed to accept kiyotaka as he is  arrives with the group at keyaki mall with keisei and airi  uniform stare at the ichinose ayanokoji conversation  the quiet member of the ayanokoji group  the one keisei is sure will simply take kiyotaka as he is  undisturbed trust  sits with him through the uproar","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html#sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p12-1\">Miyake shakes off the tension<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits with Yukimura, Haruka and Sakura up front; the classroom heavy with speculation over the math score. Packs up his archery-club things ahead of the others and leaves the turbulent classroom, seen off by Sakura and Haruka; more than half the class stays behind after him. Arrives with the group at Keyaki mall with Keisei and Airi; uniform stare at the Ichinose–Ayanokōji conversation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mentioned by name in Keisei&#x27;s worry about who else doesn&#x27;t know; Akito is assumed to accept Kiyotaka as he is.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The quiet member of the Ayanokōji group; the one Keisei is sure will simply take Kiyotaka as he is.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Undisturbed trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Sits with him through the uproar.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p179-1\">→ After: Miyake&#x27;s group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi sakura s soft landing sits with yukimura  haruka and miyake  the class is on edge over the math results  she tries to defuse the tension with a sage smile   s so he solved such a question  kiyotaka kun sure is amazing  the attempt lands badly   yukimura s face tightens  sees miyake off with haruka before the class empties  she tries to soften his agitation  sees him off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p12-1\">Sakura&#x27;s soft landing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits with Yukimura, Haruka and Miyake; the class is on edge over the math results; she tries to defuse the tension with a sage smile. Sees Miyake off with Haruka before the class empties.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “S-so he solved such a question, Kiyotaka-kun sure is amazing!”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The attempt lands badly — Yukimura&#x27;s face tightens.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> She tries to soften his agitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Sees him off.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p27-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka miyake-akito karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko yukimura shakes his leg  the class erupts in the front of the classroom with haruka  sakura and akito  his right leg won t stop trembling since the math results dropped   five minutes ago kiyopon was called out by the teacher and has not returned   can you calm down a little  it hasn t even been 5 minutes since kiyopon left  he was called out by the teacher  right  it s going to be a while   i m calm  don t worry  haruka steers the conversation to what she wanted to know  how he could not understand the question at all  he recounts that the paper was completely out of range for a high school student and that he could not even parse it  the points for each subject dropped drastically as a result   was the question that hard   it s not a question of whether it s hard or not  i didn t even understand the meaning of the question during the exam   after the exam  i tried to analyze the question through my memory and found that it was completely out of range for a highschool student  in other words  this was a question that we shouldn t have been able to solve   what s up with that  what s the school s problem  it s not even a question of what s beyond the range of an exam anymore   it really is unreasonable  that s why the points you could get for each subject dropped drastically  but  there were also a lot of questions that weren t as hard as what chabshira told us they would be   ayanokouji got a perfect score  which should be impossible  i it s like i m witnessing a magic trick  shinohara joins in  do tell me more  he tells the class not a single student in the 2nd year  not even ichinose or sakayanagi  got a perfect score  nobody notices the tablet results are published  karuizawa calls him a math genius and he snaps at her   you ve all checked the tablet  right  is there anyone in the class who got a perfect score in one of the subjects  no  look at the other classes as well  and it ll be clear  look at the entirety of the 2nd year  not a single student  not even ichinose or sakayanagi  got a perfect score  he dismisses karuizawa s tv drama theory  then tell me  why didn t he get a perfect score on his previous math tests  maezono takes karuizawa s side  he loses the thread and starts explaining what he actually suspects   then tell me  why didn t he get a perfect score on his previous math tests  if he can solve questions of the kind that came this time  it doesn t make sense for him to not have gotten a full score or something close to it all along   this isn t something that can be done in a short amount of time  even if he had studied at a higher level than i could imagine  it doesn t explain how he was able to solve questions that are far beyond the knowledge of a high school student  if you can t even understand that  then keep your mouth shut   have you forgotten already  the question was such that even sakayanagi and ichinose couldn t get full marks   i  well  basically  that guy  could probably be good at math at an unbelievable degree  i think   that s not the main point  if that s the case  then that guy  minami setsuya raises the  done something shady  possibility  ike pivots to a leaked paper scenario  he loses patience  it s like i m witnessing a magic trick   that s as stupid as what karuizawa said  sudo stands and shuts the cheating talk down  miyamoto quotes last month s oaa  was 51  now 54  hirata breaks the tension by pointing out club activities  he remains the most agitated in the room as the class thins out  his choice of calling him by last name  ayanokouji  is explicitly marked as resentment  the class notices too  the tutor and the pupil  the confrontation is personal for him  she tries  fails  and steps back  sits with him  heads to club  battles of wits begin and grow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p12-1\">Yukimura shakes his leg; the class erupts<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the front of the classroom with Haruka, Sakura and Akito; his right leg won&#x27;t stop trembling since the math results dropped — five minutes ago Kiyopon was called out by the teacher and has not returned. Haruka steers the conversation to what she wanted to know: how he could not understand the question at all; he recounts that the paper was completely out of range for a high-school student and that he could not even parse it; the points for each subject dropped drastically as a result. Shinohara joins in (“Do tell me more.”); he tells the class not a single student in the 2nd year, not even Ichinose or Sakayanagi, got a perfect score; nobody notices the tablet results are published; Karuizawa calls him a math genius and he snaps at her. He dismisses Karuizawa&#x27;s TV-drama theory (“Then tell me, why didn’t he get a perfect score on his previous math tests?”); Maezono takes Karuizawa&#x27;s side; he loses the thread and starts explaining what he actually suspects. Minami Setsuya raises the “done something shady” possibility; Ike pivots to a leaked-paper scenario; he loses patience (…it’s like I’m witnessing a magic trick). Sudō stands and shuts the cheating talk down; Miyamoto quotes last month&#x27;s OAA (was 51, now 54); Hirata breaks the tension by pointing out club activities; he remains the most agitated in the room as the class thins out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “Can you calm down a little? It hasn’t even been 5 minutes since Kiyopon left. He was called out by the teacher, right? It’s going to be a while.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I’m calm… don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Was the question that hard?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not a question of whether it’s hard or not. I didn’t even understand the meaning of the question during the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After the exam, I tried to analyze the question through my memory and found that it was completely out of range for a highschool student. In other words, this was a question that we shouldn’t have been able to solve.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s up with that? What’s the school’s problem? It’s not even a question of what’s beyond the range of an exam anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It really is unreasonable. That’s why the points you could get for each subject dropped drastically. But, there were also a lot of questions that weren’t as hard as what Chabshira told us they would be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji got a perfect score, which should be impossible. I…it’s like I’m witnessing a magic trick!”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve all checked the tablet, right? Is there anyone in the class who got a perfect score in one of the subjects? No, look at the other classes as well, and it’ll be clear. Look at the entirety of the 2nd year. Not a single student, not even Ichinose or Sakayanagi, got a perfect score.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then tell me, why didn’t he get a perfect score on his previous math tests? If he can solve questions of the kind that came this time, it doesn’t make sense for him to not have gotten a full score or something close to it all along.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t something that can be done in a short amount of time. Even if he had studied at a higher level than I could imagine, it doesn’t explain how he was able to solve questions that are far beyond the knowledge of a high school student! If you can’t even understand that, then keep your mouth shut.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Have you forgotten already? The question was such that even Sakayanagi and Ichinose couldn’t get full marks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I… well, basically, that guy… could probably be good at math at an unbelievable degree, I think.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not the main point. If that’s the case, then that guy-”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s as stupid as what Karuizawa said…”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His choice of calling him by last name (Ayanokouji) is explicitly marked as resentment; the class notices too.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The tutor and the pupil; the confrontation is personal for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She tries, fails, and steps back.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Sits with him; heads to club.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Battles of wits begin and grow.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p23-1\">→ After: The fight for his trust<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p15-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami coverage note  passing mentions  not a single student  not even ichinose or sakayanagi  got a perfect score   the question was such that even sakayanagi and ichinose couldn t get full marks   i checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the oaa  and even ichinose and sakayanagi didn t get   by may  sakayanagi san  ichinose san  and ryuuen kun would definitely have learned of his name   ayanokouji  ichinose seems to trust you a lot  but can  we  really trust you    kanzaki s probe  named in his speech   although we ve broken off the alliance  i don t consider ichinose to be an enemy   are you trying to get some sort of statement from me and have ichinose to listen to it   you  ichinose no  we underestimated your perceptiveness   i m simply going to come out and ask you for help  ichinose trusts you a lot   so you re expecting that to change the way ichinose thinks   ichinose trusts you a lot  that is why i want you to tell her yourself  the way she is right now  she isn t good enough   no matter how you spin it  ichinose  shibata and sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy   even so  ichinose really did agree to team up with that woman   she asked ichinose to help her  now  tsube from class c will help her out   sakayanagi  ichinose  and ryuuen  were also aiming for that very same goal   our first choice of student to invite wasn t sakayanagi san  ichinose san or even horikita san   there are no other student council members from the 2nd grade aside for honami right now so we ve been troubled by that    nagumo on his second year prospect","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p15-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.15–350<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Not a single student, not even Ichinose or Sakayanagi, got a perfect score.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The question was such that even Sakayanagi and Ichinose couldn’t get full marks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the OAA, and even Ichinose and Sakayanagi didn’t get”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “by May, Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san, and Ryuuen-kun would definitely have learned of his name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ayanokouji, Ichinose seems to trust you a lot, but can ‘we’ really trust you?” — Kanzaki’s probe, named in his speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Although we’ve broken off the alliance, I don’t consider Ichinose to be an enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Are you trying to get some sort of statement from me and have Ichinose to listen to it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You… Ichinose…no, we underestimated your perceptiveness.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’m simply going to come out and ask you for help. Ichinose trusts you a lot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “So you’re expecting that to change the way Ichinose thinks?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ichinose trusts you a lot. That is why I want you to tell her yourself: the way she is right now, she isn’t good enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “no matter how you spin it, Ichinose, Shibata and Sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Even so, Ichinose really did agree to team up with that woman.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “she asked Ichinose to help her. Now, Tsube from Class C will help her out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi, Ichinose, and Ryuuen, were also aiming for that very same goal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Our first choice of student to invite wasn’t Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san or even Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.342<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “There are no other student council members from the 2nd grade aside for Honami right now so we’ve been troubled by that.” — Nagumo on his second-year prospect.<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p46-1\">→ After: Ichinose at Keyaki mall; the pact<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p15-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei karuizawa s math genius theory on the anger out front of the class argument  she files ayanokoji under tv drama math genius   maybe ayanokouji kun is just a math genius  you know  sometimes in those tv dramas and stuff  isn t there  like  a protagonist that only uses math or something to solve the murder case  i m getting that kind of feeling   what s the point in asking me that  well  maybe it s something like  he studied really hard during the spring break or something   i don t know anything about that  so can you stop getting so angry so easily  you re pissing me off  maezono backs her  she digs into yukimura with the  maybe it s just you  jab   you ve got a big mouth  but couldn t it just be that you didn t understand the question  maybe it s just you that couldn t solve the question  but the question itself wasn t that hard  was it   then maybe he just happened to know that question   so what s the problem  that s what i said  that he was a math genius  right   ah  sorry for interrupting  i had a thought  picks sudo s growth story against miyamoto  then revives her own math genius reading   isn t it just as sudo kun says  after all  sudo kun s academic ability surpassed miyamoto kun s too   so that s why there s a possibility that he s holding back  just like koenji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p15-1\">Karuizawa&#x27;s math-genius theory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.15–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the anger-out front of the class argument; she files Ayanokōji under TV-drama math genius. Maezono backs her; she digs into Yukimura with the “Maybe it’s just you” jab. Picks Sudō&#x27;s growth story against Miyamoto; then revives her own math-genius reading.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Maybe Ayanokouji-kun is just a math genius! You know, sometimes in those TV dramas and stuff, isn’t there, like, a protagonist that only uses math or something to solve the murder case? I’m getting that kind of feeling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “What’s the point in asking me that? Well, maybe it’s something like, he studied really hard during the spring break or something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I don’t know anything about that. So can you stop getting so angry so easily? You’re pissing me off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve got a big mouth, but couldn’t it just be that you didn’t understand the question? Maybe it’s just you that couldn’t solve the question, but the question itself wasn’t that hard, was it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then maybe he just happened to know that question?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what’s the problem? That’s what I said, that he was a math genius, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, sorry for interrupting. I had a thought…”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it just as Sudo-kun says? After all, Sudo-kun’s academic ability surpassed Miyamoto-kun’s too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So that’s why there’s a possibility that he’s holding back, just like Koenji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p36-1\">→ After: Karuizawa protects Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p15-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu","q":"sakayanagi arisu coverage note  passing mentions  not a single student  not even ichinose or sakayanagi  got a perfect score   sakayanagi and ichinose couldn t get full marks   i checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the oaa  and even ichinose and sakayanagi didn t get   by may  sakayanagi san  ichinose san  and ryuuen kun would definitely have learned of his name   in order to avoid getting expelled  yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves  and sakayanagi san s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through   and in fact  at that time  ayanokouji kun was at risk of dropping out due to sakayanagi san s strategy  although that was when he was completely average and was coincidentally chosen as a patsy  it s possible that it really was aimed at him   speaking of sakayanagi san  she got similar scores in all her subjects  right   i know she was smart  but ever since the introduction of the oaa  her strength has become more apparent  there s a limit to test scores  the second in the year    sakayanagi san named on this page   class a s sakayanagi knew about me from before  and ryuuen had the experience of being beaten down by me  so he would naturally know that i wasn t only good at math   sakayanagi  ichinose  ryuuen  those people would probably cry from the joy   or maybe she was the same as sakayanagi  honing her abilities in a place that had nothing to do with the white room   how will sakayanagi  ryuuen  and ichinose act   but  as yosuke said  sakayanagi tended never to let the prey she decided on escape   allowing the other proposers to accept sakayanagi s hostility   if sakayanagi became aware of this information  she would naturally make her move as well   sakayanagi s   no matter how you spin it  ichinose  shibata and sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy   only on the day of the exam shall we know how sakayanagi will act  and no one will know before she says so   that s true  if you want her gone  you ll have to stab her at least twice   it was extremely difficult to get sakayanagi  who had both enough private and protection points  expelled   totsuka yahiko  a great admirer of katsuragi  was expelled from the school because of sakayanagi   the contract wasn t signed by sakayanagi  their current leader  but by katsuragi  who had receded into the shadows by now   i ll soon defeat sakayanagi  and then the entire class a will fall   without sakayanagi  their head  it would be difficult for class a to continue fighting on the front lines   after negotiating with sakayanagi  i m giving this thing up for 5 million points   albeit half the original value  sakayanagi would be able to predict what ryuuen would do with the money  the narration prints  however  sakayanagi accepted such a favourable proposal despite knowing the risks   the sentence runs across the page turn with the printed footer in between  kept as printed   if i were sakayanagi  i would have agreed to ryuuen s proposal as well   katsuragi had buried his desire for vengeance against sakayanagi in his heart   the fierce competitors and representatives of the other classes  sakayanagi  ichinose  and ryuuen  were also aiming for that very same goal   sakayanagi    the chairman s allegations  see tsukishiro s person record   our first choice of student to invite wasn t sakayanagi san  ichinose san or even horikita san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p15-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.15–342<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Not a single student, not even Ichinose or Sakayanagi, got a perfect score.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi and Ichinose couldn’t get full marks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the OAA, and even Ichinose and Sakayanagi didn’t get”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “by May, Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san, and Ryuuen-kun would definitely have learned of his name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In order to avoid getting expelled, Yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves, and Sakayanagi-san’s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “And in fact, at that time, Ayanokouji-kun was at risk of dropping out due to Sakayanagi-san’s strategy. Although that was when he was completely average and was coincidentally chosen as a patsy, it’s possible that it really was aimed at him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Speaking of Sakayanagi-san, she got similar scores in all her subjects, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I know she was smart, but ever since the introduction of the OAA, her strength has become more apparent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> there’s a limit to test scores… the second in the year. — Sakayanagi-san named on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Class A’s Sakayanagi knew about me from before, and Ryuuen had the experience of being beaten down by me, so he would naturally know that I wasn’t only good at math.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi, Ichinose, Ryuuen. Those people would probably cry from the joy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Or maybe she was the same as Sakayanagi, honing her abilities in a place that had nothing to do with the White Room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “How will Sakayanagi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose act?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But, as Yosuke said, Sakayanagi tended never to let the prey she decided on escape.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Allowing the other proposers to accept Sakayanagi’s hostility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If Sakayanagi became aware of this information, she would naturally make her move as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi’s.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “no matter how you spin it, Ichinose, Shibata and Sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Only on the day of the exam shall we know how Sakayanagi will act, and no one will know before she says so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That’s true, if you want her gone, you’ll have to stab her at least twice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It was extremely difficult to get Sakayanagi, who had both enough private and protection points, expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Totsuka Yahiko, a great admirer of Katsuragi, was expelled from the school because of Sakayanagi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “the contract wasn’t signed by Sakayanagi, their current leader, but by Katsuragi, who had receded into the shadows by now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’ll soon defeat Sakayanagi, and then the entire Class A will fall.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Without Sakayanagi, their head, it would be difficult for Class A to continue fighting on the front lines.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After negotiating with Sakayanagi, I’m giving this thing up for 5 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “albeit half the original value, Sakayanagi would be able to predict what Ryuuen would do with the money.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> The narration prints: however, Sakayanagi accepted such a favourable proposal despite knowing the risks — the sentence runs across the page turn with the printed footer in between; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If I were Sakayanagi, I would have agreed to Ryuuen’s proposal as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Katsuragi had buried his desire for vengeance against Sakayanagi in his heart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The fierce competitors and representatives of the other classes, Sakayanagi, Ichinose, and Ryuuen, were also aiming for that very same goal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi” — the chairman’s allegations; see Tsukishiro’s person record.<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Our first choice of student to invite wasn’t Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san or even Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.342<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p203-1\">→ After: The café invitation to Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-y2v2-p15-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"shinohara","q":"shinohara shinohara in the uproar the roster carries both  shinohara   this file  and  shinohara satsuki  for the same class 1 d student  scene anchors for this volume are written on shinohara satsuki md  this file keeps the same page range for traceability  see shinohara satsuki md for the lines themselves  recorded as a duplicate roster row for the owner   do not merge from this side  checks the shared tablet with the class  reacts beside ike to the cheating talk  recruited into the cover story","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-y2v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Shinohara in the uproar<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.15–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara\">Shinohara<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The roster carries both `shinohara` (this file) and `shinohara-satsuki` for the same Class 1-D student; scene anchors for this volume are written on shinohara-satsuki.md. This file keeps the same page range for traceability; see shinohara-satsuki.md for the lines themselves. Recorded as a duplicate roster row for the owner — do not merge from this side.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Checks the shared tablet with the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Reacts beside Ike to the cheating talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Recruited into the cover story.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-y2v2-p168-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions (legacy duplicate)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p15-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko shinohara-satsuki","q":"shinohara satsuki shinohara in the uproar she swipes the tablet yukimura hands her  incredulous that the 2nd year results are published   do tell me more   i didn t even notice  you can even see the results of the other classes  why is that   waaah  i hate this  wouldn t this mean that a lot of people will know my scores  this is the worst  stands beside ike  the class s talk turns to cheating  she cannot parse the leap   cheat  how would he even cheat  recruited by karuizawa to ratify the cover story  plays along with flawless instinct   that s right  i    feel like i ve been seeing horikita san and ayanokouji kun talking secretly for a long time now  but it turns out that they re really just doing it for the class  quick  trusting  literal   a player piece without knowing it  the class uses her credibility both ways  she does karuizawa s bidding without realizing the play  she watches his meltdown and echoes it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p15-1\">Shinohara in the uproar<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.15–19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She swipes the tablet Yukimura hands her, incredulous that the 2nd-year results are published. Stands beside Ike; the class&#x27;s talk turns to cheating; she cannot parse the leap. Recruited by Karuizawa to ratify the cover story; plays along with flawless instinct.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Do tell me more.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “I didn’t even notice. You can even see the results of the other classes. Why is that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Waaah, I hate this! Wouldn’t this mean that a lot of people will know my scores? This is the worst!”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cheat? How would he even cheat?”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right! I …  feel like I’ve been seeing Horikita-san and Ayanokouji-kun talking secretly for a long time now, but it turns out that they’re really just doing it for the class!”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quick, trusting, literal — a player piece without knowing it; the class uses her credibility both ways.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She does Karuizawa&#x27;s bidding without realizing the play.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> She watches his meltdown and echoes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p168-1\">→ After: The Komiya turn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-maezono-y2v2-p16-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko maezono","q":"maezono maezono backs karuizawa fires back at yukimura at the boiling point  helping karuizawa   yeah  yeah  isn t it weird that you re taking your anger out on karuizawasan  his ally in the argument  target of the jab","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-maezono-y2v2-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/maezono.html#sc-maezono-y2v2-p16-1\">Maezono backs Karuizawa<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.16–17<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/maezono.html\">Maezono<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fires back at Yukimura at the boiling point, helping Karuizawa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Maezono<\/b> “Yeah, yeah! Isn’t it weird that you’re taking your anger out on Karuizawasan?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His ally in the argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Target of the jab.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p18-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken shinohara-satsuki miyamoto-soshi ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ike s cheating theory remembers the spring past questions incident  supplies the leaked paper hypothesis out loud   it s definitely possible  like seeing the question paper beforehand or something  remember  didn t that happen in the 1st year as well  it was the one test that asked the exact same questions as the previous years  he pushes the hacking angle  shinohara beside him cannot follow the leap   hacking the school computers and stealing the answers or something  isn t that possible  pushes sudo on the fairness front  then  absorbing karuizawa s holding back theory  lands his did not contribute complaint   what do you mean  ken  don t tell me you re taking ayanokouji s side   well isn t that even more of a problem  doesn t that mean he didn t contribute to the class  ike is a long time sudo friend  the betrayal of the circle reading of the perfect score simmers underneath the jokes  he goes for the obvious angle with his old friend on the other side  she stands beside him  they trade the evidence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p18-1\">Ike&#x27;s cheating theory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.18–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Remembers the spring past-questions incident; supplies the leaked-paper hypothesis out loud. He pushes the hacking angle; Shinohara beside him cannot follow the leap. Pushes Sudō on the fairness front; then, absorbing Karuizawa&#x27;s holding-back theory, lands his did-not-contribute complaint.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyamoto-soshi.html\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “It’s definitely possible. Like seeing the question paper beforehand or something. Remember, didn’t that happen in the 1st year as well? It was the one test that asked the exact same questions as the previous years!”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Hacking the school computers and stealing the answers or something! Isn’t that possible!”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “What do you mean, Ken? Don’t tell me you’re taking Ayanokouji’s side?”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well isn’t that even more of a problem? Doesn’t that mean he didn’t contribute to the class?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike is a long-time Sudō friend; the betrayal-of-the-circle reading of the perfect score simmers underneath the jokes.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He goes for the obvious angle with his old friend on the other side.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She stands beside him.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/b> They trade the evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p54-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-minami-hakuo-y2v2-p18-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"minami-hakuo","q":"minami hakuo coverage note  zero whole word occurrences the locator hit on this page is  minami setsuya   the roster row minami setsuya  the corpus contains no occurrence of hakuo anywhere in this volume  recorded as a zero hit row  the minami setsuya page marks the actual scene","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-minami-hakuo-y2v2-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/minami-hakuo.html#sc-minami-hakuo-y2v2-p18-1\">Coverage note: zero whole-word occurrences<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.18<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/minami-hakuo.html\">Minami Hakuo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The locator hit on this page is &quot;Minami Setsuya&quot; (the roster row minami-setsuya); the corpus contains no occurrence of Hakuo anywhere in this volume. Recorded as a zero-hit row; the minami-setsuya page marks the actual scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-minami-setsuya-y2v2-p18-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko minami-setsuya","q":"minami setsuya minami raises the shady possibility throws himself into the fray as the mood darkens   ayanokouji getting a perfect score is indeed confusing  and i don t think there s anything strange with what yukimura said  it s just that  isn t this happening too suddenly  after all  he s never gotten any amazing marks before   that s why i was wondering  has this ayanokouji done something shady  he seeds the cheating hypothesis  he adds doubt from a different direction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-minami-setsuya-y2v2-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Minami raises the shady possibility<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.18<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#minami-setsuya\">Minami Setsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Throws himself into the fray as the mood darkens.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Minami Setsuya<\/b> “Ayanokouji getting a perfect score is indeed confusing, and I don’t think there’s anything strange with what Yukimura said. It’s just that, isn’t this happening too suddenly? After all, he’s never gotten any amazing marks…”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Minami Setsuya<\/b> “That’s why I was wondering, has this Ayanokouji done something shady?”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji getting a perfect score is indeed confusing, and I don’t think there’s anything strange with what Yukimura said. It’s just that, isn’t this happening too suddenly? After all, he’s never gotten any amazing marks before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He seeds the cheating hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> He adds doubt from a different direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyamoto-soshi-y2v2-p18-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji sudou-ken miyamoto-soshi","q":"miyamoto soshi miyamoto s oaa case he parses ike s leak theory with cold logic   but assuming that the questions were exactly the same as those in the past  isn t it weird that he didn t give us that information  and it s also weird that no one in the other classes noticed it as well   then  it s the method that must not be named  knowing the answer to the question in advance  cheating  he has checked the updated oaa data after school  the case is airtight in his mind   if we re talking about ability  his academic score in oaa last month was lower than mine  right  it would have been impossible if he was not cheating   we well  that s because sudo was studying hard  i acknowledge his growth  but but ayanokouji is growing too much  too fast  the data man  numbers are his character witness   and they lose him the room anyway when ike s math genius framing takes over  they trade the oaa numbers  he is stung by sudo s jump past him  54 vs 53","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyamoto-soshi-y2v2-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/miyamoto-soshi.html#sc-miyamoto-soshi-y2v2-p18-1\">Miyamoto&#x27;s OAA case<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.18–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/miyamoto-soshi.html\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He parses Ike&#x27;s leak theory with cold logic. He has checked the updated OAA data after school; the case is airtight in his mind.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/b> “But assuming that the questions were exactly the same as those in the past, isn’t it weird that he didn’t give us that information? And it’s also weird that no one in the other classes noticed it as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/b> “Then… it’s the method that must not be named, knowing the answer to the question in advance…? Cheating.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/b> “If we’re talking about ability, his academic score in OAA last month was lower than mine, right? It would have been impossible if he was not cheating!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We-well, that’s because Sudo was studying hard, I acknowledge his growth, but…but Ayanokouji is growing too much, too fast!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The data man; numbers are his character witness — and they lose him the room anyway when Ike&#x27;s math-genius framing takes over.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> They trade the OAA numbers.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He is stung by Sudō&#x27;s jump past him (54 vs 53).<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p19-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken sudo shuts down the cheating talk he had been listening silently  he stands and his 186cm frame gathers the room   you seem to be getting rather excited  but there isn t even a shred of evidence of ayanokouji cheating  is there  don t just jump to conclusions when the person in question isn t here  he weathers ike s prod  then stakes his own read   that s not what i meant  but there is no way he was easily able to see the question paper  right  i just thought that it s more likely that he got that perfect score with his own abilities   that just means he s different from last year  anyone can grow  hirata nudges him toward club  he goes   glancing at the back of suzune  who has said nothing all commotion   eh  ahhhh  now that you say that  his oaa jump to 54  physical a  96  has outrun miyamoto  53    noticed by the whole class  he is the first to wave the cheating talk off on the record","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p19-1\">Sudō shuts down the cheating talk<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.19–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He had been listening silently; he stands and his 186cm frame gathers the room. He weathers Ike&#x27;s prod, then stakes his own read. Hirata nudges him toward club; he goes — glancing at the back of Suzune, who has said nothing all commotion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “You seem to be getting rather excited, but there isn’t even a shred of evidence of Ayanokouji cheating, is there? Don’t just jump to conclusions when the person in question isn’t here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “That’s not what I meant. But there is no way he was easily able to see the question paper, right?… I just thought that it’s more likely that he got that perfect score with his own abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “That just means he’s different from last year. Anyone can grow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Ahhhh, now that you say that…”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His OAA jump to 54 (physical A+ 96) has outrun Miyamoto (53) — noticed by the whole class.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He is the first to wave the cheating talk off on the record.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p54-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s big question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p20-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke coverage note  passing mentions  so that s why there s a possibility that he s holding back  just like koenji   it s not like you re holding the class back like koenji  so no one has the right to complain   kouenji also returned to his seat  using his usual mirror to look at himself  revelling in it   there s also kouenji kun  whose strengths and limits are still a mystery  he too is a dangerous adversary   she s a lot like kouenji from your year  all her words and actions  if you take her seriously  you ll just be wasting your time   in a way  kouenji rokusuke was someone who had a unique personality  and if you were similar to him  you would be pretty strange too   from her words  she did indeed seem very similar to kouenji   kouenji also seemed to like this school  and enjoyed all of its benefits to the max   in our class  only you  i  and koenji haven t formed a group yet  us three   you and koenji are the only ones left in the class  that means there s no way to form a group anymore","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p20-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.20–317<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “So that’s why there’s a possibility that he’s holding back, just like Koenji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It’s not like you’re holding the class back like Koenji, so no one has the right to complain.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Kouenji also returned to his seat, using his usual mirror to look at himself, revelling in it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “there’s also Kouenji-kun, whose strengths and limits are still a mystery; he too is a dangerous adversary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “She’s a lot like Kouenji from your year. All her words and actions, if you take her seriously, you’ll just be wasting your time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In a way, Kouenji Rokusuke was someone who had a unique personality, and if you were similar to him, you would be pretty strange too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “From her words, she did indeed seem very similar to Kouenji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Kouenji also seemed to like this school, and enjoyed all of its benefits to the max.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In our class, only you, I, and Koenji haven’t formed a group yet, us three.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You and Koenji are the only ones left in the class. That means there’s no way to form a group anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p137-1\">→ After: The sick-leave loophole, priced in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p21-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke hirata presses pause when the speculation crests  he steps in as the class s assumed arbitrator   let s all calm down a bit  we can t solve the problem by just getting heated up here  can we   sudo kun  isn t it almost time for your club activities   i know you re concerned about this topic  but there are many things that are uncertain right now  i do not think it is good to let your club activities be affected by mere speculation  you know by now that the         excuse won t work  right  he usually leads by unifying the class  this time he keeps quiet until the end  reads the temperature precisely  then breaks the impasse by dispersing the room  he redirects sudo to club","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p21-1\">Hirata presses pause<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.21–22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">When the speculation crests, he steps in as the class&#x27;s assumed arbitrator.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Let’s all calm down a bit. We can’t solve the problem by just getting heated up here, can we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Sudo-kun, isn’t it almost time for your club activities?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I know you’re concerned about this topic, but there are many things that are uncertain right now. I do not think it is good to let your club activities be affected by mere speculation. You know by now that the …  …  … excuse…”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you’re concerned about this topic, but there are many things that are uncertain right now. I do not think it is good to let your club activities be affected by mere speculation. You know by now that the …  …  … excuse won’t work, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He usually leads by unifying the class; this time he keeps quiet until the end, reads the temperature precisely, then breaks the impasse by dispersing the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He redirects Sudō to club.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p29-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p22-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune she sits through the uproar without a word in the back of the classroom through the whole perfect score commotion  ayanokoji watches sudo leave after a glance at her back  she says nothing the entire time  the detail lands as quiet assessment  not absence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p22-1\">She sits through the uproar without a word<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the back of the classroom through the whole perfect-score commotion; Ayanokōji watches Sudō leave after a glance at her back.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She says nothing the entire time; the detail lands as quiet assessment, not absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions (Suzune)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p27-1\">→ After: The reserve strategy: Horikita saves him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after tsukishiro s office  chabashira waits under tsukishiro s watch he leaves the reception room  lets out a short breath  and concludes that the only way out of the chain following him is expulsion   you ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on   i m not too happy about it  but it was a necessary measure  i can only assume that this is within the bounds of what is permitted   ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment  how are you going to explain it to your own class  you ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous  but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math test  of course they won t leave you alone now  have you prepared for this scenario beforehand   there s no use in acting in advance  i ll start from this stage   this is going to be hard for you  prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions   i know   can we stop here  if i m walking with a teacher alone from now on  it ll attract a lot of unnecessary attention  chabashira does not know about the white room  to her he is connected to the father of one of her students  which is why her caution and warmth toward him differ from his  her joy at his perfect score is comical to him and inconvenient   a leverage point that now gets in the way  waiting not far from the reception room after tsukishiro s summons  he casts her into the back of his mind  he has just left the acting director s office under his watch  the chain that follows him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\">After Tsukishiro&#x27;s office; Chabashira waits<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23–26<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Under Tsukishiro&#x27;s watch he leaves the reception room, lets out a short breath, and concludes that the only way out of the chain following him is expulsion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “You’ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m not too happy about it, but it was a necessary measure. I can only assume that this is within the bounds of what is permitted.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment, how are you going to explain it to your own class? You’ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous, but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math…”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment, how are you going to explain it to your own class? You’ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous, but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math test. Of course they won’t leave you alone now. Have you prepared for this scenario beforehand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no use in acting in advance. I’ll start from this stage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is going to be hard for you. Prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can we stop here? If I’m walking with a teacher alone from now on, it’ll attract a lot of unnecessary attention.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Chabashira does not know about the White Room; to her he is connected to the father of one of her students, which is why her caution and warmth toward him differ from his; her joy at his perfect score is comical to him and inconvenient — a leverage point that now gets in the way.<span class=\"pg\">p.24–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Waiting not far from the reception room after Tsukishiro&#x27;s summons; he casts her into the back of his mind.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> He has just left the Acting Director&#x27;s office under his watch; the chain that follows him.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\">→ After: The class confronts him; Horikita&#x27;s cover story<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsukishiro chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira waits waiting not far from the reception room when ayanokoji emerges under tsukishiro s watch  she falls in beside him casually   you ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on   ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment  how are you going to explain it to your own class  you ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous  but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math test  of course they won t leave you alone now  have you prepared for this scenario beforehand   this is going to be hard for you  prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions  the perfect score uproar has moved her  the homeroom teacher mask slips   she is overflowing with joy she tries to suppress  and fails with him specifically  she does not know the white room exists  she waits for him wrongly  eagerly  openly   to him  a manipulable counterpart  she was briefed against leaving without seeing him  the summons was hers to answer for too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\">Chabashira waits<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23–26<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting not far from the reception room when Ayanokōji emerges under Tsukishiro&#x27;s watch; she falls in beside him casually.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “You’ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment, how are you going to explain it to your own class? You’ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous, but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math…”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “This is going to be hard for you. Prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment, how are you going to explain it to your own class? You’ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous, but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math test. Of course they won’t leave you alone now. Have you prepared for this scenario beforehand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The perfect-score uproar has moved her; the homeroom-teacher mask slips — she is overflowing with joy she tries to suppress, and fails with him specifically; she does not know the White Room exists.<span class=\"pg\">p.24–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She waits for him wrongly, eagerly, openly — to him, a manipulable counterpart.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> She was briefed against leaving without seeing him; the summons was hers to answer for too.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\">→ After: The briefing continues<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"housen-kazuomi","q":"hosen kazuomi coverage note  passing mentions  although i injured my left hand in the conflict against hosen  i managed to eliminate my risk of getting expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html#sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p23-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Although I injured my left hand in the conflict against Hosen, I managed to eliminate my risk of getting expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p220-1\">→ After: The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro","q":"tsukishiro coverage note  passing mentions  under tsukishiro s watch  i left the reception room   as of now  tsukishiro didn t know that i was working with chabashira  who was the homeroom teacher of class 2 d  and mashima sensei of class 2 a   this was tsukishiro  so i couldn t rule out the possibility of this being one of his traps   it had been just about thirty minutes since i d been summoned by tsukishiro   it seemed to be out of tsukishiro s control  but what exactly were they thinking   horikita didn t know about the individual actions that tsukishiro might take  so her options were bound to be limited   this was because of tsukishiro and the white room student lurking in the 1st year   this was because of tsukishiro and the white room student lurking in the 1st year   it s possible that tsukishiro had given me the card in order to help force my expulsion  but given that the card can be transferred  that was far too weak of a strategy to pressure me   it was absolutely inconceivable that tsukishiro had nothing to do with it   tsukishiro    the class s understanding that he s the one behind the spring exam   it was now confirmed that tsukishiro and nagumo were the ones behind the 20 million points   tsukishiro s likely involvement finally revealed itself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html#sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p23-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23–257<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Under Tsukishiro’s watch, I left the reception room…”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “As of now, Tsukishiro didn’t know that I was working with Chabashira, who was the homeroom teacher of Class 2-D, and Mashima-sensei of Class 2-A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “this was Tsukishiro, so I couldn’t rule out the possibility of this being one of his traps.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It had been just about thirty minutes since I’d been summoned by Tsukishiro.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It seemed to be out of Tsukishiro’s control, but what exactly were they thinking?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita didn’t know about the individual actions that Tsukishiro might take, so her options were bound to be limited.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “This was because of Tsukishiro and the White Room student lurking in the 1st year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “This was because of Tsukishiro and the White Room student lurking in the 1st year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It’s possible that Tsukishiro had given me the card in order to help force my expulsion, but given that the card can be transferred, that was far too weak of a strategy to pressure me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It was absolutely inconceivable that Tsukishiro had nothing to do with it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Tsukishiro.” — the class’s understanding that he&#x27;s the one behind the spring exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It was now confirmed that Tsukishiro and Nagumo were the ones behind the 20 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Tsukishiro’s likely involvement finally revealed itself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p336-1\">→ After: Tsukishiro&#x27;s fireworks<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hasebe-haruka sakura-airi horikita-suzune miyake-akito yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko the fight for his trust after chabashira s exchange with ayanokoji  unseen by him  the classroom empties of club students  he waits through the whole thirty minutes  ayanokoji returns  he leads the charge with haruka and airi behind him  he confronts the perfect score head on   you  what s with the 100 points in math  i checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the oaa  and even ichinose and sakayanagi didn t get   p   erfect score   s  you re the only one in the entire year   i m  asking kiyotaka    what do you mean   that s right  to be honest  my head is a mess  i said this before  right  the questions at the end of the paper were impossible to solve  but kiyotaka did them all like nobody s business  and i just can t understand it   kiyotaka should know very well that nobody in the class could solve those problems  yet we didn t even see him brag about how he solved them  isn t that weird  it even makes it seem like he has something he can t reveal  maybe he did something bad  and knew the answers from the start  or something like that   better than you in academics  hold on  i remember kiyotaka s scores being about average all around since school started  i m sorry  but i can t see anything about it being worthy of special attention  isn t his grade on the oaa a c  the overall average   a little strategy   your words are hardly convincing  if you had doubts surrounding the rules of the school  it would be beneficial for the class as a whole for him to get higher scores from the start  since he got a perfect score on this exam  getting an a or a  in academic ability isn t impossible  you could say it was just one person s grades  but even that could ve slowly increased the number of points of our class   what i think his future would have been like   so you re saying  people might have targeted him   no  that s wrong  if kiyotaka had been serious from the start  even if we were to put yamauchi and him at different ends of a balance the result would have been clear as day   so why are you revealing this now  if you carelessly reveal his strength  the results will be the same  he s been drawing attention now that you suddenly showed his strength to everyone  and soon he could also become a target   the student known as ayanokouji kiyotaka  has he shown the full extent of his abilities  or is he still holding back  no matter what the real truth is  we can hide it to ensure ayanokouji continues to remain a thorn on their side for the other classes   a strategy of hiding our strength  that s true  the other classes must also be quite shocked now  the group corners him in the hallway after class  he confesses he was determined to leave  haruka forces the handshake  he accepts continued tutoring   kiyotaka   why didn t you tell us before  if it s to hide information as horikita said  does that mean that you don t trust us at all   to be honest  i m still angry  you could have told me from the start that you didn t need to be taught  that you could have passed the exam without any problems  and that you could have handled it on your own   and based on what horikita said  you ll continue to hold back after this  right  if you don t tell me which subject you will and will not hold back in  i can t completely trust you   i want out of this group  well  i d be lying if i said i didn t have that thought   yeah  i m serious  until i heard horikita s explanation  i was determined to leave because i didn t think kiyotaka could be trusted at all  but even so  after being in the same group for so long  i can still understand some things  i know that kiyotaka isn t a bad person  since he was hiding something for the sake of the entire class  it s understandable that he didn t want to tell anyone  kiyotaka could have told me that he didn t need tutoring  that is true  but he s bad with words  so he couldn t say it  i can understand that too   it s just yeah  it s just  i need some time to sort my thoughts out   there s no advantage in taking this further  in the end  what i wanted to say  what i wanted to express is  it doesn t matter even if you hide your strength in other areas  it s not like you re holding the class back like koenji  so no one has the right to complain  if i continue to criticize you forcefully  the atmosphere will become even worse   even though my rational side is clear with that  i can t suppress it emotionally  so i ll need to reflect on that  next  i ll recognize the part of your strength that you revealed as a real thing  as for the other subjects  i ll      continue to    use my previous assumption that you re passable  and i ll continue to tutor you  is that fine   don t  it s embarrassing   i know  i know   i m fine with it  but akito still doesn t know anything   miyacchi probably won t be a problem  i think he ll just accept kiyopon like normal right   well  everything s back to normal  it feels we ve taken a huge weight off our shoulders  right   isn t getting full marks a bit excessive  sakayanagi  who was 2nd in the year  got 91 points   speaking of sakayanagi san  she got similar scores in all her subjects  right   i know she was smart  but ever since the introduction of the oaa  her strength has become more apparent  a perfectionist s pride bruised in public  he holds the line of honesty but breaks anyway  because he cannot out logic his own hurt  his forgiveness is real but partial  the wound between them  the reconciliation  she buffers him and airi from the worst of it  she sees haruka s strange stiffness too  she shields the truth  he audits it  the one he trusts will just take kiyotaka as he is","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p23-1\">The fight for his trust<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23–45<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After Chabashira&#x27;s exchange with Ayanokōji (unseen by him), the classroom empties of club students; he waits through the whole thirty minutes. Ayanokōji returns; he leads the charge with Haruka and Airi behind him; he confronts the perfect score head-on. The group corners him in the hallway after class; he confesses he was determined to leave; Haruka forces the handshake; he accepts continued tutoring.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You… what’s with the 100 points in math? I checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the OAA, and even Ichinose and Sakayanagi didn’t get … p … erfect score … s. You’re the only one in the entire year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I’m… asking Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “… What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>34 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right… To be honest, my head is a mess. I said this before, right? The questions at the end of the paper were impossible to solve. But Kiyotaka did them all like nobody’s business, and I just can’t understand it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka should know very well that nobody in the class could solve those problems. Yet we didn’t even see him brag about how he solved them. Isn’t that weird? It even makes it seem like he has something he can’t reveal… maybe he did something bad, and knew the answers from the start, or something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Better than you in academics? Hold on. I remember Kiyotaka’s scores being about average all around since school started. I’m sorry, but I can’t see anything about it being worthy of special attention. Isn’t his grade on the OAA a C, the overall average?”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…A little strategy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your words are hardly convincing. If you had doubts surrounding the rules of the school, it would be beneficial for the class as a whole for him to get higher scores from the start. Since he got a perfect score on this exam, getting an A or A+ in academic ability isn’t impossible. You could say it was just one person’s grades, but even that could’ve slowly increased the number of points of our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I think his future would have been like…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re saying, people might have targeted him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s wrong. If Kiyotaka had been serious from the start, even if we were to put Yamauchi and him at different ends of a balance the result would have been clear as day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So why are you revealing this now? If you carelessly reveal his strength, the results will be the same. He’s been drawing attention now that you suddenly showed his strength to everyone, and soon he could also become a target.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student known as Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, has he shown the full extent of his abilities, or is he still holding back? No matter what the real truth is, we can hide it to ensure Ayanokouji continues to remain a thorn on their side for the other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A strategy of hiding our strength…. That’s true, the other classes must also be quite shocked now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why didn’t you tell us before?… If it’s to hide information as Horikita said, does that mean that you don’t trust us at all?”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I’m still angry. You could have told me from the start that you didn’t need to be taught, that you could have passed the exam without any problems, and that you could have handled it on your own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And based on what Horikita said, you’ll continue to hold back after this, right? If you don’t tell me which subject you will and will not hold back in, I can’t completely trust you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want out of this group- Well, I’d be lying if I said I didn’t have that thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, I’m serious. Until I heard Horikita’s explanation, I was determined to leave because I didn’t think Kiyotaka could be trusted at all. But…even so, after being in the same group for so long, I can still understand some things. I know that Kiyotaka isn’t a bad person. Since he was hiding something for the sake of the entire class, it’s understandable that he didn’t want to tell anyone. Kiyotaka could have told me that he didn’t need tutoring, that is true, but he’s bad with words, so he couldn’t say it. I can understand that too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s just…yeah, it’s just… I need some time to sort my thoughts out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no advantage in taking this further… In the end, what I wanted to say, what I wanted to express is… it doesn’t matter even if you hide your strength in other areas. It’s not like you’re holding the class back like Koenji, so no one has the right to complain. If I continue to criticize you forcefully, the atmosphere will become even worse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though my rational side is clear with that, I can’t suppress it emotionally, so I’ll need to reflect on that. Next, I’ll recognize the part of your strength that you revealed as a real thing. As for the other subjects, I’ll …  … continue to …  use my previous assumption that you’re passable, and I’ll continue to tutor you. Is that fine?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t, it’s embarrassing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know, I know…!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m fine with it, but Akito still doesn’t know anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Miyacchi probably won’t be a problem. I think he’ll just accept Kiyopon like normal right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, everything’s back to normal. It feels we’ve taken a huge weight off our shoulders, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t getting full marks a bit excessive? Sakayanagi, who was 2nd in the year, got 91 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of Sakayanagi-san, she got similar scores in all her subjects, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know she was smart, but ever since the introduction of the OAA, her strength has become more apparent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> A perfectionist&#x27;s pride bruised in public; he holds the line of honesty but breaks anyway, because he cannot out-logic his own hurt; his forgiveness is real but partial.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The wound between them; the reconciliation.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She buffers him and Airi from the worst of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She sees Haruka&#x27;s strange stiffness too.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She shields the truth; he audits it.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> The one he trusts will just take Kiyotaka as he is.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Yukimura shakes his leg; the class erupts<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p59-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y2v2-p24-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"mashima-tomonari","q":"mashima tomonari mashima mentioned in passing named in the context of ayanokoji s injured left hand  chabashira asks about it  passing mention  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y2v2-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y2v2-p24-1\">Mashima mentioned in passing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the context of Ayanokōji&#x27;s injured left hand; Chabashira asks about it.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the class confronts him  horikita s cover story about thirty minutes after the summons he is back in class  students without club activities are waiting for him  keisei leads the charge with haruka and airi behind him  miyake is at archery club  horikita has not answered his call but stays   you  what s with the 100 points in math  i checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the oaa  and even ichinose and sakayanagi didn t get   p      erfect score      s  you re the only one in the entire year   well  let me explain this   i m  asking kiyotaka   yes  but  yukimura kun  i am the one who has the answers you are looking for    what do you mean   yukimura kun and i  no  the entire 2nd year couldn t get this perfect score  so how was ayanokouji kun able to achieve that  don t you all think that s inconceivable   that s right     to be honest  my head is a mess  i said this before  right  the questions at the end of the paper were impossible to solve  but kiyotaka did them all like nobody s business  and i just can t understand it   kiyotaka should know very well that nobody in the class could solve those problems  yet we didn t even see him brag about how he solved them  isn t that weird  it even makes it seem like he has something he can t reveal  maybe he did something bad  and knew the answers from the start  or something like that   he cheated  of course  it s not surprising that you want to think that   in this situation  it s hard not to be suspicious  if i were a student who knew nothing  i would definitely feel the same way  and believe that ayanokouji kun had been secretly cheating  however  that isn t the case here   i m planning to explain the same thing for the people who aren t here now  to solve the mystery of ayanokouji kun s perfect score  we ll have to go back to spring of last year   we have since switched seats  but it must still be fresh in your memory that until recently  we were seatmates  right  not long after school started  when i was talking to ayanokouji kun  i happened to find out that he was extremely good at academics  even better than me   better than you in academics  hold on  i remember kiyotaka s scores being about average all around since school started  i m sorry  but i can t see anything about it being worthy of special attention  isn t his grade on the oaa a c  the overall average   of course  that s because my strategy was already in motion before the first exam was completed   from the very    start he had the knowledge to get perfect scores in math  as i knew this before anyone else  i thought up a little strategy   a little strategy   last april  we of class d were overjoyed to have received such a large sum of money  i m ashamed to say that i was also one of them  but i had a feeling something unexpected was going to happen in turn  during that time  i asked ayanokouji kun  who sat next to me  if he could hold back in the exam  you could call this a reserve tactic or a trump card  of course  i told him to keep it at a level which wouldn t hold the class back  and that s how his academic ability got rated c by the school   your words are hardly convincing  if you had doubts surrounding the rules of the school  it would be beneficial for the class as a whole for him to get higher scores from the start  since he got a perfect score on this exam  getting an a or a  in academic ability isn t impossible  you could say it was just one person s grades  but even that could ve slowly increased the number of points of our class   that  huh  if we were only looking at the class points in front of us  that would be fine  but if he had gone all out from the start   what do you think would ve happened to ayanokouji by now  no  to put it more accurately  what do you think his future would have been like   what i think his future would have been like   let us go by what yukimura kun said  and assume that ayanokouji kun had gone all out since april of last year  if that was the case  then by may  sakayanagi san  ichinose san  and ryuuen kun would definitely have learned of his name  if they ignored the person who was the best in math in the entire year  he would become an obstacle to them sooner or later  it wouldn t be surprising if someone moved to try and get him expelled   so you re saying  people might have targeted him   correct  anything can happen in this school  after all  there was even an         exam which forcibly expelled people through an intra class vote  and in fact  at that time  ayanokouji kun was at risk of dropping out due to sakayanagi san s strategy  although that was when he was completely average and was coincidentally chosen as a patsy  it s possible that it really was aimed at him   no  that s wrong  if kiyotaka had been serious from the start  even if we were to put yamauchi and him at different ends of a balance the result would have been clear as day   i wonder  in order to avoid getting expelled  yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves  and sakayanagi san s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through  besides  yamauchi kun had at least had more people close to him than ayanokouji kun  as the things put on both ends of the scales would be different  opinions would follow that change   so why are you revealing this now  if you carelessly reveal his strength  the results will be the same  he s been drawing attention now that you suddenly showed his strength to everyone  and soon he could also become a target   no  there s a huge difference between showing his strength a year ago and revealing his strength now  in the past year  the unity of our class d had         grown by leaps and bounds  and each of us has grown in individual strength  we ve become able to make the right decisions   but now  if someone has their attention on ayanokouji kun  we could now work together to protect him  that is how i have judged it  and that s why i ve made ayanokouji kun s true strength public  and started to raise the overall strength of our class   i understand  if only a little bit  this reserve strategy of yours  horikita  on that basis  i have another question  is ayanokouji outstanding at math alone   i can t comment on that at this stage   the student    known as ayanokouji kiyotaka  has he shown the full extent of his abilities  or is he still holding back  no matter what the real truth is  we can hide it to ensure ayanokouji continues to remain a thorn on their side for the other classes   i see  i clearly understand what horikita san is trying to say   i didn t get it at first  but i ve been listening to the discussion  and now i understand  it s true that an enemy whose abilities are unknown can be dangerous  they will then want to know more and try to gather information  but if even our own classmates don t know the truth  it ll be pointless for them to keep digging   yeah  he s bound to attract attention in the future anyway  so let s just make full use of him  letting our opponents see him as an unknown factor is the better course of action  there might even be students outside listening in on us right now  this is that kind of school   horikita san       really is good  isn t she  i m a little moved   don t you think so as well  shinohara san   that s right  i    feel like i ve been seeing horikita san and ayanokouji kun talking secretly for a long time now  but it turns out that they re really just doing it for the class   a strategy of hiding our strength  that s true  the other classes must also be quite shocked now   although i didn t completely understand the situation of the school  i thought keeping an insurance plan would be good  i don t know if this is fortunate or unfortunate  but ayanokouji kun is bad at communicating  and it seems like he didn t like to stand out  for those reasons as well  i also wanted him to hide it   that s the secret of how ayanokouji kun got a full score in math  sorry for surprising you all   i think it would be better if we left it at that for now  as horikita san said  the walls have ears  horikita s story is built on things he knows to be false  but it lands  most of the class cannot reconstruct last spring  and yousuke s covering fire closes the topic before doubt regrows  he is grateful for the improvisation he never rehearsed with her  she manufactures the reserve strategy cover from the lectern and carries it to the end  confronts him  the doubt stays live but contained  yousuke closes the discussion cleanly  she shifts the room s attention to horikita without a signal from him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\">The class confronts him; Horikita&#x27;s cover story<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.27–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">About thirty minutes after the summons he is back in class; students without club activities are waiting for him; Keisei leads the charge with Haruka and Airi behind him; Miyake is at archery club; Horikita has not answered his call but stays.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You… what’s with the 100 points in math? I checked the scores of all the other 2nd years with the OAA, and even Ichinose and Sakayanagi didn’t get … p …  … erfect score …  … s. You’re the only one in the entire year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Well, let me explain this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I’m… asking Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>43 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. But, Yukimura-kun, I am the one who has the answers you are looking for.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yukimura-kun and I- no, the entire 2nd year couldn’t get this perfect score, so how was Ayanokouji-kun able to achieve that? Don’t you all think that’s inconceivable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right … … To be honest, my head is a mess. I said this before, right? The questions at the end of the paper were impossible to solve. But Kiyotaka did them all like nobody’s business, and I just can’t understand it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka should know very well that nobody in the class could solve those problems. Yet we didn’t even see him brag about how he solved them. Isn’t that weird? It even makes it seem like he has something he can’t reveal… maybe he did something bad, and knew the answers from the start, or something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He cheated… Of course, it’s not surprising that you want to think that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this situation, it’s hard not to be suspicious. If I were a student who knew nothing, I would definitely feel the same way, and believe that Ayanokouji-kun had been secretly cheating. However, that isn’t the case here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m planning to explain the same thing for the people who aren’t here now. To solve the mystery of Ayanokouji-kun’s perfect score, we’ll have to go back to spring of last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have since switched seats, but it must still be fresh in your memory that until recently, we were seatmates, right? Not long after school started, when I was talking to Ayanokouji-kun, I happened to find out that he was extremely good at academics… Even better than me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Better than you in academics? Hold on. I remember Kiyotaka’s scores being about average all around since school started. I’m sorry, but I can’t see anything about it being worthy of special attention. Isn’t his grade on the OAA a C, the overall average?”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. That’s because my strategy was already in motion before the first exam was completed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From the very …  start he had the knowledge to get perfect scores in math. As I knew this before anyone else, I thought up a little strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…A little strategy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Last April, we of Class D were overjoyed to have received such a large sum of money. I’m ashamed to say that I was also one of them. But I had a feeling something unexpected was going to happen in turn. During that time, I asked Ayanokouji-kun, who sat next to me, if he could hold back in the exam. You could call this a reserve tactic or a trump card. Of course, I told him to keep it at a level which wouldn’t hold the class back. And that’s how his academic ability got rated C by the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your words are hardly convincing. If you had doubts surrounding the rules of the school, it would be beneficial for the class as a whole for him to get higher scores from the start. Since he got a perfect score on this exam, getting an A or A+ in academic ability isn’t impossible. You could say it was just one person’s grades, but even that could’ve slowly increased the number of points of our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That, huh. If we were only looking at the class points in front of us, that would be fine. But if he had gone all out from the start – what do you think would’ve happened to Ayanokouji by now? No, to put it more accurately, what do you think his future would have been like?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I think his future would have been like…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let us go by what Yukimura-kun said, and assume that Ayanokouji-kun had gone all out since April of last year. If that was the case, then by May, Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san, and Ryuuen-kun would definitely have learned of his name. If they ignored the person who was the best in math in the entire year, he would become an obstacle to them sooner or later. It wouldn’t be surprising if someone moved to try and get him expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re saying, people might have targeted him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Correct. Anything can happen in this school. After all, there was even an …  …  … exam which forcibly expelled people through an intra-class vote. And in fact, at that time, Ayanokouji-kun was at risk of dropping out due to Sakayanagi-san’s strategy. Although that was when he was completely average and was coincidentally chosen as a patsy, it’s possible that it really was aimed at him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s wrong. If Kiyotaka had been serious from the start, even if we were to put Yamauchi and him at different ends of a balance the result would have been clear as day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder. In order to avoid getting expelled, Yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves, and Sakayanagi-san’s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through. Besides, Yamauchi-kun had at least had more people close to him than Ayanokouji-kun. As the things put on both ends of the scales would be different, opinions would follow that change.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So why are you revealing this now? If you carelessly reveal his strength, the results will be the same. He’s been drawing attention now that you suddenly showed his strength to everyone, and soon he could also become a target.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, there’s a huge difference between showing his strength a year ago and revealing his strength now. In the past year, the unity of our Class D had …  …  … grown by leaps and bounds, and each of us has grown in individual strength. We’ve become able to make the right decisions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33–34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But now, if someone has their attention on Ayanokouji-kun, we could now work together to protect him. That is how I have judged it. And that’s why I’ve made Ayanokouji-kun’s true strength public, and started to raise the overall strength of our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand, if only a little bit, this reserve strategy of yours, Horikita. On that basis, I have another question. Is Ayanokouji outstanding at math alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t comment on that at this stage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student …  known as Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, has he shown the full extent of his abilities, or is he still holding back? No matter what the real truth is, we can hide it to ensure Ayanokouji continues to remain a thorn on their side for the other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. I clearly understand what Horikita-san is trying to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t get it at first, but I’ve been listening to the discussion, and now I understand. It’s true that an enemy whose abilities are unknown can be dangerous. They will then want to know more and try to gather information. But if even our own classmates don’t know the truth, it’ll be pointless for them to keep digging.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. He’s bound to attract attention in the future anyway, so let’s just make full use of him. Letting our opponents see him as an unknown factor is the better course of action. There might even be students outside listening in on us right now. This is that kind of school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san …  …  really is good, isn’t she? I’m a little moved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think so as well, Shinohara-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right! I …  feel like I’ve been seeing Horikita-san and Ayanokouji-kun talking secretly for a long time now, but it turns out that they’re really just doing it for the class!”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A strategy of hiding our strength…. That’s true, the other classes must also be quite shocked now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I didn’t completely understand the situation of the school, I thought keeping an insurance plan would be good. I don’t know if this is fortunate or unfortunate, but Ayanokouji-kun is bad at communicating, and it seems like he didn’t like to stand out. For those reasons as well, I also wanted him to hide it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s the secret of how Ayanokouji-kun got a full score in math. Sorry for surprising you all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it would be better if we left it at that for now. As Horikita-san said, the walls have ears.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s story is built on things he knows to be false, but it lands: most of the class cannot reconstruct last spring, and Yousuke&#x27;s covering fire closes the topic before doubt regrows. He is grateful for the improvisation he never rehearsed with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She manufactures the reserve-strategy cover from the lectern and carries it to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Confronts him; the doubt stays live but contained.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Yousuke closes the discussion cleanly.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She shifts the room&#x27;s attention to Horikita without a signal from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: After Tsukishiro&#x27;s office; Chabashira waits<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p39-1\">→ After: The Ayanokōji group corners him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p27-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the reserve strategy  horikita saves him she stays in the classroom after the others have gone   she had not answered his call but assessed that the remaining students would stay for him  she stands up and walks to his side to collect the dispersed attention   well  let me explain this   yes  but  yukimura kun  i am the one who has the answers you are looking for   yukimura kun and i  no  the entire 2nd year couldn t get this perfect score  so how was ayanokouji kun able to achieve that  don t you all think that s inconceivable   he cheated  of course  it s not surprising that you want to think that   in this situation  it s hard not to be suspicious  if i were a student who knew nothing  i would definitely feel the same way  and believe that ayanokouji kun had been secretly cheating  however  that isn t the case here   i m planning to explain the same thing for the people who aren t here now  to solve the mystery of ayanokouji kun s perfect score  we ll have to go back to spring of last year   we have since switched seats  but it must still be fresh in your memory that until recently  we were seatmates  right  not long after school started  when i was talking to ayanokouji kun  i happened to find out that he was extremely good at academics  even better than me   of course  that s because my strategy was already in motion before the first exam was completed   from the very    start he had the knowledge to get perfect scores in math  as i knew this before anyone else  i thought up a little strategy   last april  we of class d were overjoyed to have received such a large sum of money  i m ashamed to say that i was also one of them  but i had a feeling something unexpected was going to happen in turn  during that time  i asked ayanokouji kun  who sat next to me  if he could hold back in the exam  you could call this a reserve tactic or a trump card  of course  i told him to keep it at a level which wouldn t hold the class back  and that s how his academic ability got rated c by the school   that  huh  if we were only looking at the class points in front of us  that would be fine  but if he had gone all out from the start   what do you think would ve happened to ayanokouji by now  no  to put it more accurately  what do you think his future would have been like   let us go by what yukimura kun said  and assume that ayanokouji kun had gone all out since april of last year  if that was the case  then by may  sakayanagi san  ichinose san  and ryuuen kun would definitely have learned of his name  if they ignored the person who was the best in math in the entire year  he would become an obstacle to them sooner or later  it wouldn t be surprising if someone moved to try and get him expelled   correct  anything can happen in this school  after all  there was even an         exam which forcibly expelled people through an intra class vote  and in fact  at that time  ayanokouji kun was at risk of dropping out due to sakayanagi san s strategy  although that was when he was completely average and was coincidentally chosen as a patsy  it s possible that it really was aimed at him   i wonder  in order to avoid getting expelled  yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves  and sakayanagi san s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through  besides  yamauchi kun had at least had more people close to him than ayanokouji kun  as the things put on both ends of the scales would be different  opinions would follow that change   no  there s a huge difference between showing his strength a year ago and revealing his strength now  in the past year  the unity of our class d had         grown by leaps and bounds  and each of us has grown in individual strength  we ve become able to make the right decisions   it isn t just ayanokouji kun  let s say  yes  he isn t here  but it might be easier to understand with the example of sudo kun  this time last year  he was hard to look at  and undoubtedly the biggest burden to our class  but what about now  although there s still remnants of his wild nature left over  he has improved dramatically  in terms of academic ability  he s shown outstanding growth  and with his already excellent physical abilities combined  his oaa evaluation as of may is even higher than yours  yukimura kun   when we first entered this school  did either of us have the strength or willingness to protect sudo kun   but now  if someone has their attention on ayanokouji kun  we could now work together to protect him  that is how i have judged it  and that s why i ve made ayanokouji kun s true strength public  and started to raise the overall strength of our class   i can t comment on that at this stage   that   yeah  he s bound to attract attention in the future anyway  so let s just make full use of him  letting our opponents see him as an unknown factor is the better course of action  there might even be students outside listening in on us right now  this is that kind of school   although i didn t completely understand the situation of the school  i thought keeping an insurance plan would be good  i don t know if this is fortunate or unfortunate  but ayanokouji kun is bad at communicating  and it seems like he didn t like to stand out  for those reasons as well  i also wanted him to hide it   that s the secret of how ayanokouji kun got a full score in math  sorry for surprising you all  moves to the lectern to shift the room s attention onto herself  the cover story is improvised but airtight in the moment  she does not prepare  rehearse or hesitate   she tells the story with total conviction and lets the half that survives be enough  she single handledly contains the perfect score uproar  he is grateful to her for the improvisation  she faces his sharp questions head on and wins by force of structure  he backs her logic and closes the topic  she covers for her without being asked","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p27-1\">The reserve strategy: Horikita saves him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.27–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She stays in the classroom after the others have gone — she had not answered his call but assessed that the remaining students would stay for him; she stands up and walks to his side to collect the dispersed attention.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Well, let me explain this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yes. But, Yukimura-kun, I am the one who has the answers you are looking for.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yukimura-kun and I- no, the entire 2nd year couldn’t get this perfect score, so how was Ayanokouji-kun able to achieve that? Don’t you all think that’s inconceivable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He cheated… Of course, it’s not surprising that you want to think that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this situation, it’s hard not to be suspicious. If I were a student who knew nothing, I would definitely feel the same way, and believe that Ayanokouji-kun had been secretly cheating. However, that isn’t the case here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m planning to explain the same thing for the people who aren’t here now. To solve the mystery of Ayanokouji-kun’s perfect score, we’ll have to go back to spring of last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have since switched seats, but it must still be fresh in your memory that until recently, we were seatmates, right? Not long after school started, when I was talking to Ayanokouji-kun, I happened to find out that he was extremely good at academics… Even better than me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. That’s because my strategy was already in motion before the first exam was completed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From the very …  start he had the knowledge to get perfect scores in math. As I knew this before anyone else, I thought up a little strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Last April, we of Class D were overjoyed to have received such a large sum of money. I’m ashamed to say that I was also one of them. But I had a feeling something unexpected was going to happen in turn. During that time, I asked Ayanokouji-kun, who sat next to me, if he could hold back in the exam. You could call this a reserve tactic or a trump card. Of course, I told him to keep it at a level which wouldn’t hold the class back. And that’s how his academic ability got rated C by the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That, huh. If we were only looking at the class points in front of us, that would be fine. But if he had gone all out from the start – what do you think would’ve happened to Ayanokouji by now? No, to put it more accurately, what do you think his future would have been like?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let us go by what Yukimura-kun said, and assume that Ayanokouji-kun had gone all out since April of last year. If that was the case, then by May, Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san, and Ryuuen-kun would definitely have learned of his name. If they ignored the person who was the best in math in the entire year, he would become an obstacle to them sooner or later. It wouldn’t be surprising if someone moved to try and get him expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Correct. Anything can happen in this school. After all, there was even an …  …  … exam which forcibly expelled people through an intra-class vote. And in fact, at that time, Ayanokouji-kun was at risk of dropping out due to Sakayanagi-san’s strategy. Although that was when he was completely average and was coincidentally chosen as a patsy, it’s possible that it really was aimed at him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder. In order to avoid getting expelled, Yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves, and Sakayanagi-san’s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through. Besides, Yamauchi-kun had at least had more people close to him than Ayanokouji-kun. As the things put on both ends of the scales would be different, opinions would follow that change.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, there’s a huge difference between showing his strength a year ago and revealing his strength now. In the past year, the unity of our Class D had …  …  … grown by leaps and bounds, and each of us has grown in individual strength. We’ve become able to make the right decisions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33–34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It isn’t just Ayanokouji-kun. Let’s say, yes… He isn’t here, but it might be easier to understand with the example of Sudo-kun. This time last year, he was hard to look at, and undoubtedly the biggest burden to our class. But what about now? Although there’s still remnants of his wild nature left over, he has improved dramatically. In terms of academic ability, he’s shown outstanding growth. And with his already excellent physical abilities combined, his OAA evaluation as of May is even higher than yours, Yukimura-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we first entered this school, did either of us have the strength or willingness to protect Sudo-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But now, if someone has their attention on Ayanokouji-kun, we could now work together to protect him. That is how I have judged it. And that’s why I’ve made Ayanokouji-kun’s true strength public, and started to raise the overall strength of our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t comment on that at this stage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thatー”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. He’s bound to attract attention in the future anyway, so let’s just make full use of him. Letting our opponents see him as an unknown factor is the better course of action. There might even be students outside listening in on us right now. This is that kind of school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I didn’t completely understand the situation of the school, I thought keeping an insurance plan would be good. I don’t know if this is fortunate or unfortunate, but Ayanokouji-kun is bad at communicating, and it seems like he didn’t like to stand out. For those reasons as well, I also wanted him to hide it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s the secret of how Ayanokouji-kun got a full score in math. Sorry for surprising you all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Moves to the lectern to shift the room&#x27;s attention onto herself; the cover story is improvised but airtight in the moment; she does not prepare, rehearse or hesitate — she tells the story with total conviction and lets the half that survives be enough.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She single-handledly contains the perfect-score uproar; he is grateful to her for the improvisation.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> She faces his sharp questions head-on and wins by force of structure.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He backs her logic and closes the topic.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She covers for her without being asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p22-1\">← Before: She sits through the uproar without a word<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p65-1\">→ After: Walking to school; the council decision<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p27-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi coverage note  passing mentions  haruka and airi  who were also from the ayanokouji group  gathered around him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p27-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Haruka and Airi, who were also from the Ayanokouji group, gathered around him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Sakura&#x27;s soft landing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p39-1\">→ After: The reconciliation handshake; Keyaki mall<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p29-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke coverage note  passing mentions  starting with keisei and yosuke  the students who had the best grades were discussing the extremely difficult questions   i ll thank horikita and yosuke another day   i heard about it from yousuke afterwards  you put in a good word for me  didn t you   if he could improve his academics and social contribution in the future  he might even be able to stand shoulder to shoulder with yosuke and kushida  chabashira s example member    the trio of hirata  sudo  and hondou    used to illustrate the single survivor rule   in order to decide on the groupings  horikita used yosuke s words as a basis to speak to everyone   yousuke had seen the whole scene  and after ike left he approached me   after leaving yosuke  i gave ishizaki  from komiya s class  a call  and asked him out    ayanokoji s narration on the page  he is present through the ishizaki briefing   let s discuss this with yosuke as well  he s thinking about the best group for ike right now   headed by hirata kun and kushida san  who have strong communication skills  and have well balanced grades   even though his grandfather mentioned something about being bad at studying  he got an a in the oaa evaluation for academic ability  he was an honor student who wasn t obnoxious  and he gave me the same sort of feeling as yosuke did","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p29-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.29–252<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Starting with Keisei and Yosuke, the students who had the best grades were discussing the extremely difficult questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’ll thank Horikita and Yosuke another day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I heard about it from Yousuke afterwards. You put in a good word for me, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If he could improve his academics and social contribution in the future, he might even be able to stand shoulder to shoulder with Yosuke and Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Chabashira’s example member — “the trio of Hirata, Sudo, and Hondou” — used to illustrate the single-survivor rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In order to decide on the groupings, Horikita used Yosuke’s words as a basis to speak to everyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Yousuke had seen the whole scene, and after Ike left he approached me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After leaving Yosuke, I gave Ishizaki, from Komiya’s class, a call, and asked him out.” — Ayanokōji’s narration on the page; he is present through the Ishizaki briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Let’s discuss this with Yosuke as well. He’s thinking about the best group for Ike right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Headed by Hirata-kun and Kushida-san, who have strong communication skills, and have well-balanced grades…”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Even though his grandfather mentioned something about being bad at studying, he got an A in the OAA evaluation for Academic Ability. He was an honor student who wasn’t obnoxious, and he gave me the same sort of feeling as Yosuke did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p21-1\">← Before: Hirata presses pause<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p35-1\">→ After: Hirata&#x27;s covering fire<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p32-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru coverage note  passing mentions  by may  sakayanagi san  ichinose san  and ryuuen kun would definitely have learned of his name   he didn t use dirty tricks as ryuuen did as well   ryuuen had the experience of being beaten down by me  so he would naturally know that i wasn t only good at math   sakayanagi  ichinose  ryuuen  those people would probably cry from the joy   how will sakayanagi  ryuuen  and ichinose act   ichinose aside  it s hard to imagine ryuuen would readily agree to it   i thought ryuuen would be here too  but that didn t seem to be the case   well   course it s just you  i reckon you re just as powerful as ryuuen  nah  if i had to say  it s cuz i now think that you re even better than him   was it ryuuen who decided to invite me  or is this ishizaki s arbitrary decision   it s my own decision  ryuuen knows nothing about it   have you thought about what would happen if ryuuen found out about this   if it was up to me to choose the small group hmm  ryuuen kun  kaneda kun  and ayanokouji kun  those three  it s fine if kaneda kun is replaced by yamada kun  but ryuuen kun is indispensable   if it was up to me to choose the small group hmm  ryuuen kun  kaneda kun  and ayanokouji kun  those three  it s fine if kaneda kun is replaced by yamada kun  but ryuuen kun is indispensable   don t be ridiculous  do you think ryuuen kun will ever approve of our plan   kaneda kun is the same  he won t ignore ryuuen kun s orders and participate in a strategy he s unsure of   b led by ryuuen  whom she was chasing after  was only 26 points  when ryuuen s class rose to class b  there were no holes found in his class from such everyday actions that would have decreased their class points  when ryuuen s class rose to class b  there were no holes found in his class from such everyday actions that would have decreased their class points   however  both ryuuen kun and i are able to bare our fangs even if we re in a disadvantageous situation  you know   although the gap with our class wouldn t be narrowed  you can catch up with ryuuen kun s class  and widen the gap with class d   but if you and i group up  horikita san and ryuuen kun might also group up   however  both ryuuen kun and horikita san are formidable opponents   ryuuen and horikita s classes along with the 1st and 3rd years   whether it be ayanokouji  ryuuen  or the others  whoever comes at me with their fangs  i ll crush them all   expressed his doubts on ryuuen s strategy   ryuuen said that with nary a consideration for my preferences about that matter   he turned to ryuuen and i to confirm if it was the truth   if i were sakayanagi  i would have agreed to ryuuen s proposal as well   that s why ryuuen was willing to pay as much as it takes   ryuuen brilliantly exploited this  and successfully brought him into his ranks   ryuuen asked me with a baffled expression  as i poured water into the remaining one fifth of the coffee   ryuuen mentioned the card that had been given to me   even on the rooftop  after i beat both ryuuen and ibuki  she still challenged me again later on   sakayanagi  ichinose  and ryuuen  were also aiming for that very same goal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p32-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.32–335<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>34 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “by May, Sakayanagi-san, Ichinose-san, and Ryuuen-kun would definitely have learned of his name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “He didn’t use dirty tricks as Ryuuen did as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ryuuen had the experience of being beaten down by me, so he would naturally know that I wasn’t only good at math.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi, Ichinose, Ryuuen. Those people would probably cry from the joy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “How will Sakayanagi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose act?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ichinose aside, it’s hard to imagine Ryuuen would readily agree to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I thought Ryuuen would be here too, but that didn’t seem to be the case.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Well, ‘course it’s just you. I reckon you’re just as powerful as Ryuuen… Nah, if I had to say, it’s cuz I now think that you’re even better than him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Was it Ryuuen who decided to invite me? Or is this Ishizaki’s arbitrary decision?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It’s my own decision. Ryuuen knows nothing about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Have you thought about what would happen if Ryuuen found out about this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If it was up to me to choose the small group Hmm. Ryuuen-kun, Kaneda-kun, and Ayanokouji-kun, those three. It’s fine if Kaneda-kun is replaced by Yamada-kun, but Ryuuen-kun is indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If it was up to me to choose the small group Hmm. Ryuuen-kun, Kaneda-kun, and Ayanokouji-kun, those three. It’s fine if Kaneda-kun is replaced by Yamada-kun, but Ryuuen-kun is indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Don’t be ridiculous! Do you think Ryuuen-kun will ever approve of our plan!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Kaneda-kun is the same, he won’t ignore Ryuuen-kun’s orders and participate in a strategy he’s unsure of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “B led by Ryuuen, whom she was chasing after, was only 26 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> when Ryuuen’s class rose to Class B, there were no holes found in his class from such everyday actions that would have decreased their class points.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> when Ryuuen’s class rose to Class B, there were no holes found in his class from such everyday actions that would have decreased their class points.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “However, both Ryuuen-kun and I are able to bare our fangs even if we’re in a disadvantageous situation, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Although the gap with our class wouldn’t be narrowed, you can catch up with Ryuuen-kun’s class, and widen the gap with Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But if you and I group up, Horikita-san and Ryuuen-kun might also group up…”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “However, both Ryuuen-kun and Horikita-san are formidable opponents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ryuuen and Horikita’s classes along with the 1st and 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Whether it be Ayanokouji, Ryuuen, or the others, whoever comes at me with their fangs, I’ll crush them all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “expressed his doubts on Ryuuen’s strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ryuuen said that with nary a consideration for my preferences about that matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “He turned to Ryuuen and I to confirm if it was the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If I were Sakayanagi, I would have agreed to Ryuuen’s proposal as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That’s why Ryuuen was willing to pay as much as it takes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ryuuen brilliantly exploited this, and successfully brought him into his ranks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ryuuen asked me with a baffled expression, as I poured water into the remaining one-fifth of the coffee.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ryuuen mentioned the card that had been given to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Even on the rooftop, after I beat both Ryuuen and Ibuki, she still challenged me again later on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sakayanagi, Ichinose, and Ryuuen, were also aiming for that very same goal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p294-1\">→ After: The café gambit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki yamauchi mentioned in passing his name comes up in horikita s retelling of last spring  she says he would have been more careful with his moves had ayanokoji been serious from the start  and that sakayanagi s strategy would have been more complex   a passing mention  not a scene presence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-1\">Yamauchi mentioned in passing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.33<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> His name comes up in Horikita&#x27;s retelling of last spring: she says he would have been more careful with his moves had Ayanokōji been serious from the start, and that Sakayanagi&#x27;s strategy would have been more complex – a passing mention, not a scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-2\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-2","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki coverage note  passing mentions  in order to avoid getting expelled  yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves  and sakayanagi san s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through   it might be cold coming from a friend of haruki  but i m glad you didn t get expelled during the class vote    the page does not disambiguate whether  haruki  here is yamauchi haruki  unresolved  kept as printed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-2\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.33, 62<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In order to avoid getting expelled, Yamauchi would have been more careful when making his moves, and Sakayanagi-san’s strategy would have been more complex and harder to see through.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It might be cold coming from a friend of Haruki, but I’m glad you didn’t get expelled during the class vote.” — the page does not disambiguate whether “Haruki” here is Yamauchi Haruki; unresolved, kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y2v2-p33-1\">← Before: Yamauchi mentioned in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p35-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke hirata s covering fire while horikita holds the floor  he observes from the front  ayanokoji catches his eye   i understand  if only a little bit  this reserve strategy of yours  horikita  on that basis  i have another question  is ayanokouji outstanding at math alone   i see  i clearly understand what horikita san is trying to say   i didn t get it at first  but i ve been listening to the discussion  and now i understand  it s true that an enemy whose abilities are unknown can be dangerous  they will then want to know more and try to gather information  but if even our own classmates don t know the truth  it ll be pointless for them to keep digging   i think it would be better if we left it at that for now  as horikita san said  the walls have ears  the class s social load bearing wall  he fills the gaps in horikita s argument in plain words and closes the topic on cue  he is her ally on the floor  he understands the situation and silently takes the cue","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p35-1\">Hirata&#x27;s covering fire<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.35–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">While Horikita holds the floor, he observes from the front; Ayanokōji catches his eye.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I understand, if only a little bit, this reserve strategy of yours, Horikita. On that basis, I have another question. Is Ayanokouji outstanding at math alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I see. I clearly understand what Horikita-san is trying to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I didn’t get it at first, but I’ve been listening to the discussion, and now I understand. It’s true that an enemy whose abilities are unknown can be dangerous. They will then want to know more and try to gather information. But…”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t get it at first, but I’ve been listening to the discussion, and now I understand. It’s true that an enemy whose abilities are unknown can be dangerous. They will then want to know more and try to gather information. But if even our own classmates don’t know the truth, it’ll be pointless for them to keep digging.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it would be better if we left it at that for now. As Horikita-san said, the walls have ears.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The class&#x27;s social load-bearing wall; he fills the gaps in Horikita&#x27;s argument in plain words and closes the topic on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He is her ally on the floor.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He understands the situation and silently takes the cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p29-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p123-1\">→ After: Hirata challenges the exam&#x27;s premise<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p36-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko shinohara-satsuki sudou-ken karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei karuizawa protects horikita she strikes with a casual statement that pulls the room off ayanokoji and onto horikita   horikita san       really is good  isn t she  i m a little moved   don t you think so as well  shinohara san  laughs with the girls at the center as the class empties after the meeting  fast  insincere on the surface  shrewd in the play  she senses the temperature of the room and shifts the spotlight when it matters  her dramas orbit his anomaly  she snipes at him and wins the exchange  she recruits her to the cover  she cites his oaa jump to corner miyamoto","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p36-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p36-1\">Karuizawa protects Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.36–39<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She strikes with a casual statement that pulls the room off Ayanokōji and onto Horikita. Laughs with the girls at the center as the class empties after the meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Horikita-san …  …  really is good, isn’t she? I’m a little moved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Don’t you think so as well, Shinohara-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fast, insincere on the surface, shrewd in the play: she senses the temperature of the room and shifts the spotlight when it matters.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her dramas orbit his anomaly.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> She snipes at him and wins the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She recruits her to the cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> She cites his OAA jump to corner Miyamoto.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p15-1\">← Before: Karuizawa&#x27;s math-genius theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p83-1\">→ After: Kei&#x27;s visit; the near-kiss<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p39-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko hasebe-haruka sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the ayanokoji group corners him dismissed  the ayanokoji group catches him in the hallway  keisei at the front  haruka and airi behind him   kiyotaka   going back without even saying hello  isn t that a bit cruel   why didn t you tell us before  if it s to hide information as horikita said  does that mean that you don t trust us at all   i ve always trusted you guys  but i judged that not revealing it to anyone         was better for the plan in the future  it s because i ve been so close to you guys that i ve had to stifle my desire to tell you and keep quiet   i completely understand your anger over this incident  after all  this is related to the group you re closest with  and you even tutored me  i m truly sorry   to be honest  i m still angry  you could have told me from the start that you didn t need to be taught  that you could have passed the exam without any problems  and that you could have handled it on your own   you re right   and based on what horikita said  you ll continue to hold back after this  right  if you don t tell me which subject you will and will not hold back in  i can t completely trust you   i want out of this group  well  i d be lying if i said i didn t have that thought   yukimuu  are you serious   yeah  i m serious  until i heard horikita s explanation  i was determined to leave because i didn t think kiyotaka could be trusted at all  but even so  after being in the same group for so long  i can still understand some things  i know that kiyotaka isn t a bad person  since he was hiding something for the sake of the entire class  it s understandable that he didn t want to tell anyone  kiyotaka could have told me that he didn t need tutoring  that is true  but he s bad with words  so he couldn t say it  i can understand that too   it s just yeah  it s just  i need some time to sort my thoughts out   there s no advantage in taking this further  in the end  what i wanted to say  what i wanted to express is  it doesn t matter even if you hide your strength in other areas  it s not like you re holding the class back like koenji  so no one has the right to complain  if i continue to criticize you forcefully  the atmosphere will become even worse   even though my rational side is clear with that  i can t suppress it emotionally  so i ll need to reflect on that  next  i ll recognize the part of your strength that you revealed as a real thing  as for the other subjects  i ll         continue to       use my previous assumption that you re passable  and i ll continue to tutor you  is that fine   thank you  keisei   h how about you two do a reconciliation handshake   a reconciliation handshake  that s nice   don t  it s embarrassing   alright  make up   if you don t shake hands  i won t let go  alright   i know  i know   i m fine with it  but akito still doesn t know anything   miyacchi probably won t be a problem  i think he ll just accept kiyopon like normal right   well  everything s back to normal  it feels we ve taken a huge weight off our shoulders  right   what s wrong  haruka chan   oh  ahh  well  it s nothing  anyway  it s going to be hard for you since you re a celebrity now   isn t getting full marks a bit excessive  sakayanagi  who was 2nd in the year  got 91 points   speaking of sakayanagi san  she got similar scores in all her subjects  right   i know she was smart  but ever since the introduction of the oaa  her strength has become more apparent   as a commemoration of our conciliation  why don t we meet at keyaki mall once miyacchi s club activities end  he apologizes without blaming horikita  chooses honesty with his friends over the easy excuse  and accepts keisei s renewed tutoring proposal  the group holds together  hurt and mistrust  then grudging acceptance  forces the handshake  proposes the handshake  worries about haruka","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p39-1\">The Ayanokōji group corners him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.39–45<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dismissed, the Ayanokōji group catches him in the hallway; Keisei at the front, Haruka and Airi behind him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “Going back without even saying hello, isn’t that a bit cruel?”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Why didn’t you tell us before?… If it’s to hide information as Horikita said, does that mean that you don’t trust us at all?”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>31 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve always trusted you guys. But I judged that not revealing it to anyone …  …  … was better for the plan in the future. It’s because I’ve been so close to you guys that I’ve had to stifle my desire to tell you and keep quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I completely understand your anger over this incident. After all, this is related to the group you’re closest with, and you even tutored me. I’m truly sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I’m still angry. You could have told me from the start that you didn’t need to be taught, that you could have passed the exam without any problems, and that you could have handled it on your own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And based on what Horikita said, you’ll continue to hold back after this, right? If you don’t tell me which subject you will and will not hold back in, I can’t completely trust you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want out of this group- Well, I’d be lying if I said I didn’t have that thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yukimuu, are you serious?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, I’m serious. Until I heard Horikita’s explanation, I was determined to leave because I didn’t think Kiyotaka could be trusted at all. But…even so, after being in the same group for so long, I can still understand some things. I know that Kiyotaka isn’t a bad person. Since he was hiding something for the sake of the entire class, it’s understandable that he didn’t want to tell anyone. Kiyotaka could have told me that he didn’t need tutoring, that is true, but he’s bad with words, so he couldn’t say it. I can understand that too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s just…yeah, it’s just… I need some time to sort my thoughts out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no advantage in taking this further… In the end, what I wanted to say, what I wanted to express is… it doesn’t matter even if you hide your strength in other areas. It’s not like you’re holding the class back like Koenji, so no one has the right to complain. If I continue to criticize you forcefully, the atmosphere will become even worse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though my rational side is clear with that, I can’t suppress it emotionally, so I’ll need to reflect on that. Next, I’ll recognize the part of your strength that you revealed as a real thing. As for the other subjects, I’ll …  …  … continue to …  …  use my previous assumption that you’re passable, and I’ll continue to tutor you. Is that fine?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you, Keisei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-how about you two do a…reconciliation handshake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A reconciliation handshake? That’s nice!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t, it’s embarrassing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alright, make up!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t shake hands, I won’t let go, alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know, I know…!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m fine with it, but Akito still doesn’t know anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Miyacchi probably won’t be a problem. I think he’ll just accept Kiyopon like normal right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, everything’s back to normal. It feels we’ve taken a huge weight off our shoulders, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s wrong, Haruka-chan?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, ahh. Well, it’s nothing. Anyway, it’s going to be hard for you since you’re a celebrity now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t getting full marks a bit excessive? Sakayanagi, who was 2nd in the year, got 91 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of Sakayanagi-san, she got similar scores in all her subjects, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know she was smart, but ever since the introduction of the OAA, her strength has become more apparent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a commemoration of our conciliation, why don’t we meet at Keyaki mall once Miyacchi’s club activities end?”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He apologizes without blaming Horikita, chooses honesty with his friends over the easy excuse, and accepts Keisei&#x27;s renewed tutoring proposal; the group holds together.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Hurt and mistrust, then grudging acceptance.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Forces the handshake.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Proposes the handshake; worries about Haruka.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\">← Before: The class confronts him; Horikita&#x27;s cover story<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\">→ After: Keyaki Mall: Ichinose and Kanzaki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p39-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko sakura-airi hasebe-haruka","q":"hasebe haruka haruka mediates and manages catches up with ayanokoji in the hallway with keisei and airi  she voices what the group cannot   going back without even saying hello  isn t that a bit cruel   yukimuu  are you serious   a reconciliation handshake  that s nice   alright  make up   if you don t shake hands  i won t let go  alright  she glances at ayanokoji as if she remembered something and stiffens  airi notices  she covers it with a new subject   oh  ahh  well  it s nothing  anyway  it s going to be hard for you since you re a celebrity now   as a commemoration of our conciliation  why don t we meet at keyaki mall once miyacchi s club activities end  at keyaki mall with miyake  keisei and airi  the group uniform stare at ayanokoji talking with ichinose  she doesn t push   what were you talking about with ichinose san just now  she keeps the peace and notices what escapes the others  her p 44 stiffness is unexplained on page and is not resolved here  she manages his classmates  she clocks what he will not say  she buffers him from his own anger  they exchange a glance  airi worries about her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html#sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p39-1\">Haruka mediates and manages<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Catches up with Ayanokōji in the hallway with Keisei and Airi; she voices what the group cannot. She glances at Ayanokōji as if she remembered something and stiffens; Airi notices; she covers it with a new subject. At Keyaki mall with Miyake, Keisei and Airi; the group uniform stare at Ayanokōji talking with Ichinose; she doesn’t push.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “Going back without even saying hello, isn’t that a bit cruel?”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “Yukimuu, are you serious?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “A reconciliation handshake? That’s nice!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alright, make up!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t shake hands, I won’t let go, alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, ahh. Well, it’s nothing. Anyway, it’s going to be hard for you since you’re a celebrity now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a commemoration of our conciliation, why don’t we meet at Keyaki mall once Miyacchi’s club activities end?”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What were you talking about with Ichinose-san just now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She keeps the peace and notices what escapes the others; her p.44 stiffness is unexplained on page and is not resolved here.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She manages his classmates; she clocks what he will not say.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> She buffers him from his own anger.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> They exchange a glance; Airi worries about her.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Haruka watches the uproar<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p179-1\">→ After: Haruka&#x27;s group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p39-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko hasebe-haruka sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi the reconciliation handshake  keyaki mall with haruka and keisei in the hallway  she waits behind them and finds the courage to speak   h how about you two do a reconciliation handshake   what s wrong  haruka chan  touched that the reconciliation happened  exchanges a glance with haruka  right  arrives with the group at keyaki mall  does not question the ichinose conversation directly  the empath of the group  she names the reconciliation before the boys can  and she sees haruka s strange moment on p 44  she watches him become a celebrity  she propels the peace process  she notices haruka freeze","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p39-1\">The reconciliation handshake; Keyaki mall<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With Haruka and Keisei in the hallway; she waits behind them and finds the courage to speak. Touched that the reconciliation happened; exchanges a glance with Haruka (“Right~?”). Arrives with the group at Keyaki mall; does not question the Ichinose conversation directly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “H-how about you two do a…reconciliation handshake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “What’s wrong, Haruka-chan?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The empath of the group; she names the reconciliation before the boys can, and she sees Haruka&#x27;s strange moment on p.44.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She watches him become a celebrity.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> She propels the peace process.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She notices Haruka freeze.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p27-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p179-1\">→ After: Sakura groups up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka keyaki mall  ichinose and kanzaki he arrives from 6 30 at keyaki mall  agreed time is 7 00  to wait alone   his  special skill  of emptying his mind  airi posts in the group chat that she is leaving the dorm  the others have read it   say  i ve seen your exam results  you actually got a perfect score in math  that s amazing   judging from last year s oaa  you shouldn t have the strength to get a full score   ayanokouji kun  are you waiting for someone   i m waiting for my friends to go eat  how about you guys   there s a lot of reasons for this  it was only after discussing with my comrades that i decided to hide the fact that i m good at math   so you re saying that    you ve been hiding it all this time  it looks like you re even more of an issue than i thought   ayanokouji kun is not our enemy   our alliance has been dissolved  there s no doubt that class 2 d is our enemy   that s but there s no point for us to engage in a pointless dispute   this isn t a dispute  it s just necessary for us to know the true strength of our opponent   ayanokouji kun did indeed hide the fact that he was good at math  this was a fact that had been hidden   then  what else  is it just math  no  it can t be just math  what other abilities are you hiding  did you hide those legs you re so proud of during last year s sports festival because of orders from your comrades  to class b  no  class c  the worst thing is that you still have other strengths hidden away   however  there s a limit to test scores  no matter how good you are at studying  the max you can get on a subject is 100 points  and the highest grade is an a  even if he gets full marks in all of them  there s not much of a gap between him and sakayanagi san  the second in the year   our overall scores in class c are much higher than that  the point difference from ayanokouji kun after showing his true strength  we just have to make up for that with our whole class   that might be true if it s just a written test  but   we should stop here  kanzaki kun  you also know that this isn t a thing we should be arguing about heatedly here  right   it seems like    i ve indeed lost my cool   i ll go first   i m sorry  but given the current situation  kanzaki kun definitely doesn t have much legroom   do you remember what i told you before   yes  you told me to stick with my classmates and go forward  right  didn t you   there may be s      tudents who want to change their own class appearing from         now on  just like kanzaki  or there may be some that are dissatisfied with you and want to stop you  maybe even some that will betray the class too  it won t be surprising to think some will do whatever just to make a change  class 1 b  the class that only you protected  that class doesn t exist anymore   no matter what    happens from here  i want for you to trust your classmates  put their safety first and continue the fight   it s okay  i m definitely going to protect them  if there comes a time someone from my class has to leave  i think i will be the first one   i won t ever let you get expelled   dissatisfied   t that  y yeah  i ll  definitely stay   y you  are really amazing  ayanokouji kun   it may be my only redeeming feature at school  though   even so that s still amazing  it just means you have a weapon that won t lose to anyone else   you are the same too  you certainly have such a weapon yourself   that would be    nice  but   i need to leave soon  we re standing too much out here  and i feel bad letting kanzaki wait for me  ichinose will certainly sacrifice herself for the class if it comes to it  her way of including people kills her classmates  individuality   a weapon she wields without noticing  with too few people around who can use it well  between trust and duty  he vows never to let her be expelled  hostile and suspicious  correctly guarded  wrong conclusion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\">Keyaki Mall: Ichinose and Kanzaki<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.46–52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He arrives from 6:30 at Keyaki mall (agreed time is 7:00) to wait alone — his “special skill” of emptying his mind; Airi posts in the group chat that she is leaving the dorm; the others have read it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Say, I’ve seen your exam results. You actually got a perfect score in math, that’s amazing!”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Judging from last year’s OAA, you shouldn’t have the strength to get a full score.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun, are you waiting for someone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m waiting for my friends to go eat. How about you guys?”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a lot of reasons for this. It was only after discussing with my comrades that I decided to hide the fact that I’m good at math.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re saying that …  you’ve been hiding it all this time. It looks like you’re even more of an issue than I thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun is not our enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our alliance has been dissolved. There’s no doubt that Class 2-D is our enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s…but there’s no point for us to engage in a pointless dispute!”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t a dispute. It’s just necessary for us to know the true strength of our opponent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun did indeed hide the fact that he was good at math; this was a fact that had been hidden.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, what else? Is it just math? No, it can’t be just math. What other abilities are you hiding? Did you hide those legs you’re so proud of during last year’s sports festival because of orders from your comrades? To Class B… No, Class C, the worst thing is that you still have other strengths hidden away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, there’s a limit to test scores. No matter how good you are at studying, the max you can get on a subject is 100 points, and the highest grade is an A+. Even if he gets full marks in all of them, there’s not much of a gap between him and Sakayanagi-san, the second in the year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our overall scores in Class C are much higher than that. The point difference from Ayanokouji-kun after showing his true strength, we just have to make up for that with our whole class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That might be true if it’s just a written test… but-”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We should stop here, Kanzaki-kun. You also know that this isn’t a thing we should be arguing about heatedly here, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like …  I’ve indeed lost my cool.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll go first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but given the current situation, Kanzaki-kun definitely doesn’t have much legroom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you remember what I told you before?”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, you told me to stick with my classmates and go forward, right, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There may be s …  … tudents who want to change their own class appearing from …  …  … now on, just like Kanzaki. Or there may be some that are dissatisfied with you and want to stop you. Maybe even some that will betray the class too. It won’t be surprising to think some will do whatever just to make a change. Class 1-B, the class that only you protected, that class doesn’t exist anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter what …  happens from here, I want for you to trust your classmates, put their safety first and continue the fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s okay. I’m definitely going to protect them. If there comes a time someone from my class has to leave, I think I will be the first one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t ever let you get expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dissatisfied…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “T-that… y-yeah… I’ll …definitely…stay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-you…. Are really amazing, Ayanokouji-kun…”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It may be my only redeeming feature at school, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so that’s still amazing. It just means you have a weapon that won’t lose to anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You are the same too. You certainly have such a weapon yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That would be …  nice, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…I need to leave soon. We’re standing too much out here, and I feel bad letting Kanzaki wait for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose will certainly sacrifice herself for the class if it comes to it; her way of including people kills her classmates&#x27; individuality — a weapon she wields without noticing, with too few people around who can use it well.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Between trust and duty; he vows never to let her be expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Hostile and suspicious; correctly guarded, wrong conclusion.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p39-1\">← Before: The Ayanokōji group corners him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\">→ After: Sudō at the lockers; the real question of strength<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p46-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ichinose at keyaki mall  the pact at the mall entrance at 6 30 with kanzaki  she greets ayanokoji warmly   say  i ve seen your exam results  you actually got a perfect score in math  that s amazing  she holds off kanzaki  then privately tells ayanoji to trust his classmates  she will leave first if anyone must   ayanokouji kun is not our enemy   i m sorry  but given the current situation  kanzaki kun definitely doesn t have much legroom   there may be s      tudents who want to change their own class appearing from         now on  just like kanzaki  or there may be some that are dissatisfied with you and want to stop you  maybe even some that will betray the class too  it won t be surprising to think some will do whatever just to make a change  class 1 b  the class that only you protected  that class doesn t exist anymore   no matter what    happens from here  i want for you to trust your classmates  put their safety first and continue the fight   dissatisfied   t that  y yeah  i ll  definitely stay   i need to leave soon  we re standing too much out here  and i feel bad letting kanzaki wait for me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p46-1\">Ichinose at Keyaki mall; the pact<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.46–53, 203–218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the mall entrance at 6:30 with Kanzaki; she greets Ayanokōji warmly. She holds off Kanzaki; then privately tells Ayanōji to trust his classmates; she will leave first if anyone must.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Say, I’ve seen your exam results. You actually got a perfect score in math, that’s amazing!”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun is not our enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I’m sorry, but given the current situation, Kanzaki-kun definitely doesn’t have much legroom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There may be s …  … tudents who want to change their own class appearing from …  …  … now on, just like Kanzaki. Or there may be some that are dissatisfied with you and want to stop you. Maybe even some that will betray the class too. It won’t be surprising to think some will do whatever just to make a change. Class 1-B, the class that only you protected, that class doesn’t exist anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter what …  happens from here, I want for you to trust your classmates, put their safety first and continue the fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dissatisfied…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “T-that… y-yeah… I’ll …definitely…stay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…I need to leave soon. We’re standing too much out here, and I feel bad letting Kanzaki wait for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p15-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p203-1\">→ After: The Sakayanagi pact<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p46-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji kanzaki s interrogation sees ayanokouji alone at keyaki mall at 6 30  opens with the oaa discrepancy   judging from last year s oaa  you shouldn t have the strength to get a full score  he presses  ichinose holds him back twice  he loses his cool for a moment   so you re saying that    you ve been hiding it all this time  it looks like you re even more of an issue than i thought   our alliance has been dissolved  there s no doubt that class 2 d is our enemy   this isn t a dispute  it s just necessary for us to know the true strength of our opponent   that s true  he didn t use dirty tricks as ryuuen did as well  still  there s a few things i don t like about him  ichinose  you should be very aware of the fact that it s not at all easy to be able to solve that extremely difficult question to get full marks  he says he s following his comrade s instructions but   ayanokouji kun did indeed hide the fact that he was good at math  this was a fact that had been hidden   then  what else  is it just math  no  it can t be just math  what other abilities are you hiding  did you hide those legs you re so proud of during last year s sports festival because of orders from your comrades  to class b  no  class c  the worst thing is that you still have other strengths hidden away   that might be true if it s just a written test  but   it seems like    i ve indeed lost my cool  he leaves first into the mall  the talk is unfinished on purpose   i ll go first  the alliance is dead to him  guarding class c is a duty he will see through to the end  he asks the questions nobody wants to hear  his friend  his opposite  his shield  an enemy whose file he refuses to close","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p46-1\">Kanzaki&#x27;s interrogation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.46–52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sees Ayanokouji alone at Keyaki mall at 6:30; opens with the OAA discrepancy. He presses; Ichinose holds him back twice; he loses his cool for a moment. He leaves first into the mall; the talk is unfinished on purpose.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Judging from last year’s OAA, you shouldn’t have the strength to get a full score.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “So you’re saying that …  you’ve been hiding it all this time. It looks like you’re even more of an issue than I thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Our alliance has been dissolved. There’s no doubt that Class 2-D is our enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t a dispute. It’s just necessary for us to know the true strength of our opponent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. He didn’t use dirty tricks as Ryuuen did as well. Still, there’s a few things I don’t like about him. Ichinose, you should be very aware of the fact that it’s not at all easy to be able to solve that extremely difficult question to get full marks. He says he’s following his comrade’s instructions but-”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun did indeed hide the fact that he was good at math; this was a fact that had been hidden.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, what else? Is it just math? No, it can’t be just math. What other abilities are you hiding? Did you hide those legs you’re so proud of during last year’s sports festival because of orders from your comrades? To Class B… No, Class C, the worst thing is that you still have other strengths hidden away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That might be true if it’s just a written test… but-”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like …  I’ve indeed lost my cool.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll go first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The alliance is dead to him; guarding Class C is a duty he will see through to the end; he asks the questions nobody wants to hear.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> His friend, his opposite, his shield.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> An enemy whose file he refuses to close.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p204-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"inner spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudo at the lockers  the real question of strength after golden week s end  at the shoe lockers  sudo matches his walking pace to his  the talk turns to the perfect score and the housen fight   so you were hiding the fact you re good at studying because of suzune s strategy  right   well  you two have been close ever since school started  a bit late now  but i understand that   we didn t get along  if anything  at first it was more like we wanted to keep our distance from each other   it was like that  sorry  didn t look like that to me   i heard about it from yousuke afterwards  you put in a good word for me  didn t you   i can t say i was covering for you  i was only stating the facts   you call them facts  but you didn t know the truth at that time either   course i know that   it was a secret that you re a genius at math  but is the fact that you re good at fighting also a secret   i don t know what you    mean   don t play dumb with me  i fought with housen  so i m clear on it  his         superhuman strength is the real deal  and he s faster than anyone i ve fought so far  honestly  he s a monster   that was the first time i ve ever felt scared in a fight  even now his smiling face is burnt into my brain   you were scared  huh  even so  it looked like you fought bravely for horikita   well  there was no other choice  that guy has more than a few screws loose   but you had a chance to win  too  didn t you   who knows  in a real  serious fight  i don t think i can win against him   hey  that s not what i wanted to talk about  my affairs don t matter   you  you surpassed that monster housen s strength and stopped him  i m not wrong  am i   and you re sure it wasn t just a misunderstanding  sudou   yeah  that s right   i ve had this feeling since last year  when i saw you at the pool  you weren t even participating in any club activities  but you had a super muscular body  it s hard to tell with clothes on  but those firm muscles  you wouldn t get those without considerable training   speaking of that  your grip strength when we measured it before the sports festival was around 60kg  right   that time  i already thought that was amazing  but you were holding back  how much can you grip exactly   who knows  i honestly don t know   you don t know   i don t remember ever measuring my grip strength properly   how is that even possible  we have physical evaluations so many times in primary and middle school   you really don t know   back then  i heard that a grip strength of 60kg was the average for a 1st year at high school  so i adjusted my strength to around that  i was trying not         to stand out   i m talking about you  how strong is the real you   forget it  you don t have to answer   powerful or not  there s no point if i don t see it with my own eyes   but i understand now that you re a pretty unbelievable guy  you re seriously powerful  ayanokouji   doesn t it upset you that i ve always been hiding my strength   well  in the beginning i thought  what s with that  and i get how yukimura feels  if i feel like i m already super powerful  it sure wouldn t feel         good to know that someone by my side was hiding his powers and is actually more powerful than me  but it s not like i can t understand what you re thinking  you don t like to stand out  right  somehow  i ve come to understand your approach  i guess   it would definitely be a lie if i said i didn t care  but i m doing my best in my own way to grow  that s got nothing to do with how other guys are  that s what i think   besides  no matter how amazing you are  at basketball  i m definitely better   if it s basketball  we can have a match any time   spare me  i don t want to become your punching bag   hahahahah  i see you understand that   so i won t talk about the situation with housen to anyone  i feel like this         was very roundabout  but that was what i wanted to say today   alright   ah yes  let s not talk about housen again  but can i ask one last thing   if it s something that i can answer   did you not think i would tell anybody else about the fight with housen   if it were the old sudou  i probably would ve arranged for it  i d even go so far as to request horikita to tell you to keep quiet   if it were the old me   from the oaa evaluation  the one with the highest growth in class d is you  unlike the time when you were hotheaded  you re now able to calmly assess the situation  that s why i didn t take any measures   i feel like  i m being talked up to   i m totally convinced  doesn t feel bad to know that you have a high opinion of me   there s one more question i d like to ask  you and suzune   we re not dating   oh   for that  well  it s not like i m telling you not to date her  suzune is free to go out with me  or you  or anyone else if she wants  but  well  if you re deliberately hiding it  then i won t have any mercy on you   okay  okay  if  by any chance  that happens  i ll tell you right away  alright   good  wait  no  that s not o   k  but  no  that s fine   it might be cold coming from a friend of haruki  but i m glad you didn t get expelled during the class vote  there s no doubt that you re someone we need to rise up to class a  see you later  ayanokouji   someone we need to rise to class a huh  sudo s second year oaa  academics c  54  physical a   96  adaptability c   42  social contribution c   60  overall b   63    first place in the year for growth  first year overall was 47  he holds the wild nature but has out grown being a burden  and ak decides no counter measures are needed on him  trusts him  he stays silent on the housen fight","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\">Sudō at the lockers; the real question of strength<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.53–63<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After Golden Week&#x27;s end, at the shoe lockers; Sudō matches his walking pace to his; the talk turns to the perfect score and the Housen fight.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “So you were hiding the fact you’re good at studying because of Suzune’s strategy, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Well, you two have been close ever since school started. A bit late now, but I understand that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “We didn’t get along. If anything, at first it was more like we wanted to keep our distance from each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>57 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was like that? Sorry, didn’t look like that to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard about it from Yousuke afterwards. You put in a good word for me, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say I was covering for you; I was only stating the facts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You call them facts, but you didn’t know the truth at that time either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “’Course I know that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was a secret that you’re a genius at math, but is the fact that you’re good at fighting also a secret?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you …  mean.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t play dumb with me. I fought with Housen, so I’m clear on it. His …  …  … superhuman strength is the real deal. And he’s faster than anyone I’ve fought so far. Honestly, he’s a monster.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was the first time I’ve ever felt scared in a fight. Even now his smiling face is burnt into my brain.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were scared, huh. Even so, it looked like you fought bravely for Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there was no other choice. That guy has more than a few screws loose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But you had a chance to win, too, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows… In a real, serious fight, I don’t think I can win against him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey- that’s not what I wanted to talk about! My affairs don’t matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You… you surpassed that monster Housen’s strength and stopped him. I’m not wrong, am I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And you’re sure it wasn’t just a misunderstanding, Sudou?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve had this feeling since last year, when I saw you at the pool. You weren’t even participating in any club activities, but you had a super muscular body. It’s hard to tell with clothes on, but those firm muscles… you wouldn’t get those without considerable training.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of that, your grip strength when we measured it before the sports festival was around 60kg, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That time, I already thought that was amazing… but you were holding back. How much can you grip exactly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows. I honestly don’t know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember ever measuring my grip strength properly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How is that even possible? We have physical evaluations so many times in primary and middle school!”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really don’t know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Back then, I heard that a grip strength of 60kg was the average for a 1st year at high school, so I adjusted my strength to around that. I was trying not …  …  … to stand out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m talking about you, how strong is the real you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Forget it. You don’t have to answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Powerful or not, there’s no point if I don’t see it with my own eyes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I understand now that you’re a pretty unbelievable guy. You’re seriously powerful, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Doesn’t it upset you that I’ve always been hiding my strength?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, in the beginning I thought, what’s with that?, and I get how Yukimura feels. If I feel like I’m already super powerful, it sure wouldn’t feel …  …  … good to know that someone by my side was hiding his powers and is actually more powerful than me. But it’s not like I can’t understand what you’re thinking, you don’t like to stand out, right? Somehow, I’ve come to understand your approach, I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would definitely be a lie if I said I didn’t care, but I’m doing my best in my own way to grow. That’s got nothing to do with how other guys are, that’s what I think.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, no matter how amazing you are, at basketball, I’m definitely better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s basketball, we can have a match any time!”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Spare me. I don’t want to become your punching bag.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hahahahah! I see you understand that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So I won’t talk about the situation with Housen to anyone. I feel like this …  …  … was very roundabout, but that was what I wanted to say today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alright.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah yes, let’s not talk about Housen again, but can I ask one last thing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s something that I can answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you not think I would tell anybody else about the fight with Housen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it were the old Sudou, I probably would’ve arranged for it. I’d even go so far as to request Horikita to tell you to keep quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it were the old me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From the OAA evaluation, the one with the highest growth in Class D is you. Unlike the time when you were hotheaded, You’re now able to calmly assess the situation. That’s why I didn’t take any measures.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel like… I’m being talked up to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m totally convinced. Doesn’t feel bad to know that you have a high opinion of me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s one more question I’d like to ask. You and Suzune…”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re not dating.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh…”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For that, well, it’s not like I’m telling you not to date her. Suzune is free to go out with me, or you, or anyone else if she wants. But, well, if you’re deliberately hiding it, then I won’t have any mercy on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, okay… If, by any chance, that happens, I’ll tell you right away, alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good. Wait, no, that’s not oー! …k, but, no, that’s fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It might be cold coming from a friend of Haruki, but I’m glad you didn’t get expelled during the class vote. There’s no doubt that you’re someone we need to rise up to Class A. See you later, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Someone we need to rise to Class A…huh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudō&#x27;s second-year OAA: Academics C (54), Physical A+ (96), Adaptability C- (42), Social Contribution C+ (60), Overall B- (63) — first place in the year for growth (first-year overall was 47); he holds the wild nature but has out-grown being a burden, and AK decides no counter-measures are needed on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Trusts him; he stays silent on the Housen fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\">← Before: Keyaki Mall: Ichinose and Kanzaki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\">→ After: The OAA update and the 20-million bounty<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p54-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hondou-ryoutaro","q":"hondo ryotaro coverage note  passing mentions  sudou  must have heard the details from ike or hondou afterwards   but if it were another student such as ike or hondou in that situation  there could have been different developments  chabashira s example member    the trio of hirata  sudo  and hondou","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html#sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p54-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.54–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sudou… must have heard the details from Ike or Hondou afterwards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But if it were another student such as Ike or Hondou in that situation, there could have been different developments.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Chabashira’s example member — “the trio of Hirata, Sudo, and Hondou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p168-1\">→ After: Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p54-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji coverage note  passing mentions  sudou must have heard the details from ike or hondou afterwards   but if it were another student such as ike or hondou in that situation  there could have been different developments   it s ike  ike from my class likes shinohara   after all  even though ike and shinohara liked each other  neither was willing to take a step forward   i expressed my concerns to horikita about the current situation between ike  shinohara  and komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam   why don t we just make ike kun confess  if shinohara san accepts  ike kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he s in  right   since we ve already reached this point  we must take measures to prevent ike kun s loss of motivation   today s conversation focused on the groupings for the exam  starting with the fight between ike and shinohara","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p54-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.54–198<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sudou must have heard the details from Ike or Hondou afterwards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But if it were another student such as Ike or Hondou in that situation, there could have been different developments.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It’s Ike. Ike from my class likes Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After all, even though Ike and Shinohara liked each other, neither was willing to take a step forward.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I expressed my concerns to Horikita about the current situation between Ike, Shinohara, and Komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Why don’t we just make Ike-kun confess? If Shinohara-san accepts, Ike-kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he’s in, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Since we’ve already reached this point, we must take measures to prevent Ike-kun’s loss of motivation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Today’s conversation focused on the groupings for the exam, starting with the fight between Ike and Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p18-1\">← Before: Ike&#x27;s cheating theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p169-1\">→ After: The boy-scout confession attempt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p54-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken sudo s big question run in at the shoe lockers after golden week  he falls into step without saying hello first    yo   so you were hiding the fact you re good at studying because of suzune s strategy  right   well  you two have been close ever since school started  a bit late now  but i understand that   it was like that  sorry  didn t look like that to me   i heard about it from yousuke afterwards  you put in a good word for me  didn t you   you call them facts  but you didn t know the truth at that time either   it was a secret that you re a genius at math  but is the fact that you re good at fighting also a secret  he relives the housen fight out loud   the first time he felt scared   don t play dumb with me  i fought with housen  so i m clear on it  his         superhuman strength is the real deal  and he s faster than anyone i ve fought so far  honestly  he s a monster   that was the first time i ve ever felt scared in a fight  even now his smiling face is burnt into my brain   well  there was no other choice  that guy has more than a few screws loose   who knows  in a real  serious fight  i don t think i can win against him  he grips ak s bicep  measures grips and recalculates  then releases the question unanswered   hey  that s not what i wanted to talk about  my affairs don t matter   you  you surpassed that monster housen s strength and stopped him  i m not wrong  am i   yeah  that s right   i ve had this feeling since last year  when i saw you at the pool  you weren t even participating in any club activities  but you had a super muscular body  it s hard to tell with clothes on  but those firm muscles  you wouldn t get those without considerable training   speaking of that  your grip strength when we measured it before the sports festival was around 60kg  right   that time  i already thought that was amazing  but you were holding back  how much can you grip exactly   you don t know   how is that even possible  we have physical evaluations so many times in primary and middle school   you really don t know   i m talking about you  how strong is the real you   forget it  you don t have to answer   powerful or not  there s no point if i don t see it with my own eyes   but i understand now that you re a pretty unbelievable guy  you re seriously powerful  ayanokouji  he lands his own position  admiration without envy  the suzune question  the relief   well  in the beginning i thought  what s with that  and i get how yukimura feels  if i feel like i m already super powerful  it sure wouldn t feel         good to know that someone by my side was hiding his powers and is actually more powerful than me  but it s not like i can t understand what you re thinking  you don t like to stand out  right  somehow  i ve come to understand your approach  i guess   it would definitely be a lie if i said i didn t care  but i m doing my best in my own way to grow  that s got nothing to do with how other guys are  that s what i think   besides  no matter how amazing you are  at basketball  i m definitely better   spare me  i don t want to become your punching bag   hahahahah  i see you understand that   so i won t talk about the situation with housen to anyone  i feel like this         was very roundabout  but that was what i wanted to say today   ah yes  let s not talk about housen again  but can i ask one last thing   did you not think i would tell anybody else about the fight with housen   if it were the old me   i feel like  i m being talked up to   i m totally convinced  doesn t feel bad to know that you have a high opinion of me   there s one more question i d like to ask  you and suzune   oh   for that  well  it s not like i m telling you not to date her  suzune is free to go out with me  or you  or anyone else if she wants  but  well  if you re deliberately hiding it  then i won t have any mercy on you   good  wait  no  that s not o   k  but  no  that s fine   it might be cold coming from a friend of haruki  but i m glad you didn t get expelled during the class vote  there s no doubt that you re someone we need to rise up to class a  see you later  ayanokouji  competitive  warm  loud  and precise about his lane   basketball stays his  the fight with housen haunts him but does not own him  he is the one who calls ak seriously powerful to his face  hirata keeps him moving  old friends on the same fight","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p54-1\">Sudō&#x27;s big question<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.54–63<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Run-in at the shoe lockers after Golden Week; he falls into step without saying hello first. He relives the Housen fight out loud — the first time he felt scared. He grips AK&#x27;s bicep, measures grips and recalculates; then releases the question unanswered. He lands his own position: admiration without envy; the Suzune question; the relief.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “… Yo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “So you were hiding the fact you’re good at studying because of Suzune’s strategy, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Well, you two have been close ever since school started. A bit late now, but I understand that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was like that? Sorry, didn’t look like that to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard about it from Yousuke afterwards. You put in a good word for me, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You call them facts, but you didn’t know the truth at that time either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was a secret that you’re a genius at math, but is the fact that you’re good at fighting also a secret?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t play dumb with me. I fought with Housen, so I’m clear on it. His …  …  … superhuman strength is the real deal. And he’s faster than anyone I’ve fought so far. Honestly, he’s a monster.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was the first time I’ve ever felt scared in a fight. Even now his smiling face is burnt into my brain.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there was no other choice. That guy has more than a few screws loose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows… In a real, serious fight, I don’t think I can win against him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey- that’s not what I wanted to talk about! My affairs don’t matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You… you surpassed that monster Housen’s strength and stopped him. I’m not wrong, am I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve had this feeling since last year, when I saw you at the pool. You weren’t even participating in any club activities, but you had a super muscular body. It’s hard to tell with clothes on, but those firm muscles… you wouldn’t get those without considerable training.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of that, your grip strength when we measured it before the sports festival was around 60kg, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That time, I already thought that was amazing… but you were holding back. How much can you grip exactly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How is that even possible? We have physical evaluations so many times in primary and middle school!”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really don’t know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m talking about you, how strong is the real you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Forget it. You don’t have to answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Powerful or not, there’s no point if I don’t see it with my own eyes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I understand now that you’re a pretty unbelievable guy. You’re seriously powerful, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, in the beginning I thought, what’s with that?, and I get how Yukimura feels. If I feel like I’m already super powerful, it sure wouldn’t feel …  …  … good to know that someone by my side was hiding his powers and is actually more powerful than me. But it’s not like I can’t understand what you’re thinking, you don’t like to stand out, right? Somehow, I’ve come to understand your approach, I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would definitely be a lie if I said I didn’t care, but I’m doing my best in my own way to grow. That’s got nothing to do with how other guys are, that’s what I think.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, no matter how amazing you are, at basketball, I’m definitely better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Spare me. I don’t want to become your punching bag.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hahahahah! I see you understand that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So I won’t talk about the situation with Housen to anyone. I feel like this …  …  … was very roundabout, but that was what I wanted to say today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah yes, let’s not talk about Housen again, but can I ask one last thing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you not think I would tell anybody else about the fight with Housen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it were the old me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel like… I’m being talked up to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m totally convinced. Doesn’t feel bad to know that you have a high opinion of me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s one more question I’d like to ask. You and Suzune…”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh…”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For that, well, it’s not like I’m telling you not to date her. Suzune is free to go out with me, or you, or anyone else if she wants. But, well, if you’re deliberately hiding it, then I won’t have any mercy on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good. Wait, no, that’s not oー! …k, but, no, that’s fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It might be cold coming from a friend of Haruki, but I’m glad you didn’t get expelled during the class vote. There’s no doubt that you’re someone we need to rise up to Class A. See you later, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Competitive, warm, loud, and precise about his lane — basketball stays his; the fight with Housen haunts him but does not own him.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He is the one who calls AK seriously powerful to his face.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata keeps him moving.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Old friends on the same fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p19-1\">← Before: Sudō shuts down the cheating talk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p66-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p56-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu coverage note  passing mentions  manabu  sudo names him as one who studied martial arts and still could not beat hosen   as i told you before  the president won t reject anyone who comes to him    nagumo at manabu s graduation  the sister who followed him wherever he went  horikita manabu s sister  horikita suzune  is the one to stop nagumo if nagumo is going in the wrong direction  unlike manabu  opening the door to anyone is how nagumo operates  nagumo asks why manabu s sister wants to join the student council   awareness to pursue manabu    the narration over horikita s stated purpose for joining the council as a path toward manabu   this system had completely deviated from what manabu once defended   and  i guess that the area where i could interrupt them had already passed  kiriyama supported manabu and schemed  he discovers manabu s sister horikita was going to join the student council  so he might have wanted to act   the student council president who graduated last year    kiriyama on manabu  nagumo s rival tradition   i sent horikita suzune to the student council on the wish of her brother  the former student council president    kiriyama on horikita s mandate   it was the policy of the former student council president horikita manabu to continue on with the school s premise of winning by class   if manabu senpai had heard those words  he would be disappointed  she is  someone nagumo or manabu senpai would pay attention to   there was a time when i was interested in you and horikita manabu   i don t have the leadership skills that you or horikita manabu possessed  nagumo   you seem to be bored ever since horikita manabu left   if i had to say  it s his aura  i feel that he has a different aura from you and horikita manabu   as horikita manabu s sister  it seems it was necessary for me to complete some kind of task","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p56-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions (Manabu)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.56–348<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Sudō names him as one who studied martial arts and still could not beat Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “As I told you before, the president won’t reject anyone who comes to him.” — Nagumo at Manabu’s graduation; the sister who followed him wherever he went.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Horikita Manabu’s sister, Horikita Suzune, is the one to stop Nagumo if Nagumo is going in the wrong direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Unlike Manabu, opening the door to anyone is how Nagumo operates.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Nagumo asks why Manabu’s sister wants to join the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “awareness to pursue Manabu.” — the narration over Horikita’s stated purpose for joining the council as a path toward Manabu.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “This system had completely deviated from what Manabu once defended” (and “I guess that the area where I could interrupt them had already passed”).<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Kiriyama supported Manabu and schemed; he discovers Manabu’s sister Horikita was going to join the student council, so he might have wanted to act.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “the student council president who graduated last year” — Kiriyama on Manabu; Nagumo’s rival tradition.<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I sent Horikita Suzune to the student council on the wish of her brother, the former student council president.” — Kiriyama on Horikita’s mandate.<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It was the policy of the former student council president Horikita Manabu to continue on with the school’s premise of winning by class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If Manabu-senpai had heard those words, he would be disappointed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> She is “someone Nagumo or Manabu-senpai would pay attention to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “There was a time when I was interested in you and Horikita Manabu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I don’t have the leadership skills that you or Horikita Manabu possessed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Nagumo: “You seem to be bored ever since Horikita Manabu left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If I had to say, it’s his aura. I feel that he has a different aura from you and Horikita Manabu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “As Horikita Manabu’s sister, it seems it was necessary for me to complete some kind of task.”<span class=\"pg\">p.348<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions (shared token)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p59-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko coverage note  passing mentions  yukimura feels  if i feel like i m already super powerful  it sure wouldn t feel    fragment torn at the page turn  the sentence continues on the next page   good to know that someone by my side was hiding his powers and is actually more powerful than me    continuation of the same utterance  printed on the next page   sudou  just like keisei  had started to digest things by himself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p59-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.59<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Yukimura feels. If I feel like I’m already super powerful, it sure wouldn’t feel” — fragment torn at the page turn; the sentence continues on the next page.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “good to know that someone by my side was hiding his powers and is actually more powerful than me.” — continuation of the same utterance, printed on the next page.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Sudou, just like Keisei, had started to digest things by himself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: The fight for his trust<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p120-1\">→ After: Keisei&#x27;s group situation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi chabashira-sae nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the oaa update and the 20 million bounty may 2nd  he waits at the lobby for horikita  two weeks have passed since the summons  he re opens the just updated oaa app  2nd year values  his second year evaluation printed  academics a   81  physical ability b   61  adaptability d   40  social contribution b  68  overall b   62  total 386  the class s biggest climber is sudo  academics c 54  physical a  96  adaptability c  42  social contribution c  60  overall b  63  up from a 1st year 47  sudo now outscores keisei and akito in the aggregate  horikita arrives a little early  they walk to school  the attention has mostly died down  the talk turns to the 20 million point bounty   thanks again  because of your quick witted speech  i didn t need to be baptized under the attentive eyes of my classmates for this to end  it left a similar impression in the other classes as well   it s nothing  i just thought that it would be good for the class in the future  if i said that you were the one who took the liberty of holding back  you d be disliked  wouldn t you  by the way  what would you have done if i hadn t been there at the time   who knows what i would have done   it s slowly recovering  it s going to take a while  but it s not that big of a deal since it s not my dominant hand   is your left hand alright now   not at all  i passed by housen and nanase once  but i didn t say anything   they hadn t come to offer an apology  but at least they re aware that they ve done something bad   who knows  it doesn t feel like they did   both of them   yeah   that  if someone gets you expelled  they get 20 million points  is that true   i don t have any proof at the moment  but  if there wasn t a reward for it  nobody would do something like that   it ll be clear soon enough if it s true or not   but that s  that s not a good development  although the exam was unreasonable  if it s a special exam  all four classes should know about it  right   nanase said so too  in order to make us alert of all the other classes   class a s amasawa san  although we re indebted to her since she teamed up with sudo  she definitely joined housen kun  right   that s as far as i ve noticed   that s a bit weird  even if i m trying to be polite here  housen kun shouldn t be that popular in the first year  could they really ignore him while he confidently snatches those points away   what do you think is the reason why the first years don t share information between them   yes  if the entire grade was told about the special exam of getting you expelled  there is a high probability that the 2nd and 3rd years will hear about it in a matter of time  not only just the 1st years  hearing about this unreasonable special exam  our class would surely do everything we could do to fight back  so they did it in a way to prevent us from knowing about it  right   did the school really approve of such an unreasonable special exam   yes  although i tried to confirm it with chabashira sensei tactfully  she didn t show signs she knew about it   the other possibility is that it wasn t really a special exam  in other words  someone offered to pay 20 million private points in order to get me expelled  and thus inciting the first years to go and do it   i see  it would make sense if an individual set the bounty on you   in other words  there s someone in the same or a higher grade that had prepared that many points   although we can t rule out the chance that this was a game set up by a first year  i don t think they have the trust or the capital to make a deal under those conditions because they ve just entered school  so the probability for that is low   someone who can pay 20 million points  and is also trusted by the first years    his inner line  printed in quotes  speaker is himself   the student    council president   could it be that president nagumo might have something to do with this   how would that work  it s true that he doesn t like me  but using such a large amount of points as 20 million all to get me expelled  i have many doubts about that  and using 1st year students of unknown ability in itself is extremely strange   but  there might be a chance that it has nothing to do with him   without realizing it  maybe you aroused nagumo s jealousy  president nagumo had always been interested in brother s affairs  because he had always been only interested in your affairs  even if he has complicated feelings like me  it s not strange    the translation leaves the speaker and the referent of  brother your affairs  untagged and unresolvable on page  recorded as printed  speaker unassigned   although it s a bit late  this is the topic of today s conversation with you  i m preparing after school to go to the student council  and ask president nagumo about joining it   i see   but if i can t get nagumo s approval  it s not my responsibility   as i told you before  the president won t reject anyone who comes to him   you did say that   the reason why you wanted me to join the student council  it was so i         could spy on president nagumo  but actually  that s not the only reason  right   i think you already slightly noticed  what your brother thinks is completely different from what nagumo thinks  it s because he values tradition that he thinks nagumo s reforms are wrong  he said it to me right before he left  the class is a community that should share the same fate  he didn t want the framework to be changed   but i m not going to judge who s right and who s wrong  now  i just want to see nagumo s reforms   so that s why you won t give me specific instructions   mhm   then why do you need me to join  if the only thing you want is to see nagumo s reforms  there s no need for me to monitor the student council at all  then   if nagumo is going in the wrong direction  there s a need to stop him   there s still some things i m not satisfied with  but i ll put it as convenient   i don t think    it s good for me to ask anything of you since i lost the match  but will you come with me   come with you   well  i d like to show you using the meeting with nagumo as evidence   if president nagumo has something to do with that bounty  we might also see some kind of reaction   i see  after school  then  reads the oaa like an account book  weighs the bounty s possibilities   special exam vs private contract vs scam   in sequence  never landing on one until horikita lands on nagumo  they walk and reason together  she commits to the council  he gets her in the room for him  suspected of the bounty by elimination  the cold open of the duel  she shows no sign of knowing about the bounty  she is the source of the second special exam intelligence  her silence reads as complicity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\">The OAA update and the 20-million bounty<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.65–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">May 2nd: he waits at the lobby for Horikita; two weeks have passed since the summons; he re-opens the just-updated OAA app (2nd-year values). Horikita arrives a little early; they walk to school; the attention has mostly died down; the talk turns to the 20-million-point bounty.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Thanks again. Because of your quick-witted speech, I didn’t need to be baptized under the attentive eyes of my classmates for this to end. It left a similar impression in the other classes as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s nothing; I just thought that it would be good for the class in the future. If I said that you were the one who took the liberty of holding back, you’d be disliked, wouldn’t you? By the way, what would you have done if I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Who knows what I would have done.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>54 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His second-year evaluation printed: Academics A- (81), Physical Ability B- (61), Adaptability D+ (40), Social Contribution B (68), Overall B- (62); total 386; the class&#x27;s biggest climber is Sudō (Academics C 54, Physical A+ 96, Adaptability C- 42, Social Contribution C+ 60, Overall B- 63, up from a 1st-year 47); Sudō now outscores Keisei and Akito in the aggregate.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing; I just thought that it would be good for the class in the future. If I said that you were the one who took the liberty of holding back, you’d be disliked, wouldn’t you? By the way, what would you have done if I hadn’t been there at the time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s slowly recovering. It’s going to take a while, but it’s not that big of a deal since it’s not my dominant hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is your left hand alright now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not at all. I passed by Housen and Nanase once, but I didn’t say anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They hadn’t come to offer an apology, but at least they’re aware that they’ve done something bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows, it doesn’t feel like they did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both of them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That, if someone gets you expelled, they get 20 million points, is that true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t have any proof at the moment. But, if there wasn’t a reward for it, nobody would do something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’ll be clear soon enough if it’s true or not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s- that’s not a good development. Although the exam was unreasonable, if it’s a special exam, all four classes should know about it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nanase said so too. In order to make us alert of all the other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A’s Amasawa-san… Although we’re indebted to her since she teamed up with Sudo, she definitely joined Housen-kun, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s as far as I’ve noticed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a bit weird… Even if I’m trying to be polite here, Housen-kun shouldn’t be that popular in the first year. Could they really ignore him while he confidently snatches those points away?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you think is the reason why the first years don’t share information between them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes… If the entire grade was told about the special exam of getting you expelled, there is a high probability that the 2nd and 3rd years will hear about it in a matter of time, not only just the 1st years. Hearing about this unreasonable special exam, our class would surely do everything we could do to fight back. So they did it in a way to prevent us from knowing about it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did the school really approve of such an unreasonable special exam…”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Although I tried to confirm it with Chabashira-sensei tactfully, she didn’t show signs she knew about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The other possibility is that it wasn’t really a special exam. In other words, someone offered to pay 20 million private points in order to get me expelled, and thus inciting the first years to go and do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. It would make sense if an individual set the bounty on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, there’s someone in the same or a higher grade that had prepared that many points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although we can’t rule out the chance that this was a game set up by a first year, I don’t think they have the trust or the capital to make a deal under those conditions because they’ve just entered school, so the probability for that is low.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Someone who can pay 20 million points, and is also trusted by the first years.” — his inner line; printed in quotes, speaker is himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “–The student …  council president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could it be that President Nagumo might have something to do with this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How would that work? It’s true that he doesn’t like me, but using such a large amount of points as 20 million all to get me expelled? I have many doubts about that. And using 1st-year students of unknown ability in itself is extremely strange.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, there might be a chance that it has nothing to do with him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Without realizing it, maybe you aroused Nagumo’s jealousy. President Nagumo had always been interested in brother’s affairs, because he had always been only interested in your affairs. Even if he has complicated feelings like me, it’s not strange.” — the translation leaves the speaker and the referent of “brother”/“your affairs” untagged and unresolvable on page; recorded as printed, speaker unassigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although it’s a bit late, this is the topic of today’s conversation with you. I’m preparing after school to go to the student council, and ask President Nagumo about joining it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if I can’t get Nagumo’s approval, it’s not my responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As I told you before, the president won’t reject anyone who comes to him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…You did say that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The reason why you wanted me to join the student council… It was so I …  …  … could spy on President Nagumo, but actually, that’s not the only reason, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think you already slightly noticed. What your brother thinks is completely different from what Nagumo thinks. It’s because he values tradition that he thinks Nagumo’s reforms are wrong. He said it to me right before he left. The class is a community that should share the same fate. He didn’t want the framework to be changed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I’m not going to judge who’s right and who’s wrong. Now, I just want to see Nagumo’s reforms.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So that’s why you won’t give me specific instructions?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mhm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then why do you need me to join, if the only thing you want is to see Nagumo’s reforms? There’s no need for me to monitor the student council at all, then!”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Nagumo is going in the wrong direction, there’s a need to stop him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s still some things I’m not satisfied with, but I’ll put it as convenient.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’s good for me to ask anything of you since I lost the match, but will you come with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’d like to show you using the meeting with Nagumo as evidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If President Nagumo has something to do with that bounty, we might also see some kind of reaction.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. After school, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the OAA like an account book; weighs the bounty&#x27;s possibilities — special exam vs private contract vs scam — in sequence, never landing on one until Horikita lands on Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> They walk and reason together; she commits to the council; he gets her in the room for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Suspected of the bounty by elimination; the cold open of the duel.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She shows no sign of knowing about the bounty.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She is the source of the second-special-exam intelligence; her silence reads as complicity.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\">← Before: Sudō at the lockers; the real question of strength<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\">→ After: The student council meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p65-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi chabashira-sae nanase-tsubasa horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune walking to school  the council decision he waits at the lobby as arranged  she arrives a little early  they walk to school and pick apart the second year oaa  they compare notes on who could know about the bounty  she suspects the 1st years she does know  she gives him the credit for being the bait   thanks again  because of your quick witted speech  i didn t need to be baptized under the attentive eyes of my classmates for this to end  it left a similar impression in the other classes as well   it s nothing  i just thought that it would be good for the class in the future  if i said that you were the one who took the liberty of holding back  you d be disliked  wouldn t you  by the way  what would you have done if i hadn t been there at the time   is your left hand alright now   they hadn t come to offer an apology  but at least they re aware that they ve done something bad   both of them   that  if someone gets you expelled  they get 20 million points  is that true   but that s  that s not a good development  although the exam was unreasonable  if it s a special exam  all four classes should know about it  right   class a s amasawa san  although we re indebted to her since she teamed up with sudo  she definitely joined housen kun  right   that s as far as i ve noticed   that s a bit weird  even if i m trying to be polite here  housen kun shouldn t be that popular in the first year  could they really ignore him while he confidently snatches those points away   yes  if the entire grade was told about the special exam of getting you expelled  there is a high probability that the 2nd and 3rd years will hear about it in a matter of time  not only just the 1st years  hearing about this unreasonable special exam  our class would surely do everything we could do to fight back  so they did it in a way to prevent us from knowing about it  right   yes  although i tried to confirm it with chabashira sensei tactfully  she didn t show signs she knew about it   i see  it would make sense if an individual set the bounty on you   in other words  there s someone in the same or a higher grade that had prepared that many points   the student    council president   could it be that president nagumo might have something to do with this   without realizing it  maybe you aroused nagumo s jealousy  president nagumo had always been interested in brother s affairs  because he had always been only interested in your affairs  even if he has complicated feelings like me  it s not strange    speaker untagged by the translation  nagumo s name precedes it  horikita s rapport with ayanokoji says this is hers  unassigned as printed   although it s a bit late  this is the topic of today s conversation with you  i m preparing after school to go to the student council  and ask president nagumo about joining it   but if i can t get nagumo s approval  it s not my responsibility   you did say that   the reason why you wanted me to join the student council  it was so i         could spy on president nagumo  but actually  that s not the only reason  right   what the student council    is doing now  that s certainly the complete opposite   so that s why you won t give me specific instructions   then why do you need me to join  if the only thing you want is to see nagumo s reforms  there s no need for me to monitor the student council at all  then   there s still some things i m not satisfied with  but i ll put it as convenient   i don t think    it s good for me to ask anything of you since i lost the match  but will you come with me   well  i d like to show you using the meeting with nagumo as evidence   if president nagumo has something to do with that bounty  we might also see some kind of reaction  the 20 million bounty reasoning lands on nagumo by elimination  she s the one who says it aloud  they walk together  the plan is hers to execute  she suspects him and intends to watch him  she tactfully checked with her  nothing  she treats the 1st year silence as strategic  not accidental","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p65-1\">Walking to school; the council decision<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.65–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He waits at the lobby as arranged; she arrives a little early; they walk to school and pick apart the second-year OAA. They compare notes on who could know about the bounty; she suspects the 1st years she does know; she gives him the credit for being the bait.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Thanks again. Because of your quick-witted speech, I didn’t need to be baptized under the attentive eyes of my classmates for this to end. It left a similar impression in the other classes as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s nothing; I just thought that it would be good for the class in the future. If I said that you were the one who took the liberty of holding back, you’d be disliked, wouldn’t you? By the way, what would you have done if I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Is your left hand alright now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>31 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing; I just thought that it would be good for the class in the future. If I said that you were the one who took the liberty of holding back, you’d be disliked, wouldn’t you? By the way, what would you have done if I hadn’t been there at the time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They hadn’t come to offer an apology, but at least they’re aware that they’ve done something bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both of them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That, if someone gets you expelled, they get 20 million points, is that true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s- that’s not a good development. Although the exam was unreasonable, if it’s a special exam, all four classes should know about it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A’s Amasawa-san… Although we’re indebted to her since she teamed up with Sudo, she definitely joined Housen-kun, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s as far as I’ve noticed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a bit weird… Even if I’m trying to be polite here, Housen-kun shouldn’t be that popular in the first year. Could they really ignore him while he confidently snatches those points away?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes… If the entire grade was told about the special exam of getting you expelled, there is a high probability that the 2nd and 3rd years will hear about it in a matter of time, not only just the 1st years. Hearing about this unreasonable special exam, our class would surely do everything we could do to fight back. So they did it in a way to prevent us from knowing about it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Although I tried to confirm it with Chabashira-sensei tactfully, she didn’t show signs she knew about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. It would make sense if an individual set the bounty on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, there’s someone in the same or a higher grade that had prepared that many points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “–The student …  council president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could it be that President Nagumo might have something to do with this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Without realizing it, maybe you aroused Nagumo’s jealousy. President Nagumo had always been interested in brother’s affairs, because he had always been only interested in your affairs. Even if he has complicated feelings like me, it’s not strange.” — speaker untagged by the translation (Nagumo&#x27;s name precedes it; Horikita&#x27;s rapport with Ayanokōji says this is hers); unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although it’s a bit late, this is the topic of today’s conversation with you. I’m preparing after school to go to the student council, and ask President Nagumo about joining it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if I can’t get Nagumo’s approval, it’s not my responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…You did say that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The reason why you wanted me to join the student council… It was so I …  …  … could spy on President Nagumo, but actually, that’s not the only reason, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What the student council …  is doing now, that’s certainly the complete opposite.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So that’s why you won’t give me specific instructions?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then why do you need me to join, if the only thing you want is to see Nagumo’s reforms? There’s no need for me to monitor the student council at all, then!”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s still some things I’m not satisfied with, but I’ll put it as convenient.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’s good for me to ask anything of you since I lost the match, but will you come with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’d like to show you using the meeting with Nagumo as evidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If President Nagumo has something to do with that bounty, we might also see some kind of reaction.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The 20-million bounty reasoning lands on Nagumo by elimination; she&#x27;s the one who says it aloud.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> They walk together; the plan is hers to execute.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She suspects him and intends to watch him.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She tactfully checked with her; nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She treats the 1st-year silence as strategic, not accidental.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p27-1\">← Before: The reserve strategy: Horikita saves him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p75-1\">→ After: Horikita joins the student council<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p66-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo coverage note  passing mentions  if he could improve his academics and social contribution in the future  he might even be able to stand shoulder to shoulder with yosuke and kushida   here  ike left together with kushida with a spring in his step   headed by hirata kun and kushida san  who have strong communication skills  and have well balanced grades   after kushida and yagami left  i approached the convenience store","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p66-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.66–264<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If he could improve his academics and social contribution in the future, he might even be able to stand shoulder to shoulder with Yosuke and Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “here, Ike left together with Kushida with a spring in his step.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Headed by Hirata-kun and Kushida-san, who have strong communication skills, and have well-balanced grades…”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After Kushida and Yagami left, I approached the convenience store.”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p171-1\">→ After: Kushida redirects Ike<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p66-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken coverage note  passing mentions  as said before  the one with the most significant increase was sudou  second year oaa print out   academics c  54  physical a   96  adaptability c   42  social contribution c   60  overall b   63   later  if sudo lived a serious life for the past six months  his social contribution number would rise at the very least   leaving beside sudo  the overall strength of the other students had also improved from the first year   although we re indebted to her since she teamed up with sudo  she definitely joined housen kun  right   the thing about teaming up with sudou senpai  you haven t forgotten about that have you   the trio of hirata  sudo  and hondou challenges the exam till the end   by the way  i heard from sudo kun that you re gonna be a regular on the basketball team   along with sudo kun  who s the only one to get an a  rating in physical ability in the entire 2nd year   he was similar to sudou in terms of enthusiasm  but ishizaki was different in his own way","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p66-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.66–320<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “as said before, the one with the most significant increase was Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Second-year OAA print-out — Academics C (54), Physical A+ (96), Adaptability C- (42), Social Contribution C+ (60), Overall B- (63).<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “later, if Sudo lived a serious life for the past six months, his social contribution number would rise at the very least.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Leaving beside Sudo, the overall strength of the other students had also improved from the first year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Although we’re indebted to her since she teamed up with Sudo, she definitely joined Housen-kun, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The thing about teaming up with Sudou-senpai, you haven’t forgotten about that have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “the trio of Hirata, Sudo, and Hondou challenges the exam till the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “By the way, I heard from Sudo-kun that you’re gonna be a regular on the basketball team?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “along with Sudo-kun, who’s the only one to get an A+ rating in physical ability in the entire 2nd year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “He was similar to Sudou in terms of enthusiasm, but Ishizaki was different in his own way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p54-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s big question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p142-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s alliance idea<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-wang-mei-yu-y2v2-p66-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"wang-mei-yu","q":"wang mei yu wang  mii chan  mentioned in passing named in the student council recruitment context  passing mention  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-wang-mei-yu-y2v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/wang-mei-yu.html#sc-wang-mei-yu-y2v2-p66-1\">Wang (Mii-chan) mentioned in passing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.66<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the student council recruitment context.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p68-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"nanase-tsubasa","q":"nanase tsubasa named by ayanokoji  ch 2 backreference  he names her in his secret exam intel exchange with horikita  not present in those pages   see horikita s person record and ayanokoji s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html#sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p68-1\">Named by Ayanokōji (Ch.2 backreference)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.68–72<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He names her in his secret-exam intel exchange with Horikita; not present in those pages — see Horikita&#x27;s person record and Ayanokōji&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p111-1\">→ After: The confession on the way to school<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p69-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"amasawa-ichika","q":"amasawa ichika coverage note  passing mentions  class a s amasawa san  although we re indebted to her since she teamed up with sudo  she definitely joined housen kun  right  ayanokoji cites the precedent set by amasawa for u locking the door   the strategy adopted against her earlier visit  see the amasawa room scene  ch 2 p 83 108   everything was a defense strategy carried out based on amasawa   up to now  the only thing that had affected me was the time when amasawa came to my room  and the major crisis concerning whether or not i would get expelled hadn t happened at all   like amasawa  if it were a normal person  feeling that it was hard to approach me would not be surprising at all   what was most intriguing though  was that amasawa s name didn t appear on that list  the first year threat on the page is  the up and coming group of the first years consisting of housen and amasawa","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p69-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html#sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p69-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.69–335<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Class A’s Amasawa-san… Although we’re indebted to her since she teamed up with Sudo, she definitely joined Housen-kun, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Ayanokōji cites the precedent set by Amasawa for U-locking the door — the strategy adopted against her earlier visit (see the Amasawa room scene, Ch.2 p.83–108).<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Everything was a defense strategy carried out based on Amasawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Up to now, the only thing that had affected me was the time when Amasawa came to my room, and the major crisis concerning whether or not I would get expelled hadn’t happened at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Like Amasawa, if it were a normal person, feeling that it was hard to approach me would not be surprising at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “What was most intriguing though, was that Amasawa’s name didn’t appear on that list.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> The first-year threat on the page is “the up and coming group of the first years consisting of Housen and Amasawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p6-1\">← Before: Amasawa: White Room prologue (her POV)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p92-1\">→ After: The intrusion; the 20-million confirmation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p71-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi coverage note  passing mentions  could it be that president nagumo might have something to do with this   without realizing it  maybe you aroused nagumo s jealousy  president nagumo had always been interested in brother s affairs  because he had always been only interested in your affairs   the issue of nagumo that manabu was worried about   could spy on president nagumo  but actually  that s not the only reason  right   different from what nagumo thinks   if nagumo is going in the wrong direction  there s a need to stop him   well  i d like to show you using the meeting with nagumo as evidence   if president nagumo has something to do with that bounty  we might also see some kind of reaction  kiriyama was someone who had struggled to overthrow nagumo  the battle between kiriyama and nagumo had already been settled   but as long as nagumo continues to pursue his policies  we would definitely compete with each other sooner or later   president nagumo about the uninhabited island survival exam held two years ago  and he kindly told me   it all started when i was contacted by president nagumo of the student council   the student council president nagumo senpai told the six of us that he ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled   president nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years  it was a simple game of chance  1 in 157   it was now confirmed that tsukishiro and nagumo were the ones behind the 20 million points   putting aside personal opinions of nagumo  the student council operated smoothly   if he wanted to keep this a secret from nagumo  he could have chose to meet late at night or early in the morning   i wanted to personally battle nagumo in this special exam   after which  nagumo became the student council president  and took control over the entire 3rd year  and eventually the entire school   however  nagumo s overall strength was even higher than his  so you could say that nagumo s boisterous attitude was in line with his strength   in that aspect  i don t think i can lose to nagumo   you wanted horikita manabu s sister to join the student council to monitor nagumo  right   that means she won t get in nagumo s way  right   unless horikita thinks nagumo s an obstacle   that won t work  forget all thoughts about dealing with nagumo   nagumo was more or less aware of what i d been doing with horikitasenpai   i didn t want to interfere in the relationship between nagumo and kiriyama  in which the winner and the loser had already been decided   nagumo s idea  the one in which anyone can graduate from class a   he wasn t really going to challenge nagumo   she doesn t even have a single friend    kiriyama speaking to ayanokoji about kiryuin  noting she lacks nagumo s supporters   she s just a good student  but kiryuuin doesn t have anyone supporting her  unlike nagumo  she doesn t even have a single friend   if she had been someone nagumo or manabu senpai would pay attention to  it wouldn t have been strange to hear about her   nagumo and kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place  and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen  right   and it might prove to be even more troublesome than defeating nagumo and kiriyama   there were the elites of the 3rd year  nagumo  kiriyama and kiryuuin   when i told him i wanted to join the council  president nagumo looked surprised at me   president nagumo who was speaking in front of me and acknowledged by my brother is certainly an amazing student  no doubt about that  but if compared to ayanokouji kun that impressions strangely changes everything   i had to enter the student council and confirm president nagumo s movements","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p71-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html#sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p71-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.71–350<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Could it be that President Nagumo might have something to do with this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Without realizing it, maybe you aroused Nagumo’s jealousy. President Nagumo had always been interested in brother’s affairs, because he had always been only interested in your affairs.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “the issue of Nagumo that Manabu was worried about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “could spy on President Nagumo, but actually, that’s not the only reason, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “different from what Nagumo thinks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If Nagumo is going in the wrong direction, there’s a need to stop him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Well, I’d like to show you using the meeting with Nagumo as evidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If President Nagumo has something to do with that bounty, we might also see some kind of reaction.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Kiriyama was someone who had struggled to overthrow Nagumo… the battle between Kiriyama and Nagumo had already been settled.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But as long as Nagumo continues to pursue his policies, we would definitely compete with each other sooner or later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “President Nagumo about the uninhabited island survival exam held two years ago, and he kindly told me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It all started when I was contacted by President Nagumo of the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The student council president Nagumo-senpai told the six of us that he’ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “President Nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years’. It was a simple game of chance, 1 in 157.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It was now confirmed that Tsukishiro and Nagumo were the ones behind the 20 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Putting aside personal opinions of Nagumo, the student council operated smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If he wanted to keep this a secret from Nagumo, he could have chose to meet late at night or early in the morning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I wanted to personally battle Nagumo in this special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After which, Nagumo became the student council president, and took control over the entire 3rd year, and eventually the entire school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “However, Nagumo’s overall strength was even higher than his, so you could say that Nagumo’s boisterous attitude was in line with his strength.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In that aspect, I don’t think I can lose to Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You wanted Horikita Manabu’s sister to join the student council to monitor Nagumo, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That means she won’t get in Nagumo’s way, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Unless Horikita thinks Nagumo’s an obstacle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That won’t work. Forget all thoughts about dealing with Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo was more or less aware of what I’d been doing with Horikitasenpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I didn’t want to interfere in the relationship between Nagumo and Kiriyama, in which the winner and the loser had already been decided.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo’s idea, the one in which anyone can graduate from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “He wasn’t really going to challenge Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “She doesn’t even have a single friend.” — Kiriyama speaking to Ayanokōji about Kiryūin, noting she lacks Nagumo’s supporters.<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “She’s just a good student, but Kiryuuin doesn’t have anyone supporting her, unlike Nagumo. She doesn’t even have a single friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If she had been someone Nagumo or Manabu-senpai would pay attention to, it wouldn’t have been strange to hear about her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo and Kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place, and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “And it might prove to be even more troublesome than defeating Nagumo and Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “there were the elites of the 3rd year- Nagumo, Kiriyama and Kiryuuin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “When I told him I wanted to join the council, president Nagumo looked surprised at me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.348<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “President Nagumo who was speaking in front of me and acknowledged by my brother is certainly an amazing student, no doubt about that… but if compared to Ayanokouji-kun that impressions strangely changes everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I had to enter the student council and confirm President Nagumo’s movements.”<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1\">→ After: Horikita joins the council; his challenge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi kiriyama-ikuto ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the student council meeting both go to the office  nagumo welcomes her  the two council members react similarly  surprise without welcome or rejection   i know that your time is valuable  president  so i ll get straight into it  i want to join the student council   well  what a turn of events  i don t really want to obediently say yes   so i m not welcome to join you   not really  i m basically one of those people who can t refuse  as long as there s space in the student council  i ll allow people to join  i won t even care about your reason for joining the council  it doesn t matter if it s for the oaa  or wanting to assume a post in the future  or maybe you just have a sense of righteousness  i don t really care   but then again  you re special  horikita suzune  let me at least mention one condition for your membership   what condition   why do you choose to join the student council at this time  would you please tell me that   i had an argument with my brother in the past  and so i chose to enter this school to settle them  but my relationship with my brother hasn t changed since i ve entered this school   my brother couldn t possibly approve of me who hadn t grown in the slightest  as a result  i hadn t spoken to him properly this year  at least up until his graduation   and then  have you reconciled   yes  at the very last second  i ve reconciled with him  and then  for the first time  i became interested in the student council that my brother devoted         his school life to  although i ve taken a long detour  i also want to walk the same path my brother has   the road brother took  it really is a nice story   in other words  can i assume that you have the intention to become the student council president   that s right  just like the road my brother walked  i also want to become student council president   i see  but honami has been working hard behind the scenes for a year as a member of the student council  you re already a year behind her in your quest in becoming the student council president  you can understand that  right   i don t think    it s a distance that can t be recovered   she doesn t look that similar to him  but she really is horikita senpai s little sister   i m kind of comfortable calling you horikita  i may have referred to you with that already but i ll call you suzune from now on  okay   do as you wish   i was troubled since the only member in the student council from the 2nd year was just honami    speaker untagged by the translation  it follows horikita s  do as you wish  in kiriyama s paragraph  unassigned  recorded as printed   welcome to the student council  from today onward  i want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries  suzune   of course   as a congratulations for joining  i ll tell you something interesting  the past presidents of the student council have always graduated in class a  remember that and work towards a higher goal   don t worry  i    don t plan to graduate outside of class a   then show me that isn t just all talk   it s a pleasure   are you going to    join the student council by the way  ayanokouji   what are you thinking  nagumo  you would even invite him into the council   it s nothing strange  he had the attention of horikita senpai after all  i don t       have a reason to refuse him  and in the special test the other day he was the only one who got a perfect score in a subject   i ll pass  my personality isn t suited to being on the council   i knew you would say that   ayanokouji   there s a lot more work in the student council than i thought   but everything has started to calm down now  so when summer starts  i ll spend my time with my kouhais   i ll play with you  so look forward to it   by the way  kiriyama  why did you get involved with this today   what do you mean   when the 1st and 2nd years requested to enter the student council you had no intention to attend  but this time when horikita suzune said she wanted to meet me  you showed up  it s weird isn t it   i just was interested in horikita senpai s little sister  anything wrong with that   it s nothing  nothing  don t mind it   then  suzune  i want to introduce you to the student council members outside of kiriyama  you stay right here   i understand  nagumo has evidently already read 2nd year results  he voices no suspicion of ayanokoji s interest   he simply extends the invitation and then dismisses it with one look  declines the council  reads nagumo s play with him line as an order  not a joke  he invites him  then dismisses the answer in one breath  he studies him  he is shaken by the vice president s attendance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\">The student council meeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.75–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Both go to the office; Nagumo welcomes her; the two council members react similarly (surprise without welcome or rejection).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I know that your time is valuable, president, so I’ll get straight into it. I want to join the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “Well, what a turn of events! I don’t really want to obediently say yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “So I’m not welcome to join you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>42 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not really, I’m basically one of those people who can’t refuse. As long as there’s space in the student council, I’ll allow people to join. I won’t even care about your reason for joining the council. It doesn’t matter if it’s for the OAA, or wanting to assume a post in the future, or maybe you just have a sense of righteousness. I don’t really care.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But then again, you’re special, Horikita Suzune. Let me at least mention one condition for your membership.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What condition?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you choose to join the student council at this time? Would you please tell me that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I had an argument with my brother in the past, and so I chose to enter this school to settle them. But my relationship with my brother hasn’t changed since I’ve entered this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My brother couldn’t possibly approve of me who hadn’t grown in the slightest. As a result, I hadn’t spoken to him properly this year, at least up until his graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And then? Have you reconciled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. At the very last second, I’ve reconciled with him. And then, for the first time, I became interested in the student council that my brother devoted …  …  … his school life to. Although I’ve taken a long detour, I also want to walk the same path my brother has.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The road brother took, it really is a nice story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, can I assume that you have the intention to become the student council president?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. Just like the road my brother walked, I also want to become student council president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. But Honami has been working hard behind the scenes for a year as a member of the student council. You’re already a year behind her in your quest in becoming the student council president. You can understand that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’s a distance that can’t be recovered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She doesn’t look that similar to him, but she really is Horikita-senpai’s little sister!”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m kind of comfortable calling you Horikita. I may have referred to you with that already but I’ll call you Suzune from now on, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do as you wish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I was troubled since the only member in the student council from the 2nd year was just Honami.” — speaker untagged by the translation (it follows Horikita&#x27;s “Do as you wish.” in Kiriyama&#x27;s paragraph); unassigned, recorded as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Welcome to the student council. From today onward, I want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a congratulations for joining, I’ll tell you something interesting. The past presidents of the student council have always graduated in Class A. Remember that and work towards a higher goal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I …  don’t plan to graduate outside of Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then show me that isn’t just all talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s a pleasure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you going to …  join the student council by the way? Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you thinking, Nagumo? You would even invite him into the council?”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing strange. He had the attention of Horikita-senpai after all. I don’t …  …  have a reason to refuse him. And in the special test the other day he was the only one who got a perfect score in a subject.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll pass, my personality isn’t suited to being on the council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I knew you would say that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a lot more work in the student council than I thought , but everything has started to calm down now, so when summer starts, I’ll spend my time with my kouhais.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll play with you, so look forward to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, Kiriyama, why did you get involved with this today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the 1st and 2nd years requested to enter the student council you had no intention to attend. But this time when Horikita Suzune said she wanted to meet me, you showed up. It’s weird isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just was interested in Horikita-senpai’s little sister, anything wrong with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing, nothing. Don’t mind it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, Suzune, I want to introduce you to the student council members outside of Kiriyama. You stay right here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nagumo has evidently already read 2nd-year results; he voices no suspicion of Ayanokōji&#x27;s interest — he simply extends the invitation and then dismisses it with one look.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Declines the council; reads Nagumo&#x27;s play-with-him line as an order, not a joke.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He invites him, then dismisses the answer in one breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> He studies him; he is shaken by the vice-president&#x27;s attendance.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\">← Before: The OAA update and the 20-million bounty<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p83-1\">→ After: Kei&#x27;s visit; the near-kiss<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p75-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi kiriyama-ikuto ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune horikita joins the student council she tells the council her reason   a blend of her true and negotiable motives   i know that your time is valuable  president  so i ll get straight into it  i want to join the student council   so i m not welcome to join you   what condition   i had an argument with my brother in the past  and so i chose to enter this school to settle them  but my relationship with my brother hasn t changed since i ve entered this school   my brother couldn t possibly approve of me who hadn t grown in the slightest  as a result  i hadn t spoken to him properly this year  at least up until his graduation   yes  at the very last second  i ve reconciled with him  and then  for the first time  i became interested in the student council that my brother devoted         his school life to  although i ve taken a long detour  i also want to walk the same path my brother has   that s right  just like the road my brother walked  i also want to become student council president   i don t think    it s a distance that can t be recovered   do as you wish   of course   don t worry  i    don t plan to graduate outside of class a   i understand  nagumo sees through the half truths but accepts them  kiriyama lingers as her handler ish vice president   honami  is the 1st 2nd year council member she s compared against   an ichinose mention  she sells the council a truth shaped motive  membership earned by admission of intent  and she signs the record as class d  she is admitted on the strength of her ambition  he gives no indication of knowing more  he attaches the horikita senpai comparisons to her  he calls her suzune from now on  she is the standard she s measured against for being a year ahead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p75-1\">Horikita joins the student council<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.75–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She tells the council her reason — a blend of her true and negotiable motives.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I know that your time is valuable, president, so I’ll get straight into it. I want to join the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “So I’m not welcome to join you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What condition?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I had an argument with my brother in the past, and so I chose to enter this school to settle them. But my relationship with my brother hasn’t changed since I’ve entered this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My brother couldn’t possibly approve of me who hadn’t grown in the slightest. As a result, I hadn’t spoken to him properly this year, at least up until his graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. At the very last second, I’ve reconciled with him. And then, for the first time, I became interested in the student council that my brother devoted …  …  … his school life to. Although I’ve taken a long detour, I also want to walk the same path my brother has.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. Just like the road my brother walked, I also want to become student council president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’s a distance that can’t be recovered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do as you wish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I …  don’t plan to graduate outside of Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nagumo sees through the half-truths but accepts them; Kiriyama lingers as her handler-ish vice president; “Honami” is the 1st 2nd-year council member she&#x27;s compared against — an Ichinose mention.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She sells the council a truth-shaped motive; membership earned by admission of intent, and she signs the record as Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She is admitted on the strength of her ambition; he gives no indication of knowing more.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> He attaches the Horikita-senpai comparisons to her; he calls her Suzune from now on.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She is the standard she&#x27;s measured against for being a year ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p65-1\">← Before: Walking to school; the council decision<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p119-1\">→ After: The exam; the alliance debate; the quiet phones<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kiriyama-ikuto ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi horikita joins the council  his challenge horikita s request lands  the two council members react the same way  in a manner that is neither welcoming nor rejecting   well  what a turn of events  i don t really want to obediently say yes   not really  i m basically one of those people who can t refuse  as long as there s space in the student council  i ll allow people to join  i won t even care about your reason for joining the council  it doesn t matter if it s for the oaa  or wanting to assume a post in the future  or maybe you just have a sense of righteousness  i don t really care   but then again  you re special  horikita suzune  let me at least mention one condition for your membership   why do you choose to join the student council at this time  would you please tell me that   and then  have you reconciled   the road brother took  it really is a nice story   in other words  can i assume that you have the intention to become the student council president   i see  but honami has been working hard behind the scenes for a year as a member of the student council  you re already a year behind her in your quest in becoming the student council president  you can understand that  right   welcome to the student council  from today onward  i want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries  suzune   as a congratulations for joining  i ll tell you something interesting  the past presidents of the student council have always graduated in class a  remember that and work towards a higher goal   then show me that isn t just all talk   are you going to    join the student council by the way  ayanokouji   it s nothing strange  he had the attention of horikita senpai after all  i don t       have a reason to refuse him  and in the special test the other day he was the only one who got a perfect score in a subject   i knew you would say that   ayanokouji   there s a lot more work in the student council than i thought   but everything has started to calm down now  so when summer starts  i ll spend my time with my kouhais   i ll play with you  so look forward to it   by the way  kiriyama  why did you get involved with this today   when the 1st and 2nd years requested to enter the student council you had no intention to attend  but this time when horikita suzune said she wanted to meet me  you showed up  it s weird isn t it   it s nothing  nothing  don t mind it   then  suzune  i want to introduce you to the student council members outside of kiriyama  you stay right here  horikita was prompting her own designs on the presidency  his mention of honami is the second year council seat ichinose holds  he notes kiriyama s attendance was for suzune  not for him  welcoming and unreading on the surface  the council is a meritocracy now  he openly says presidents graduate in class a   and means it as a challenge  he accepts her  he sets the presidential bar out loud  he tests and dismisses him in the same breath  he invites him  is declined  and declares he ll play with him  she is the one year ahead standard he sets for horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html#sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1\">Horikita joins the council; his challenge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.75–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita&#x27;s request lands; the two council members react the same way, in a manner that is neither welcoming nor rejecting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “Well, what a turn of events! I don’t really want to obediently say yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “Not really, I’m basically one of those people who can’t refuse. As long as there’s space in the student council, I’ll allow people to join. I won’t even care about your reason for joining the council. It doesn’t matter if it’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “But then again, you’re special, Horikita Suzune. Let me at least mention one condition for your membership.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not really, I’m basically one of those people who can’t refuse. As long as there’s space in the student council, I’ll allow people to join. I won’t even care about your reason for joining the council. It doesn’t matter if it’s for the OAA, or wanting to assume a post in the future, or maybe you just have a sense of righteousness. I don’t really care.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you choose to join the student council at this time? Would you please tell me that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And then? Have you reconciled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The road brother took, it really is a nice story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, can I assume that you have the intention to become the student council president?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. But Honami has been working hard behind the scenes for a year as a member of the student council. You’re already a year behind her in your quest in becoming the student council president. You can understand that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Welcome to the student council. From today onward, I want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a congratulations for joining, I’ll tell you something interesting. The past presidents of the student council have always graduated in Class A. Remember that and work towards a higher goal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then show me that isn’t just all talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you going to …  join the student council by the way? Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing strange. He had the attention of Horikita-senpai after all. I don’t …  …  have a reason to refuse him. And in the special test the other day he was the only one who got a perfect score in a subject.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I knew you would say that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a lot more work in the student council than I thought , but everything has started to calm down now, so when summer starts, I’ll spend my time with my kouhais.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll play with you, so look forward to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, Kiriyama, why did you get involved with this today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the 1st and 2nd years requested to enter the student council you had no intention to attend. But this time when Horikita Suzune said she wanted to meet me, you showed up. It’s weird isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing, nothing. Don’t mind it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, Suzune, I want to introduce you to the student council members outside of Kiriyama. You stay right here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita was prompting her own designs on the presidency; his mention of Honami is the second-year council seat Ichinose holds. He notes Kiriyama&#x27;s attendance was for Suzune, not for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Welcoming and unreading on the surface; the council is a meritocracy now; he openly says presidents graduate in Class A — and means it as a challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He accepts her; he sets the presidential bar out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> He tests and dismisses him in the same breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He invites him, is declined, and declares he&#x27;ll play with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She is the one-year-ahead standard he sets for Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p71-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p286-1\">→ After: Nagumo and Kiryūin<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p78-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kiriyama","q":"kiriyama kiriyama attends the roster carries both  kiriyama ikuto  and  kiriyama   legacy  for the same class 2 b 2  student   this file keeps a duplicate of the ch 2 note for traceability  scene lines live on kiriyama ikuto md  recorded as a duplicate roster row for the owner   do not merge from this side  present as vice president  rattled by nagumo s question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiriyama attends<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.78–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kiriyama\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The roster carries both `kiriyama-ikuto` and `kiriyama` (legacy) for the same Class 2-B/2? student — this file keeps a duplicate of the Ch.2 note for traceability; scene lines live on kiriyama-ikuto.md. Recorded as a duplicate roster row for the owner — do not merge from this side.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Present as Vice President.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Rattled by Nagumo&#x27;s question.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p83-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p78-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiriyama-ikuto","q":"kiriyama ikuto kiriyama attends he has remained silent through the whole interview  then he speaks to nagumo for the first time   she doesn t look that similar to him  but she really is horikita senpai s little sister   i m kind of comfortable calling you horikita  i may have referred to you with that already but i ll call you suzune from now on  okay   i was troubled since the only member in the student council from the 2nd year was just honami    speaker untagged by the translation  it continues his paragraph to nagumo  unassigned as printed  he attends despite having no 1st 2nd year applicants to care about  nagumo clocks it and probes   what are you thinking  nagumo  you would even invite him into the council   it s a pleasure   what do you mean   i just was interested in horikita senpai s little sister  anything wrong with that  he has given up on overthrowing nagumo but not on attaching himself to the horikita name  he is rattled when nagumo names the real reason he came  he serves him  watched  he attaches to her arrival  calls her suzune from now on  he is shaken to see ak inside","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html#sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p78-1\">Kiriyama attends<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.78–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He has remained silent through the whole interview; then he speaks to Nagumo for the first time. He attends despite having no 1st/2nd-year applicants to care about; Nagumo clocks it and probes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “She doesn’t look that similar to him, but she really is Horikita-senpai’s little sister!”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “I’m kind of comfortable calling you Horikita. I may have referred to you with that already but I’ll call you Suzune from now on, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “What are you thinking, Nagumo? You would even invite him into the council?”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I was troubled since the only member in the student council from the 2nd year was just Honami.” — speaker untagged by the translation (it continues his paragraph to Nagumo); unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s a pleasure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just was interested in Horikita-senpai’s little sister, anything wrong with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He has given up on overthrowing Nagumo but not on attaching himself to the Horikita name; he is rattled when Nagumo names the real reason he came.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He serves him, watched.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He attaches to her arrival; calls her Suzune from now on.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He is shaken to see AK inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p83-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p83-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kei s visit  the near kiss after the council he checks his phone and replies to kei s hang out proposal  he tells her to come over after twenty minutes  with the usual precautions   i ll come   is it alright if i come now   i m coming in   i really panicked when i saw the elevator stop at the 4th floor   i know that   that s good   do you want something to drink   i ll do it   that s a surprise  what made you want to do it  you wouldn t normally do this   it s hard when your left hand is injured  right  look  even i know how to boil water   ok  i ll have black tea  what would you like  kiyotaka   then  i ll have the same  kei   you don t have any faith in me  do you   i see  then i ll have a cup of coffee   leave it to me  isn t it in that cabinet over there  they study  as cover  trivial talk  the conversation thins  the mood changes  the kiss nearly happens  the entrance doorbell rings   by the way  i was thinking of telling you this when we met  but kiyotaka  you have a big responsibility   because you ve gotten a full score in math  it s become harder for me to come out with the dating thing   who knows what would happen if we publicize that we re dating now   so is this situation going to continue as it is for a while   it can t be helped     it s annoying  making it feel like i m dating you because of your status   is it bad to date someone for status   no  i m not saying it s bad either   like dating a cute girl is a symbol of status for guys  right  wouldn t it be a little too harsh to ask for people not to want that   a am i cute   would you want to date someone who s not cute   ahhh  me too  i also think you re super handsome  kiyotaka   ahhh  me too  i also think you re super handsome  kiyotaka  an indoor date  talk winds down  they drift toward each other  one breath from kissing  the doorbell rings   ah  eh  the door  their near kiss is interrupted by the call  the secret stays sealed for another day","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p83-1\">Kei&#x27;s visit; the near-kiss<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.83–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the council he checks his phone and replies to Kei&#x27;s hang-out proposal; he tells her to come over after twenty minutes, with the usual precautions. They study (as cover); trivial talk; the conversation thins; the mood changes; the kiss nearly happens; the entrance doorbell rings. An indoor date; talk winds down; they drift toward each other; one breath from kissing; the doorbell rings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “’I’ll come!”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Is it alright if I come now!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I’m coming in!”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really panicked when I saw the elevator stop at the 4th floor~!”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know that…”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you want something to drink?”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a surprise, what made you want to do it? You wouldn’t normally do this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s hard when your left hand is injured, right? Look, even I know how to boil water!”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ok. I’ll have black tea, what would you like, Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then… I’ll have the same, Kei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t have any faith in me, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…I see, then I’ll have a cup of coffee.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Leave it to me! Isn’t it in that cabinet over there?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, I was thinking of telling you this when we met, but Kiyotaka, you have a big responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because you’ve gotten a full score in math, it’s become harder for me to come out with the dating thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows what would happen if we publicize that we’re dating now…”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So is this situation going to continue as it is for a while?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It can’t be helped … … It’s annoying, making it feel like I’m dating you because of your status.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it bad to date someone for status?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m not saying it’s bad either…”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Like dating a cute girl is a symbol of status for guys, right? Wouldn’t it be a little too harsh to ask for people not to want that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A-am I cute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you want to date someone who’s not cute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahhh… me too, I also think you’re super handsome, Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahhh… me too, I also think you’re super handsome, Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, eh, the door…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Their near-kiss is interrupted by the call; the secret stays sealed for another day.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\">← Before: The student council meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p92-1\">→ After: Amasawa&#x27;s intrusion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p83-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei kei s visit  the near kiss he replies to her messages at the student council exit  she races to his room  shoes hidden in the closet  the signal chain locked   i ll come   is it alright if i come now   i m coming in   i really panicked when i saw the elevator stop at the 4th floor   whew  i m relieved   i ll do it   that s a surprise  what made you want to do it  you wouldn t normally do this   it s hard when your left hand is injured  right  look  even i know how to boil water   ok  i ll have black tea  what would you like  kiyotaka   you don t have any faith in me  do you   leave it to me  isn t it in that cabinet over there  tea becomes cafe au lait  they study as cover  the chit chat thins  the room changes temperature   by the way  i was thinking of telling you this when we met  but kiyotaka  you have a big responsibility   because you ve gotten a full score in math  it s become harder for me to come out with the dating thing   it can t be helped     it s annoying  making it feel like i m dating you because of your status   no  i m not saying it s bad either   a am i cute   ahhh  me too  i also think you re super handsome  kiyotaka  they drift into each other  one breath from kissing  the entrance doorbell breaks it   ah  eh  the door  the near kiss is interrupted by amasawa  their secret stays unbroken this time  the risk counter  the 1 in 10 000  stays on the books  she measures the distance to  us  and almost crosses it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p83-1\">Kei&#x27;s visit; the near-kiss<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.83–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He replies to her messages at the student council exit; she races to his room; shoes hidden in the closet; the signal chain locked. Tea becomes café-au-lait; they study as cover; the chit-chat thins; the room changes temperature. They drift into each other; one breath from kissing; the entrance doorbell breaks it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “’I’ll come!”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Is it alright if I come now!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I’m coming in!”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really panicked when I saw the elevator stop at the 4th floor~!”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whew… I’m relieved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a surprise, what made you want to do it? You wouldn’t normally do this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s hard when your left hand is injured, right? Look, even I know how to boil water!”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ok. I’ll have black tea, what would you like, Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t have any faith in me, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Leave it to me! Isn’t it in that cabinet over there?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, I was thinking of telling you this when we met, but Kiyotaka, you have a big responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because you’ve gotten a full score in math, it’s become harder for me to come out with the dating thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It can’t be helped … … It’s annoying, making it feel like I’m dating you because of your status.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m not saying it’s bad either…”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A-am I cute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahhh… me too, I also think you’re super handsome, Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, eh, the door…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The near-kiss is interrupted by Amasawa; their secret stays unbroken this time; the risk-counter (the 1-in-10,000) stays on the books.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She measures the distance to “us” and almost crosses it.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p36-1\">← Before: Karuizawa protects Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p92-1\">→ After: Amasawa in the room with them<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p83-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kiriyama","q":"kiriyama coverage note  passing mentions scene lines are on kiriyama ikuto md  roster carries both  kiriyama  and  kiriyama ikuto  do not merge from this side   well  if kiriyama hasn t given up yet  eventually he might act   next to him stood kiriyama  the vice president of the student council  who had just left   because the one who left and as returned is you  kiriyama  and so that fits the image of a loyal dog   you ve got a dirty mouth  kiriyama  it doesn t suit the image of a serious vice president   nagumo tapped kiriyama on the shoulder and interrupted him  he forced kiriyama to move away a little  and stood in front of kiryuuin   i heard something from kiriyama  i would have never thought that someone who wasn t interested in both horikita senpai or i  would be interested in ayanokouji   up till now  nagumo had competed with kiriyama s class many times in the past special exams   kiriyama simply glared at kiryuuin  who was merrily talking  but didn t interfere with their conversation  after he said that  nagumo turned his attention to kiriyama  who was waiting for him   or maybe it ll be kiriyama  who s been dying to fight me   nagumo gave instructions to withdraw and headed over to kiriyama   then there were the elites of the 3rd year  nagumo  kiriyama and kiryuuin","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.83–335<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kiriyama\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Scene lines are on kiriyama-ikuto.md (roster carries both `kiriyama` and `kiriyama-ikuto`; do not merge from this side).<span class=\"pg\">p.271–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Well… If Kiriyama hasn’t given up yet, eventually he might act.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Next to him stood Kiriyama, the vice president of the student council, who had just left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Because the one who left and as returned is you, Kiriyama, and so that fits the image of a loyal dog.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You’ve got a dirty mouth, Kiriyama, it doesn’t suit the image of a serious vice president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo tapped Kiriyama on the shoulder and interrupted him. He forced Kiriyama to move away a little, and stood in front of Kiryuuin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I heard something from Kiriyama. I would have never thought that someone who wasn’t interested in both Horikita-senpai or I, would be interested in Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Up till now, Nagumo had competed with Kiriyama’s class many times in the past special exams.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Kiriyama simply glared at Kiryuuin, who was merrily talking, but didn’t interfere with their conversation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> After he said that, Nagumo turned his attention to Kiriyama, who was waiting for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Or maybe it’ll be Kiriyama, who’s been dying to fight me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo gave instructions to withdraw and headed over to Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “then there were the elites of the 3rd year- Nagumo, Kiriyama and Kiryuuin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p78-1\">← Before: Kiriyama attends<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p271-1\">→ After: Kiriyama&#x27;s warning (and the bench)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p83-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kiriyama-ikuto","q":"kiriyama ikuto coverage note  passing mentions  well  if kiriyama hasn t given up yet  eventually he might act   next to him stood kiriyama  the vice president of the student council  who had just left   because the one who left and as returned is you  kiriyama  and so that fits the image of a loyal dog   you ve got a dirty mouth  kiriyama  it doesn t suit the image of a serious vice president   nagumo tapped kiriyama on the shoulder and interrupted him  he forced kiriyama to move away a little  and stood in front of kiryuuin   i heard something from kiriyama  i would have never thought that someone who wasn t interested in both horikita senpai or i  would be interested in ayanokouji   up till now  nagumo had competed with kiriyama s class many times in the past special exams   kiriyama simply glared at kiryuuin  who was merrily talking  but didn t interfere with their conversation  after he said that  nagumo turned his attention to kiriyama  who was waiting for him   or maybe it ll be kiriyama  who s been dying to fight me   nagumo gave instructions to withdraw and headed over to kiriyama   then there were the elites of the 3rd year  nagumo  kiriyama and kiryuuin","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html#sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p83-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.83–335<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Well… If Kiriyama hasn’t given up yet, eventually he might act.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Next to him stood Kiriyama, the vice president of the student council, who had just left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Because the one who left and as returned is you, Kiriyama, and so that fits the image of a loyal dog.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You’ve got a dirty mouth, Kiriyama, it doesn’t suit the image of a serious vice president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo tapped Kiriyama on the shoulder and interrupted him. He forced Kiriyama to move away a little, and stood in front of Kiryuuin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I heard something from Kiriyama. I would have never thought that someone who wasn’t interested in both Horikita-senpai or I, would be interested in Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Up till now, Nagumo had competed with Kiriyama’s class many times in the past special exams.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Kiriyama simply glared at Kiryuuin, who was merrily talking, but didn’t interfere with their conversation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> After he said that, Nagumo turned his attention to Kiriyama, who was waiting for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Or maybe it’ll be Kiriyama, who’s been dying to fight me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nagumo gave instructions to withdraw and headed over to Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “then there were the elites of the 3rd year- Nagumo, Kiriyama and Kiryuuin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p78-1\">← Before: Kiriyama attends<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p271-1\">→ After: Kiriyama&#x27;s warning (and the bench)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p92-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei amasawa-ichika","q":"amasawa ichika the intrusion  the 20 million confirmation he peeps  red hair  a sweet voice  her casual clothes  hands empty  he opens the door to amasawa from class 1 a   she entered with another senpai returning from outside  surprise visit after the hosen plan s failure   senpai   it s me   how did you get into the dormitory   there was another senpai who was returning  so i went in with him  i thought i d give you a surprise   and   is your hand alright now  i was worried so i came to see you   this  can you unlock it for me   senpai  you look like you are alone anyway  so cook for me   i have that right  right  the thing about teaming up with sudou senpai  you haven t forgotten about that have you   i m sorry  but i    ran out of ingredients  there s nothing in the fridge   eeeh  is that so  you should have reserves   if it has to be today  how about i go and get ready now  and we can buy the ingredients together   i see  you don t have any ingredients that s too bad  she reveals she watched karuizawa enter his room  pushes him to the wall in under a second   did you lie to me because you didn t want me to come into the room   senpai is not alone right   why do you think that   because  i saw it  i ve been watching karuizawa senpai all the time since she came back to the dormitories   from the fact that you ve hidden your girlfriend s shoes  were you two doing lewd things   it was just a precaution because we didn t tell anyone that we were dating yet   ah  are you finally admitting it  well  it s not like i don t understand your feelings of wanting to hide it  but i know about it already  so there s no need to lie to me  ok   i kept it a secret for now out of goodwill  but  i wonder if i shall reveal it  he lets her in  she drops the contraceptive on the table  kei makes the coffee   okay   this isn t good  a young couple alone with the door locked   well  that s true  but when i look at you two  i feel something lewd between you   your clothes aren t messy  and the bed is tidy  so it doesn t look like you were doing anything   i thought you would have an illicit sexual relationship for sure  i mean having sex   if you go to the convenience store there are contraceptives  in fact i tried to buy it once  and the employee pretended not to see  well  if everything is forbidden and a young guy goes berserk and it results in a pregnancy  that would be the real problem  right   take this as a gift from me  no  take it as an apology   quit playing dumb  the wound on your hand  i had a part in that right  because i teamed up with housen  she admits her piece of the expulsion plan  the 20 million bounty drops out between them   ayanokouji senpai  i think you re misunderstanding me a bit   i m not ayanokouji senpai s enemy   is that so  just because i shared my knowledge out to housen kun from the sidelines   let me guess what senpai is thinking about now  i played a part in housen s plan to get you expelled  which raised the possibility of your expulsion  that s why you think it s ridiculous for someone like that to say that they were not an enemy  is that right  i ve been underestimated by senpai   really  i don t think so   ayanokouji senpai  haven t you told your girlfriend about that  then what about the 20 million point bounty   let your boyfriend tell you the details later  alright  senpai   housen kun and i wanted to use that knife to get senpai expelled and the reason why senpai noticed this was because you went shopping with me  right   how considerate of you   because senpai suddenly had a bounty for his head  and i thought that it was a pity that you would be expelled without even knowing the situation   ahh my mouth is a little dry  i d like some coffee or something   sugar and milk as well please   don t put garbage or sewage into my coffee because you don t like me   let s see  hmmm  what was the convention adopted at the general conference of the united nations educational  scientific and cultural organization in 1972   correct  correct   isn t it alright  just a little bit   senpai s girlfriend  seems to have a habit of being angry   well  i ve already given you my condolence gift  so it s time for me to go back  please feel free to use the ingredients   i don t mind relaxing here  but how about you   that s what i thought  then i ll go now  playful  shameless  razor sharp   probes the couple mercilessly  admits her role in the knife plot openly  denies being his enemy  and leaves his guard permanently up  she is almost certainly the 5th generation white room student of the prologue  same voice  same obsession    the volume does not state it outright  she  left a trace  deliberately  the knife choice  so he could defend himself  her vigilance raising move is calculated  not sentimental  she pressures him  he concedes the room  his suspicion of her upgrades  she teases her relentlessly and learns she s dating him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p92-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html#sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p92-1\">The intrusion; the 20-million confirmation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.92–108<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He peeps; red hair, a sweet voice; her casual clothes, hands empty; he opens the door to Amasawa from Class 1-A — she entered with another senpai returning from outside; surprise visit after the Hōsen plan&#x27;s failure. She reveals she watched Karuizawa enter his room; pushes him to the wall in under a second. He lets her in; she drops the contraceptive on the table; Kei makes the coffee. She admits her piece of the expulsion plan; the 20-million bounty drops out between them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “Senpai~”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “It’s me~”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “How did you get into the dormitory?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>50 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There was another senpai who was returning, so I went in with him. I thought I’d give you a surprise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is your hand alright now? I was worried so I came to see you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This, can you unlock it for me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai, you look like you are alone anyway, so cook for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have that right, right? The thing about teaming up with Sudou-senpai, you haven’t forgotten about that have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I …  ran out of ingredients. There’s nothing in the fridge.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eeeh—— Is that so—? You should have reserves~”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it has to be today, how about I go and get ready now, and we can buy the ingredients together?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, you don’t have any ingredients~That’s too bad~”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you lie to me because you didn’t want me to come into the room?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai is not alone right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you think that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because~ I saw it. I’ve been watching Karuizawa-senpai all the time since she came back to the dormitories~”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From the fact that you’ve hidden your girlfriend’s shoes, were you two doing lewd things?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was just a precaution because we didn’t tell anyone that we were dating yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, are you finally admitting it? Well, it’s not like I don’t understand your feelings of wanting to hide it, but I know about it already, so there’s no need to lie to me, OK?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I kept it a secret for now out of goodwill… But, I wonder if I shall reveal it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay~”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t good, a young couple alone with the door locked~”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well~ that’s true. But when I look at you two, I feel something lewd between you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your clothes aren’t messy, and the bed is tidy, so it doesn’t look like you were doing anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought you would have an illicit sexual relationship for sure… I mean having sex.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you go to the convenience store there are contraceptives. In fact I tried to buy it once, and the employee pretended not to see. Well, if everything is forbidden and a young guy goes berserk…and it results in a pregnancy, that would be the real problem, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Take this as a gift from me… No, take it as an apology.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Quit playing dumb, the wound on your hand, I had a part in that right? Because I teamed up with Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-senpai, I think you’re misunderstanding me a bit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not Ayanokouji-senpai’s enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Just because I shared my knowledge out to Housen-kun from the sidelines?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me guess what senpai is thinking about now. I played a part in Housen’s plan to get you expelled, which raised the possibility of your expulsion. That’s why you think it’s ridiculous for someone like that to say that they were not an enemy. Is that right? I’ve been underestimated by senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? I don’t think so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-senpai, haven’t you told your girlfriend about that? Then what about the 20 million point bounty?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let your boyfriend tell you the details later, alright, senpai?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen-kun and I wanted to use that knife to get senpai expelled——And the reason why senpai noticed this was because you went shopping with me, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How considerate of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because senpai suddenly had a bounty for his head, and I thought that it was a pity that you would be expelled without even knowing the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahh——My mouth is a little dry~. I’d like some coffee or something.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sugar and milk as well please~”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t put garbage or sewage into my coffee because you don’t like me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s see, hmmm? What was the convention adopted at the General Conference of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization in 1972?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Correct, correct～”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it alright? Just a little bit”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai’s girlfriend… seems to have a habit of being angry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’ve already given you my condolence gift, so it’s time for me to go back. Please feel free to use the ingredients.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t mind relaxing here, but how about you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what I thought~ Then I’ll go now~”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Playful, shameless, razor-sharp — probes the couple mercilessly, admits her role in the knife plot openly, denies being his enemy, and leaves his guard permanently up; she is almost certainly the 5th-generation White Room student of the prologue (same voice, same obsession) — the volume does not state it outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She “left a trace” deliberately (the knife choice) so he could defend himself; her vigilance-raising move is calculated, not sentimental.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She pressures him; he concedes the room; his suspicion of her upgrades.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She teases her relentlessly and learns she&#x27;s dating him.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p69-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p236-1\">→ After: The alliance terms with Housen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p92-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka amasawa s intrusion peephole  red hair and a sweet voice  it s amasawa  he opens the door   senpai    it s me   how did you get into the dormitory   there was another senpai who was returning  so i went in with him  i thought i d give you a surprise   and   is your hand alright now  i was worried so i came to see you   this  can you unlock it for me   it s late in the evening already  so can we talk tomorrow  it ll be a problem bringing in a kouhai in my room without any reason   senpai  you look like you are alone anyway  so cook for me   i have that right  right  the thing about teaming up with sudou senpai  you haven t forgotten about that have you   i m sorry  but i    ran out of ingredients  there s nothing in the fridge   eeeh  is that so  you should have reserves   if it has to be today  how about i go and get ready now  and we can buy the ingredients together   i see  you don t have any ingredients that s too bad   did you lie to me because you didn t want me to come into the room   senpai is not alone right   why do you think that   because  i saw it  i ve been watching karuizawa senpai all the time since she came back to the dormitories   from the fact that you ve hidden your girlfriend s shoes  were you two doing lewd things   it was just a precaution because we didn t tell anyone that we were dating yet   ah  are you finally admitting it  well  it s not like i don t understand your feelings of wanting to hide it  but i know about it already  so there s no need to lie to me  ok   i kept it a secret for now out of goodwill  but  i wonder if i shall reveal it   hold on  i ll unlock the door   okay   this isn t good  a young couple alone with the door locked   well  that s true  but when i look at you two  i feel something lewd between you   your clothes aren t messy  and the bed is tidy  so it doesn t look like you were doing anything   well isn t that normal  anyway  why did you come here all of a sudden   i thought you would have an illicit sexual relationship for sure  i mean having sex   that s something forbidden by the school rules   if you go to the convenience store there are contraceptives  in fact i tried to buy it once  and the employee pretended not to see  well  if everything is forbidden and a young guy goes berserk and it results in a pregnancy  that would be the real problem  right   take this as a gift from me  no  take it as an apology   i don t remember you having anything to apologize for   quit playing dumb  the wound on your hand  i had a part in that right  because i teamed up with housen   is that so   ayanokouji senpai  i think you re misunderstanding me a bit   misunderstand   i m not ayanokouji senpai s enemy   is that so  just because i shared my knowledge out to housen kun from the sidelines   let me guess what senpai is thinking about now  i played a part in housen s plan to get you expelled  which raised the possibility of your expulsion  that s why you think it s ridiculous for someone like that to say that they were not an enemy  is that right  i ve been underestimated by senpai   i don t remember underestimating you  i ve made a full evaluation of you   really  i don t think so   wa wait a minute  you said you were going to get kiyotaka expelled        what does that mean   ayanokouji senpai  haven t you told your girlfriend about that  then what about the 20 million point bounty   w what  you said 20 million   let your boyfriend tell you the details later  alright  senpai   housen kun and i wanted to use that knife to get senpai expelled and the reason why senpai noticed this was because you went shopping with me  right   how considerate of you   because senpai suddenly had a bounty for his head  and i thought that it was a pity that you would be expelled without even knowing the situation   ahh my mouth is a little dry  i d like some coffee or something   go make a cup of coffee for amasawa   i ll do it   sugar and milk as well please   argh  i got it  i got it   don t put garbage or sewage into my coffee because you don t like me   i wouldn t do anything of the sort   isn t it alright  just a little bit   not at all   senpai s girlfriend  seems to have a habit of being angry   here  you  are   thank you  karuizawa senpai   well  i ve already given you my condolence gift  so it s time for me to go back  please feel free to use the ingredients   huh  what do you mean  not drinking  you told me to make it though   i don t mind relaxing here  but how about you   that fine go home   that s what i thought  then i ll go now   kiyotaka  what s wrong with that kid   i d like to know that too   made me so mad   explain  what exactly is the 20 million point bounty  and does it have anything to do with your injury  she forces her way in  drops the contraceptive on the table  and extracts the 20 million bounty confirmation from kei  their secret relationship is now known to amasawa","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p92-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p92-1\">Amasawa&#x27;s intrusion<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.92–108<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Peephole: red hair and a sweet voice; it&#x27;s Amasawa; he opens the door.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “Senpai~ … It’s me~”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “How did you get into the dormitory?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “There was another senpai who was returning, so I went in with him. I thought I’d give you a surprise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>68 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is your hand alright now? I was worried so I came to see you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This, can you unlock it for me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s late in the evening already, so can we talk tomorrow? It’ll be a problem bringing in a kouhai in my room without any reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai, you look like you are alone anyway, so cook for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have that right, right? The thing about teaming up with Sudou-senpai, you haven’t forgotten about that have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I …  ran out of ingredients. There’s nothing in the fridge.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eeeh—— Is that so—? You should have reserves~”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it has to be today, how about I go and get ready now, and we can buy the ingredients together?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, you don’t have any ingredients~That’s too bad~”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you lie to me because you didn’t want me to come into the room?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai is not alone right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you think that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because~ I saw it. I’ve been watching Karuizawa-senpai all the time since she came back to the dormitories~”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From the fact that you’ve hidden your girlfriend’s shoes, were you two doing lewd things?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was just a precaution because we didn’t tell anyone that we were dating yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, are you finally admitting it? Well, it’s not like I don’t understand your feelings of wanting to hide it, but I know about it already, so there’s no need to lie to me, OK?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I kept it a secret for now out of goodwill… But, I wonder if I shall reveal it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hold on, I’ll unlock the door.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay~”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t good, a young couple alone with the door locked~”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well~ that’s true. But when I look at you two, I feel something lewd between you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your clothes aren’t messy, and the bed is tidy, so it doesn’t look like you were doing anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well isn’t that normal! Anyway, why did you come here all of a sudden!”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought you would have an illicit sexual relationship for sure… I mean having sex.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s something forbidden by the school rules.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you go to the convenience store there are contraceptives. In fact I tried to buy it once, and the employee pretended not to see. Well, if everything is forbidden and a young guy goes berserk…and it results in a pregnancy, that would be the real problem, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Take this as a gift from me… No, take it as an apology.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember you having anything to apologize for.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Quit playing dumb, the wound on your hand, I had a part in that right? Because I teamed up with Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is…that so?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-senpai, I think you’re misunderstanding me a bit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Misunderstand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not Ayanokouji-senpai’s enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Just because I shared my knowledge out to Housen-kun from the sidelines?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me guess what senpai is thinking about now. I played a part in Housen’s plan to get you expelled, which raised the possibility of your expulsion. That’s why you think it’s ridiculous for someone like that to say that they were not an enemy. Is that right? I’ve been underestimated by senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember underestimating you. I’ve made a full evaluation of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? I don’t think so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wa-wait a minute. You said you were going to get Kiyotaka expelled …  … … What does that mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-senpai, haven’t you told your girlfriend about that? Then what about the 20 million point bounty?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-what!? You said 20 million?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let your boyfriend tell you the details later, alright, senpai?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen-kun and I wanted to use that knife to get senpai expelled——And the reason why senpai noticed this was because you went shopping with me, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How considerate of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because senpai suddenly had a bounty for his head, and I thought that it was a pity that you would be expelled without even knowing the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahh——My mouth is a little dry~. I’d like some coffee or something.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Go make a cup of coffee for Amasawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…I’ll do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sugar and milk as well please~”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Argh! I got it, I got it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t put garbage or sewage into my coffee because you don’t like me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wouldn’t do anything of the sort!”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it alright? Just a little bit”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not at all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai’s girlfriend… seems to have a habit of being angry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Here. You. Are!”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you, Karuizawa-senpai~”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’ve already given you my condolence gift, so it’s time for me to go back. Please feel free to use the ingredients.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What do you mean? Not drinking? You told me to make it though?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t mind relaxing here, but how about you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That…fine…go home.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what I thought~ Then I’ll go now~”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka! What’s wrong with that kid!”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to know that too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Made me so mad!”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Explain, what exactly is the 20 million point bounty, and does it have anything to do with your injury?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She forces her way in, drops the contraceptive on the table, and extracts the 20-million bounty confirmation from Kei.<span class=\"pg\">p.93–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Their secret relationship is now known to Amasawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p83-1\">← Before: Kei&#x27;s visit; the near-kiss<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\">→ After: Nanase walks with him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p92-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei amasawa in the room with them the doorbell rings  she watches him unlock the door for the kouhai  amasawa sweeps in  her shoes argument  she is forced to serve coffee   it was just a precaution because we didn t tell anyone that we were dating yet  amasawa probes the couple  the contraceptive is produced  the 20 million bounty drops on the table  kei panics and hears it all   well isn t that normal  anyway  why did you come here all of a sudden   wa wait a minute  you said you were going to get kiyotaka expelled        what does that mean   w what  you said 20 million   i ll do it   argh  i got it  i got it   i wouldn t do anything of the sort   not at all   here  you  are   huh  what do you mean  not drinking  you told me to make it though   kiyotaka  what s wrong with that kid   made me so mad   explain  what exactly is the 20 million point bounty  and does it have anything to do with your injury  she hates amasawa openly  her panic at the bounty is real  she is dragged into the open for the first time  the kouhai who ruins the evening on purpose  he gives her the outline after amasawa leaves  the trust is forced forward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p92-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p92-1\">Amasawa in the room with them<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.92–108<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The doorbell rings; she watches him unlock the door for the kouhai; Amasawa sweeps in; her shoes argument; she is forced to serve coffee. Amasawa probes the couple; the contraceptive is produced; the 20-million bounty drops on the table; Kei panics and hears it all.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “It was just a precaution because we didn’t tell anyone that we were dating yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Well isn’t that normal! Anyway, why did you come here all of a sudden!”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Wa-wait a minute. You said you were going to get Kiyotaka expelled …  … … What does that mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102–103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-what!? You said 20 million?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…I’ll do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Argh! I got it, I got it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wouldn’t do anything of the sort!”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not at all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Here. You. Are!”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What do you mean? Not drinking? You told me to make it though?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka! What’s wrong with that kid!”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Made me so mad!”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Explain, what exactly is the 20 million point bounty, and does it have anything to do with your injury?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She hates Amasawa openly; her panic at the bounty is real; she is dragged into the open for the first time.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> The kouhai who ruins the evening on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He gives her the outline after Amasawa leaves; the trust is forced forward.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p83-1\">← Before: Kei&#x27;s visit; the near-kiss<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p110-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase walks with him mid june morning  he meets nanase tsubasa  class 1 d  walking to school  she stops and falls into step  or deliberately waits   he can t tell which   i ve always felt sorry for what i did to you  ayanokouji senpai   senpai  do you hate me   i don t have any reason to hate you  it was for the special exam  right  there s no way out of it  besides  i saw how you were trying to protect me  nanase   is that special exam over  i didn t hear you mentioning anything about a deadline   no  the exam is still going on  the deadline is the start of the second semester   because of what happened last time  i m convinced that even with a plan  it might not work out that easily  also  after you knew our purpose  it would be very hard to pressure you in your everyday life   then are you waiting for the other years to have their special exams  but what about the rest of you students   i don t know how  but i think they already know that housen kun has already made a move   and since even someone like housen failed  people judged that it wouldn t work out without good preparation  then it s worthwhile for me to be so badly injured   i don t know if that s worth the cost of your left hand  senpai   yes  i think the students in my grade  including myself  have become able to deal with all sorts of special situations  although i don t know how much the upperclassmen know  us 1st years had taken our 2nd special exam at the end of may   although i haven t heard from anyone directly  i ve noticed rumors that there was already someone who was expelled   ah  so you do know about it  one boy dropped out of class c in the first year   how did your class d place in the results of the exam   the previous time  we came in last  and this time  unfortunately  we only made third  but this time  class a and b battled fiercely  so the point difference created between the classes is very small   it d be a lie if i said he hadn t done anything  but it s true that he has nothing to do with this time s expulsion  you re the only one in his eyes now  ayanokouji senpai   although it s a far fetched theory based on only the result  i think it s thanks to you that he has become a bit more well behaved  i guess you could say that he s taking some of the energy focused on the first year students and placing it on the upperclassmen  recently  he keeps saying things like   let me fight the 2nd years  that s just great   there should be a chance to fight with you first years sooner or later   i hope i can spend my school life here without any regrets   you must not leave any regrets in your school life as well  ayanokouji senpai   of course  i ll do my best to leave no regrets   then i ll take my leave  her eyes carry a strong determination  the 1 d third place result  the class c a ranked dropout  his left hand still carries the price of the april fight  her class took third  she apologizes yet speaks to him as his equal  their exchange ends without resolving anything  he keeps staring him down on the way to class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\">Nanase walks with him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.110–116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mid-June morning; he meets Nanase Tsubasa (Class 1-D) walking to school; she stops and falls into step (or deliberately waits — he can&#x27;t tell which).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “I’ve always felt sorry for what I did to you, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “Senpai, do you hate me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I don’t have any reason to hate you. It was for the special exam, right? There’s no way out of it. Besides, I saw how you were trying to protect me, Nanase.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that special exam over? I didn’t hear you mentioning anything about a deadline.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, the exam is still going on. The deadline is the start of the second semester.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because of what happened last time, I’m convinced that even with a plan, it might not work out that easily. Also, after you knew our purpose, it would be very hard to pressure you in your everyday life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then are you waiting for the other years to have their special exams? But what about the rest of you students?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know how, but I think they already know that Housen-kun has already made a move.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And since even someone like Housen failed, people judged that it wouldn’t work out without good preparation? Then it’s worthwhile for me to be so badly injured.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know if that’s worth the cost of your left hand, senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I think the students in my grade, including myself, have become able to deal with all sorts of special situations. Although I don’t know how much the upperclassmen know, us 1st years had taken our 2nd special exam at the end of May.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I haven’t heard from anyone directly, I’ve noticed rumors that there was already someone who was expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, so you do know about it? One boy dropped out of Class C in the first year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How did your Class D place in the results of the exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The previous time, we came in last, and this time, unfortunately, we only made third. But this time, Class A and B battled fiercely, so the point difference created between the classes is very small.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’d be a lie if I said he hadn’t done anything. But it’s true that he has nothing to do with this time’s expulsion. You’re the only one in his eyes now, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although it’s a far-fetched theory based on only the result, I think it’s thanks to you that he has become a bit more well-behaved. I guess you could say that he’s taking some of the energy focused on the first year students and placing it on the upperclassmen. Recently, he keeps saying things like, “Let me fight the 2nd years”. That’s just great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There should be a chance to fight with you first years sooner or later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hope I can spend my school life here without any regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You must not leave any regrets in your school life as well, Ayanokouji-senpai”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, I’ll do my best to leave no regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then I’ll take my leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her eyes carry a strong determination; the 1-D third-place result; the Class C A-ranked dropout; his left hand still carries the price of the April fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Her class took third; she apologizes yet speaks to him as his equal; their exchange ends without resolving anything.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> He keeps staring him down on the way to class.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p92-1\">← Before: Amasawa&#x27;s intrusion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s briefing: the Uninhabited Island Survival exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p110-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei coverage note  passing mentions  over time  kei would be able to slowly remove that wall herself  moving onto the next stage naturally   at least i can get some money for kei   i ve been keeping an eye on karuizawa kei from class 2 d for almost 2 weeks   karuizawa was returning straight to the 2nd year dorm today  a bit unusual","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p110-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.110–346<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Over time, Kei would be able to slowly remove that wall herself, moving onto the next stage naturally.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “at least I can get some money for Kei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’ve been keeping an eye on Karuizawa Kei from Class 2-D for almost 2 weeks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.345<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Karuizawa was returning straight to the 2nd year dorm today, a bit unusual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.346<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p92-1\">← Before: Amasawa in the room with them<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p198-1\">→ After: Kei asks for his help<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p111-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka housen-kazuomi nanase-tsubasa","q":"nanase tsubasa the confession on the way to school she is on her way to school alone on the mid june morning  she falls into step with him or he falls into hers   good morning  ayanokouji senpai   is there something in the sky   looking at the       blue sky  huh   what a beautiful day   yes  we haven t met for about a month and a half   i ve always felt sorry for what i did to you  ayanokouji senpai   senpai  do you hate me   no  the exam is still going on  the deadline is the start of the second semester   are you wondering why i haven t visited you since then   because of what happened last time  i m convinced that even with a plan  it might not work out that easily  also  after you knew our purpose  it would be very hard to pressure you in your everyday life   i don t know how  but i think they already know that housen kun has already made a move   i don t know if that s worth the cost of your left hand  senpai   yes  i think the students in my grade  including myself  have become able to deal with all sorts of special situations  although i don t know how much the upperclassmen know  us 1st years had taken our 2nd special exam at the end of may   ah  so you do know about it  one boy dropped out of class c in the first year   how did your class d place in the results of the exam   the previous time  we came in last  and this time  unfortunately  we only made third  but this time  class a and b battled fiercely  so the point difference created between the classes is very small   it d be a lie if i said he hadn t done anything  but it s true that he has nothing to do with this time s expulsion  you re the only one in his eyes now  ayanokouji senpai   although it s a far fetched theory based on only the result  i think it s thanks to you that he has become a bit more well behaved  i guess you could say that he s taking some of the energy focused on the first year students and placing it on the upperclassmen  recently  he keeps saying things like   let me fight the 2nd years  that s just great   i hope i can spend my school life here without any regrets   you must not leave any regrets in your school life as well  ayanokouji senpai   then i ll take my leave  her 1 d placed 3rd at the end of may exam  class c lost a boy  her apology changes nothing and she knows it  the strong determination is still in her eyes  cold  composed  and not forgiving herself  she carries the plan as her duty  she watches the blue sky the way a sniper watches a road  she apologizes  he absolves  neither moves  his new obsession is the 2nd years  she s disgusted and relieved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p111-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html#sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p111-1\">The confession on the way to school<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.111–116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She is on her way to school alone on the mid-June morning; she falls into step with him or he falls into hers.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “Good morning, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “Is there something in the sky?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “Looking at the …  …  blue sky, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a beautiful day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, we haven’t met for about a month and a half.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve always felt sorry for what I did to you, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Senpai, do you hate me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, the exam is still going on. The deadline is the start of the second semester.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you wondering why I haven’t visited you since then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because of what happened last time, I’m convinced that even with a plan, it might not work out that easily. Also, after you knew our purpose, it would be very hard to pressure you in your everyday life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know how, but I think they already know that Housen-kun has already made a move.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know if that’s worth the cost of your left hand, senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I think the students in my grade, including myself, have become able to deal with all sorts of special situations. Although I don’t know how much the upperclassmen know, us 1st years had taken our 2nd special exam at the end of May.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, so you do know about it? One boy dropped out of Class C in the first year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How did your Class D place in the results of the exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The previous time, we came in last, and this time, unfortunately, we only made third. But this time, Class A and B battled fiercely, so the point difference created between the classes is very small.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’d be a lie if I said he hadn’t done anything. But it’s true that he has nothing to do with this time’s expulsion. You’re the only one in his eyes now, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although it’s a far-fetched theory based on only the result, I think it’s thanks to you that he has become a bit more well-behaved. I guess you could say that he’s taking some of the energy focused on the first year students and placing it on the upperclassmen. Recently, he keeps saying things like, “Let me fight the 2nd years”. That’s just great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hope I can spend my school life here without any regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You must not leave any regrets in your school life as well, Ayanokouji-senpai”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then I’ll take my leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her 1-D placed 3rd at the end-of-May exam; Class C lost a boy; her apology changes nothing and she knows it; the strong determination is still in her eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold, composed, and not forgiving herself; she carries the plan as her duty; she watches the blue sky the way a sniper watches a road.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She apologizes; he absolves; neither moves.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> His new obsession is the 2nd years; she&#x27;s disgusted and relieved.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p68-1\">← Before: Named by Ayanokōji (Ch.2 backreference)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p236-1\">→ After: The alliance terms with Housen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune nishimura-ryuuko hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka chabashira s briefing  the uninhabited island survival exam home room  chabashira works the tablet  the ship appears  the students brace   it seems like everyone is here  that s good   i ve been with you guys for a while now  so i m sure you must ve guessed what this is   it s true that we ll be discussing the topic of the special exam after this  but to maintain the suspense for a bit longer  i ll pick it up later  first  let s talk about summer vacation   now i ll explain to you what ll happen in the summer vacation before it actually starts   from august 4 to august 11  you can enjoy to your heart s content your summer vacation on this luxury cruise for a total of eight days and seven nights  you can watch plays or pamper your taste buds  and there will not be anything like a special exam on the cruise   but in order to fully enjoy this cruise trip  you must successfully complete the next special exam   looks like you re indeed learning   when would the special exam begin   usually  the course of events would be such that the test would start the same day or the next day  but unfortunately  this test is still a ways away  the next special exam will be held during summer vacation   you will have to participate in the  uninhabited island survival  special exam and compete with each other   you all probably recalled the uninhabited island survival exam from last year  but the exam this year is very different from the previous one  it s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before  of course  in turn  the number of class points and private points you can get has increased dramatically   first  i ll start by explaining the schedule in detail  there s no need to take notes now because you can download and check them afterwards on your smartphone or tablet  schedule on the screen  july 19 assemble bus port boarding  july 20 briefing exam start  aug 3 exam end  rankings on the ship  rewards  aug 4 11 cruise  aug 16 closing ceremony   sensei  based on this schedule  won t our summer vacation be very short   unfortunately  there will be no making up for that time  the shortening of the summer vacation is final   however  as compensation  there ll be a week s voyage on the luxury cruise ship  based on how you think about it  this week should be worth more than       the two weeks that you will lose  as i just said  that period of time during the voyage would be free time purely for your enjoyment   okay  now back to the topic at hand  although the uninhabited island survival exam was also held last year  the biggest difference between them can be said to be  scale  the duration of the exam is two weeks  and the area of the uninhabited island used for this exam will be larger than before   also  not just students from the same year  but all the students from all the school years will be competing against each other   the number of people you ll have to fight will also be higher than ever before   wouldn t that  be extremely disadvantageous to the first year students  and advantageous for the third years   i know what you re saying  but i m going to state in advance that no exam can be 100  fair  even just taking you 2nd years as an example  there s almost a year s difference between the students who were born late and early in the same year  but you re still fighting on the same stage  right   if a first year asked for advice  as a senpai  it is the nature of a senior to at least answer it  but how much one says is up to them  it is the same when you ask the third years for advice   although there are more or less some gaps between the school years  everyone s basically fighting under the same stage  therefore  in order to fill in the gaps between the school years  the younger students will receive higher rewards  and their corresponding penalties will be lighter   in order to understand the rules of the uninhabited island survival exam  you must understand the groups   the next special exam  the uninhabited island survival exam  will have a rule which allows a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other  remember this first  if the people you group with are in the same year  you will be allowed to form the group regardless of any class boundaries   which means  the students in the 2nd year  are our allies   in the period from today till friday  july 16 inclusive  approximately four       weeks  you have the right to select up to two second year students of your choice to form a small group of a maximum of 3 people  the small groups form the basis of the big groups  however  although i said you could form the group with whoever you liked  there are still rules that exist  first  as i already said  you can only group up with students from the same grade  you can t form a group with 1st or 3rd years   and then  for the ratio of boys to girls in the next exam  when both boys and girls form a mixed group  the proportion of girls to boys must be at least 2 to 3   what happen   s if you don t form a group  or if you can t form a group   although there will also be students who think that it would be easier with only one person  there would be nothing better than having as many people as possible  apart from the advantages of having more people  special privileges are afforded to groups with more people  therefore  i would not recommend choosing to fight on your own except as a last resort   there s nothing but advantages to forming a group  but there s also a point worthy of attention  that is  once you ve established a group  you can t switch to another group whatever the reason may be   we can t change groups  but we could form a group of up to 6 for the special exam  right  but so far  we can only form small groups of up to three people  what s up with that   yeah  that s the key point  after the special exam starts  the small groups will be allowed to come together  2 groups of 3 people or 3 groups of 2 p   eople or even 6 lone wolves could form one big group  however  the conditions for forming a group still exist  in a big group of more than 4 people  the percentage of girls in the group must be at least 50   in last year s uninhabited island survival exam  there were many students who were worried because they didn t get a chance to show their potential  but this year s exam can be considered to require  all types of abilities  academic ability  physical ability  mental ability  communication ability  in addition to the abilities i just listed  there s a high likelihood that you ll need to use the abilities in which you re good at   although forming a group with students who you are close with is important  it s very likely that the overall ability of the group will directly relate to the results you ll get on the special exam  so i advise everyone to consider the right talents when forming your groups   suppose that during the special exam  hirata is met with some kind of accident and could not continue the exam  of course  if he was participating alone  his group would be disqualified immediately  and will pay the penalties   while hirata will be disqualified and sent back to the ship  the other two members can continue the exam without any issues  and if that group persevered until the very end and got first place  hirata  as one of the group members  would also be considered as ending up in first place   no matter how many    people drop out in the middle of the exam  the group can continue to function without any issues until the last person drops out  to put it simply  the more people there are in a group  the more chances they have to survive  rewards penalties printed  1st 300 cp   1 000 000 pts   1 protection point  2nd 200 cp   500 000  3rd 100 cp   250 000  top 50  50 000  top 70  10 000  top 3 classes take 600 cp from bottom 3 groups  bottom 5 groups expelled  relief 6m pts  1m each for six  mixed class group rewards split per class  6 firsts 75 cp each   if you form a group with the other classes  the reward will be split equally among the classes  wouldn t that rule result in only choosing people from your own class to form the groups   if you decide that there s no benefit in that  then you can just form groups with students of your own class  that is all   these are like items that can affect the uninhabited island survival exam  and everyone will receive one of these  except for one of them  there is no harm to having one of these  you can more or less understand that by reading the instructions   each student will receive one of these eight cards at random  the cards will be distributed tomorrow morning  and until the special exam begins  you can transfer or trade the card you get  so long as it is within your school year  anyone can look up who holds what card in the oaa  you can either sell them to students who want to buy them  or you could collect multiple cards by buying them  but the effects of the same cards do not stack  so there s absolutely no point in getting two identical cards   also  of the three special cards  they will be randomly distributed  and each school year will get only one of each type  therefore  it is possible that one       class might       coincidentally end up with all three of the special cards  that is all   there s plenty of time for you to think slowly about what strategy for grouping to use  she cross examines the rules from the front row  he challenges the fairness gap and the small group rule  she objects to the shortened summer  she runs the briefing like a drill","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\">Chabashira&#x27;s briefing: the Uninhabited Island Survival exam<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.117–137<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Home room; Chabashira works the tablet; the ship appears; the students brace.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nishimura-ryuuko.html\">Nishimura Ryūko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “It seems like everyone is here, that’s good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I’ve been with you guys for a while now, so I’m sure you must’ve guessed what this is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “It’s true that we’ll be discussing the topic of the special exam after this, but to maintain the suspense for a bit longer, I’ll pick it up later. First, let’s talk about summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>46 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now I’ll explain to you what’ll happen in the summer vacation before it actually starts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From August 4 to August 11, you can enjoy to your heart’s content your summer vacation on this luxury cruise for a total of eight days and seven nights. You can watch plays or pamper your taste buds. And there will not be anything like a special exam on the cruise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But in order to fully enjoy this cruise trip, you must successfully complete the next special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you’re indeed learning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When would the special exam begin?”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Usually, the course of events would be such that the test would start the same day or the next day, but unfortunately, this test is still a ways away. The next special exam will be held during summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You will have to participate in the “Uninhabited Island Survival” special exam and compete with each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You all probably recalled the uninhabited island survival exam from last year, but the exam this year is very different from the previous one. It’s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before. Of course, in turn, the number of class points and private points you can get has increased dramatically.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First, I’ll start by explaining the schedule in detail. There’s no need to take notes now because you can download and check them afterwards on your smartphone or tablet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Schedule on the screen: July 19 assemble/bus/port boarding; July 20 briefing/exam start; Aug 3 exam end, rankings on the ship, rewards; Aug 4–11 cruise; Aug 16 closing ceremony.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sensei, based on this schedule, won’t our summer vacation be very short?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, there will be no making up for that time. The shortening of the summer vacation is final.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, as compensation, there’ll be a week’s voyage on the luxury cruise ship. Based on how you think about it, this week should be worth more than …  …  the two weeks that you will lose. As I just said, that period of time during the voyage would be free time purely for your enjoyment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, now back to the topic at hand. Although the uninhabited island survival exam was also held last year, the biggest difference between them can be said to be “scale”. The duration of the exam is two weeks, and the area of the uninhabited island used for this exam will be larger than before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, not just students from the same year, but all the students from all the school years will be competing against each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The number of people you’ll have to fight will also be higher than ever before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wouldn’t that… be extremely disadvantageous to the first-year students, and advantageous for the third years?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know what you’re saying, but I’m going to state in advance that no exam can be 100% fair. Even just taking you 2nd years as an example, there’s almost a year’s difference between the students who were born late and early in the same year, but you’re still fighting on the same stage, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If a first-year asked for advice, as a senpai, it is the nature of a senior to at least answer it, but how much one says is up to them. It is the same when you ask the third years for advice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although there are more or less some gaps between the school years, everyone’s basically fighting under the same stage. Therefore, in order to fill in the gaps between the school years, the younger students will receive higher rewards, and their corresponding penalties will be lighter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In order to understand the rules of the uninhabited island survival exam, you must understand the groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next special exam, the uninhabited island survival exam, will have a rule which allows a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other. Remember this first; if the people you group with are in the same year, you will be allowed to form the group regardless of any class boundaries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Which means… the students in the 2nd year, are our allies…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the period from today till Friday, July 16 inclusive, approximately four …  …  weeks, you have the right to select up to two second-year students of your choice to form a small group of a maximum of 3 people. The small groups form the basis of the big groups. However, although I said you could form the group with whoever you liked, there are still rules that exist. First, as I already said, you can only group up with students from the same grade. You can’t form a group with 1st or 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And then, for the ratio of boys to girls in the next exam, when both boys and girls form a mixed group, the proportion of girls to boys must be at least 2 to 3.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What happen … s if you don’t form a group… or if you can’t form a group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although there will also be students who think that it would be easier with only one person, there would be nothing better than having as many people as possible. Apart from the advantages of having more people, special privileges are afforded to groups with more people. Therefore, I would not recommend choosing to fight on your own except as a last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing but advantages to forming a group, but there’s also a point worthy of attention. That is, once you’ve established a group, you can’t switch to another group whatever the reason may be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can’t change groups, but we could form a group of up to 6 for the special exam, right? But so far, we can only form small groups of up to three people. What’s up with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s the key point. After the special exam starts, the small groups will be allowed to come together. 2 groups of 3 people or 3 groups of 2 p … eople or even 6 lone wolves could form one big group. However, the conditions for forming a group still exist. In a big group of more than 4 people, the percentage of girls in the group must be at least 50%.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In last year’s uninhabited island survival exam, there were many students who were worried because they didn’t get a chance to show their potential. But this year’s exam can be considered to require ‘all types of abilities’. Academic ability, physical ability, mental ability, communication ability. In addition to the abilities I just listed, there’s a high likelihood that you’ll need to use the abilities in which you’re good at.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although forming a group with students who you are close with is important, it’s very likely that the overall ability of the group will directly relate to the results you’ll get on the special exam, so I advise everyone to consider the right talents when forming your groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Suppose that during the special exam, Hirata is met with some kind of accident and could not continue the exam. Of course, if he was participating alone, his group would be disqualified immediately, and will pay the penalties.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While Hirata will be disqualified and sent back to the ship, the other two members can continue the exam without any issues. And if that group persevered until the very end and got first place, Hirata, as one of the group members, would also be considered as ending up in first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter how many …  people drop out in the middle of the exam, the group can continue to function without any issues until the last person drops out. To put it simply, the more people there are in a group, the more chances they have to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Rewards/penalties printed: 1st 300 CP + 1,000,000 pts + 1 protection point; 2nd 200 CP + 500,000; 3rd 100 CP + 250,000; top-50% 50,000; top-70% 10,000; top-3 classes take 600 CP from bottom-3 groups; bottom-5 groups expelled (relief 6M pts, 1M each for six); mixed-class group rewards split per class (6 firsts 75 CP each).<span class=\"pg\">p.130–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you form a group with the other classes, the reward will be split equally among the classes. Wouldn’t that rule result in only choosing people from your own class to form the groups?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you decide that there’s no benefit in that, then you can just form groups with students of your own class. That is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “These are like items that can affect the uninhabited island survival exam, and everyone will receive one of these. Except for one of them, there is no harm to having one of these. You can more or less understand that by reading the instructions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Each student will receive one of these eight cards at random. The cards will be distributed tomorrow morning, and until the special exam begins, you can transfer or trade the card you get, so long as it is within your school year. Anyone can look up who holds what card in the OAA. You can either sell them to students who want to buy them, or you could collect multiple cards by buying them. But the effects of the same cards do not stack, so there’s absolutely no point in getting two identical cards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, of the three special cards, they will be randomly distributed, and each school year will get only one of each type. Therefore, it is possible that one …  …  class might …  …  coincidentally end up with all three of the special cards. That is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s plenty of time for you to think slowly about what strategy for grouping to use.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She cross-examines the rules from the front row.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He challenges the fairness gap and the small-group rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishimura Ryūko<\/b> She objects to the shortened summer.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She runs the briefing like a drill.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\">← Before: Nanase walks with him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p137-1\">→ After: Kouenji&#x27;s retirement plan collapses<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the briefing continues the first class begins differently   she brings up the general exam topic after the attendance ceremony   it seems like everyone is here  that s good   i ve been with you guys for a while now  so i m sure you must ve guessed what this is   it s true that we ll be discussing the topic of the special exam after this  but to maintain the suspense for a bit longer  i ll pick it up later  first  let s talk about summer vacation   now i ll explain to you what ll happen in the summer vacation before it actually starts   from august 4 to august 11  you can enjoy to your heart s content your summer vacation on this luxury cruise for a total of eight days and seven nights  you can watch plays or pamper your taste buds  and there will not be anything like a special exam on the cruise   but in order to fully enjoy this cruise trip  you must successfully complete the next special exam   looks like you re indeed learning   usually  the course of events would be such that the test would start the same day or the next day  but unfortunately  this test is still a ways away  the next special exam will be held during summer vacation   you will have to participate in the  uninhabited island survival  special exam and compete with each other   you all probably recalled the uninhabited island survival exam from last year  but the exam this year is very different from the previous one  it s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before  of course  in turn  the number of class points and private points you can get has increased dramatically   first  i ll start by explaining the schedule in detail  there s no need to take notes now because you can download and check them afterwards on your smartphone or tablet   unfortunately  there will be no making up for that time  the shortening of the summer vacation is final   however  as compensation  there ll be a week s voyage on the luxury cruise ship  based on how you think about it  this week should be worth more than       the two weeks that you will lose  as i just said  that period of time during the voyage would be free time purely for your enjoyment   okay  now back to the topic at hand  although the uninhabited island survival exam was also held last year  the biggest difference between them can be said to be  scale  the duration of the exam is two weeks  and the area of the uninhabited island used for this exam will be larger than before   also  not just students from the same year  but all the students from all the school years will be competing against each other   the number of people you ll have to fight will also be higher than ever before   i know what you re saying  but i m going to state in advance that no exam can be 100  fair  even just taking you 2nd years as an example  there s almost a year s difference between the students who were born late and early in the same year  but you re still fighting on the same stage  right   if a first year asked for advice  as a senpai  it is the nature of a senior to at least answer it  but how much one says is up to them  it is the same when you ask the third years for advice   although there are more or less some gaps between the school years  everyone s basically fighting under the same stage  therefore  in order to fill in the gaps between the school years  the younger students will receive higher rewards  and their corresponding penalties will be lighter   in order to understand the rules of the uninhabited island survival exam  you must understand the groups   the next special exam  the uninhabited island survival exam  will have a rule which allows a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other  remember this first  if the people you group with are in the same year  you will be allowed to form the group regardless of any class boundaries   in the period from today till friday  july 16 inclusive  approximately four       weeks  you have the right to select up to two second year students of your choice to form a small group of a maximum of 3 people  the small groups form the basis of the big groups  however  although i said you could form the group with whoever you liked  there are still rules that exist  first  as i already said  you can only group up with students from the same grade  you can t form a group with 1st or 3rd years   and then  for the ratio of boys to girls in the next exam  when both boys and girls form a mixed group  the proportion of girls to boys must be at least 2 to 3   what happen   s if you don t form a group  or if you can t form a group   although there will also be students who think that it would be easier with only one person  there would be nothing better than having as many people as possible  apart from the advantages of having more people  special privileges are afforded to groups with more people  therefore  i would not recommend choosing to fight on your own except as a last resort   there s nothing but advantages to forming a group  but there s also a point worthy of attention  that is  once you ve established a group  you can t switch to another group whatever the reason may be   yeah  that s the key point  after the special exam starts  the small groups will be allowed to come together  2 groups of 3 people or 3 groups of 2 p   eople or even 6 lone wolves could form one big group  however  the conditions for forming a group still exist  in a big group of more than 4 people  the percentage of girls in the group must be at least 50   although you are allowed to group with anyone freely  it will be extremely difficult to form your ideal big group in the exam  situations  where one wants to form a big group with the maximum of 6 people but isn t able to  could be very common   okay  i also know that asking you guys to form groups as you please might still leave you confused  after all  if you don t know the contents of the exam  you won t be able to target the people you need   i cannot tell you the contents of the next exam  however  let me touch upon what kinds of abilities will be needed   in last year s uninhabited island survival exam  there were many students who were worried because they didn t get a chance to show their potential  but this year s exam can be considered to require  all types of abilities  academic ability  physical ability  mental ability  communication ability  in addition to the abilities i just listed  there s a high likelihood that you ll need to use the abilities in which you re good at   although forming a group with students who you are close with is important  it s very likely that the overall ability of the group will directly relate to the results you ll get on the special exam  so i advise everyone to consider the right talents when forming your groups   suppose that during the special exam  hirata is met with some kind of accident and could not continue the exam  of course  if he was participating alone  his group would be disqualified immediately  and will pay the penalties   while hirata will be disqualified and sent back to the ship  the other two members can continue the exam without any issues  and if that group persevered until the very end and got first place  hirata  as one of the group members  would also be considered as ending up in first place   no matter how many    people drop out in the middle of the exam  the group can continue to function without any issues until the last person drops out  to put it simply  the more people there are in a group  the more chances they have to survive   if you decide that there s no benefit in that  then you can just form groups with students of your own class  that is all   i ve given you all a tedious explanation so far  but there s more to explain apart from that   take a look at this   these are like items that can affect the uninhabited island survival exam  and everyone will receive one of these  except for one of them  there is no harm to having one of these  you can more or less understand that by reading the instructions   each student will receive one of these eight cards at random  the cards will be distributed tomorrow morning  and until the special exam begins  you can transfer or trade the card you get  so long as it is within your school year  anyone can look up who holds what card in the oaa  you can either sell them to students who want to buy them  or you could collect multiple cards by buying them  but the effects of the same cards do not stack  so there s absolutely no point in getting two identical cards   also  of the three special cards  they will be randomly distributed  and each school year will get only one of each type  therefore  it is possible that one       class might       coincidentally end up with all three of the special cards  that is all   there s plenty of time for you to think slowly about what strategy for grouping to use  the rewards structure and the card system as printed  she briefed him on the end  he watched every word","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\">The briefing continues<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.117–137<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The first class begins differently — she brings up the general exam topic after the attendance ceremony.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “It seems like everyone is here, that’s good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I’ve been with you guys for a while now, so I’m sure you must’ve guessed what this is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “It’s true that we’ll be discussing the topic of the special exam after this, but to maintain the suspense for a bit longer, I’ll pick it up later. First, let’s talk about summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now I’ll explain to you what’ll happen in the summer vacation before it actually starts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From August 4 to August 11, you can enjoy to your heart’s content your summer vacation on this luxury cruise for a total of eight days and seven nights. You can watch plays or pamper your taste buds. And there will not be anything like a special exam on the cruise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But in order to fully enjoy this cruise trip, you must successfully complete the next special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you’re indeed learning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Usually, the course of events would be such that the test would start the same day or the next day, but unfortunately, this test is still a ways away. The next special exam will be held during summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You will have to participate in the “Uninhabited Island Survival” special exam and compete with each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You all probably recalled the uninhabited island survival exam from last year, but the exam this year is very different from the previous one. It’s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before. Of course, in turn, the number of class points and private points you can get has increased dramatically.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First, I’ll start by explaining the schedule in detail. There’s no need to take notes now because you can download and check them afterwards on your smartphone or tablet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, there will be no making up for that time. The shortening of the summer vacation is final.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, as compensation, there’ll be a week’s voyage on the luxury cruise ship. Based on how you think about it, this week should be worth more than …  …  the two weeks that you will lose. As I just said, that period of time during the voyage would be free time purely for your enjoyment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, now back to the topic at hand. Although the uninhabited island survival exam was also held last year, the biggest difference between them can be said to be “scale”. The duration of the exam is two weeks, and the area of the uninhabited island used for this exam will be larger than before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, not just students from the same year, but all the students from all the school years will be competing against each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The number of people you’ll have to fight will also be higher than ever before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know what you’re saying, but I’m going to state in advance that no exam can be 100% fair. Even just taking you 2nd years as an example, there’s almost a year’s difference between the students who were born late and early in the same year, but you’re still fighting on the same stage, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If a first-year asked for advice, as a senpai, it is the nature of a senior to at least answer it, but how much one says is up to them. It is the same when you ask the third years for advice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although there are more or less some gaps between the school years, everyone’s basically fighting under the same stage. Therefore, in order to fill in the gaps between the school years, the younger students will receive higher rewards, and their corresponding penalties will be lighter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In order to understand the rules of the uninhabited island survival exam, you must understand the groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next special exam, the uninhabited island survival exam, will have a rule which allows a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other. Remember this first; if the people you group with are in the same year, you will be allowed to form the group regardless of any class boundaries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the period from today till Friday, July 16 inclusive, approximately four …  …  weeks, you have the right to select up to two second-year students of your choice to form a small group of a maximum of 3 people. The small groups form the basis of the big groups. However, although I said you could form the group with whoever you liked, there are still rules that exist. First, as I already said, you can only group up with students from the same grade. You can’t form a group with 1st or 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And then, for the ratio of boys to girls in the next exam, when both boys and girls form a mixed group, the proportion of girls to boys must be at least 2 to 3.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What happen … s if you don’t form a group… or if you can’t form a group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although there will also be students who think that it would be easier with only one person, there would be nothing better than having as many people as possible. Apart from the advantages of having more people, special privileges are afforded to groups with more people. Therefore, I would not recommend choosing to fight on your own except as a last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing but advantages to forming a group, but there’s also a point worthy of attention. That is, once you’ve established a group, you can’t switch to another group whatever the reason may be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s the key point. After the special exam starts, the small groups will be allowed to come together. 2 groups of 3 people or 3 groups of 2 p … eople or even 6 lone wolves could form one big group. However, the conditions for forming a group still exist. In a big group of more than 4 people, the percentage of girls in the group must be at least 50%.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although you are allowed to group with anyone freely, it will be extremely difficult to form your ideal big group in the exam. Situations, where one wants to form a big group with the maximum of 6 people but isn’t able to, could be very common.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, I also know that asking you guys to form groups as you please might still leave you confused. After all, if you don’t know the contents of the exam, you won’t be able to target the people you need.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I cannot tell you the contents of the next exam. However, let me touch upon what kinds of abilities will be needed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In last year’s uninhabited island survival exam, there were many students who were worried because they didn’t get a chance to show their potential. But this year’s exam can be considered to require ‘all types of abilities’. Academic ability, physical ability, mental ability, communication ability. In addition to the abilities I just listed, there’s a high likelihood that you’ll need to use the abilities in which you’re good at.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although forming a group with students who you are close with is important, it’s very likely that the overall ability of the group will directly relate to the results you’ll get on the special exam, so I advise everyone to consider the right talents when forming your groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Suppose that during the special exam, Hirata is met with some kind of accident and could not continue the exam. Of course, if he was participating alone, his group would be disqualified immediately, and will pay the penalties.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While Hirata will be disqualified and sent back to the ship, the other two members can continue the exam without any issues. And if that group persevered until the very end and got first place, Hirata, as one of the group members, would also be considered as ending up in first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter how many …  people drop out in the middle of the exam, the group can continue to function without any issues until the last person drops out. To put it simply, the more people there are in a group, the more chances they have to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you decide that there’s no benefit in that, then you can just form groups with students of your own class. That is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve given you all a tedious explanation so far, but there’s more to explain apart from that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Take a look at this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “These are like items that can affect the uninhabited island survival exam, and everyone will receive one of these. Except for one of them, there is no harm to having one of these. You can more or less understand that by reading the instructions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Each student will receive one of these eight cards at random. The cards will be distributed tomorrow morning, and until the special exam begins, you can transfer or trade the card you get, so long as it is within your school year. Anyone can look up who holds what card in the OAA. You can either sell them to students who want to buy them, or you could collect multiple cards by buying them. But the effects of the same cards do not stack, so there’s absolutely no point in getting two identical cards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, of the three special cards, they will be randomly distributed, and each school year will get only one of each type. Therefore, it is possible that one …  …  class might …  …  coincidentally end up with all three of the special cards. That is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s plenty of time for you to think slowly about what strategy for grouping to use.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The rewards structure and the card system as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She briefed him on the end; he watched every word.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: Chabashira waits<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s last blessing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p119-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the exam  the alliance debate  the quiet phones she asks the timing question from the front row s centre seat   when would the special exam begin  the allies line murmur leaves her mouth on its own   which means  the students in the 2nd year  are our allies  she raises her hand on the mixed groups reward question   if you form a group with the other classes  the reward will be split equally among the classes  wouldn t that rule result in only choosing people from your own class to form the groups  the front row strategy circle thinks aloud   she leads it  yosuke anchors it  after school  nobody calls her  she hooks ayanokoji in the corridor   it seems like everyone s quickly making their move  after all  it s natural to want to bring the outstanding students into one s group   no  i didn t   you knew it already  and you still had to mention it deliberately  you re a nasty guy  so  did anyone contact you  ayanokouji kun  who got a perfect score in math  your cell phone is surprisingly quiet   if you don t use your phone frequently  you ll charge it less often   i ve already    instructed them on what they should do earlier  i summed it up in an easy to understand way and sent it to everyone  but you didn t seem to notice it  since your battery s dead   this is not enforced  because this matter ultimately depends on personal judgement   this time s uninhabited island exam  can you get first place by yourself   i was wondering if    you  who got a perfect score in math  even needed a group   if we come in first place  our class d will gain points for certain  we can let the 1st and 3rd years fight for the 2nd and 3rd place  better than letting the other 2nd years get it   if that is the case  we can form the groups with the core objective of avoiding any dropouts  and forming the groups would be easier    yes  for the students who are a little worried  i would like to collect as many private points as possible  but if the student who lends me points receives the penalty of expulsion  there s no helping it   although a method that would result in no dropouts exists  i don t think anyone would want to do it   it feels like we can only rely on our own strength to survive   that s true  can i consult you again   that s enough  thank you  her instruction text  shown on the tablet   please don t form a group before class d reaches an agreement     nevertheless  if you absolutely want to decide on your group as early as possible  please contact horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p119-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p119-1\">The exam; the alliance debate; the quiet phones<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.119–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She asks the timing question from the front row&#x27;s centre seat. The allies-line murmur leaves her mouth on its own. She raises her hand on the mixed-groups reward question. The front-row strategy circle thinks aloud — she leads it, Yosuke anchors it. After school, nobody calls her; she hooks Ayanokōji in the corridor.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “When would the special exam begin?”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Which means… the students in the 2nd year, are our allies…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “If you form a group with the other classes, the reward will be split equally among the classes. Wouldn’t that rule result in only choosing people from your own class to form the groups?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like everyone’s quickly making their move. After all, it’s natural to want to bring the outstanding students into one’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I didn’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You knew it already, and you still had to mention it deliberately. You’re a nasty guy. So, did anyone contact you? Ayanokouji-kun, who got a perfect score in math? Your cell phone is surprisingly quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t use your phone frequently, you’ll charge it less often.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already …  instructed them on what they should do earlier. I summed it up in an easy to understand way and sent it to everyone. But you didn’t seem to notice it, since your battery’s dead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is not enforced, because this matter ultimately depends on personal judgement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This time’s uninhabited island exam… Can you get first place by yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was wondering if …  you, who got a perfect score in math, even needed a group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we come in first place, our Class D will gain points for certain. We can let the 1st and 3rd years fight for the 2nd and 3rd place. Better than letting the other 2nd years get it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that is the case, we can form the groups with the core objective of avoiding any dropouts, and forming the groups would be easier .”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. For the students who are a little worried, I would like to collect as many private points as possible, but if the student who lends me points receives the penalty of expulsion, there’s no helping it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although a method that would result in no dropouts exists, I don’t think anyone would want to do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It feels like we can only rely on our own strength to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. Can I consult you again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s enough, thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her instruction text, shown on the tablet: “Please don’t form a group before Class D reaches an agreement.” / “Nevertheless, if you absolutely want to decide on your group as early as possible, please contact Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p75-1\">← Before: Horikita joins the student council<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p174-1\">→ After: The Trial card; the Ike plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p120-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko keisei s group situation  keisei  who usually would quietly listen to the instructions of the special exams  murmured as if recalling memories of that    on page  in the classroom  at the exam announcement  not a spoken line  his name is floated as the  left out  scout   the classes want his mind  his own small group is not settled yet on this page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p120-1\">Keisei&#x27;s group situation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.120–179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Keisei, who usually would quietly listen to the instructions of the special exams, murmured as if recalling memories of that.” — on page, in the classroom, at the exam announcement; not a spoken line.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His name is floated as the “left out” scout — the classes want his mind; his own small group is not settled yet on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p59-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p327-1\">→ After: Keisei&#x27;s pre-exam fear<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nishimura-ryuuko-y2v2-p121-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nishimura-ryuuko","q":"nishimura ryuko nishimura objects she fires the shorter summer objection   sensei  based on this schedule  won t our summer vacation be very short","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nishimura-ryuuko-y2v2-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nishimura-ryuuko.html#sc-nishimura-ryuuko-y2v2-p121-1\">Nishimura objects<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.121<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nishimura-ryuuko.html\">Nishimura Ryūko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She fires the shorter-summer objection.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nishimura Ryūko<\/b> “Sensei, based on this schedule, won’t our summer vacation be very short?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p123-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke hirata challenges the exam s premise in the front rows he challenges the gap between the years on day one   wouldn t that  be extremely disadvantageous to the first year students  and advantageous for the third years  he presses the small group big group mechanics next   we can t change groups  but we could form a group of up to 6 for the special exam  right  but so far  we can only form small groups of up to three people  what s up with that  he usually leads the class and did so with the homework question yesterday  the briefing exposed the exam s built in unfairness and he made it visible for everyone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p123-1\">Hirata challenges the exam&#x27;s premise<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.123–126<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the front rows he challenges the gap between the years on day one. He presses the small-group/big-group mechanics next.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Wouldn’t that… be extremely disadvantageous to the first-year students, and advantageous for the third years?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “We can’t change groups, but we could form a group of up to 6 for the special exam, right? But so far, we can only form small groups of up to three people. What’s up with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He usually leads the class and did so with the homework question yesterday; the briefing exposed the exam&#x27;s built-in unfairness and he made it visible for everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p35-1\">← Before: Hirata&#x27;s covering fire<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p142-1\">→ After: The strategy circle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p137-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke chabashira-sae horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kouenji s retirement plan collapses the bell rings  kouenji slips out faster than usual  ayanokoji follows  the corridor corner eavesdrop   i just don t think teacher explained a crucial point   and here i was wondering what you d ask  how boring   you withdrew from the exam last year by taking sick leave  right  unfortunately  that won t work this year  you will be penalized without any special treatment  in other words  you ll have to pay 6 million private points  from what you have on hand  it s impossible   fufu  that s true  i m an avaricious and insatiable person  so this is quite troubling   really  i wonder what i should do  you can leave now  teacher   by the way  who s the one who s hiding and spying on me  and from where   whether you come out or not is up to you   horikita told me to keep an eye out on your actions  we don t know how kouenji will act  she said   hmm   you seem to be good at hiding yourself  but i can t see through your truths and lies  ayanokouji boy  i won t trust the words of someone like that   fufufu  that s true  i have no trust in anyone except myself  rather  it s more like i have no interest in anyone else   that applies to you as well  ayanokouji boy   what are you    going to do in this special exam   yeah  speaking of that  can i join your group   sorry  but i ll have to reject you  i don t have the leisure to accept someone who s guaranteed to quit at the very beginning   fufufu  is that so  there s no helping it then   but is that way of thinking really good  even if you find a group that you can join  you ll end up having to trust others with your fate of getting expelled   that s true  if    i quit without doing anything   what should i do  i ll carefully think about it until it officially starts  his mirror look  his sick leave loophole priced at 6m   he can t afford it  his  join your group  line half expecting the refusal  he tries the loophole  sizes ayanokoji up  and withdraws the idea  she sees through the withdrawal instantly  she set him to watch kouenji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p137-1\">Kouenji&#x27;s retirement plan collapses<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.137–141<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The bell rings; Kouenji slips out faster than usual; Ayanokōji follows; the corridor corner eavesdrop.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I just don’t think Teacher explained a crucial point.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “And here I was wondering what you’d ask. How boring.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “You withdrew from the exam last year by taking sick leave, right? Unfortunately, that won’t work this year. You will be penalized without any special treatment. In other words, you’ll have to pay 6 million private points. From…”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You withdrew from the exam last year by taking sick leave, right? Unfortunately, that won’t work this year. You will be penalized without any special treatment. In other words, you’ll have to pay 6 million private points. From what you have on hand, it’s impossible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufu, that’s true. I’m an avaricious and insatiable person, so this is quite troubling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really, I wonder what I should do? You can leave now, teacher.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, who’s the one who’s hiding and spying on me, and from where?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether you come out or not is up to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita told me to keep an eye out on your actions. We don’t know how Kouenji will act, she said.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be good at hiding yourself. But I can’t see through your truths and lies, Ayanokouji boy. I won’t trust the words of someone like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufufu, that’s true. I have no trust in anyone except myself. Rather, it’s more like I have no interest in anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That applies to you as well, Ayanokouji boy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you …  going to do in this special exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah… Speaking of that, can I join your group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I’ll have to reject you. I don’t have the leisure to accept someone who’s guaranteed to quit at the very beginning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufufu, is that so, there’s no helping it then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But is that way of thinking really good? Even if you find a group that you can join, you’ll end up having to trust others with your fate of getting expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, if …  I quit without doing anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What should I do? I’ll carefully think about it until it officially starts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His mirror-look; his sick-leave loophole priced at 6M — he can&#x27;t afford it; his “join your group” line half-expecting the refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> He tries the loophole, sizes Ayanokōji up, and withdraws the idea.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She sees through the withdrawal instantly.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She set him to watch Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\">← Before: Chabashira&#x27;s briefing: the Uninhabited Island Survival exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p142-1\">→ After: The group problem; Horikita&#x27;s relief plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p137-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke the sick leave loophole  priced in class over  he leaves faster than usual  ayanokoji follows him out  the corridor corner  chabashira and kouenji face off   i just don t think teacher explained a crucial point   fufu  that s true  i m an avaricious and insatiable person  so this is quite troubling   really  i wonder what i should do  you can leave now  teacher  ayanokoji reveals himself  the exchange on the 6 million price tag   by the way  who s the one who s hiding and spying on me  and from where   whether you come out or not is up to you   you seem to be good at hiding yourself  but i can t see through your truths and lies  ayanokouji boy  i won t trust the words of someone like that   fufufu  that s true  i have no trust in anyone except myself  rather  it s more like i have no interest in anyone else   that applies to you as well  ayanokouji boy   yeah  speaking of that  can i join your group   fufufu  is that so  there s no helping it then   that s true  if    i quit without doing anything   what should i do  i ll carefully think about it until it officially starts  his sick leave gambit is priced at 6m private points   a sum he cannot produce  the exam s designers anticipated his exact move  he confesses nothing and hints everything  his silence after the bell rings is a fuse burning in plain sight  he sizes him up and leaves the hook hanging  she burns his excuse in front of him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p137-1\">The sick-leave loophole, priced in<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.137–141<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class over; he leaves faster than usual; Ayanokōji follows him out; the corridor corner; Chabashira and Kouenji face off. Ayanokōji reveals himself; the exchange on the 6-million price tag.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I just don’t think Teacher explained a crucial point.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Fufu, that’s true. I’m an avaricious and insatiable person, so this is quite troubling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Really, I wonder what I should do? You can leave now, teacher.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, who’s the one who’s hiding and spying on me, and from where?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether you come out or not is up to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be good at hiding yourself. But I can’t see through your truths and lies, Ayanokouji boy. I won’t trust the words of someone like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufufu, that’s true. I have no trust in anyone except myself. Rather, it’s more like I have no interest in anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That applies to you as well, Ayanokouji boy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah… Speaking of that, can I join your group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufufu, is that so, there’s no helping it then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, if …  I quit without doing anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What should I do? I’ll carefully think about it until it officially starts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His sick-leave gambit is priced at 6M private points — a sum he cannot produce; the exam&#x27;s designers anticipated his exact move.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He confesses nothing and hints everything; his silence after the bell rings is a fuse burning in plain sight.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He sizes him up and leaves the hook hanging.<span class=\"pg\">p.139–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She burns his excuse in front of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p20-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p330-1\">→ After: The full-freedom deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p142-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the group problem  horikita s relief plan after returning to class  the front row gathering thinks aloud about alliances  the cards are due tomorrow   but  what about the distribution of class points when you win  although i understand the reason behind it  there s no benefit in grouping up with other classes  it just feels like we d be messing around if we do that   but if we rely on only our class  there are some talents that can t be offset  and if it s only our class that forms groups within our own class  what if the other classes join forces  the worst case scenario would be that only class d falls behind as the gap widens   how will sakayanagi  ryuuen  and ichinose act   class a  who is in the leading position  probably wouldn t be troubled by the mixing together of the classes  it doesn t matter which group wins  as long as the gap of points between their class and the other classes does not become narrower  on the contrary  the next three classes that rank below them  including us  would like to narrow that gap   then how about an alliance between the three classes  if the gap is extended by class a  let s first establish an alliance from class b to d  to be able to narrow that gap with class a wouldn t be bad   the enemy of my enemy is my friend  is what you mean  it s not a bad objective to isolate class a  if it is ichinose  she probably will accept this proposal   but if we propose to isolate class a  we have to be prepared for class a s hostility  considering sakayanagi s character  i think that  even with our class d  the bottommost class  she ll still mercilessly use her resources to       deal with us   we still need to quietly get closer to the top classes as much as possible   even if the three classes are to fight together  it s better if it s not us who makes that proposal   it would be of great help if another class raises a similar proposal   just forming a group by itself is quite a headache   actually  most people will probably start to act tomorrow   yeah  gathering effective cards into a group is also a key point  after school  every excellent student s phone rings at once  hers does not  she stops him in the corridor   it seems like everyone s quickly making their move  after all  it s natural to want to bring the outstanding students into one s group   did you not get any messages  horikita   no  i didn t   i see  after all  there are only very few people who know your contact   you knew it already  and you still had to mention it deliberately  you re a nasty guy  so  did anyone contact you  ayanokouji kun  who got a perfect score in math  your cell phone is surprisingly quiet   unfortunately  my battery s dead  i haven t charged it for two or three days   if you don t use your phone frequently  you ll charge it less often   i ve already    instructed them on what they should do earlier  i summed it up in an easy to understand way and sent it to everyone  but you didn t seem to notice it  since your battery s dead  her instruction text  printed on the tablet   please don t form a group before class d reaches an agreement     nevertheless  if you absolutely want to decide on your group as early as possible  please contact horikita   this is not enforced  because this matter ultimately depends on personal judgement   this time s uninhabited island exam  can you get first place by yourself   leave me alone  the only thing we know now is that it s an uninhabited island special exam   i was wondering if    you  who got a perfect score in math  even needed a group   if we come in first place  our class d will gain points for certain  we can let the 1st and 3rd years fight for the 2nd and 3rd place  better than letting the other 2nd years get it   if that is the case  we can form the groups with the core objective of avoiding any dropouts  and forming the groups would be easier    not everyone can afford to pay the private points for relief   yes  for the students who are a little worried  i would like to collect as many private points as possible  but if the student who lends me points receives the penalty of expulsion  there s no helping it   if you don t want that  then you can only ask students with a points surplus   although a method that would result in no dropouts exists  i don t think anyone would want to do it   the plan to withdraw intentionally from the start  her loophole  5 sacrificial groups withdrawing at the start spares the rest   30m pts needed  the school s top 3 bottom 3 point link deters it  he understands both sides   it feels like we can only rely on our own strength to survive   that s true  can i consult you again   if it s within the acceptable range   that s enough  thank you  the council s quiet mobilization begins  she asks him to hold  he proposes the three class alliance  he centers the room s talk  he s worried","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p142-1\">The group problem; Horikita&#x27;s relief plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.142–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After returning to class, the front-row gathering thinks aloud about alliances; the cards are due tomorrow. After school, every excellent student&#x27;s phone rings at once; hers does not; she stops him in the corridor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “But, what about the distribution of class points when you win? Although I understand the reason behind it, there’s no benefit in grouping up with other classes. It just feels like we’d be messing around if we do that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “But if we rely on only our class, there are some talents that can’t be offset. And if it’s only our class that forms groups within our own class… What if the other classes join forces? The worst-case scenario would be that only…”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “How will Sakayanagi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose act?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>39 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if we rely on only our class, there are some talents that can’t be offset. And if it’s only our class that forms groups within our own class… What if the other classes join forces? The worst-case scenario would be that only Class D falls behind as the gap widens.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A, who is in the leading position, probably wouldn’t be troubled by the mixing together of the classes. It doesn’t matter which group wins, as long as the gap of points between their class and the other classes does not become narrower. On the contrary, the next three classes that rank below them, including us, would like to narrow that gap.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then how about an alliance between the three classes? If the gap is extended by Class A, let’s first establish an alliance from Class B to D. To be able to narrow that gap with Class A wouldn’t be bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The enemy of my enemy is my friend, is what you mean. It’s not a bad objective to isolate Class A. If it is Ichinose, she probably will accept this proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if we propose to isolate Class A, we have to be prepared for Class A’s hostility. Considering Sakayanagi’s character, I think that, even with our Class D, the bottommost class, she’ll still mercilessly use her resources to …  …  deal with us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We still need to quietly get closer to the top classes as much as possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if the three classes are to fight together, it’s better if it’s not us who makes that proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would be of great help if another class raises a similar proposal…”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just forming a group by itself is quite a headache.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, most people will probably start to act tomorrow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Gathering effective cards into a group is also a key point.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like everyone’s quickly making their move. After all, it’s natural to want to bring the outstanding students into one’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you not get any messages, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I didn’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. After all, there are only very few people who know your contact.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You knew it already, and you still had to mention it deliberately. You’re a nasty guy. So, did anyone contact you? Ayanokouji-kun, who got a perfect score in math? Your cell phone is surprisingly quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, my battery’s dead. I haven’t charged it for two or three days.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t use your phone frequently, you’ll charge it less often.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already …  instructed them on what they should do earlier. I summed it up in an easy to understand way and sent it to everyone. But you didn’t seem to notice it, since your battery’s dead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her instruction text, printed on the tablet: “Please don’t form a group before Class D reaches an agreement.” / “Nevertheless, if you absolutely want to decide on your group as early as possible, please contact Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is not enforced, because this matter ultimately depends on personal judgement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This time’s uninhabited island exam… Can you get first place by yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Leave me alone. The only thing we know now is that it’s an uninhabited island special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was wondering if …  you, who got a perfect score in math, even needed a group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we come in first place, our Class D will gain points for certain. We can let the 1st and 3rd years fight for the 2nd and 3rd place. Better than letting the other 2nd years get it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that is the case, we can form the groups with the core objective of avoiding any dropouts, and forming the groups would be easier .”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not everyone can afford to pay the private points for relief.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. For the students who are a little worried, I would like to collect as many private points as possible, but if the student who lends me points receives the penalty of expulsion, there’s no helping it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t want that, then you can only ask students with a points surplus.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although a method that would result in no dropouts exists, I don’t think anyone would want to do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The plan to withdraw intentionally from the start?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her loophole: 5 sacrificial groups withdrawing at the start spares the rest — 30M pts needed; the school&#x27;s top-3/bottom-3 point-link deters it; he understands both sides.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It feels like we can only rely on our own strength to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. Can I consult you again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s within the acceptable range.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s enough, thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The council&#x27;s quiet mobilization begins; she asks him to hold.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He proposes the three-class alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He centers the room&#x27;s talk; he&#x27;s worried.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p137-1\">← Before: Kouenji&#x27;s retirement plan collapses<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ishizaki, Albert, Hiyori: the Class B recruitment<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p142-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke the strategy circle after the briefing everyone gathers around horikita s desk  he is explicitly named as the circle s anchor  everyone  along with yosuke  sakayanagi  tended never to let the prey she decided on escape    his own assessment  used as the class s common sense","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p142-1\">The strategy circle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.142–145<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the briefing everyone gathers around Horikita&#x27;s desk; he is explicitly named as the circle&#x27;s anchor (“Everyone, along with Yosuke”).<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi “tended never to let the prey she decided on escape” — his own assessment, used as the class&#x27;s common sense.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p123-1\">← Before: Hirata challenges the exam&#x27;s premise<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p177-1\">→ After: The café watch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p142-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken sudo s alliance idea the strategy circle runs its third pass  sudo floats the three class alliance   but  what about the distribution of class points when you win  although i understand the reason behind it  there s no benefit in grouping up with other classes  it just feels like we d be messing around if we do that   then how about an alliance between the three classes  if the gap is extended by class a  let s first establish an alliance from class b to d  to be able to narrow that gap with class a wouldn t be bad   the particularly important part of this exam  and  but if we rely on only our class  are untagged group talk in the translation  speakers unassigned as printed  he works alongside him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p142-1\">Sudō&#x27;s alliance idea<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.142–144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The strategy circle runs its third pass; Sudō floats the three-class alliance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “But, what about the distribution of class points when you win? Although I understand the reason behind it, there’s no benefit in grouping up with other classes. It just feels like we’d be messing around if we do that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Then how about an alliance between the three classes? If the gap is extended by Class A, let’s first establish an alliance from Class B to D. To be able to narrow that gap with Class A wouldn’t be bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “The particularly important part of this exam...” and “But if we rely on only our class…” are untagged group-talk in the translation; speakers unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He works alongside him.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p66-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p169-1\">→ After: The OAA bench situation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ishizaki  albert  hiyori  the class b recruitment after school  ishizaki intercepts him in the corridor  albert materializes  hiyori joins   yo   i contacted you through your cell phone  but there was no response  so i came straight to you   sorry about that  my phone happened to run out of battery   forget it  it s fine  just do me a favour and give me some time  alright   is that supposed to be a threat   wha  that s an interesting joke  does a guy who can intimidate you really exist in this school   are you busy after this   no  i m just about to go back   really  then there s no problem  come  albert waits like a wall with his right hand out  hiyori takes his arm   let s go   hey    hey   hi  ayanokouji kun   what a rare combination   what are you doing here  let s go   won t let me go back  what are you doing   ok   no problem  in a way  it s also a kind of dissemination   i see  as expected of shiina  great idea  great idea  albert s flag room  the pitch lands  20m to ak to join class b  hiyori dissects it  he pockets the offer   let s cut to the chase  here s my proposal  let s form a group for the next special exam   form a group  can you give me more details   more details  that s all there is to it   with whoever you want  it can be me  albert  shiina  anybody really  the point is that you team up with somebody from our class   in other words  you want me to enter into a group with two people from your class   right  and then when the exam starts  you ll combine your group with another three person group from class b  so it ll be a perfect six person group  with five people from our class  and you being the sixth  ayanakouji  let s aim for first place   hiyori  did you carefully explain the exam rules to ishizaki   no   if i d interrupted and tried to explain  i felt like there would ve been something i needed to correct within 5 seconds  so  i thought it would be better to let him carry on with his momentum   really   if you organize the exam description  that s what it means  basically  depending on the situation  we might have to work with a group we didn t expect or want   during the exam there might just be certain conditions that we need to meet in order to combine our groups  that s what i m talking about   well   course it s just you  i reckon you re just as powerful as ryuuen  nah  if i had to say  it s cuz i now think that you re even better than him        you re strong as hell at fighting  and your mental agility is even acknowledged by him  plus  in the spring exam  you got a perfect score in math  that was truly incredible  the group which has ayanokouji has the exam in the bag  so i see no reason for us not to invite you  eh   that was high praise  ayanokouji kun  but my opinion is also the same   then  the third  this proposal  how does it benefit me  if i assume that the top places are taken by class b  then it s just you guys that benefit   the heck  of course you can t be the only one who doesn t get any benefits  if we re promoted to class a  we ll give you 20 million points to come to our class  ayanokouji  waddya say   in other words  you can get either your class into class a  or our class into class a  this way  you have a 50  chance of graduating from class a   are hiyori and albert of the same opinion   yes  we d love to have you   yes   was it ryuuen who decided to invite me  or is this ishizaki s arbitrary decision   it s my own decision  ryuuen knows nothing about it   never thought    about it  no need to dwell on that  even so  i m ready for that   the rules allow us to form groups with students from within the same year  right  so i thought ayanokouji was absolutely necessary in order to form the best team  what s wrong about that     the key point of this special exam is to prevent the 2nd year students  class points from being taken away by the others  of course  it s also necessary to aim for the top spots in the overall ranking  for which  ayanokouji is indispensable   that s right   anyway  even though there are still many aspects to this plan that i m concerned about  i understand what you mean   then  will you join our group   although i don t think there s anything wrong in inviting me  i can t say yes to it right now   wh why   it s because he has his own class to deal with  right   besides  i think the terms we ve offered him are weak as well   weak  you sayin  20 million points ain t enough   i m not saying anything like that  i think it s certainly an exceptional amount  that is  in terms of quantity  but in effect  the only thing we d really be giving him is the right to transfer over to our class  yes   b but we can t just fork over 20 million and let  im transfer over to sakayanagi s   additionally  ishizaki kun did say that it d be fine so long as ayanokouji kun joins up with somebody from class b  but there s a problem with that as well  surviving on the uninhabited island won t be a one man effort  if you re really aiming for the top spot  you ll be better off with a strong team to back you up   th then anyone would be fine   if it was up to me to choose the small group hmm  ryuuen kun  kaneda kun  and ayanokouji kun  those three  it s fine if kaneda kun is replaced by yamada kun  but ryuuen kun is indispensable   don t be ridiculous  do you think ryuuen kun will ever approve of our plan   i don t think          he will   exactly   kaneda kun is the same  he won t ignore ryuuen kun s orders and participate in a strategy he s unsure of   at this stage  i guess it can t be helped   i don t know if    i can do what you want  let me think about it for now  he confirms they moved on him solo   tsukishiro s shadow covers the exam  he resolves to keep casualties minimal  he recruits him  ayanokoji owes him nothing and takes the meeting seriously  the wall of a man  he carries him  she pilots the room s negotiation  he knows nothing of this  hiyori names him as the alternate member","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\">Ishizaki, Albert, Hiyori: the Class B recruitment<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.152–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After school; Ishizaki intercepts him in the corridor; Albert materializes; Hiyori joins. Albert waits like a wall with his right hand out; Hiyori takes his arm; “let’s go.” Albert&#x27;s flag room; the pitch lands; 20M to AK to join Class B; Hiyori dissects it; he pockets the offer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Yo!”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “I contacted you through your cell phone, but there was no response, so I came straight to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sorry about that, my phone happened to run out of battery.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>65 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Forget it, it’s fine, just do me a favour and give me some time, alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that supposed to be a threat?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wha, that’s an interesting joke. Does a guy who can intimidate you really exist in this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you busy after this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m just about to go back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? Then there’s no problem. Come.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… Hey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hi, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a rare combination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing here, let’s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Won’t let me go back… what are you doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “OK.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problem. In a way, it’s also a kind of dissemination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, as expected of Shiina! Great idea, great idea!”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s cut to the chase, here’s my proposal…. Let’s form a group for the next special exam!”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Form…a group? Can you give me more details?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More details? That’s all there is to it”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With whoever you want. It can be me, Albert, Shiina, anybody really. The point is that you team up with somebody from our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, you want me to enter into a group with two people from your class?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. And then when the exam starts, you’ll combine your group with another three person group from Class B, so it’ll be a perfect six person group. With five people from our class, and you being the sixth, Ayanakouji, let’s aim for first place!”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hiyori, did you carefully explain the exam rules to Ishizaki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I’d interrupted and tried to explain, I felt like there would’ve been something I needed to correct within 5 seconds. So, I thought it would be better to let him carry on with his momentum.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you organize the exam description, that’s what it means. Basically, depending on the situation, we might have to work with a group we didn’t expect or want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “During the exam there might just be certain conditions that we need to meet in order to combine our groups. That’s what I’m talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, ‘course it’s just you. I reckon you’re just as powerful as Ryuuen… Nah, if I had to say, it’s cuz I now think that you’re even better than him …  … . You’re strong as hell at fighting, and your mental agility is even acknowledged by him. Plus, in the spring exam, you got a perfect score in math. That was truly incredible. The group which has Ayanokouji has the exam in the bag. So I see no reason for us not to invite you, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was high praise, Ayanokouji-kun, but my opinion is also the same.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, the third… this proposal, how does it benefit me? If I assume that the top places are taken by Class B, then it’s just you guys that benefit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The heck, of course you can’t be the only one who doesn’t get any benefits! If we’re promoted to Class A, we’ll give you 20 million points to come to our class, Ayanokouji. Waddya say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, you can get either your class into Class A, or our class into Class A. This way, you have a 50% chance of graduating from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are Hiyori and Albert of the same opinion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. We’d love to have you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “YES.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Was it Ryuuen who decided to invite me? Or is this Ishizaki’s arbitrary decision?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s my own decision. Ryuuen knows nothing about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Never thought …  about it! No need to dwell on that! Even so… I’m ready for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The rules allow us to form groups with students from within the same year, right? So I thought Ayanokouji was absolutely necessary in order to form the best team. What’s wrong about that? ”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The key point of this special exam is to prevent the 2nd year students’ class points from being taken away by the others. Of course, it’s also necessary to aim for the top spots in the overall ranking. For which, Ayanokouji is indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, even though there are still many aspects to this plan that I’m concerned about… I understand what you mean.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, will you join our group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I don’t think there’s anything wrong in inviting me, I can’t say yes to it right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s because he has his own class to deal with, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, I think the terms we’ve offered him are weak as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Weak…? You sayin’ 20 million points ain’t enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not saying anything like that. I think it’s certainly an exceptional amount, that is, in terms of quantity. But in effect, the only thing we’d really be giving him is the right to transfer over to our class, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “B-but we can’t just fork over 20 million and let ‘im transfer over to Sakayanagi’s.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Additionally, Ishizaki-kun did say that it’d be fine so long as Ayanokouji-kun joins up with somebody from Class B, but there’s a problem with that as well. Surviving on the uninhabited island won’t be a one-man effort. If you’re really aiming for the top spot, you’ll be better off with a strong team to back you up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Th-then anyone would be fine!”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it was up to me to choose the small group Hmm. Ryuuen-kun, Kaneda-kun, and Ayanokouji-kun, those three. It’s fine if Kaneda-kun is replaced by Yamada-kun, but Ryuuen-kun is indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be ridiculous! Do you think Ryuuen-kun will ever approve of our plan!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  …  …  he will.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly!”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kaneda-kun is the same, he won’t ignore Ryuuen-kun’s orders and participate in a strategy he’s unsure of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At this stage, I guess it can’t be helped.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know if …  I can do what you want, let me think about it for now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He confirms they moved on him solo — Tsukishiro&#x27;s shadow covers the exam; he resolves to keep casualties minimal.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> He recruits him; Ayanokōji owes him nothing and takes the meeting seriously.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> The wall of a man; he carries him.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> She pilots the room&#x27;s negotiation.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He knows nothing of this.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Hiyori names him as the alternate member.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p142-1\">← Before: The group problem; Horikita&#x27;s relief plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p168-1\">→ After: The Trial card; Shinohara and Ike at the elevator<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p152-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamada-albert shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru kaneda-satoru ishizaki-daichi","q":"ishizaki daichi ishizaki s class b recruitment pitch he intercepts ayanokoji in the corridor after school  delivers him to albert and hiyori  together they walk him to albert s room   yo   i contacted you through your cell phone  but there was no response  so i came straight to you   forget it  it s fine  just do me a favour and give me some time  alright   wha  that s an interesting joke  does a guy who can intimidate you really exist in this school   are you busy after this   really  then there s no problem  come  in albert s flag room he pitches the alliance  ayanokoji   him   albert  then merge with another class b 3 man group mid exam  20m points if class b reaches class a   let s cut to the chase  here s my proposal  let s form a group for the next special exam   more details  that s all there is to it   right  and then when the exam starts  you ll combine your group with another three person group from class b  so it ll be a perfect six person group  with five people from our class  and you being the sixth  ayanakouji  let s aim for first place   really   ain t no point in worrying about things i don t understand   well   course it s just you  i reckon you re just as powerful as ryuuen  nah  if i had to say  it s cuz i now think that you re even better than him        you re strong as hell at fighting  and your mental agility is even acknowledged by him  plus  in the spring exam  you got a perfect score in math  that was truly incredible  the group which has ayanokouji has the exam in the bag  so i see no reason for us not to invite you  eh   the heck  of course you can t be the only one who doesn t get any benefits  if we re promoted to class a  we ll give you 20 million points to come to our class  ayanokouji  waddya say   in other words  you can get either your class into class a  or our class into class a  this way  you have a 50  chance of graduating from class a   it s my own decision  ryuuen knows nothing about it   never thought    about it  no need to dwell on that  even so  i m ready for that   the rules allow us to form groups with students from within the same year  right  so i thought ayanokouji was absolutely necessary in order to form the best team  what s wrong about that     the key point of this special exam is to prevent the 2nd year students  class points from being taken away by the others  of course  it s also necessary to aim for the top spots in the overall ranking  for which  ayanokouji is indispensable   then  will you join our group   wh why   don t be ridiculous  do you think ryuuen kun will ever approve of our plan   that s right   kaneda kun is the same  he won t ignore ryuuen kun s orders and participate in a strategy he s unsure of    i get it  well  if that s the case  there s no helping it  hiyori quietly reminds everyone of the merge conditions  the 20m offer stays on the table  he blinks and accepts the postponement gracefully  he recruits him  ayanokoji keeps the meeting open but undecided  his right hand in the plan  she enables and edits the pitch  deliberately excluded from this  named as the alternate sixth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html#sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p152-1\">Ishizaki&#x27;s Class B recruitment pitch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.152–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He intercepts Ayanokōji in the corridor after school; delivers him to Albert and Hiyori; together they walk him to Albert&#x27;s room. In Albert&#x27;s flag room he pitches the alliance: Ayanokōji + him + Albert, then merge with another Class B 3-man group mid-exam; 20M points if Class B reaches Class A.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Yo!”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “I contacted you through your cell phone, but there was no response, so I came straight to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Forget it, it’s fine, just do me a favour and give me some time, alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wha, that’s an interesting joke. Does a guy who can intimidate you really exist in this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you busy after this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? Then there’s no problem. Come.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s cut to the chase, here’s my proposal…. Let’s form a group for the next special exam!”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More details? That’s all there is to it”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. And then when the exam starts, you’ll combine your group with another three person group from Class B, so it’ll be a perfect six person group. With five people from our class, and you being the sixth, Ayanakouji, let’s aim for first place!”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ain’t no point in worrying about things I don’t understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, ‘course it’s just you. I reckon you’re just as powerful as Ryuuen… Nah, if I had to say, it’s cuz I now think that you’re even better than him …  … . You’re strong as hell at fighting, and your mental agility is even acknowledged by him. Plus, in the spring exam, you got a perfect score in math. That was truly incredible. The group which has Ayanokouji has the exam in the bag. So I see no reason for us not to invite you, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The heck, of course you can’t be the only one who doesn’t get any benefits! If we’re promoted to Class A, we’ll give you 20 million points to come to our class, Ayanokouji. Waddya say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, you can get either your class into Class A, or our class into Class A. This way, you have a 50% chance of graduating from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s my own decision. Ryuuen knows nothing about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Never thought …  about it! No need to dwell on that! Even so… I’m ready for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The rules allow us to form groups with students from within the same year, right? So I thought Ayanokouji was absolutely necessary in order to form the best team. What’s wrong about that? ”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The key point of this special exam is to prevent the 2nd year students’ class points from being taken away by the others. Of course, it’s also necessary to aim for the top spots in the overall ranking. For which, Ayanokouji is indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, will you join our group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be ridiculous! Do you think Ryuuen-kun will ever approve of our plan!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kaneda-kun is the same, he won’t ignore Ryuuen-kun’s orders and participate in a strategy he’s unsure of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… I get it. Well, if that’s the case, there’s no helping it…”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hiyori quietly reminds everyone of the merge conditions; the 20M offer stays on the table; he blinks and accepts the postponement gracefully.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He recruits him; Ayanokōji keeps the meeting open but undecided.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> His right hand in the plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> She enables and edits the pitch.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Deliberately excluded from this.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Named as the alternate sixth.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p187-1\">→ After: The Komiya investigation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p152-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert ryuuen-kakeru shiina-hiyori","q":"shiina hiyori hiyori s capture  the recruitment play she appears beside albert and calls out to ayanokoji  nobody knows how long she was waiting   hi  ayanokouji kun   no problem  in a way  it s also a kind of dissemination   we wouldn t mind if your room is a bit messy  right  she edits ishizaki in real time  her calculus is the plan s real brain   no   if i d interrupted and tried to explain  i felt like there would ve been something i needed to correct within 5 seconds  so  i thought it would be better to let him carry on with his momentum   if you organize the exam description  that s what it means  basically  depending on the situation  we might have to work with a group we didn t expect or want   during the exam there might just be certain conditions that we need to meet in order to combine our groups  that s what i m talking about   yes  we d love to have you   it s because he has his own class to deal with  right   besides  i think the terms we ve offered him are weak as well   i m not saying anything like that  i think it s certainly an exceptional amount  that is  in terms of quantity  but in effect  the only thing we d really be giving him is the right to transfer over to our class  yes   additionally  ishizaki kun did say that it d be fine so long as ayanokouji kun joins up with somebody from class b  but there s a problem with that as well  surviving on the uninhabited island won t be a one man effort  if you re really aiming for the top spot  you ll be better off with a strong team to back you up   if it was up to me to choose the small group hmm  ryuuen kun  kaneda kun  and ayanokouji kun  those three  it s fine if kaneda kun is replaced by yamada kun  but ryuuen kun is indispensable   i don t think          he will   kaneda kun is the same  he won t ignore ryuuen kun s orders and participate in a strategy he s unsure of   at this stage  i guess it can t be helped   we were able to convey ours and ishizaki s thoughts to you  so we should be satisfied with that for now  she runs the room s negotiation with minimal words and maximal effect  she sees through the plan s weaknesses before ishizaki does  she wanted to deliver the message  not close the deal  she recruits him on behalf of class b  he is charmed  she loves him and fixes his mistakes  he echoes  yes  after hers  she rules him necessary","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html#sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p152-1\">Hiyori&#x27;s capture: the recruitment play<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.152–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She appears beside Albert and calls out to Ayanokōji; nobody knows how long she was waiting. She edits Ishizaki in real time; her calculus is the plan&#x27;s real brain.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “Hi, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “No problem. In a way, it’s also a kind of dissemination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “We wouldn’t mind if your room is a bit messy, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I’d interrupted and tried to explain, I felt like there would’ve been something I needed to correct within 5 seconds. So, I thought it would be better to let him carry on with his momentum.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you organize the exam description, that’s what it means. Basically, depending on the situation, we might have to work with a group we didn’t expect or want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “During the exam there might just be certain conditions that we need to meet in order to combine our groups. That’s what I’m talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. We’d love to have you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s because he has his own class to deal with, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, I think the terms we’ve offered him are weak as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not saying anything like that. I think it’s certainly an exceptional amount, that is, in terms of quantity. But in effect, the only thing we’d really be giving him is the right to transfer over to our class, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Additionally, Ishizaki-kun did say that it’d be fine so long as Ayanokouji-kun joins up with somebody from Class B, but there’s a problem with that as well. Surviving on the uninhabited island won’t be a one-man effort. If you’re really aiming for the top spot, you’ll be better off with a strong team to back you up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it was up to me to choose the small group Hmm. Ryuuen-kun, Kaneda-kun, and Ayanokouji-kun, those three. It’s fine if Kaneda-kun is replaced by Yamada-kun, but Ryuuen-kun is indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  …  …  he will.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kaneda-kun is the same, he won’t ignore Ryuuen-kun’s orders and participate in a strategy he’s unsure of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At this stage, I guess it can’t be helped.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We were able to convey ours and Ishizaki’s thoughts to you, so we should be satisfied with that for now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She runs the room&#x27;s negotiation with minimal words and maximal effect; she sees through the plan&#x27;s weaknesses before Ishizaki does; she wanted to deliver the message, not close the deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She recruits him on behalf of Class B; he is charmed.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> She loves him and fixes his mistakes.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> He echoes &quot;YES&quot; after hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> She rules him necessary.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p342-1\">→ After: SS: An excuse (Shiina Hiyori POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamada-albert-y2v2-p152-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka shiina-hiyori yamada-albert","q":"yamada albert the wall who carries ayanokoji between the corner and the door  he materializes  his right hand lands on ayanokoji s shoulder   hey   it s okay  yamada kun is very strong   ok  in his room  the plan is laid out over flags  he offers no doubt at all   albert s a flag fanatic  surprised ain tcha   that was high praise  ayanokouji kun  but my opinion is also the same   yes  his japanese is serviceable  he understood everything ishizaki blurted  his room is wallpapered with fabric flags  his classmate  his member  his driver  the partner in crime  she leads the capture","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamada-albert-y2v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamada-albert.html#sc-yamada-albert-y2v2-p152-1\">The wall who carries Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.152–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Between the corner and the door, he materializes; his right hand lands on Ayanokōji&#x27;s shoulder. In his room, the plan is laid out over flags; he offers no doubt at all.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> “Hey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> “It’s okay. Yamada-kun is very strong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> “OK.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Albert’s a flag fanatic. Surprised ain’tcha?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was high praise, Ayanokouji-kun, but my opinion is also the same.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “YES.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His Japanese is serviceable; he understood everything Ishizaki blurted; his room is wallpapered with fabric flags.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His classmate; his member; his driver.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> The partner-in-crime.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> She leads the capture.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p163-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio coverage note  passing mentions  although i had speculated this would be the case  this really was reckless  now  i could understand why ibuki who normally hung around ishizaki wasn t present here   ibuki was also a lone wolf  and nishino seemed to belong to the same category","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p163-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.163, 188<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Although I had speculated this would be the case, this really was reckless. Now, I could understand why Ibuki who normally hung around Ishizaki wasn’t present here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ibuki was also a lone wolf, and Nishino seemed to belong to the same category.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p315-1\">→ After: Ibuki, the lone wolf<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kaneda-satoru-y2v2-p165-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kaneda-satoru","q":"kaneda satoru kaneda mentioned in passing named in ishizaki s invitation scene   he mentions kaneda as a possible group member  passing mention  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kaneda-satoru-y2v2-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kaneda-satoru.html#sc-kaneda-satoru-y2v2-p165-1\">Kaneda mentioned in passing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.165–166<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ishizaki&#x27;s invitation scene — he mentions Kaneda as a possible group member.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amikura-mako-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"amikura-mako","q":"amikura mako named in passing  ch 3  amikura mako   roster twin of asakura mako for the same class c student  the corpus prints  asakura mako  at p 168 as the more people card holder  scenes tracked on asakura mako md  flagged as a duplicate roster row for the owner  do not merge from this side","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amikura-mako-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amikura-mako.html#sc-amikura-mako-y2v2-p168-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amikura-mako.html\">Amikura Mako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Amikura Mako — roster twin of asakura-mako for the same Class C student; the corpus prints “Asakura Mako” at p.168 as the More People card holder; scenes tracked on asakura-mako.md; flagged as a duplicate roster row for the owner, do not merge from this side.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"asakura-mako","q":"asakura mako named in passing  ch 3  asakura mako   class c  named at p 168 as the holder of the more people card  special card  one per year","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/asakura-mako.html#sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p168-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/asakura-mako.html\">Asakura Mako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Asakura Mako — Class C; named at p.168 as the holder of the More People card (special card, one per year).<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p300-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji shinohara-satsuki kushida-kikyou komiya-kyogo horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the trial card  shinohara and ike at the elevator personal email  the  trial  card is his  the other special cards went to class c s asakura mako  more people  and class a s yano koharu  nullify  he leaves earlier than usual  bumps shinohara in the elevator  ike waits in the lobby  follows her outside   hey  shinohara   uh  it s gotta do with that  ya know  the groups for this new uninhabited island exam  have you talked to anyone about grouping up yet   no  not yet  why do you ask   nothing  just askin  is all   oh  really  what about you  you re gonna be with sudo kun and hondo kun either way  right   sorry  it d probably be a blast to be with them   probably  huh   but  well  those guys can get by on their own  ya know  plus  like  ken s pretty strong  so i think they ve got more than enough manpower with just him in the group   i guess   how do i say this  i should be able to help you where you need it  so  if you re feeling troubled  uh  i can form a group with you  yeah   the heck  look at you acting all high and mighty   you saw it last year  right  i m a boy scout  so i d like to think i m pretty useful in an exam like this   well  i guess i can consider it  but  you sure want to be in the same group as me   ah  hey  don t get me wrong  you see  you re one of those people at risk of being expelled right  which is why i m being nice here and offering to make some sacrifices to protect you   huh  sacrifice what  i didn t ask for that   ah  good morning  ike kun  are you free right now   what  what is it  i m super free right now   actually  kobashi san from class c said she wants to invite you to her group  ike kun  she seems to be at school already  could you go discuss it with her   seriously  let s go  let s go  i ll go right now   ah  but just now you seemed to be talking to shinohara san about that  is it alright   no  it s alright  he s been bothering me since he first called out to me  take him   you re the one who s    been bothering me  outside  shinohara stops and stands alone  he passes her  komiya finds her there  red eyes   satsuki   ah  komiya kun  good morning   what s wrong  are you crying   eh  w why do you ask   well  because your eyes are red   ah  you got me  huh  something got in my eyes just now  oww   by the way  i heard from sudo kun that you re gonna be a regular on the basketball team   yeah  it s been a long time coming   yeah you always practice until late at night  so i d be lying if i said you       didn t deserve it  horikita needles him about the trial card in class  ike erupts at shinohara s komiya announcement   you re having a string of bad luck  huh  drawing the trial card and all  i m sure you re drawing attention again   i  too  was distressed by the same thing this morning   it would ve been nice if we could trade cards freely within the class  no student who isn t confident of winning would want the trial card  and yet we cannot just give it to a student who is confident of winning   that being the case  you have no choice but to be in the top 30  and maybe even get a podium finish  isn t it   if you really want to rely on me  i ll certainly lend a hand   i m sorry  but if i find someone who wanted to buy it off me  i might just let him have it   what you decide to do is up to you  although  it would be nice if you could easily find a buyer  the trial card affects not just the person holding the card but their entire group  it s a dangerous risk to take   for the record  i m being sarcastic   this is payback for all the times you ve teased me so far   i don t remember teasing you  though   since it s you  can i take it as you can handle yourself   well  i ll try my best   huh  you  er  found someone to group up with   yeah  anything wrong with that   forbidden what  i haven t officially confirmed yet  well  i m going to confirm today though   and what are you talking about  saying that you invited me  who s the one who got all horny and ignored me   ah  that wasn t like that  i even turned them down for you  you know   turned someone down  ah  you re really pissing me off  you really are a horrible person   group  who did you decide to group up with   what s it got to do with you   nothing  but    i m just curious  okay   class b s komiya san  he invited me just after the special exam started yesterday   ah  komiya  komiya  he s that flashy guy on the basketball team  right  unbelievable   he isn t flashy  and i promised to meet up at the cafe after school to discuss it  shinohara watches ichinose  no ike watches shinohara leave  the group he can still save is slipping  he fumbles the confession  shinohara slips away to komiya  she chose komiya over him  she said  take him  to kushida  she redirects him to kobashi s offer  he s noticed her crying  he waits for her  her needling is entirely deliberate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p168-1\">The Trial card; Shinohara and Ike at the elevator<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168–177<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Personal email: the “Trial” card is his; the other special cards went to Class C&#x27;s Asakura Mako (More People) and Class A&#x27;s Yano Koharu (Nullify). He leaves earlier than usual; bumps Shinohara in the elevator; Ike waits in the lobby; follows her outside. Outside, Shinohara stops and stands alone; he passes her; Komiya finds her there (red eyes). Horikita needles him about the Trial card in class; Ike erupts at Shinohara&#x27;s Komiya announcement.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hey, Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Uh, it’s gotta do with that. Ya know, the groups for this new uninhabited island exam… Have you talked to anyone about grouping up yet?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “No, not yet… Why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>58 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing. Just askin’ is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, really? What about you? You’re gonna be with Sudo-kun and Hondo-kun either way, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. It’d probably be a blast to be with them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Probably, huh~.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, well, those guys can get by on their own, ya know… plus, like, Ken’s pretty strong, so I think they’ve got more than enough manpower with just him in the group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How do I say this. I should be able to help you where you need it… So, if you’re feeling troubled… uh, I can form a group with you, yeah?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The heck? Look at you acting all high and mighty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You saw it last year, right? I’m a boy scout, so I’d like to think I’m pretty useful in an exam like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I guess I can consider it, but… You sure want to be in the same group as me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, hey, don’t get me wrong. You see, you’re one of those people at risk of being expelled right? Which is why I’m being nice here and offering to make some sacrifices to protect you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh!? Sacrifice what? I didn’t ask for that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, good morning, Ike-kun, are you free right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, what is it!? I’m super free right now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, Kobashi-san from Class C said she wants to invite you to her group, Ike-kun. She seems to be at school already. Could you go discuss it with her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seriously? Let’s go, let’s go! I’ll go right now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, but just now you seemed to be talking to Shinohara-san about that… Is it alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, it’s alright, he’s been bothering me since he first called out to me. Take him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the one who’s …  been bothering me!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Satsuki.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, Komiya-kun… Good morning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s wrong? Are you crying?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? W-why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, because your eyes are red.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, you got me, huh? Something got in my eyes just now… Oww.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, I heard from Sudo-kun that you’re gonna be a regular on the basketball team?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, it’s been a long time coming.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah you always practice until late at night, so I’d be lying if I said you …  …  didn’t deserve it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re having a string of bad luck, huh, drawing the Trial card and all. I’m sure you’re drawing attention again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I, too, was distressed by the same thing this morning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would’ve been nice if we could trade cards freely within the class. No student who isn’t confident of winning would want the Trial card, and yet we cannot just give it to a student who is confident of winning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That being the case, you have no choice but to be in the top 30%, and maybe even get a podium finish, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you really want to rely on me, I’ll certainly lend a hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but if I find someone who wanted to buy it off me, I might just let him have it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What you decide to do is up to you. Although, it would be nice if you could easily find a buyer. The Trial card affects not just the person holding the card but their entire group. It’s a dangerous risk to take.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the record, I’m being sarcastic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is payback for all the times you’ve teased me so far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember teasing you, though…”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since it’s you, can I take it as you can handle yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’ll try my best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? You, er… found someone to group up with?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, anything wrong with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Forbidden what, I haven’t officially confirmed yet. Well, I’m going to confirm today though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And what are you talking about, saying that you invited me. Who’s the one who got all horny and ignored me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, that wasn’t like that! I even turned them down for you, you know!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Turned someone down? Ah, you’re really pissing me off. You really are a horrible person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Group… Who did you decide to group up with?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s it got to do with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing, but …  I’m just curious, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class B’s Komiya-san. He invited me just after the special exam started yesterday.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah? Komiya? Komiya, he’s that flashy guy on the basketball team, right? Unbelievable!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He isn’t flashy, and I promised to meet up at the cafe after school to discuss it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Shinohara watches Ichinose... no—Ike watches Shinohara leave; the group he can still save is slipping.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He fumbles the confession; Shinohara slips away to Komiya.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She chose Komiya over him; she said “take him” to Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She redirects him to Kobashi&#x27;s offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> He&#x27;s noticed her crying; he waits for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her needling is entirely deliberate.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ishizaki, Albert, Hiyori: the Class B recruitment<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p177-1\">→ After: The café watch, Matsushita; the Ike counter-plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hondou-ryoutaro","q":"hondo ryotaro named in passing  ch 3  hondo ryotaro   named at p 144 as a chabashira example member  hirata  sudo  and hondou  not present","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html#sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p168-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Hondō Ryōtarō — named at p.144 as a Chabashira example member (Hirata, Sudo, and Hondou); not present.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y2v2-p54-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"shinohara","q":"shinohara coverage note  passing mentions  legacy duplicate  scene lines are on shinohara satsuki md  roster carries both  shinohara  and  shinohara satsuki  do not merge from this side   good morning    the elevator greeting scene with ayanokoji   no  it s alright  he s been bothering me since he first called out to me  take him   satsuki    komiya  tells ayanokoji what happened in the cafe confrontation   late night practice explained   printed across the page turn  kept as printed   huh  sacrifice what  i didn t ask for that   forbidden what  i haven t officially confirmed yet  well  i m going to confirm today though   i spotted shinohara and komiya  who were talking and laughing in the cafe   it seems like one of them invited the other to form a group  are they dating  the print reports on komiya liking shinohara san although they re not dating   printed across the page turn  kept as printed   the more strained their relationship became  the more chance ike would go off in a strange direction   that komiya guy  he s planning to confess to shinohara on the uninhabited island   i expressed my concerns to horikita about the current situation between ike  shinohara  and komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam   unfortunately  it seems like we re too late   today s conversation focused on the groupings for the exam  starting with the fight between ike and shinohara","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Coverage note: passing mentions (legacy duplicate)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168–198<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara\">Shinohara<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Scene lines are on shinohara-satsuki.md (roster carries both `shinohara` and `shinohara-satsuki`; do not merge from this side).<span class=\"pg\">p.168–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Good morning.” — the elevator greeting scene with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “No, it’s alright, he’s been bothering me since he first called out to me. Take him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Satsuki.” — Komiya.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Tells Ayanōkoji what happened in the cafe confrontation — late-night practice explained — printed across the page turn; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Huh!? Sacrifice what? I didn’t ask for that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Forbidden what, I haven’t officially confirmed yet. Well, I’m going to confirm today though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I spotted Shinohara and Komiya, who were talking and laughing in the cafe.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It seems like one of them invited the other to form a group, are they dating?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> The print reports on Komiya liking Shinohara-san although they’re not dating — printed across the page turn; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The more strained their relationship became, the more chance Ike would go off in a strange direction.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That Komiya guy, he’s planning to confess to Shinohara on the uninhabited island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I expressed my concerns to Horikita about the current situation between Ike, Shinohara, and Komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Unfortunately, it seems like we’re too late.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Today’s conversation focused on the groupings for the exam, starting with the fight between Ike and Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-y2v2-p15-1\">← Before: Shinohara in the uproar<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji komiya-kyogo kushida-kikyou shinohara-satsuki","q":"shinohara satsuki the komiya turn he hails her in the lobby  she dodges gently  she lets him walk with her   no  not yet  why do you ask   oh  really  what about you  you re gonna be with sudo kun and hondo kun either way  right   probably  huh   i guess   the heck  look at you acting all high and mighty   well  i guess i can consider it  but  you sure want to be in the same group as me   huh  sacrifice what  i didn t ask for that  kushida s invitation pulls ike away mid sentence  she watches him leave  he doesn t turn around   no  it s alright  he s been bothering me since he first called out to me  take him  she stops on the steps  komiya finds her there  her eyes are red   ah  komiya kun  good morning   eh  w why do you ask   ah  you got me  huh  something got in my eyes just now  oww   yeah  it s been a long time coming  back in class she announces she s grouped with komiya  leaves early for the cafe  ike deflates behind her   yeah  anything wrong with that   forbidden what  i haven t officially confirmed yet  well  i m going to confirm today though   and what are you talking about  saying that you invited me  who s the one who got all horny and ignored me   turned someone down  ah  you re really pissing me off  you really are a horrible person   what s it got to do with you   class b s komiya san  he invited me just after the special exam started yesterday   he isn t flashy  and i promised to meet up at the cafe after school to discuss it  she did not cry over ike  something else reddened her eyes  she chooses komiya s orbit   he notices  then confesses he likes her  she does not return his feelings  she tolerates him politely  he sees her red eyes  he intends to walk the island with her  she hands ike to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p168-1\">The Komiya turn<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168–177<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He hails her in the lobby; she dodges gently; she lets him walk with her. Kushida&#x27;s invitation pulls Ike away mid-sentence; she watches him leave; he doesn&#x27;t turn around. She stops on the steps; Komiya finds her there; her eyes are red. Back in class she announces she&#x27;s grouped with Komiya; leaves early for the café; Ike deflates behind her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “No, not yet… Why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Oh, really? What about you? You’re gonna be with Sudo-kun and Hondo-kun either way, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Probably, huh~.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The heck? Look at you acting all high and mighty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I guess I can consider it, but… You sure want to be in the same group as me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh!? Sacrifice what? I didn’t ask for that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, it’s alright, he’s been bothering me since he first called out to me. Take him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, Komiya-kun… Good morning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? W-why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, you got me, huh? Something got in my eyes just now… Oww.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, it’s been a long time coming.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, anything wrong with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Forbidden what, I haven’t officially confirmed yet. Well, I’m going to confirm today though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And what are you talking about, saying that you invited me. Who’s the one who got all horny and ignored me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Turned someone down? Ah, you’re really pissing me off. You really are a horrible person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s it got to do with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class B’s Komiya-san. He invited me just after the special exam started yesterday.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He isn’t flashy, and I promised to meet up at the cafe after school to discuss it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She did not cry over Ike; something else reddened her eyes; she chooses Komiya&#x27;s orbit — he notices, then confesses he likes her.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> She does not return his feelings; she tolerates him politely.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> He sees her red eyes; he intends to walk the island with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She hands Ike to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p15-1\">← Before: Shinohara in the uproar<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p185-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yano-koharu-y2v2-p168-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"yano-koharu","q":"yano koharu named in passing  ch 3  yano koharu   class a  named at p 168 as the holder of the nullify card  special card  one per year","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yano-koharu-y2v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yano-koharu.html#sc-yano-koharu-y2v2-p168-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yano-koharu.html\">Yano Koharu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Yano Koharu — Class A; named at p.168 as the holder of the Nullify card (special card, one per year).<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p169-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke komiya-kyogo ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji the boy scout confession attempt ayanokoji passes the elevator  ike waits in the lobby and follows shinohara outside   hey  shinohara   uh  it s gotta do with that  ya know  the groups for this new uninhabited island exam  have you talked to anyone about grouping up yet   nothing  just askin  is all   sorry  it d probably be a blast to be with them   but  well  those guys can get by on their own  ya know  plus  like  ken s pretty strong  so i think they ve got more than enough manpower with just him in the group   how do i say this  i should be able to help you where you need it  so  if you re feeling troubled  uh  i can form a group with you  yeah   you saw it last year  right  i m a boy scout  so i d like to think i m pretty useful in an exam like this   ah  hey  don t get me wrong  you see  you re one of those people at risk of being expelled right  which is why i m being nice here and offering to make some sacrifices to protect you  kushida taps his shoulder mid sentence  he s gone before shinohara can answer   what  what is it  i m super free right now   seriously  let s go  let s go  i ll go right now   you re the one who s    been bothering me  back in class he erupts  then trails shinohara out and follows komiya s lead to the cafe  he sulks at a distance   huh  you  er  found someone to group up with   ah  that wasn t like that  i even turned them down for you  you know   group  who did you decide to group up with   nothing  but    i m just curious  okay   ah  komiya  komiya  he s that flashy guy on the basketball team  right  unbelievable  shinohara simply watches from beside him as he runs off with kushida   not speech  he slumps outside the cafe as komiya and shinohara laugh inside  hirata worries about what will happen if he watches that scene in his state  yousuke proposes checking on him  the girl he can t get to look at him  she redirects him to kobashi s invite  he comes to check on him  his rival  in the cafe  alive and talking","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p169-1\">The boy-scout confession attempt<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.169–177<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji passes the elevator; Ike waits in the lobby and follows Shinohara outside. Kushida taps his shoulder mid-sentence; he&#x27;s gone before Shinohara can answer. Back in class he erupts; then trails Shinohara out and follows Komiya&#x27;s lead to the café; he sulks at a distance. He slumps outside the café as Komiya and Shinohara laugh inside.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Hey, Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Uh, it’s gotta do with that. Ya know, the groups for this new uninhabited island exam… Have you talked to anyone about grouping up yet?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Nothing. Just askin’ is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. It’d probably be a blast to be with them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, well, those guys can get by on their own, ya know… plus, like, Ken’s pretty strong, so I think they’ve got more than enough manpower with just him in the group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How do I say this. I should be able to help you where you need it… So, if you’re feeling troubled… uh, I can form a group with you, yeah?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You saw it last year, right? I’m a boy scout, so I’d like to think I’m pretty useful in an exam like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, hey, don’t get me wrong. You see, you’re one of those people at risk of being expelled right? Which is why I’m being nice here and offering to make some sacrifices to protect you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, what is it!? I’m super free right now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seriously? Let’s go, let’s go! I’ll go right now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the one who’s …  been bothering me!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? You, er… found someone to group up with?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, that wasn’t like that! I even turned them down for you, you know!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Group… Who did you decide to group up with?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing, but …  I’m just curious, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah? Komiya? Komiya, he’s that flashy guy on the basketball team, right? Unbelievable!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Shinohara simply watches from beside him as he runs off with Kushida — not speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata worries about what will happen if he watches that scene in his state; Yousuke proposes checking on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> The girl he can&#x27;t get to look at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She redirects him to Kobashi&#x27;s invite.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He comes to check on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> His rival, in the café, alive and talking.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y2v2-p54-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p169-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken the oaa bench situation ike s shinohara pitch references him and hondo as the  natural  group  shinohara lets it bounce off  his name is the reason his corner of the class forms its own gravity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p169-1\">The OAA bench situation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.169–170<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike&#x27;s Shinohara-pitch references him and Hondō as the &quot;natural&quot; group; Shinohara lets it bounce off.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His name is the reason his corner of the class forms its own gravity.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y2v2-p142-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s alliance idea<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kobashi-yume-y2v2-p171-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kobashi-yume","q":"kobashi yume kobashi invites ike to a class c group kushida relays kobashi s invitation for ike to join a class c group  proactive in recruiting group members","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kobashi-yume-y2v2-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kobashi-yume.html#sc-kobashi-yume-y2v2-p171-1\">Kobashi invites Ike to a Class C group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.171<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kobashi-yume.html\">Kobashi Yume<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida relays Kobashi&#x27;s invitation for Ike to join a Class C group.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Proactive in recruiting group members.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p171-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji shinohara-satsuki kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo kushida redirects ike she runs up behind ike and taps him at the height of his shinohara pitch   ah  good morning  ike kun  are you free right now   actually  kobashi san from class c said she wants to invite you to her group  ike kun  she seems to be at school already  could you go discuss it with her   ah  but just now you seemed to be talking to shinohara san about that  is it alright  she clocks the shinohara interaction and quietly offers him an out   he takes it  she handles him like a crisis manager  she confirms ike s rescue with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p171-1\">Kushida redirects Ike<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.171<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She runs up behind Ike and taps him at the height of his Shinohara pitch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ah, good morning, Ike-kun, are you free right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Actually, Kobashi-san from Class C said she wants to invite you to her group, Ike-kun. She seems to be at school already. Could you go discuss it with her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ah, but just now you seemed to be talking to Shinohara-san about that… Is it alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She clocks the Shinohara interaction and quietly offers him an out — he takes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> She handles him like a crisis manager.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She confirms Ike&#x27;s rescue with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p66-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p243-1\">→ After: The 1st-year meeting set-up; the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p172-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki ike-kanji ishizaki-daichi komiya-kyogo","q":"komiya kyogo komiya finds her on the steps he spots her stopped on the steps with red eyes  walks with her at her pace  she opens up a crack   satsuki   what s wrong  are you crying   well  because your eyes are red   by the way  i heard from sudo kun that you re gonna be a regular on the basketball team   yeah you always practice until late at night  so i d be lying if i said you       didn t deserve it  he keeps her company at the cafe  ike can t watch  he invited her the day after the rules dropped  the group is him  her and kinoshita minori of class b  he told ishizaki he ll confess on the island  he is the one who gets the seat beside her  his silent defeat is witnessed  he unknowingly briefs him via the pact question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html#sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p172-1\">Komiya finds her on the steps<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.172–177<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He spots her stopped on the steps with red eyes; walks with her at her pace; she opens up a crack. He keeps her company at the café; Ike can&#x27;t watch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “Satsuki.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “What’s wrong? Are you crying?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “Well, because your eyes are red.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, I heard from Sudo-kun that you’re gonna be a regular on the basketball team?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah you always practice until late at night, so I’d be lying if I said you …  …  didn’t deserve it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He invited her the day after the rules dropped; the group is him, her and Kinoshita Minori of Class B; he told Ishizaki he&#x27;ll confess on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> He is the one who gets the seat beside her.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> His silent defeat is witnessed.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> He unknowingly briefs him via the pact question.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p194-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p174-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the trial card  the ike plan she intercepts him in class about the trial card  then the ike flare   you re having a string of bad luck  huh  drawing the trial card and all  i m sure you re drawing attention again   it would ve been nice if we could trade cards freely within the class  no student who isn t confident of winning would want the trial card  and yet we cannot just give it to a student who is confident of winning   that being the case  you have no choice but to be in the top 30  and maybe even get a podium finish  isn t it   if you really want to rely on me  i ll certainly lend a hand   what you decide to do is up to you  although  it would be nice if you could easily find a buyer  the trial card affects not just the person holding the card but their entire group  it s a dangerous risk to take   for the record  i m being sarcastic   i don t remember teasing you  though  she meets him at the cafeteria  the ike plan  too late   shinohara komiya kinoshita is already grouped on the oaa   isn t it fine to just leave them alone   i thought we had a serious problem on our hands  since you re the one coming to consult me  but this isn t our problem to fix  besides  i ve evaluated ike kun s ability as a boy scout to be high  so we should group him with regards to his ability  not his feelings   so he could be expelled due to his feelings for shinohara leading him by the nose    that would be    problematic  this is so stupid   so you re saying it s necessary to prevent that  but if we stop them from forming a group  won t komiya kun just change the timing of his confession  depending on the situation  he might just confess on that same day   this is a lot more complicated than it sounds  we can t take care of them until they start dating   why don t we just make ike kun confess  if shinohara san accepts  ike kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he s in  right  on the other hand  if he gets rejected  he can forget about this whole matter and focus on the exam   although you re good at many things  you don t seem to be good at       romance at all   i m studying hard right now   unfortunately  it seems like we re too late   since we ve already reached this point  we must take measures to prevent ike kun s loss of motivation  the plan aimed at him is stillborn   the oaa betrayed them  he is the trial card holder everyone can see  she leans on his calm in the strategy circle","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p174-1\">The Trial card; the Ike plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.174–197<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She intercepts him in class about the Trial card; then the Ike flare. She meets him at the cafeteria; the Ike plan; too late — Shinohara-Komiya-Kinoshita is already grouped on the OAA.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re having a string of bad luck, huh, drawing the Trial card and all. I’m sure you’re drawing attention again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It would’ve been nice if we could trade cards freely within the class. No student who isn’t confident of winning would want the Trial card, and yet we cannot just give it to a student who is confident of winning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That being the case, you have no choice but to be in the top 30%, and maybe even get a podium finish, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you really want to rely on me, I’ll certainly lend a hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What you decide to do is up to you. Although, it would be nice if you could easily find a buyer. The Trial card affects not just the person holding the card but their entire group. It’s a dangerous risk to take.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the record, I’m being sarcastic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember teasing you, though…”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it fine to just leave them alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought we had a serious problem on our hands, since you’re the one coming to consult me… but this isn’t our problem to fix. Besides, I’ve evaluated Ike-kun’s ability as a boy scout to be high, so we should group him with regards to his ability, not his feelings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So he could be expelled due to his feelings for Shinohara leading him by the nose?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… That would be …  problematic. This is so stupid.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re saying it’s necessary to prevent that? But if we stop them from forming a group, won’t Komiya-kun just change the timing of his confession? Depending on the situation, he might just confess on that same day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a lot more complicated than it sounds. We can’t take care of them until they start dating.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why don’t we just make Ike-kun confess? If Shinohara-san accepts, Ike-kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he’s in, right? On the other hand, if he gets rejected, he can forget about this whole matter and focus on the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although you’re good at many things, you don’t seem to be good at …  …  romance at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m studying hard right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, it seems like we’re too late.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’ve already reached this point, we must take measures to prevent Ike-kun’s loss of motivation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The plan aimed at him is stillborn — the OAA betrayed them.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He is the Trial card-holder everyone can see.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> She leans on his calm in the strategy circle.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p119-1\">← Before: The exam; the alliance debate; the quiet phones<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p255-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p177-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke matsushita-chiaki nishino-takeko ishizaki-daichi horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ike-kanji shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe watch  matsushita  the ike counter plan ike stalks shinohara  yousuke intercepts  they agree to stake out the cafe   about ike  i don t think it s too good to leave him alone like this   yes  seeing that  i m also worried about what will happen if he watches the discussion between shinohara and komiya while he s like that   i d like to go see what s going on  if you re okay with it  can you come along  i don t think ike kun likes me very much   yeah  shall we go and see what s going on  just in case   it seems like we can only form groups that leave us with no regrets   for me  i d like to select 2 people from class d to form a group  instead of aiming for the top places  i d rather fight to not get penalized   is sakura san alright   miyake kun has good motor skills  so i feel the group is well balanced  matsushita chiaki follows at a distance  corners him when yosuke peels off to the cafe   you don t seem very surprised  did you notice from the start   i just don t show any surprise in my expression   is that any of your business  matsushita   it s not so much about me  as it s about us  ayanokouji kun  you re an important existence for us to get into class a   don t be so cautious  i approached you because i just had something to tell you today as soon as possible   the trial card is an item with a very powerful effect  but it s difficult to use it  if you ve got any problems  i would like to help you  ayanokouji kun  how about it   of course  during the exam  i ll completely follow your instructions   although i m happy that you re willing to assist me  if we don t make it to the top 30  you ll be penalized  you know the risks  right   i do  that s why i think it s important for me to cooperate with you to help you   so i ve been exposed   i don t think    it d be difficult to stay in the top ranks if it were you  even if we don t end up on the podium  we re bound to reach the top 30  it would be more dangerous if i put my friends first and make a half assed group with them   i thought you d get snapped up quickly  ayanokouji kun   i won t decide on my group  at least for this month   you mean that you want to wait and watch how things go   after all  i d like to see how the other classes move   it seems like i won t get a satisfactory answer now  i see  give it some thought   ah  right  here s my contact information  they spot shinohara and komiya laughing in the cafe  ike depressed behind them   i ll think about who would be the best person for ike to group up with if he can t group with shinohara   i don t think    it ll be as bad as it can be  but   anyway  i wanted to ask about komiya first  why did komiya invite shinohara to his group  if we re not sure about that  we can t take any action  he calls ishizaki  nishino corners them  the komiya investigation  komiya plans to confess on the island   what  you said you  something  did you mean a meeting with ayanokouji kun   you re rather close with ishizaki  that s a surprise   hey  you didn t listen to me at all  this is why you re ostracized   ostracized          i m hardly troubled by that   but i m curious as to why you and ayanokouji kun are secretly meeting  ishizaki   our relationship became better after being in the same group in last year s mixed training camp   i contacted ishizaki because i wanted to ask him a few questions about komiya from your class  i decided to meet here because this conversation isn t meant for others to hear   because of komiya kun  what s going on   because even in the kindest of terms  shinohara isn t the kind of person who would be very active in this uninhabited island exam  so our class is worried about whether her grouping up with komiya is a good idea or not  we want to know what kind of person he is beforehand   he s just a nice guy in general  right  he also has good motor skills  and because he s in the basketball club  he has good physical strength as well   it seems like one of them invited the other to form a group  are they dating   eh  th that s hard to say   even if you ask ishizaki these things  he wouldn t understand  you don t know anything about love  do you   at least more than you  although they re not dating  komiya kun certainly       likes shinohara san  right   eh  komiya likes shinohara  really  oh  but he did say he liked a girl from another class  although i only vaguely remember it   but why do you care about that   i saw the two of them together this morning  since komiya called shinohara by her first name  i felt that they were close  which is why i thought it might be the case   ahh  eh  what  don t tell me  ayanokouji  that  you like shinohara   no   don t hide it from me  we re close friends  eh   but since it s you  i m pretty sure you can aim for a cuter girl   it s ike  ike from my class likes shinohara   i get it now  but  love isn t something that others can interfere with   i also agree with that  meddling in someone else s business is out of the question   normally  that would be true  however  for our class  it s a situation that we can t ignore  ike being active in the special exam is indispensable to class d   alrighty  i can help out if you need it  what can i do   so i should just ignore ayanokouji  who s currently in dire straits   no  you have to leave it alone  i understand that you re friends  but you re also supposed to be enemies   isn t there a saying  that yesterday s enemies are tomorrow s friends   although that s very generous of you  i d be troubled if you want something in return   something in return  i won t ask for anything  it s normal to want to help out a friend who is in trouble   in that case  hmmm  could you first ask about komiya s feelings for me  ishizaki   ayanokouji kun  you saw the two of them enjoying each other s company  right  then let s just pretend that ishizaki was the one who witnessed this instead of you and use it to find out whether they re dating  as a guy who s       not popular with girls  it would simply look like he cared that his friend might have gotten a girlfriend before him  right    ah  komiya  sorry to call you right before club activities start  ah no  i ve got something i wanted to ask you  did you talk to shinohara from class d this morning    just as i thought  no  we formed a pact of not getting a girlfriend before telling each other  but i think you might be leaving me behind in that respect   you re telling    me you aren t dating  really  if you re lying  then you ll be in trouble later  eh   eh  seriously  oh  oh  i see  ahh   that komiya guy  he s planning to confess to shinohara on the uninhabited island   what can we do  in the end  there s no way we can stop it   i said i don t need anything in return   we should help each other when things are tough  i ll help you as much as i can   thanks  although it s not easy for you either  do your best  he calls horikita to the cafeteria  they plot ike s confession  the oaa says they re too late   isn t it fine to just leave them alone   i thought we had a serious problem on our hands  since you re the one coming to consult me  but this isn t our problem to fix  besides  i ve evaluated ike kun s ability as a boy scout to be high  so we should group him with regards to his ability  not his feelings   so he could be expelled due to his feelings for shinohara leading him by the nose   i can t say that he definitely won t be    that would be    problematic  this is so stupid   it seems like komiya and shinohara have already agreed to form a group  but because of your orders  they haven t confirmed yet  however  if you give them permission  9 times out of 10  they ll form a group  you re the leader of class d now  so if you tell shinohara that grouping up with komiya is strategically disadvantageous  she can t forcefully disobey   so you re saying it s necessary to prevent that  but if we stop them from forming a group  won t komiya kun just change the timing of his confession  depending on the situation  he might just confess on that same day   we can t discount that possibility   this is a lot more complicated than it sounds  we can t take care of them until they start dating   why don t we just make ike kun confess  if shinohara san accepts  ike kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he s in  right  on the other hand  if he gets rejected  he can forget about this whole matter and focus on the exam   although you re good at many things  you don t seem to be good at       romance at all   unfortunately  it seems like we re too late   since we ve already reached this point  we must take measures to prevent ike kun s loss of motivation   let s discuss this with yosuke as well  he s thinking about the best group for ike right now  kei s visit  the math of her expulsion  his trial card is her way out   hey  kiyotaka  who do you plan to group up with for this uninhabited island exam   at the moment  i ve no plans to group up with anyone   eh  wh why   kiyotaka  if it s you  are you able to take first place   i feel like  you d take first place non nonchalantly  eh  but wait a minute  in that case  wouldn t it be harder to say that we re dating   you re getting overly excited  don t worry  securing first place is not an easy task by any means   so  so  even you don t think you can win  kiyotaka   let s just say  there s a 50 50 chance   just answering that there s a 50  chance is already super impressive   anyway  the thing you should be worried about isn t who you should group up with  kei   right  this special exam does involve expulsion  if you are in the bottom 5 groups  you ll have to face that penalty  that s why you can t randomly choose who you group up with   yeah  that s why  i wanted to group up with you  kiyotaka  i hoped you       could protect me   even if i don t protect you  there s still a way to save yourself  right  that is  to keep a deposit of the amount of private points needed to nullify the expulsion   that s true  but even if you do form a group of 6 students in the exam  you ll still need 1 million points to avoid expulsion  right  i don t have that much   um  240 000 points  e even so  i m considered to be someone who has saved up a lot recently   so you re short 760 000 points    sure enough  that s true   kiyotaka  your card is the trial card  right  it s a card that has a strong effect if you win  but conversely if you lose it would be tragic  ah  of course  i know that you ll have no problem at all  i wanted the half off or the nullify card though   i ll prepare the points   eh  you say you ll prepare  how   there are many ways  but selling the trial card is one way to get you the required points   but then  you ll have to give up the trial card  is that really okay   it s more important to prevent you from getting expelled   ye yeah  th thanks  he prices her survival into his own exam arithmetic  kei  240 000 pts  the trial card s going rate matters for her 760 000 shortfall  his answer is to protect her  he offers to sell his trial card to fund her relief  she offers herself  he defers  they rehearse the ike confession plan  too late  the boy he must not lose to the island  she is grouping with komiya and kinoshita minori","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p177-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p177-1\">The café watch, Matsushita; the Ike counter-plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.177–202<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike stalks Shinohara; Yousuke intercepts; they agree to stake out the café. Matsushita Chiaki follows at a distance; corners him when Yosuke peels off to the cafe. They spot Shinohara and Komiya laughing in the café; Ike depressed behind them. He calls Ishizaki; Nishino corners them; the Komiya investigation; Komiya plans to confess on the island. He calls Horikita to the cafeteria; they plot Ike&#x27;s confession; the OAA says they&#x27;re too late. Kei&#x27;s visit; the math of her expulsion; his Trial card is her way out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nishino-takeko.html\">Nishino Takeko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “About Ike, I don’t think it’s too good to leave him alone like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. Seeing that, I’m also worried about what will happen if he watches the discussion between Shinohara and Komiya while he’s like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’d like to go see what’s going on. If you’re okay with it, can you come along? I don’t think Ike-kun likes me very much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>111 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Shall we go and see what’s going on, just in case?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like we can only form groups that leave us with no regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For me, I’d like to select 2 people from Class D to form a group. Instead of aiming for the top places, I’d rather fight to not get penalized.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is Sakura-san alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Miyake-kun has good motor skills, so I feel the group is well balanced.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t seem very surprised. Did you notice from the start?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just don’t show any surprise in my expression.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that any of your business, Matsushita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not so much about me, as it’s about us. Ayanokouji-kun, you’re an important existence for us to get into Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be so cautious, I approached you because I just had something to tell you today as soon as possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The Trial card is an item with a very powerful effect. But it’s difficult to use it. If you’ve got any problems, I would like to help you, Ayanokouji-kun. How about it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, during the exam, I’ll completely follow your instructions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I’m happy that you’re willing to assist me, if we don’t make it to the top 30%, you’ll be penalized. You know the risks, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I do. That’s why I think it’s important for me to cooperate with you to help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…So I’ve been exposed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’d be difficult to stay in the top ranks if it were you. Even if we don’t end up on the podium, we’re bound to reach the top 30%. It would be more dangerous if I put my friends first and make a half-assed group with them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought you’d get snapped up quickly, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t decide on my group, at least for this month.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean that you want to wait and watch how things go?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After all, I’d like to see how the other classes move.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like I won’t get a satisfactory answer now. I see, give it some thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, right. Here’s my contact information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll think about who would be the best person for Ike to group up with if he can’t group with Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’ll be as bad as it can be, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, I wanted to ask about Komiya first. Why did Komiya invite Shinohara to his group? If we’re not sure about that, we can’t take any action.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, you said you ‘something’, did you mean a meeting with Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re rather close with Ishizaki. That’s a surprise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you didn’t listen to me at all! This is why you’re ostracized!”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ostracized …  … ? … I’m hardly troubled by that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I’m curious as to why you and Ayanokouji-kun are secretly meeting, Ishizaki.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our relationship became better after being in the same group in last year’s Mixed Training Camp.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I contacted Ishizaki because I wanted to ask him a few questions about Komiya from your class. I decided to meet here because this conversation isn’t meant for others to hear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because of Komiya-kun? What’s going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because even in the kindest of terms, Shinohara isn’t the kind of person who would be very active in this uninhabited island exam. So our class is worried about whether her grouping up with Komiya is a good idea or not. We want to know what kind of person he is beforehand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s just a nice guy in general, right? He also has good motor skills, and because he’s in the basketball club, he has good physical strength as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like one of them invited the other to form a group, are they dating?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Th-that’s hard to say…”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you ask Ishizaki these things, he wouldn’t understand. You don’t know anything about love, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At least more than you. Although they’re not dating, Komiya-kun certainly …  …  likes Shinohara-san, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Komiya likes Shinohara, really? Oh, but he did say he liked a girl from another class… although I only vaguely remember it…”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But why do you care about that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I saw the two of them together this morning. Since Komiya called Shinohara by her first name, I felt that they were close, which is why I thought it might be the case.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahh… Eh, what? Don’t tell me, Ayanokouji, that…. You like Shinohara?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t hide it from me, we’re close friends, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But since it’s you, I’m pretty sure you can aim for a cuter girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s Ike. Ike from my class likes Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I get it now, but, love isn’t something that others can interfere with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I also agree with that, meddling in someone else’s business is out of the question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Normally, that would be true. However, for our class, it’s a situation that we can’t ignore. Ike being active in the special exam is indispensable to Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alrighty, I can help out if you need it. What can I do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So I should just ignore Ayanokouji, who’s currently in dire straits?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, you have to leave it alone. I understand that you’re friends, but you’re also supposed to be enemies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t there a saying, that yesterday’s enemies are tomorrow’s friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although that’s very generous of you, I’d be troubled if you want something in return.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Something in return? I won’t ask for anything. It’s normal to want to help out a friend who is in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, hmmm… Could you first ask about Komiya’s feelings for me, Ishizaki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, you saw the two of them enjoying each other’s company, right? Then let’s just pretend that Ishizaki was the one who witnessed this instead of you and use it to find out whether they’re dating. As a guy who’s …  …  not popular with girls, it would simply look like he cared that his friend might have gotten a girlfriend before him, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… Ah, Komiya? Sorry to call you right before club activities start. Ah no, I’ve got something I wanted to ask you. Did you talk to Shinohara from Class D this morning? … Just as I thought. No, we formed a pact of not getting a girlfriend before telling each other, but I think you might be leaving me behind in that respect.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re telling …  me you aren’t dating? Really? If you’re lying, then you’ll be in trouble later, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh… Seriously? Oh, oh, I see, ahh…”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That Komiya guy, he’s planning to confess to Shinohara on the uninhabited island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What can we do? In the end, there’s no way we can stop it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said I don’t need anything in return.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We should help each other when things are tough. I’ll help you as much as I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks, although it’s not easy for you either, do your best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it fine to just leave them alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought we had a serious problem on our hands, since you’re the one coming to consult me… but this isn’t our problem to fix. Besides, I’ve evaluated Ike-kun’s ability as a boy scout to be high, so we should group him with regards to his ability, not his feelings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So he could be expelled due to his feelings for Shinohara leading him by the nose?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say that he definitely won’t be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… That would be …  problematic. This is so stupid.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like Komiya and Shinohara have already agreed to form a group, but because of your orders, they haven’t confirmed yet. However, if you give them permission, 9 times out of 10, they’ll form a group. You’re the leader of Class D now, so if you tell Shinohara that grouping up with Komiya is strategically disadvantageous, she can’t forcefully disobey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re saying it’s necessary to prevent that? But if we stop them from forming a group, won’t Komiya-kun just change the timing of his confession? Depending on the situation, he might just confess on that same day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can’t discount that possibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a lot more complicated than it sounds. We can’t take care of them until they start dating.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why don’t we just make Ike-kun confess? If Shinohara-san accepts, Ike-kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he’s in, right? On the other hand, if he gets rejected, he can forget about this whole matter and focus on the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although you’re good at many things, you don’t seem to be good at …  …  romance at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, it seems like we’re too late.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’ve already reached this point, we must take measures to prevent Ike-kun’s loss of motivation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s discuss this with Yosuke as well. He’s thinking about the best group for Ike right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey… Kiyotaka, who do you plan to group up with for this uninhabited island exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At the moment, I’ve no plans to group up with anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Wh-why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka, if it’s you, are you able to take first place?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel like… You’d take first place non-nonchalantly. Eh, but wait a minute. In that case, wouldn’t it be harder to say that we’re dating!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re getting overly excited. Don’t worry, securing first place is not an easy task by any means.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, so… even you don’t think you can win, Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s just say, there’s a 50/50 chance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just answering that there’s a 50% chance is already super impressive…”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, the thing you should be worried about isn’t who you should group up with, Kei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right, this special exam does involve expulsion. If you are in the bottom 5 groups, you’ll have to face that penalty. That’s why you can’t randomly choose who you group up with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s why, I wanted to group up with you, Kiyotaka… I hoped you …  …  could protect me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I don’t protect you, there’s still a way to save yourself, right? That is, to keep a deposit of the amount of private points needed to nullify the expulsion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, but even if you do form a group of 6 students in the exam, you’ll still need 1 million points to avoid expulsion, right? I don’t have that much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um… 240,000 points…. E-even so, I’m considered to be someone who has saved up a lot recently!”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re short 760,000 points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… Sure enough, that’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka, your card is the Trial card, right? It’s a card that has a strong effect if you win, but conversely if you lose it would be tragic… Ah, of course, I know that you’ll have no problem at all. I wanted the Half Off or the Nullify card though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll prepare the points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? You say you’ll prepare… How?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are many ways, but selling the Trial card is one way to get you the required points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But then, you’ll have to give up the Trial card… Is that really okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s more important to prevent you from getting expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ye-yeah… Th-thanks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He prices her survival into his own exam arithmetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kei: 240,000 pts; the Trial card&#x27;s going rate matters for her 760,000 shortfall; his answer is to protect her.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> He offers to sell his Trial card to fund her relief.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> She offers herself; he defers.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> They rehearse the Ike confession plan; too late.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The boy he must not lose to the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She is grouping with Komiya and Kinoshita Minori.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p168-1\">← Before: The Trial card; Shinohara and Ike at the elevator<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p203-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi and Ichinose (not present)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p177-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji sakura-airi miyake-akito ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke the cafe watch he s watched the whole ike shinohara scene from the back  he intercepts ayanokoji in the corridor  worried   about ike  i don t think it s too good to leave him alone like this   yeah  he might be a bit arrogant  but ike s knowledge and experience will be of use in the uninhabited island survival exam  it s possible this incident with shinohara may prevent him from fulfilling his potential   yes  seeing that  i m also worried about what will happen if he watches the discussion between shinohara and komiya while he s like that   i d like to go see what s going on  if you re okay with it  can you come along  i don t think ike kun likes me very much   yeah  shall we go and see what s going on  just in case   it seems like we can only form groups that leave us with no regrets   for me  i d like to select 2 people from class d to form a group  instead of aiming for the top places  i d rather fight to not get penalized   miyake kun has good motor skills  so i feel the group is well balanced   i don t think    it ll be as bad as it can be  but   anyway  i wanted to ask about komiya first  why did komiya invite shinohara to his group  if we re not sure about that  we can t take any action  he knows ike s potential is rotting in private  he worries about airi in sakura s circle  he rates his skills  he trusts his read of the room over his own hunches","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p177-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p177-1\">The café watch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.177–186<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He&#x27;s watched the whole Ike–Shinohara scene from the back; he intercepts Ayanokōji in the corridor, worried.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “About Ike, I don’t think it’s too good to leave him alone like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yeah. He might be a bit arrogant, but Ike’s knowledge and experience will be of use in the uninhabited island survival exam. It’s possible this incident with Shinohara may prevent him from fulfilling his potential.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. Seeing that, I’m also worried about what will happen if he watches the discussion between Shinohara and Komiya while he’s like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to go see what’s going on. If you’re okay with it, can you come along? I don’t think Ike-kun likes me very much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Shall we go and see what’s going on, just in case?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like we can only form groups that leave us with no regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For me, I’d like to select 2 people from Class D to form a group. Instead of aiming for the top places, I’d rather fight to not get penalized.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Miyake-kun has good motor skills, so I feel the group is well balanced.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’ll be as bad as it can be, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, I wanted to ask about Komiya first. Why did Komiya invite Shinohara to his group? If we’re not sure about that, we can’t take any action.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He knows Ike&#x27;s potential is rotting in private.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He worries about Airi in Sakura&#x27;s circle.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> He rates his skills.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He trusts his read of the room over his own hunches.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y2v2-p142-1\">← Before: The strategy circle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p179-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hasebe-haruka","q":"hasebe haruka haruka s group she groups with akito and airi  the group is well balanced by motor skills","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html#sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p179-1\">Haruka&#x27;s group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She groups with Akito and Airi; the group is well balanced by motor skills.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p39-1\">← Before: Haruka mediates and manages<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p243-1\">→ After: Haruka at the after-school gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p179-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka matsushita-chiaki","q":"matsushita chiaki matsushita recruits him she trails him at a distance till yosuke peels off  edges him into a conversation he didn t plan   you don t seem very surprised  did you notice from the start   is that any of your business  matsushita   it s not so much about me  as it s about us  ayanokouji kun  you re an important existence for us to get into class a  she offers to be his point blank support under the trial card  he defers the decision   don t be so cautious  i approached you because i just had something to tell you today as soon as possible   the trial card is an item with a very powerful effect  but it s difficult to use it  if you ve got any problems  i would like to help you  ayanokouji kun  how about it   of course  during the exam  i ll completely follow your instructions   i do  that s why i think it s important for me to cooperate with you to help you   so i ve been exposed   i don t think    it d be difficult to stay in the top ranks if it were you  even if we don t end up on the podium  we re bound to reach the top 30  it would be more dangerous if i put my friends first and make a half assed group with them   i thought you d get snapped up quickly  ayanokouji kun   i won t decide on my group  at least for this month   you mean that you want to wait and watch how things go   it seems like i won t get a satisfactory answer now  i see  give it some thought   ah  right  here s my contact information  he handed her his id  she handed him hers  she s class d  the trial card looms over the offer  calculated opportunist with genuine respect for strength  she stalks him only on paper  she holds the cards patiently  she wants to sign him  he defers  she keeps the line open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html#sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p179-1\">Matsushita recruits him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.179–185<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She trails him at a distance till Yosuke peels off; edges him into a conversation he didn&#x27;t plan. She offers to be his point-blank support under the Trial card; he defers the decision.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> “You don’t seem very surprised. Did you notice from the start?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> “Is that any of your business, Matsushita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> “It’s not so much about me, as it’s about us. Ayanokouji-kun, you’re an important existence for us to get into Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be so cautious, I approached you because I just had something to tell you today as soon as possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The Trial card is an item with a very powerful effect. But it’s difficult to use it. If you’ve got any problems, I would like to help you, Ayanokouji-kun. How about it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, during the exam, I’ll completely follow your instructions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I do. That’s why I think it’s important for me to cooperate with you to help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…So I’ve been exposed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think …  it’d be difficult to stay in the top ranks if it were you. Even if we don’t end up on the podium, we’re bound to reach the top 30%. It would be more dangerous if I put my friends first and make a half-assed group with them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought you’d get snapped up quickly, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t decide on my group, at least for this month.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean that you want to wait and watch how things go?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like I won’t get a satisfactory answer now. I see, give it some thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, right. Here’s my contact information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He handed her his ID; she handed him hers; she&#x27;s Class D; the Trial card looms over the offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculated opportunist with genuine respect for strength; she stalks him only on paper; she holds the cards patiently.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She wants to sign him; he defers; she keeps the line open.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p294-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p179-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito miyake s group airi  akito and haruka form their group  yousuke rates his motor skills","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html#sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p179-1\">Miyake&#x27;s group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Airi, Akito and Haruka form their group; Yousuke rates his motor skills.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Miyake shakes off the tension<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p243-1\">→ After: Akito at his club<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p179-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi sakura groups up akito tells ayanokoji she is grouping with akito and haruka  not present in scenes  her group s arithmetic is recorded","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p179-1\">Sakura groups up<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Akito tells Ayanokōji she is grouping with Akito and Haruka.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Not present in scenes; her group&#x27;s arithmetic is recorded.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p39-1\">← Before: The reconciliation handshake; Keyaki mall<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p243-1\">→ After: The group after school<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p185-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"shinohara-satsuki","q":"shinohara satsuki coverage note  passing mentions  i spotted shinohara and komiya  who were talking and laughing in the cafe   it seems like one of them invited the other to form a group  are they dating    the ishizaki exchange about her and komiya  the print carries  although they re not dating  komiya kun certainly likes shinohara san  right    printed across the page turn  kept as printed   if that happened  the relationship between ike and shinohara might become even more tenuous than it is now   and if we forcefully separated komiya and shinohara  it would invite nishino s ire   so you just want to know if he actually likes shinohara  ayanokouji   that komiya guy  he s planning to confess to shinohara on the uninhabited island   that komiya guy  he s planning to confess to shinohara on the uninhabited island   i expressed my concerns to horikita about the current situation between ike  shinohara  and komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam   it seems like komiya and shinohara have already agreed to form a group  but because of your orders  they haven t confirmed yet   if you tell shinohara that grouping up with komiya is strategically disadvantageous  she can t forcefully disobey   why don t we just make ike kun confess  if shinohara san accepts  ike kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he s in  right   unfortunately  it seems like we re too late    the oaa check that shows shinohara and komiya already formed a group   starting with the fight between ike and shinohara","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p185-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p185-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.185–198<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I spotted Shinohara and Komiya, who were talking and laughing in the cafe.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It seems like one of them invited the other to form a group, are they dating?” — the Ishizaki exchange about her and Komiya.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> The print carries: although they’re not dating, Komiya-kun certainly likes Shinohara-san, right? — printed across the page turn; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If that happened, the relationship between Ike and Shinohara might become even more tenuous than it is now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “And if we forcefully separated Komiya and Shinohara, it would invite Nishino’s ire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “So you just want to know if he actually likes Shinohara, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That Komiya guy, he’s planning to confess to Shinohara on the uninhabited island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That Komiya guy, he’s planning to confess to Shinohara on the uninhabited island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I expressed my concerns to Horikita about the current situation between Ike, Shinohara, and Komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It seems like Komiya and Shinohara have already agreed to form a group, but because of your orders, they haven’t confirmed yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “if you tell Shinohara that grouping up with Komiya is strategically disadvantageous, she can’t forcefully disobey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Why don’t we just make Ike-kun confess? If Shinohara-san accepts, Ike-kun will fight hard to stay at the school no matter what group he’s in, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Unfortunately, it seems like we’re too late.” — the OAA check that shows Shinohara and Komiya already formed a group.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Starting with the fight between Ike and Shinohara.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y2v2-p168-1\">← Before: The Komiya turn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p187-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nishino-takeko komiya-kyogo ishizaki-daichi","q":"ishizaki daichi the komiya investigation ayanokoji calls him after class  nishino materializes mid meeting  the komiya problem opens up  nishino coaches the tactic   yo  are you finally thinking to group up with us   sorry  that s still under deliberation  i m here for something else today   so  what did you want to discuss with me   hey  you didn t listen to me at all  this is why you re ostracized   ah no  just that this girl s isolated in our class right now  that s become a bit of a problem   isolated  i m hardly troubled by that   hey  you didn t listen to me at all   he s just a nice guy in general  right  he also has good motor skills  and because he s in the basketball club  he has good physical strength as well   it seems like one of them invited the other to form a group  are they dating   ahh  eh  what  don t tell me  ayanokouji  that  you like shinohara   wha  she s the type of girl a blockhead like you d fall for though  am i right  am i right   don t hide it from me  we re close friends  eh   but since it s you  i m pretty sure you can aim for a cuter girl   i get it now  but  love isn t something that others can interfere with   something in return  i won t ask for anything  it s normal to want to help out a friend who is in trouble    ah  komiya  sorry to call you right before club activities start  ah no  i ve got something i wanted to ask you  did you talk to shinohara from class d this morning    just as i thought  no  we formed a pact of not getting a girlfriend before telling each other  but i think you might be leaving me behind in that respect   you re telling    me you aren t dating  really  if you re lying  then you ll be in trouble later  eh   eh  seriously  oh  oh  i see  ahh   that komiya guy  he s planning to confess to shinohara on the uninhabited island   what can we do  in the end  there s no way we can stop it   i said i don t need anything in return   thanks  although it s not easy for you either  do your best  he calls komiya with nishino s coaching  the pact of no girlfriends before telling  he insists on working for nothing  he helps him on instinct  she rides along and improves the plan  he extracts the planned confession","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p187-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html#sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p187-1\">The Komiya investigation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.187–194<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji calls him after class; Nishino materializes mid-meeting; the Komiya problem opens up; Nishino coaches the tactic.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nishino-takeko.html\">Nishino Takeko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Yo! Are you finally thinking to group up with us!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Sorry, that’s still under deliberation. I’m here for something else today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “So, what did you want to discuss with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you didn’t listen to me at all! This is why you’re ostracized!”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah no, just that this girl’s isolated in our class right now. That’s become a bit of a problem.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isolated? I’m hardly troubled by that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you didn’t listen to me at all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s just a nice guy in general, right? He also has good motor skills, and because he’s in the basketball club, he has good physical strength as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like one of them invited the other to form a group, are they dating?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahh… Eh, what? Don’t tell me, Ayanokouji, that…. You like Shinohara?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wha? She’s the type of girl a blockhead like you’d fall for though? Am I right, am I right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t hide it from me, we’re close friends, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But since it’s you, I’m pretty sure you can aim for a cuter girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I get it now, but, love isn’t something that others can interfere with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Something in return? I won’t ask for anything. It’s normal to want to help out a friend who is in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… Ah, Komiya? Sorry to call you right before club activities start. Ah no, I’ve got something I wanted to ask you. Did you talk to Shinohara from Class D this morning? … Just as I thought. No, we formed a pact of not getting a girlfriend before telling each other, but I think you might be leaving me behind in that respect.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re telling …  me you aren’t dating? Really? If you’re lying, then you’ll be in trouble later, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh… Seriously? Oh, oh, I see, ahh…”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That Komiya guy, he’s planning to confess to Shinohara on the uninhabited island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What can we do? In the end, there’s no way we can stop it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said I don’t need anything in return.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks, although it’s not easy for you either, do your best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He calls Komiya with Nishino&#x27;s coaching; the pact of no-girlfriends-before-telling; he insists on working for nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He helps him on instinct.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishino Takeko<\/b> She rides along and improves the plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> He extracts the planned confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ishizaki&#x27;s Class B recruitment pitch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p294-1\">→ After: Ishizaki&#x27;s email<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p187-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka nishino-takeko","q":"nishino takeko nishino follows the meeting she shows up mid meeting between ishizaki and ayanokoji   what  you said you  something  did you mean a meeting with ayanokouji kun   you re rather close with ishizaki  that s a surprise   ostracized          i m hardly troubled by that   but i m curious as to why you and ayanokouji kun are secretly meeting  ishizaki   because of komiya kun  what s going on   eh  th that s hard to say   even if you ask ishizaki these things  he wouldn t understand  you don t know anything about love  do you   shut up  do you understand it then   at least more than you  although they re not dating  komiya kun certainly       likes shinohara san  right   but why do you care about that   i also agree with that  meddling in someone else s business is out of the question   isn t there a saying  that yesterday s enemies are tomorrow s friends   ayanokouji kun  you saw the two of them enjoying each other s company  right  then let s just pretend that ishizaki was the one who witnessed this instead of you and use it to find out whether they re dating  as a guy who s       not popular with girls  it would simply look like he cared that his friend might have gotten a girlfriend before him  right  she is isolated in her class  she chirps nonstop  she has zero filter and a sharp eye  she chases his meetings  she tags him onto the investigation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p187-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nishino-takeko.html#sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p187-1\">Nishino follows the meeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.187–192<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nishino-takeko.html\">Nishino Takeko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She shows up mid-meeting between Ishizaki and Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nishino Takeko<\/b> “What, you said you ‘something’, did you mean a meeting with Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nishino Takeko<\/b> “You’re rather close with Ishizaki. That’s a surprise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nishino Takeko<\/b> “Ostracized …  … ? … I’m hardly troubled by that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I’m curious as to why you and Ayanokouji-kun are secretly meeting, Ishizaki.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because of Komiya-kun? What’s going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Th-that’s hard to say…”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you ask Ishizaki these things, he wouldn’t understand. You don’t know anything about love, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shut up! Do you understand it then?’”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At least more than you. Although they’re not dating, Komiya-kun certainly …  …  likes Shinohara-san, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But why do you care about that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I also agree with that, meddling in someone else’s business is out of the question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t there a saying, that yesterday’s enemies are tomorrow’s friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun, you saw the two of them enjoying each other’s company, right? Then let’s just pretend that Ishizaki was the one who witnessed this instead of you and use it to find out whether they’re dating. As a guy who’s …  …  not popular with girls, it would simply look like he cared that his friend might have gotten a girlfriend before him, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is isolated in her class; she chirps nonstop; she has zero filter and a sharp eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> She chases his meetings.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She tags him onto the investigation.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p193-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p193-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"nishino-takeko","q":"nishino takeko coverage note  passing mentions  ishizaki  who had little material to use as a motive for asking  immediately accepted nishino s suggestion   if nishino s having trouble forming a group  you can talk to me  i might be able to help in some way   is it about nishino  last i checked  she hadn t formed a group","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nishino-takeko.html#sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p193-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.193–315<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nishino-takeko.html\">Nishino Takeko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ishizaki, who had little material to use as a motive for asking, immediately accepted Nishino’s suggestion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If Nishino’s having trouble forming a group, you can talk to me. I might be able to help in some way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Is it about Nishino? Last I checked, she hadn’t formed a group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nishino-takeko-y2v2-p187-1\">← Before: Nishino follows the meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p194-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"komiya-kyogo","q":"komiya kyogo coverage note  passing mentions  that komiya guy  he s planning to confess to shinohara on the uninhabited island   i expressed my concerns to horikita about the current situation between ike  shinohara  and komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam   it seems like komiya and shinohara have already agreed to form a group  but because of your orders  they haven t confirmed yet   the prospect of forming groups for the uninhabited island exam would be difficult","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html#sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p194-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.194–197<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That Komiya guy, he’s planning to confess to Shinohara on the uninhabited island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I expressed my concerns to Horikita about the current situation between Ike, Shinohara, and Komiya and that it might affect this upcoming uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “It seems like Komiya and Shinohara have already agreed to form a group, but because of your orders, they haven’t confirmed yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The prospect of forming groups for the uninhabited island exam would be difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y2v2-p172-1\">← Before: Komiya finds her on the steps<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kinoshita-minori-y2v2-p197-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kinoshita-minori","q":"kinoshita minori coverage note  passing mentions  the third person in their group was kinoshita minori of class b    on the oaa listing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y2v2-p197-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html#sc-kinoshita-minori-y2v2-p197-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.197<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The third person in their group was Kinoshita Minori of Class B.” — on the OAA listing.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p198-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei kei asks for his help her visit tonight begins with the exam question   hey  kiyotaka  who do you plan to group up with for this uninhabited island exam   eh  wh why  the stakes turn personal  her 760 000 point gap on the table   kiyotaka  if it s you  are you able to take first place   i feel like  you d take first place non nonchalantly  eh  but wait a minute  in that case  wouldn t it be harder to say that we re dating   so  so  even you don t think you can win  kiyotaka   just answering that there s a 50  chance is already super impressive   right  this special exam does involve expulsion  if you are in the bottom 5 groups  you ll have to face that penalty  that s why you can t randomly choose who you group up with   yeah  that s why  i wanted to group up with you  kiyotaka  i hoped you       could protect me  the math of her survival  his trial card is the way out   that s true  but   that s true  but even if you do form a group of 6 students in the exam  you ll still need 1 million points to avoid expulsion  right  i don t have that much   um  240 000 points  e even so  i m considered to be someone who has saved up a lot recently   yeah  how much is that card worth    sure enough  that s true   kiyotaka  your card is the trial card  right  it s a card that has a strong effect if you win  but conversely if you lose it would be tragic  ah  of course  i know that you ll have no problem at all  i wanted the half off or the nullify card though   but then  you ll have to give up the trial card  is that really okay   ye yeah  th thanks  she names her fear precisely   760 000 points short and nowhere else to turn  pride makes her wait until the end of the night to say it  she asks him for protection  then accepts him paying for it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p198-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p198-1\">Kei asks for his help<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.198–202<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her visit tonight begins with the exam question. The stakes turn personal; her 760,000-point gap on the table. The math of her survival; his Trial card is the way out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hey… Kiyotaka, who do you plan to group up with for this uninhabited island exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Eh? Wh-why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Kiyotaka, if it’s you, are you able to take first place?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel like… You’d take first place non-nonchalantly. Eh, but wait a minute. In that case, wouldn’t it be harder to say that we’re dating!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, so… even you don’t think you can win, Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just answering that there’s a 50% chance is already super impressive…”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right, this special exam does involve expulsion. If you are in the bottom 5 groups, you’ll have to face that penalty. That’s why you can’t randomly choose who you group up with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s why, I wanted to group up with you, Kiyotaka… I hoped you …  …  could protect me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, but even if you do form a group of 6 students in the exam, you’ll still need 1 million points to avoid expulsion, right? I don’t have that much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um… 240,000 points…. E-even so, I’m considered to be someone who has saved up a lot recently!”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. How much is that card worth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… Sure enough, that’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka, your card is the Trial card, right? It’s a card that has a strong effect if you win, but conversely if you lose it would be tragic… Ah, of course, I know that you’ll have no problem at all. I wanted the Half Off or the Nullify card though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But then, you’ll have to give up the Trial card… Is that really okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ye-yeah… Th-thanks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She names her fear precisely — 760,000 points short and nowhere else to turn; pride makes her wait until the end of the night to say it.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She asks him for protection, then accepts him paying for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y2v2-p110-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p203-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi and ichinose  not present  he is not present for the ichinose sakayanagi meeting  the chapter focalises on them  see ichinose honami md and sakayanagi arisu md","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p203-1\">Sakayanagi and Ichinose (not present)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.203–218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is not present for the Ichinose–Sakayanagi meeting; the chapter focalises on them. See ichinose-honami.md and sakayanagi-arisu.md.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p177-1\">← Before: The café watch, Matsushita; the Ike counter-plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p219-1\">→ After: The 1st-year gathering (not present)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p203-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu kanzaki-ryuuji horikita-suzune ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami the sakayanagi pact on a cafe night sakayanagi springs the invitation  ichinose  taught by betrayal  almost refuses  almost   why  because i had nothing special planned for today   well  i don t think you did anything excessive  sakayanagi san  indeed  i have to reflect on what happened during middle school  as i also think that it was a shameful act  also  it s not like i asked you to keep it a secret  so i don t think it s right to blame you for exposing it   am i  i m not too sure about that   ahaha  truly blunt   it s true that our state of being left out in the cold can t be called good   i also know just how formidable they are   but  in order to climb the ladder  there s no avoiding that road  besides  while it s true that ryuuen kun is a tough opponent  you re not someone that can be easily defeated either  sakayanagi san  sakayanagi walks her through class 2 c s danger and offers the alliance  she wavers  exposes sakayanagi s true goal  stopping the three class alliance  accepts   indeed  there are some interesting talented individuals in class d  headed by hirata kun and kushida san  who have strong communication skills  and have well balanced grades  along with sudo kun  who s the only one to get an a  rating in physical ability in the entire 2nd year  meanwhile  their hidden trump card  ayanokouji kun  got a perfect score on an extremely difficult math test  then  there s also kouenji kun  whose strengths and limits are still a mystery  he too is a dangerous adversary   horikita san and her class are also rapidly gaining strength  in terms of individual strength  some of them wouldn t lose to anyone in the other classes  looking at it this way  it seems like i really don t have any room to spare   that  that s not the case  we ve grown as well   you might not believe it  sakayanagi san  but i don t think we ll lose   ye yes   eh   no  but that s   that s right  partnerships can t last forever   what makes me sad is that this isn t a happy proposal  after all  it implies that our class is not worthy of your caution  an insignificant existence to you   i don t think it ll be beneficial for you to cooperate with us  sakayanagi san  the negotiation closes  sakayanagi offers her trust   5 people s worth of deposits  3m repaid  5m total  sakayanagi can participate in the exam in a  semi eliminated  position  the more people card  the handshake  the first place vow   could you be a bit more specific    that s right   right  so i guess we ll inevitably have to build a winning group from our own class   although the gap with our class wouldn t be narrowed  you can catch up with ryuuen kun s class  and widen the gap with class d   but  if we do that  we ll lose a chance to catch up to your class   that   it d be lying if i said i haven t thought about that before   special   so sakayanagi san  you can participate under this special position   sakayanagi san  may i tell you how i really feel   sakayanagi san     you don t want the three classes to fight together  more than i originally thought  or to say  you re afraid of that situation  right   what do you mean   you said we were someone you could trust  and i think you meant that  however  the most important thing for you is to prevent class b  class c     and class d from working together to catch up to class a  indeed  the amount of class points we can get if we win together will decrease  but there s no guarantee that such a development wouldn t appear in the future  that the three classes would continue to help each other   an alliance between the three classes to force class a out  if that is successful  you would be forced into a bitter battle from now on  sakayanagi san  isn t that so   then can you give me five people s worth  that way i would feel completely reassured   with that our contract is complete  even if you hadn t offered to loan me the deposit points  i would have chosen to join forces with you  our main goal is of course to reach class a  but as you said  we fell to class c and we can t afford to fall even more  since  if we fall down to class d  our class s motivation would surely be greatly reduced  and that is something we want to avoid   the proposal for an alliance between class 2 c and class 2 a  i accept it   however  both ryuuen kun and horikita san are formidable opponents  sakayanagi suspects the three class alliance would beat class a in the long run  ichinose spotted it and named it  the handshake sealed the pact  the trust factor is why she chose her  the alliance partner  he stays her watchman  her value to sakayanagi and ichinose alike","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p203-1\">The Sakayanagi pact<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.203–218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On a café night Sakayanagi springs the invitation; Ichinose, taught by betrayal, almost refuses; almost. Sakayanagi walks her through Class 2-C&#x27;s danger and offers the alliance; she wavers; exposes Sakayanagi&#x27;s true goal (stopping the three-class alliance); accepts. The negotiation closes: Sakayanagi offers her trust + 5 people&#x27;s worth of deposits (3M repaid; 5M total); Sakayanagi can participate in the exam in a “semi-eliminated” position; the More People card; the handshake; the first-place vow.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Why? Because I had nothing special planned for today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well– I don’t think you did anything excessive, Sakayanagi-san. Indeed, I have to reflect on what happened during middle school, as I also think that it was a shameful act. Also, it’s not like I asked you to keep it a secret, so…”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Am I? I’m not too sure about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well– I don’t think you did anything excessive, Sakayanagi-san. Indeed, I have to reflect on what happened during middle school, as I also think that it was a shameful act. Also, it’s not like I asked you to keep it a secret, so I don’t think it’s right to blame you for exposing it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahaha… Truly blunt.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s true that our state of being left out in the cold can’t be called good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I also know just how formidable they are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, in order to climb the ladder, there’s no avoiding that road. Besides, while it’s true that Ryuuen-kun is a tough opponent, you’re not someone that can be easily defeated either, Sakayanagi-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Indeed, there are some interesting talented individuals in Class D. Headed by Hirata-kun and Kushida-san, who have strong communication skills, and have well-balanced grades, along with Sudo-kun, who’s the only one to get an A+ rating in physical ability in the entire 2nd year. Meanwhile, their hidden trump card, Ayanokouji-kun, got a perfect score on an extremely difficult math test. Then, there’s also Kouenji-kun, whose strengths and limits are still a mystery; he too is a dangerous adversary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san and her class are also rapidly gaining strength. In terms of individual strength, some of them wouldn’t lose to anyone in the other classes… Looking at it this way, It seems like I really don’t have any room to spare.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That… that’s not the case. We’ve grown as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might not believe it, Sakayanagi-san, but I don’t think we’ll lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ye…Yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, but that’s—”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right… partnerships can’t last forever.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What makes me sad is that this isn’t a happy proposal. After all, it implies that our class is not worthy of your caution, an insignificant existence to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think it’ll be beneficial for you to cooperate with us, Sakayanagi-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could you be a bit more specific?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… That’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. So I guess we’ll inevitably have to build a winning group from our own class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although the gap with our class wouldn’t be narrowed, you can catch up with Ryuuen-kun’s class, and widen the gap with Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But— If we do that, we’ll lose a chance to catch up to your class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That…”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’d be lying if I said I haven’t thought about that before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Special?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So Sakayanagi-san, you can participate under this special position?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakayanagi-san, may I tell you how I really feel?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakayanagi-san … , you don’t want the three classes to fight together, more than I originally thought. Or to say, you’re afraid of that situation, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You said we were someone you could trust, and I think you meant that. However, the most important thing for you is to prevent Class B, Class C … , and Class D from working together to catch up to Class A. Indeed, the amount of class points we can get if we win together will decrease, but there’s no guarantee that such a development wouldn’t appear in the future— That the three classes would continue to help each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An alliance between the three classes to force Class A out. If that is successful, you would be forced into a bitter battle from now on, Sakayanagi-san… Isn’t that so?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then can you give me five people’s worth? That way I would feel completely reassured.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With that our contract is complete. Even if you hadn’t offered to loan me the deposit points, I would have chosen to join forces with you. Our main goal is of course to reach Class A, but as you said, we fell to Class C and we can’t afford to fall even more. Since, if we fall down to Class D, our class’s motivation would surely be greatly reduced, and that is something we want to avoid.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The proposal for an alliance between Class 2-C and Class 2-A— I accept it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, both Ryuuen-kun and Horikita-san are formidable opponents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi suspects the three-class alliance would beat Class A in the long run; Ichinose spotted it and named it; the handshake sealed the pact.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The trust factor is why she chose her.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The alliance partner.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He stays her watchman.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her value to Sakayanagi and Ichinose alike.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y2v2-p46-1\">← Before: Ichinose at Keyaki mall; the pact<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p203-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hashibuto-masayoshi kitou-hayato kamuro-masumi shibata-sou sakayanagi-arisu","q":"sakayanagi arisu the cafe invitation to ichinose on the friday of the first weekend after group formation began  sakayanagi contacts ichinose on short notice  she lies about wanting to meet  she presses ichinose on 2 c s slide  the only catch up left is the special exams  ichinose wilts   by the way  why did you accept my sudden request   that s not what i meant  i ve done some terrible things to you before  ichinose san  it wouldn t be surprising if you hated me   you re definitely a good person  ichinose san   as you wish  i ll get to the point  but you might not be very comfortable with that either   bluntly speaking  if this continues  class a will naturally feel the danger of class b approaching them again  do you mind telling me your thoughts on this matter   it s true that our state of being left out in the cold can t be called good   he s not an ordinary person  for you who only face your problems head on  in a sense  it s no exaggeration to say that he s your greatest opponent   and then  the leader who brought them together and led them forward  horikita san  she has both excellent academic and physical abilities  and has recently joined the student council   sorry for continuing with the tough words  but i think it s only a matter of time before your class falls to class d   but what  are you going to talk about the value of effort and friendship  those kinds of abstract concepts   i didn t say that you haven t grown  it s just a matter of how much   if you look at the oaa  it s obvious at first glance that your class has grown the least out of the four when comparing the overall abilities of when we were 1st years to now  i thought you would ve done analysis on this level as well  is it that you knew  and pretended not to notice  or is it because you were afraid to face reality  that you didn t dare check   you re a smart student  if we were to compete on equal footing  you would definitely not be weaker than me  however  when you are in a disadvantageous situation  you can t demonstrate your strengths   i can say for sure now  that you have no chance at winning  ichinose san  the real reason drops  the alliance  ichinose names her fear  sakayanagi negotiates the pact   why don t you work with me  ichinose san   this is the only way you ll be able to catch up to my class   a cooperative relationship between classes isn t a bad thing  in fact  didn t you have a similar relationship with horikita san of class d when you were 1st years   what i m going to say is just speculation on my part  but i think you have already dissolved that partnership with horikita  even though they were last place  they were able to accumulate more class points than any other class last year  and are catching up with incredible momentum   that is  trust  ichinose san  i can say for sure that as long as we are joining forces  you would not betray me no matter what happens  that is a very important factor to consider when creating an alliance   just like last year  i am unable to move around the uninhabited island because of my handicap  however  i am allowed to participate in this exam  just in somewhat of a special position   students who are unable to participate due to ill health are eliminated from the start of the exam  right  however  i will be participating as a  semi eliminated  student   even though i can t walk around the island freely because of my legs  i have the right to remain at the starting point and compete within the same rules as everyone else  in other words  if you asked me for advice  i can help you  and if there s a difficult problem  we can solve it together  though  when i am the       only person left in the group  at that point the group will be eliminated   from my class  you are free to choose from 4 students   hashimoto kun  kitou kun  masumi san and myself  we are undoubtedly the main forces of class a  from class b  there are you and kanzaki kun  as well as shibata kun  right   i guess i ve underestimated you a little  ichinose san   if you work with me  i can give you three people s worth of deposits  i ll lend to you a total of 3 million points for the students who are at a high risk of expulsion  if they receive the penalty  you can use this to pay for their relief  to you  who doesn t want anyone to drop out more than any other class  this should be a proposal of great help to you   how greedy  although i was planning to spend a similar amount of money recently  i ll finance it specially  just for you   in order to maximize our chances of winning  it s necessary to start with giving the main force of class a the more people card  right   it s helpful that you understood so quickly   first place will be ours  i won t skimp on the efforts necessary for that  the trust factor is why sakayanagi chose her  the p 168 email assigns the more people card to class c s asakura mako and the nullify card to class a s yano koharu  while sakayanagi speaks of giving class a s main force the more people card   whether she means acquiring it or the print misaligns the two is left as printed  unresolved  the apex predator of the school  she deals from strength  she respects strength  she always closes  she recruits her into class a s banner  named class a main force  named class a main force   masumi san    presumably the class a one  hashimoto kito masumi sakayanagi  surname never printed on the page  noted  not resolved  she names him as a class b main force","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p203-1\">The café invitation to Ichinose<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.203–218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the Friday of the first weekend after group formation began, Sakayanagi contacts Ichinose on short notice; she lies about wanting to meet. She presses Ichinose on 2-C&#x27;s slide; the only catch-up left is the special exams; Ichinose wilts. The real reason drops: the alliance. Ichinose names her fear; Sakayanagi negotiates the pact.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “By the way, why did you accept my sudden request?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “That’s not what I meant. I’ve done some terrible things to you before, Ichinose-san. It wouldn’t be surprising if you hated me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “You’re definitely a good person, Ichinose-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As you wish, I’ll get to the point, but you might not be very comfortable with that either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Bluntly speaking, if this continues, Class A will naturally feel the danger of Class B approaching them again. Do you mind telling me your thoughts on this matter?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s true that our state of being left out in the cold can’t be called good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s not an ordinary person. For you who only face your problems head on, in a sense, it’s no exaggeration to say that he’s your greatest opponent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And then, the leader who brought them together and led them forward, Horikita-san. She has both excellent academic and physical abilities, and has recently joined the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry for continuing with the tough words, but I think it’s only a matter of time before your class falls to Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what? Are you going to talk about the value of effort and friendship, those kinds of abstract concepts?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t say that you haven’t grown. It’s just a matter of how much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you look at the OAA, it’s obvious at first glance that your class has grown the least out of the four when comparing the overall abilities of when we were 1st years to now. I thought you would’ve done analysis on this level as well… Is it that you knew, and pretended not to notice, or is it because you were afraid to face reality, that you didn’t dare check…”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a smart student. If we were to compete on equal footing, you would definitely not be weaker than me. However, when you are in a disadvantageous situation, you can’t demonstrate your strengths…”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can say for sure now, that you have no chance at winning, Ichinose-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why don’t you work with me? Ichinose-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is the only way you’ll be able to catch up to my class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A cooperative relationship between classes isn’t a bad thing. In fact, didn’t you have a similar relationship with Horikita-san of Class D when you were 1st years?”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I’m going to say is just speculation on my part, but I think you have already dissolved that partnership with Horikita. Even though they were last place, they were able to accumulate more class points than any other class last year, and are catching up with incredible momentum…”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That is— trust. Ichinose-san, I can say for sure that as long as we are joining forces, you would not betray me no matter what happens. That is a very important factor to consider when creating an alliance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just like last year, I am unable to move around the uninhabited island because of my handicap. However, I am allowed to participate in this exam, just in somewhat of a special position.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Students who are unable to participate due to ill health are eliminated from the start of the exam, right? However, I will be participating as a ‘semi-eliminated’ student.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though I can’t walk around the island freely because of my legs, I have the right to remain at the starting point and compete within the same rules as everyone else. In other words, if you asked me for advice, I can help you, and if there’s a difficult problem, we can solve it together. Though, when I am the …  …  only person left in the group, at that point the group will be eliminated.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From my class, you are free to choose from 4 students – Hashimoto-kun, Kitou-kun, Masumi-san and myself. We are undoubtedly the main forces of Class A. From Class B, there are you and Kanzaki-kun, as well as Shibata-kun, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess I’ve underestimated you a little, Ichinose-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you work with me, I can give you three people’s worth of deposits. I’ll lend to you a total of 3 million points for the students who are at a high risk of expulsion. If they receive the penalty, you can use this to pay for their relief. To you, who doesn’t want anyone to drop out more than any other class, this should be a proposal of great help to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How greedy. Although I was planning to spend a similar amount of money recently, I’ll finance it specially, just for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In order to maximize our chances of winning, it’s necessary to start with giving the main force of Class A the More People card… right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s helpful that you understood so quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First place will be ours. I won’t skimp on the efforts necessary for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The trust factor is why Sakayanagi chose her; the p.168 email assigns the More People card to Class C&#x27;s Asakura Mako and the Nullify card to Class A&#x27;s Yano Koharu, while Sakayanagi speaks of giving Class A&#x27;s main force the More People card — whether she means acquiring it or the print misaligns the two is left as printed, unresolved.<span class=\"pg\">p.211, 217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The apex predator of the school; she deals from strength; she respects strength; she always closes.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She recruits her into Class A&#x27;s banner.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">hashibuto-masayoshi<\/b> Named Class A main force.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Named Class A main force.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> “Masumi-san” — presumably the Class A one (Hashimoto/Kitō/Masumi/Sakayanagi); surname never printed on the page; noted, not resolved.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> She names him as a Class B main force.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y2v2-p15-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p204-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji coverage note  passing mentions  depending on the occasion  she might even ask a classmate like kanzaki for help   from class b  there are you and kanzaki kun  as well as shibata kun  right    said by sakayanagi  she names him as class b s main force   besides  if we need three classes  kanzaki from class c is still alone  and he should ve priority over ayanokouji    katsuragi s advice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p204-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p204-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.204–305<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Depending on the occasion, she might even ask a classmate like Kanzaki for help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “From Class B, there are you and Kanzaki-kun, as well as Shibata-kun, right?” — said by Sakayanagi; she names him as Class B’s main force.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Besides, if we need three classes, Kanzaki from Class C is still alone, and he should’ve priority over Ayanokouji.” — Katsuragi’s advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p46-1\">← Before: Kanzaki&#x27;s interrogation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p295-1\">→ After: Kanzaki at the convenience store<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p206-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei coverage note  passing mentions  although sakayanagi had a past dispute over leadership of their class with katsuragi  class a had almost twice as many points as ryuuen s class b and was the undisputed number one","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p206-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.206<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Although Sakayanagi had a past dispute over leadership of their class with Katsuragi, Class A had almost twice as many points as Ryuuen’s Class B and was the undisputed number one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p298-1\">→ After: The vendetta and the transfer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p215-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi named in passing  ch 3  hashimoto masayoshi   class a  named by sakayanagi at p 215 as a class a main force  with kito  kamuro and herself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p215-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Hashimoto Masayoshi — Class A; named by Sakayanagi at p.215 as a Class A main force (with Kitō, Kamuro and herself).<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p299-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p215-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kamuro-masumi","q":"kamuro masumi named in passing  ch 3  kamuro masumi    masumi san  named once at p 215 with no surname on the page  hashimoto kito masumi sakayanagi are the four class a names  presumably kamuro  unresolved  not decided","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kamuro-masumi.html#sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p215-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Kamuro Masumi — &quot;Masumi-san&quot; named once at p.215 with no surname on the page (Hashimoto/Kitō/Masumi/Sakayanagi are the four Class A names); presumably Kamuro; unresolved, not decided.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p299-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kitou-hayato-y2v2-p215-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kitou-hayato","q":"kito hayato named in passing  ch 3  kito hayato   class a  named by sakayanagi at p 215 as class a main force","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kitou-hayato-y2v2-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html#sc-kitou-hayato-y2v2-p215-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Kitō Hayato — Class A, named by Sakayanagi at p.215 as Class A main force.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p215-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"shibata-sou","q":"shibata so named in passing  ch 3  shibata sou   class b  named by sakayanagi at p 215 as a class b main force","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p215-1\">Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Shibata Sou — Class B, named by Sakayanagi at p.215 as a Class B main force.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p299-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p219-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the 1st year gathering  not present  he is not present in either the 1st year representatives  gathering or the housen amasawa nanase cafe scene  those scenes belong to yagami  utomiya  takahashi  housen  nanase and amasawa   see their person records","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p219-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p219-1\">The 1st-year gathering (not present)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.219–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is not present in either the 1st-year representatives’ gathering or the Housen–Amasawa–Nanase café scene; those scenes belong to Yagami, Utomiya, Takahashi, Housen, Nanase and Amasawa — see their person records.<span class=\"pg\">p.219–242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p203-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi and Ichinose (not present)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p243-1\">→ After: Kushida; the first-year defection<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p220-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi","q":"hosen kazuomi the representatives  gathering for weeks he has refused to parley  the three classes wait for july  he finally shows   don t call out my name like we re close  or i ll kill ya   so y all decided upon paying up   don t ya just start off like that   oh  you want to get in my way   huh  interesting  come and try  if you can   then let s see what ya got   looks like playing with ya is gonna be fun  i ll save it for next time   ah yea  it s a game   hey  hey  what do ya mean by that   ain t it just the small fry imploding as a result of fearing expulsion   and  you re saying it was me   ah  right  we could group up with the other classes in the next special exam   begin  who said i d join your little conversation   what if i said yes   your meek attitude is pissing me off  yagami  doesn t matter if they re 2nd or 3rd years  i have the confidence to crush them all   alright  i ll help you   what am i trying to do  didn t you guys want my help  ain t i just listening to ya cute wishes   the remaining two spots in the strongest team must be reserved for class d  that s a must   didn t i just say  my condition is that two students from class d must be in the group   i m not joking  if you don t like that  fuck off   do what ya want","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html#sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p220-1\">The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.220–235<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">For weeks he has refused to parley; the three classes wait for July; he finally shows.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> “Don’t call out my name like we’re close, or I’ll kill ya.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> “So y’all decided upon paying up?”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> “Don’t ya just start off like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? You want to get in my way?”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh, interesting. Come and try, if you can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then let’s see what ya got.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like playing with ya is gonna be fun. I’ll save it for next time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah yea, it’s a game.”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, hey, what do ya mean by that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ain’t it just the small fry imploding as a result of fearing expulsion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And, you’re saying it was me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, right, we could group up with the other classes in the next special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Begin? Who said I’d join your little conversation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What if I said yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your meek attitude is pissing me off, Yagami. Doesn’t matter if they’re 2nd or 3rd years, I have the confidence to crush them all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alright, I’ll help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What am I trying to do? Didn’t you guys want my help? Ain’t I just listening to ya cute wishes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The remaining two spots in the strongest team must be reserved for Class D. That’s a must.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t I just say? My condition is that two students from Class D must be in the group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not joking. If you don’t like that, fuck off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do what ya want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p236-1\">→ After: Housen takes the bounty deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p220-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"yagami-takuya","q":"yagami takuya coverage note  passing mentions  takuya yagami from class 1 b stood up and calmed those voices   both of you women are bolder than yagami and takahashi   after kushida and yagami left  i approached the convenience store   was it about yagami  or the special exam   even though yagami had already informed me on this matter  i pretended not to know about it   on the other hand  tsubaki also didn t mention my contact with yagami","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html#sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p220-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.220–269<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Takuya Yagami from Class 1-B stood up and calmed those voices.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “both of you women are bolder than Yagami and Takahashi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After Kushida and Yagami left, I approached the convenience store.”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Was it about Yagami, or the special exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Even though Yagami had already informed me on this matter, I pretended not to know about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “On the other hand, Tsubaki also didn’t mention my contact with Yagami.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p221-1\">→ After: The 1st-year representatives&#x27; gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p221-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yagami-takuya takahashi-osamu housen-kazuomi hatano utomiya-riku","q":"utomiya riku the representatives  gathering he shows up at the empty first year classroom  sent by his classmates who avoid troublesome matters   looks like only you re here now  yagami   although i don t think i m the type to be a leader  i came because the other students didn t want to come  while students in my class speak their minds freely in general  they don t have much taste for these troublesome matters   we ve recently lost a comrade  honestly  it s quite a heavy loss   he had once said to me that he wanted us to join the student council together and create a livelier environment for everyone in this school   do you think hosen will come   50 50  you seem to trust housen quite a bit  i bet he won t come at all   if he thinks he can simply force us to hand over our private points like that  he is too arrogant  if we can smoothly form the groups with all four classes this time  it would be meaningful  since we are facing the 2nd and 3rd years  we should cooperate  nevertheless  housen refused our offer   i understand that this is his strategy  however  it stands no chance of winning   we were told that this uninhabited island exam would also test skills other than academic ability  while class d is last place in terms of academic ability  their physical abilities are second in our year and only by a narrow margin to being the first  as a result  they might play an important role in the formation of optimal groups    housen arrives  the hatano accusation  the near fight  he grabs housen s arm   housen  don t bring your violent tendencies here   if it s necessary   unfortunately  i m not as kind as takahashi   do you think of violence as a game   how boring  but  if that s what you want  you don t have to wait until next time  i can take on the fight now  however  that is only if you promise not to attack any more of my classmates   i suspect that you re the one who got hatano expelled  he s not the kind of student who would easily break the school rules   i remember clearly the look on his face when he got expelled  he had been tricked by someone   who else could it possibly be  the negotiation closes  strongest four  two from class d  his reluctance yields to yagami   the benefits of cooperating with the other classes are too small  it s pointless  we re just giving up on class points   losing class points won t be our only concern if we end up becoming food for the upperclassmen   if we go with that strategy then we won t be able to make any difference to our current class standings    what are you trying to do  housen   but what if we can t form big groups at will   you ve got to be kidding  housen   you bastard   you re just going to give all the benefits to class d like this   if we let him take advantage of us now  he ll be sure to do it again   that   housen  no more demands  okay    i understand  cold  precise  willing to stand in front of a fist  his grief over hatano is the fuel  he yields only to coalition logic  they co chair the gathering  they disagree on class d  the peacekeeper between him and housen  he accuses  nearly fights  and swallows his pride for the pact  his class 1 c comrade  expelled  he suspects housen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html#sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p221-1\">The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.221–235<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He shows up at the empty first-year classroom, sent by his classmates who avoid troublesome matters. Housen arrives; the Hatano accusation; the near-fight; he grabs Housen&#x27;s arm. The negotiation closes: strongest four, two from Class D; his reluctance yields to Yagami.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/takahashi-osamu.html\">Takahashi Osamu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hatano\">Hatano<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> “Looks like only you’re here now, Yagami.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> “Although I don’t think I’m the type to be a leader, I came because the other students didn’t want to come. While students in my class speak their minds freely in general, they don’t have much taste for these troublesome matters.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> “We’ve recently lost a comrade. Honestly, it’s quite a heavy loss.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>31 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He had once said to me that he wanted us to join the student council together and create a livelier environment for everyone in this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think Hosen will come?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “50/50? You seem to trust Housen quite a bit. I bet he won’t come at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he thinks he can simply force us to hand over our private points like that, he is too arrogant. If we can smoothly form the groups with all four classes this time, it would be meaningful. Since we are facing the 2nd and 3rd years, we should cooperate. Nevertheless, Housen refused our offer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that this is his strategy. However, it stands no chance of winning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We were told that this uninhabited island exam would also test skills other than academic ability. While Class D is last place in terms of academic ability, their physical abilities are second in our year and only by a narrow margin to being the first. As a result, they might play an important role in the formation of optimal groups. ”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen, don’t bring your violent tendencies here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I’m not as kind as Takahashi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think of violence as a game?”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How boring, but, if that’s what you want, you don’t have to wait until next time. I can take on the fight now. However, that is only if you promise not to attack any more of my classmates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suspect that you’re the one who got Hatano expelled. He’s not the kind of student who would easily break the school rules.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I remember clearly the look on his face when he got expelled. He had been tricked by someone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who else could it possibly be?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The benefits of cooperating with the other classes are too small. It’s pointless. We’re just giving up on Class Points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Losing Class Points won’t be our only concern if we end up becoming food for the upperclassmen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we go with that strategy then we won’t be able to make any difference to our current class standings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… What are you trying to do? Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what if we can’t form big groups at will?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve got to be kidding, Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You bastard…”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re just going to give all the benefits to Class D like this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we let him take advantage of us now, he’ll be sure to do it again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That…”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen, no more demands. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… I understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold, precise, willing to stand in front of a fist; his grief over Hatano is the fuel; he yields only to coalition logic.<span class=\"pg\">p.221–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> They co-chair the gathering; they disagree on Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.221–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Takahashi Osamu<\/b> The peacekeeper between him and Housen.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> He accuses, nearly fights, and swallows his pride for the pact.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hatano<\/b> His Class 1-C comrade, expelled (he suspects Housen).<span class=\"pg\">p.222–235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p254-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p221-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yagami-takuya","q":"yagami takuya the 1st year representatives  gathering he arrives first at the corridor classroom  utomiya joins  they talk about hatano s expulsion and the rep system   hey utomiya kun  i was thinking you would be the person from class c to attend this gathering   isn t it because they believe you to be a reliable student that they sent you  i saw this month s updated oaa  and your social contribution has been raised to a b   about 50 50 chance he d come   if he fails to show up this time  then we ll just be forming groups within the remaining classes  with that  class d who were trying to extort us at high prices would be left alone  and their chances of winning would disappear as a result   it might seem like that on the surface  but i don t think that s housen kun s endgame   if he truly intended on carrying out this strategy  isn t that a blessing  that just means housen kun s not that much of a threat to our classes  takahashi arrives  talk turns to whether to include class d  housen appears   looks like you came after all  housen kun   that s such a bad joke  i am not giving you a penny   takahashi kun is right  the most important thing now is to focus on the uninhabited island exam    untagged in the translation  speakers unassigned as printed   we re wasting time  shall we begin   then why are you here  to simply pass the time   i don t believe that  you re not that stupid   of course  there are some individually outstanding students  however  you can t deny the fact that we are weaker in terms of overall ability  not everyone is as lucky as you  housen kun   that s why  i think it s necessary for us to join forces and at least form one strong  group of 4  in our year  just like what housen kun said  form a group with students that won t lose to the 2nd and 3rd years   because the rules of this exam makes cooperation within the same year difficult  it s hard for the 2nd and 3rd years who don t have much time left to squander this opportunity away to gain class points  on the other hand  we 1st years have more than two years left  which is why we should simply give up on the class points   of course  you re right  however  if we want to create a lot of strong groups from the get go  we ll have to consider the balance of each team  our opponents are older students  and they won t be easy to beat  that s why we should focus on forming a strongest team of 4 that can get first place  besides  it seems like it ll be difficult to form big groups freely during the official exam  and even if the older students cooperate with each other  they can only choose 3 people from 3 classes to work together   we can still form a really strong group if we ignore housen kun and cooperate with just three classes  but if we do that  we ll be on the same playing field as the other years  that s why i strongly hope that all four classes will cooperate with each other  not only for the sake of selecting strength from the classes but also because i think that it s essential for our class year to have a sense of unity to fight together in this exam  only us first years are allowed to form  a small group with up to 4 members  so we should take advantage of this rule  it would be a waste to throw away the upper hand that we were given   i fully understand that you have the ability to compete with the upperclassmen alone  which is why i hope you can lend us a hand   then  tell us your conditions   i see  if we can t group with the two class d students once the exam starts  then we would just clear it with the four of us   after all  if you ve already prepared the strongest small group of four  whether or not they merge into the big group shouldn t affect the result of the exam  right   calm down  utomiya kun  i m fine with this condition   the most important thing for us 1st years is to work together as a team and to not lose to the other years   then  do you think the outcome will be any different if we abandon housen kun s class d here   the most important thing in this exam is for us 1st years to win  if we do  nothing else can be considered as a loss   i agree  i understand how you feel  riku  but first  we must have the 1st years work together   lastly  there s one more thing i want to say  this is necessary for us first years to work together as a team  in order to avoid any disputes among us  i want to redistribute the item cards with rewarding effects in order to make the most out of them  it s also important to give students lacking the abilities half off cards and place them in the same group  are you fine with that  housen kun   at least  i think that all of us who participated here can be in the strongest team  of course that s including housen kun  right   well  let s carefully decide on that later  for now  isn t it already good enough that we re on the same page   if we work together  we can definitely get 1st place  let s first aim for that   it doesn t seem like we can  riku    untagged in the translation  speakers unassigned as printed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html#sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p221-1\">The 1st-year representatives&#x27; gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.221–235<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He arrives first at the corridor classroom; Utomiya joins; they talk about Hatano&#x27;s expulsion and the rep system. Takahashi arrives; talk turns to whether to include Class D; Housen appears.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> “Hey Utomiya-kun. I was thinking you would be the person from Class C to attend this gathering.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> “Isn’t it because they believe you to be a reliable student that they sent you? I saw this month’s updated OAA, and your Social Contribution has been raised to a B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> “About 50/50 chance he’d come?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he fails to show up this time, then we’ll just be forming groups within the remaining classes. With that, Class D who were trying to extort us at high prices would be left alone, and their chances of winning would disappear as a result.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It might seem like that on the surface, but I don’t think that’s Housen-kun’s endgame.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he truly intended on carrying out this strategy, isn’t that a blessing? That just means Housen-kun’s not that much of a threat to our classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you came after all, Housen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s such a bad joke. I am not giving you a penny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Takahashi-kun is right. The most important thing now is to focus on the uninhabited island exam.” — untagged in the translation; speakers unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re wasting time, shall we begin?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then why are you here? To simply pass the time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t believe that. You’re not that stupid.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, there are some individually outstanding students. However, you can’t deny the fact that we are weaker in terms of overall ability. Not everyone is as lucky as you, Housen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why— I think it’s necessary for us to join forces and at least form one strong ‘group of 4’ in our year. Just like what Housen-kun said, form a group with students that won’t lose to the 2nd and 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because the rules of this exam makes cooperation within the same year difficult, it’s hard for the 2nd and 3rd years who don’t have much time left to squander this opportunity away to gain Class Points. On the other hand, we 1st years have more than two years left, which is why we should simply give up on the Class Points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, you’re right. However, if we want to create a lot of strong groups from the get go, we’ll have to consider the balance of each team. Our opponents are older students, and they won’t be easy to beat. That’s why we should focus on forming a strongest team of 4 that can get first place. Besides, it seems like it’ll be difficult to form big groups freely during the official exam, and even if the older students cooperate with each other, they can only choose 3 people from 3 classes to work together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can still form a really strong group if we ignore Housen-kun and cooperate with just three classes, but if we do that, we’ll be on the same playing field as the other years. That’s why I strongly hope that all four classes will cooperate with each other, not only for the sake of selecting strength from the classes but also because I think that it’s essential for our class year to have a sense of unity to fight together in this exam. Only us first years are allowed to form ‘a small group with up to 4 members,’ so we should take advantage of this rule. It would be a waste to throw away the upper hand that we were given.”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I fully understand that you have the ability to compete with the upperclassmen alone, which is why I hope you can lend us a hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, tell us your conditions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. If we can’t group with the two Class D students once the exam starts, then we would just clear it with the four of us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After all, if you’ve already prepared the strongest small group of four, whether or not they merge into the big group shouldn’t affect the result of the exam, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, Utomiya-kun, I’m fine with this condition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The most important thing for us 1st years is to work together as a team and to not lose to the other years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, do you think the outcome will be any different if we abandon Housen-kun’s Class D here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The most important thing in this exam is for us 1st years to win. If we do, nothing else can be considered as a loss.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree. I understand how you feel, Riku, but first, we must have the 1st years work together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lastly, there’s one more thing I want to say. This is necessary for us first years to work together as a team. In order to avoid any disputes among us, I want to redistribute the item cards with rewarding effects in order to make the most out of them. It’s also important to give students lacking the abilities Half-Off cards and place them in the same group. Are you fine with that, Housen-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At least, I think that all of us who participated here can be in the strongest team, of course that’s including Housen-kun. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, let’s carefully decide on that later. For now, isn’t it already good enough that we’re on the same page?.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we work together, we can definitely get 1st place. Let’s first aim for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “It doesn’t seem like we can, Riku.” — untagged in the translation; speakers unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p220-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p246-1\">→ After: The walk to Keyaki Mall; the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hatano-y2v2-p222-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hatano","q":"hatano hatano  class 1 c  expelled  he had been one of the boys in class 1 c with an a in academic ability  the class 1 c classmates feel the loss  he wanted to join the student council with utomiya to make the school livelier  hatano was expelled from school  utomiya believes housen had something to do with it  the class lost 100 points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hatano-y2v2-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hatano (Class 1-C, expelled)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.222–229, 267<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hatano\">Hatano<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> He had been one of the boys in Class 1-C with an A in Academic Ability; the Class 1-C classmates feel the loss; he wanted to join the student council with Utomiya to make the school livelier.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Hatano was expelled from school; Utomiya believes Housen had something to do with it; the class lost 100 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hatano-y2v2-p229-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p223-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"utomiya-riku housen-kazuomi yagami-takuya takahashi-osamu","q":"takahashi osamu the representatives  gathering he arrives with a wave and a loud voice  good at getting along  many friends  his class leader sent him   oh  riku  takuya  as expected  it s you guys   the leader of my class is the type who dislikes these kinds of troublesome things  that s why i m the one coming to this discussion   anyway  let s calm down first  there s no way to have a discussion if you re belligerent from the start   then  now that everyone s here  let s start the conversation  the groups  hosen shoves him down  he jokes toward yagami ish calm  he mediates   you ve shown up at a great time  kazuomi   wait a minute  wait a minute  wait  i just slipped and fell  so calm down  riku   he s saying that s the case  no   calm down  both of you  if you start a fight here  you ll be doing exactly what kazuomi wants   ah  wait a moment  i have a question about what takuya said  why only make one team  all top three teams will get class points  right  if we also       take into consideration that we could merge into big groups during the official exam  isn t it better to form a lot more strong teams   so as long as we get 1st place  it doesn t matter what we sacrifice to achieve it   by the way  takuya  who do you plan to choose from class b   osamu kun  did you come because you were given this troublesome task again  and  so only kazuomi isn t here yet    untagged in the translation  speakers unassigned as printed   takahashi kun is right  the most important thing now is to focus on the uninhabited island exam    untagged  speakers unassigned as printed  the unofficial glue  peacekeeping officially  curious officially  he asks practical questions  why only one team  he smooths him  he takes a shove and jokes through it  he joins him in the cooperation camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p223-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/takahashi-osamu.html#sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p223-1\">The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.223–236<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/takahashi-osamu.html\">Takahashi Osamu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He arrives with a wave and a loud voice; good at getting along; many friends; his class leader sent him. Hōsen shoves him down; he jokes toward Yagami-ish calm; he mediates.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Takahashi Osamu<\/b> “Oh! Riku, Takuya. As expected, it’s you guys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Takahashi Osamu<\/b> “The leader of my class is the type who dislikes these kinds of troublesome things. That’s why I’m the one coming to this discussion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Takahashi Osamu<\/b> “Anyway, let’s calm down first. There’s no way to have a discussion if you’re belligerent from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, now that everyone’s here, let’s start the conversation. The groups—”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve shown up at a great time, Kazuomi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute, wait a minute, wait. I just slipped and fell, so calm down, Riku.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s saying that’s the case, no?”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, both of you. If you start a fight here, you’ll be doing exactly what Kazuomi wants.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, wait a moment. I have a question about what Takuya said. Why only make one team? All top three teams will get Class Points, right? If we also …  …  take into consideration that we could merge into big groups during the official exam, isn’t it better to form a lot more strong teams?”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So as long as we get 1st place, it doesn’t matter what we sacrifice to achieve it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, Takuya, who do you plan to choose from Class B?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Osamu-kun, did you come because you were given this troublesome task again?” and “So only Kazuomi isn&#x27;t here yet?” — untagged in the translation; speakers unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.223–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Takahashi-kun is right. The most important thing now is to focus on the uninhabited island exam.” — untagged; speakers unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The unofficial glue; peacekeeping officially; curious officially; he asks practical questions (why only one team).<span class=\"pg\">p.223–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> He smooths him.<span class=\"pg\">p.226–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> He takes a shove and jokes through it.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> He joins him in the cooperation camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.223–235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p240-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hatano-y2v2-p229-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hatano","q":"hatano coverage note  passing mentions  i remember clearly the look on his face when he got expelled  he had been tricked by someone   utomiya only realised this after his friend hatano had been forced to drop out due to housen s actions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hatano-y2v2-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.229, 270<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hatano\">Hatano<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I remember clearly the look on his face when he got expelled. He had been tricked by someone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Utomiya only realised this after his friend Hatano had been forced to drop out due to Housen’s actions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hatano-y2v2-p222-1\">← Before: Hatano (Class 1-C, expelled)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p236-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi nanase-tsubasa amasawa-ichika","q":"amasawa ichika the alliance terms with housen housen calls her to the cafe  nanase comes late  the three weigh the deal   the tick tock sound of the second hand going round  and round  and round is so annoying  i dislike these kinds of watches   worth  is it worth a lot  i don t have the time to care for things i hate   so  what do you want from me   you want me to help you out again  huh  and on the uninhabited island  are you thinking  bout doing something vulgar   want to see my panties  you can sneak a peek at them under the table     yeah   well  that s true  the other guys either knew about the bounty and didn t do anything  or wanted to do something but gave up halfway  20 million points is a large amount  isn t it normal to go all out   then what s my reward if i group with you  i m not cheap  yeah   equal  you have a cute face  but your words are so bitter  so this boldness is what housen kun likes about you   i see  so the group that housen kun was thinking of forming was the three of us  what about the fourth person   cocky  aren t you  but  it seems to me there s a lotta formidable upperclassmen compared to the first years though   well  even if you re the strongest  housen kun  didn t the 1st year agree to work together as four classes  if we re talking about the main force in class d  there s no doubt the two of you will be considered as such  right   well  teamwork probably won t be a thing if housen kun joins  in that sense  excluding him from the group is a safer option  anyway  let s go back to the topic  how much would you give me   there are no points for you  like i said earlier  you re on equal footing with us  of course  we will evenly split the extra private points our class gets from the rewards   you wanna test it now   woah  damn  you re pretty good aren t you  i love strong girls   maybe  you wanna test again   although i now know that nanase chan has considerable skill  i still don t think she and i are on equal footing   why  because two out of three of us are from class d   i don t care about that  it seems like the private points will be evenly split  but  it s you guys that asked for my help  so if i don t get extra it s kinda   since you re trying to bribe me  isn t it natural for me to increase my price   what an arrogant attitude  be it nanase or you  both of you women are bolder than yagami and takahashi   don t you know  nowadays  girls are the stronger ones   fine  i ll listen to what you have to say  what else do you want  besides the group rewards   i must receive all the points from the bounty to expel ayanokouji senpai  that s my condition for forming a group with you   so you are gonna say no  however  what will you do without me  if you don t have a comrade apart from nanase chan that you can trust  won t you have a difficult time during this special exam   besides  if i group up with housen kun  i ll be even more isolated in class a than i am now  so isn t it only natural for me to not say  yes  if i don t get the corresponding rewards that would compensate for that loss   it s true that if you give me the bounty for getting him expelled  you won t get any money  but the reputation for getting ayanokouji senpai expelled will be given entirely to you housen kun  is that enough for you to accept the condition   thanks  the fact that you re not a stingy guy is just brilliant   please take care of me during the official exam  she sets her price at the full bounty itself  housen agrees verbally without intent to pay  her reputation is the price she actually pays  the alliance partner  the equal footing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html#sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p236-1\">The alliance terms with Housen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.236–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Housen calls her to the cafe; Nanase comes late; the three weigh the deal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “The tick tock sound of the second hand going round, and round, and round is so annoying. I dislike these kinds of watches.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “Worth? Is it worth a lot? I don’t have the time to care for things I hate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “So, what do you want from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>29 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want me to help you out again, huh? And on the uninhabited island? Are you thinking ’bout doing something vulgar?”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Want to see my panties? You can sneak a peek at them under the table … , yeah?”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s true? The other guys either knew about the bounty and didn’t do anything, or wanted to do something but gave up halfway. 20 million points is a large amount, isn’t it normal to go all out?”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then what’s my reward if I group with you? I’m not cheap, yeah?”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Equal? You have a cute face, but your words are so bitter. So this boldness is what Housen-kun likes about you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So the group that Housen-kun was thinking of forming was the three of us. What about the fourth person?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cocky, aren’t you? But, it seems to me there’s a lotta formidable upperclassmen compared to the first-years though?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, even if you’re the strongest, Housen-kun… Didn’t the 1st year agree to work together as four classes? If we’re talking about the main force in Class D, there’s no doubt the two of you will be considered as such, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, teamwork probably won’t be a thing if Housen-kun joins. In that sense, excluding him from the group is a safer option. Anyway, let’s go back to the topic. How much would you give me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are no points for you. Like I said earlier, you’re on equal footing with us. Of course, we will evenly split the extra private points our class gets from the rewards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You wanna test it now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Woah. Damn, you’re pretty good aren’t you? I love strong girls.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe? You wanna test again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I now know that Nanase-chan has considerable skill, I still don’t think she and I are on equal footing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why? Because two out of three of us are from Class D?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t care about that. It seems like the private points will be evenly split, but…. it’s you guys that asked for my help, so if I don’t get extra it’s kinda…”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since you’re trying to bribe me, isn’t it natural for me to increase my price?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What an arrogant attitude. Be it Nanase or you, both of you women are bolder than Yagami and Takahashi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you know? Nowadays, girls are the stronger ones.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine, I’ll listen to what you have to say. What else do you want, besides the group rewards?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I must receive all the points from the bounty to expel Ayanokouji-senpai. That’s my condition for forming a group with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you are gonna say no? However, what will you do without me? If you don’t have a comrade apart from Nanase-chan that you can trust, won’t you have a difficult time during this special exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, if I group up with Housen-kun, I’ll be even more isolated in Class A than I am now, so isn’t it only natural for me to not say ‘yes’ if I don’t get the corresponding rewards that would compensate for that loss?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s true that if you give me the bounty for getting him expelled, you won’t get any money, but the reputation for getting Ayanokouji-senpai expelled will be given entirely to you Housen-kun. Is that enough for you to accept the condition?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks. The fact that you’re not a stingy guy is just brilliant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please take care of me during the official exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She sets her price at the full bounty itself; Housen agrees verbally without intent to pay; her reputation is the price she actually pays.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> The alliance partner.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> The equal footing.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p92-1\">← Before: The intrusion; the 20-million confirmation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p345-1\">→ After: SS: What is Reflected in Her Eyes (Amasawa POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p236-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika nanase-tsubasa yagami-takuya utomiya-riku takahashi-osamu housen-kazuomi","q":"hosen kazuomi housen takes the bounty deal amasawa calls him to the cafe  nanase joins  the three weigh the alliance   shut the fuck up  don t ya know how much this is worth   huh  this is exactly why girls are so boring   i called you out because of the upcoming uninhabited island exam  team up with me  amasawa   huh   so what  i ll crush them all   that s up to me  who s in charge of class d  to decide  understand   nanase and i  and you  we ll form a group of three  alright   there s no need to accept this condition  consider the future if class a gets an extra 20 million points   shut up  nanase   the bounty is yours   it s just a verbal agreement anyway  as long as it s clear i am the one who gets ayanakouji expelled  i ll be the one who receives the points  i don t care if she cries about it later   whether it be ayanokouji  ryuuen  or the others  whoever comes at me with their fangs  i ll crush them all  i m sick of being bogged down by the trash rules of this school  he signs away amasawa s fee  the 20m bounty  without intent to honor it  his condition for the alliance is his own dominance of class d  he courts her for the plan  she sets her price  she is leverage and friend  he toys with his proposal  then accepts  the hatano accusation hangs  he shoves him down","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html#sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p236-1\">Housen takes the bounty deal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.236–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Amasawa calls him to the cafe; Nanase joins; the three weigh the alliance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/takahashi-osamu.html\">Takahashi Osamu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> “Shut the fuck up. Don’t ya know how much this is worth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> “Huh? This is exactly why girls are so boring.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> “I called you out because of the upcoming uninhabited island exam. Team up with me, Amasawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what? I’ll crush them all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s up to me, who’s in charge of Class D, to decide. Understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nanase and I, and you. We’ll form a group of three. Alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need to accept this condition. Consider the future if Class A gets an extra 20 million points…”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shut up, Nanase.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The bounty is yours.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s just a verbal agreement anyway. As long as it’s clear I am the one who gets Ayanakouji expelled, I’ll be the one who receives the points. I don’t care if she cries about it later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether it be Ayanokouji, Ryuuen, or the others, whoever comes at me with their fangs, I’ll crush them all. I’m sick of being bogged down by the trash rules of this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He signs away Amasawa&#x27;s fee (the 20M bounty) without intent to honor it; his condition for the alliance is his own dominance of Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> He courts her for the plan; she sets her price.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She is leverage and friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> He toys with his proposal, then accepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> The Hatano accusation hangs.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Takahashi Osamu<\/b> He shoves him down.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-housen-kazuomi-y2v2-p220-1\">← Before: The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p236-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka nanase-tsubasa","q":"nanase tsubasa the alliance terms with housen she arrives late to the cafe  she checks the terms  she challenges amasawa once   we should be on equal footing  didn t i already say that before   you ve got guts  eh  trying it here   you re not bad yourself   nanase and i  and you  we ll form a group of three  alright   it s true that if you give me the bounty for getting him expelled  you won t get any money  but the reputation for getting ayanokouji senpai expelled will be given entirely to you housen kun  is that enough for you to accept the condition   shut up  nanase   are you sure about this   yeah   alright  since you re the one who makes the decision after all  but are you sure it s okay to trust amasawa san  i think she s the type who would betray her partners without giving it a second thought   trust  don t just assume that i trust her  that goes for you too  i don t trust either of you   then why did you decide to group up with her   i see  that may be true  even so  20 million points is too much   you really are a terrible person  she is the pressure holder  she tries to veto the amasawa deal and fails  she stays anyway   she has nowhere else to go  her class d co conspirator  the rival she cannot push out  she will be standing in the island exam against him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html#sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p236-1\">The alliance terms with Housen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.236–242<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She arrives late to the café; she checks the terms; she challenges Amasawa once.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “We should be on equal footing. Didn’t I already say that before?”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “You’ve got guts, eh? Trying it here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “You’re not bad yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nanase and I, and you. We’ll form a group of three. Alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s true that if you give me the bounty for getting him expelled, you won’t get any money, but the reputation for getting Ayanokouji-senpai expelled will be given entirely to you Housen-kun. Is that enough for you to accept the condition?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shut up, Nanase.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure about this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alright, since you’re the one who makes the decision after all. But are you sure it’s okay to trust Amasawa-san? I think she’s the type who would betray her partners without giving it a second thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Trust? Don’t just assume that I trust her. That goes for you too, I don’t trust either of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then why did you decide to group up with her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, that may be true. Even so, 20 million points is too much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really are a terrible person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is the pressure-holder; she tries to veto the Amasawa deal and fails; she stays anyway — she has nowhere else to go.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Her Class D co-conspirator.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> The rival she cannot push out.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She will be standing in the island exam against him.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p111-1\">← Before: The confession on the way to school<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p254-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p240-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"takahashi-osamu","q":"takahashi osamu coverage note  passing mentions  osamu kun  did you come because you were given this troublesome task again   both of you women are bolder than yagami and takahashi    amasawa   the first year students there were takahashi osamu kun and ishigami kyou kun from class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/takahashi-osamu.html#sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p240-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.240, 254<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/takahashi-osamu.html\">Takahashi Osamu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Osamu-kun, did you come because you were given this troublesome task again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “both of you women are bolder than Yagami and Takahashi.” — Amasawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The first year students there were Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyou-kun from Class A…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-takahashi-osamu-y2v2-p223-1\">← Before: The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p243-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou yagami-takuya nanase-tsubasa housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kushida  the first year defection after school the ayanokoji group gathers near his seat  kushida calls him  the 1st year wants a meeting   ayanokouji kun  can i talk to you for a second   actually  a 1st year student told me that they wanted to meet you  ayanokouji kun  is this a bad time   if that s the case  i don t think we can allow them to meet   eh  ah  that  it s actually a boy that wants to meet you  sorry   right  after all  our group isn t particularly good at interpersonal relationships  so it wouldn t be a bad thing if kiyotaka could gain some acquaintances in the 1st year   okay  what should i do   sorry about this  walking to keyaki mall  the 1st year arrives   takuya yagami of class 1 b   nice to meet you  ayanokouji senpai  thank you very much for taking your time to see me today   i believe you re in  class 1 b  right   yes  i m takuya yagami of class 1 b   standing is sort of  for the place  what about we go to my room to talk  the rare black tea i had ordered happened to arrive already  although it takes some time to steep  it s very delicious   ah  sorry yagami kun  but actually  ayanokouji kun has plans to meet up with his friends after this  so can we try to keep this within an hour   i see  that s fine  let s talk at the cafe in keyaki mall then   oh  by the way  the special exam on the uninhabited island is about to start  i heard that you guys had the same special exam last year   could you tell me about the rules and what happened  since we haven t experienced the exam as 1st years  we want to at least gather some information beforehand   are you surprised  that i have information about the 3rd years  keyaki mall cafe  yagami reveals the secret special exam   6 1st year reps summoned by nagumo with tsukishiro present  20m points on ayanokoji s head  he confirms he saw the 20m with his own eyes  he defects and warns   actually  you might think  why i am talking to you after all this time  but there s something i want to tell you  ayanokouji senpai  there s a special exam that only a very small of 1st year students have been informed about  you already know about this  right     why are you telling me now   i recently heard that housen kun had failed in his first attempt  however  ayanokouji senpai s left hand was injured in the process  i wouldn t have been surprised if he did something inhumane but this was beyond my expectations   well  there s really no denying it   in april  i received a notification about this  however  since i wasn t interested in getting paid for setting people up  i decided not to participate   for the sake of protecting the first year students  i was going to be a complete bystander  however  if i don t do anything about it  ayanokouji senpai  depending on the situation there s a possibility that the situation will also affect your classmate  kushida senpai  that s why i asked kushida senpai to help me out   excuse me  i have no idea what you guys are talking about   can i continue to talk like this   i ve got no right to stop you   it all started when i was contacted by president nagumo of the student council  he instructed that one or two representatives were to be sent from each class and would secretly gather in the student council room  actually  we were summoned there shortly after entering the school   the first year students there were takahashi osamu kun and ishigami kyou kun from class a  me from class b  utomiya riku kun from class c  and housen kazuomi kun and nanase tsubasa san from class d  a total of 6 students   eh  to get ayanokouji kun expelled   the special exam was to get the 2nd year student ayanokouji senpai expelled from the school   the deadline was the beginning of the 2nd semester  and you could use any means  in addition  we weren t allowed to tell anyone about the special exam     however  since utomiya and i were the only participants from our classes  we were allowed to tell one person in our classes about it to make it fair  but i didn t tell anyone  utomiya might have told someone though   the student council president nagumo senpai told the six of us that he ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled   th that s a lot of points  i is that sort of thing allowed   isn t it a bit strange that the student council president is conducting this special exam on his own   yes  i too think the problem lies in how i expressed it as  i m calling it a special test  but it would be easier to understand if you think of it as a challenge that president nagumo made up on his own and gave to the first year students   as far as i know  it s only ayanokouji senpai  as for why it s him  i don t think there s a specific reason behind that  president nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years  it was a simple game of chance  1 in 157   even if it s the student council president conducting this special exam on his own  how was he able to prepare 20 million points   yes  although it might not sound good  could it be a lie  a joke  i really can t believe he prepared 20 million points for an exam from an unknown source like this   wh why is it ayanokouji kun  are there no other students apart from him   in fact  i ve already confirmed with my own eyes that he has 20 million points   apart from the disagreeable content of the exam itself  there s nothing else unpleasant about it  i think that other than me  all the other students welcomed it  it s being treated as a legitimate special exam   no  it s not because we trust the president of the student council that we re participating in the exam   when the student council president announced the exam  the acting director was also present   that s all the information i have about this matter   although i m grateful that you told me about this  you might be putting yourself in some unnecessary danger by doing so   yagami kun  will you be alright  if this conversation is exposed   it s fine  kushida senpai  i didn t hear about any punishment for talking about this to anyone   plus i m already prepared to be hated by the 1st years  because i m going to have to face the other classes sooner or later   generally speaking  housen san from class 1 d is someone you need to be alert against  his complete disregard for the rules is very troublesome   i feel like this isn t something i should be telling you senpais  if i list the names of who to watch out for  they ll of course be marked by the senpais  while i think that is important for you to know  i don t think it s fair to them       if i tell you  although i already marked housen kun   i ll try to investigate in the next special exam  once i m sure that he s a threat  i ll tell you  ayanokouji senpai   be careful  yagami kun   yeah  also  after the exam on the uninhabited island is over  can i meet you alone for a bit  i d like to talk to you  kushida senpai   in any case  your information was very helpful  yagami  thank you   no problem   you saying that  is more than enough for me  if ayanokouji senpai drops out of the school  it s going tobe very hard on your class  kushida senpai  i really want you to graduate from class a  the cafe breaks up  kushida s face betrays something odd  she leaves on a cold  determined note about yagami   it doesn t make a difference either way   in other words   i ll have to get rid of him as soon as possible  yagami kun  that is   it would be hard   er to eliminate an underclassman compared to horikita and i   that only depends on the method   the more arrogant you are about your own excellence  the more simple you are  horikita san and youself are no exception to this   didn t you agree to a ceasefire   see you later  ayanokouji kun  the 6 named summoned reps  takahashi osamu  ishigami kyou  1 a  takuya yagami  1 b  utomiya riku  1 c  housen kazuomi  nanase tsubasa  1 d  amasawa s name is absent   a tell  tsukishiro was present  nagumo offered 20m   1 in 157  he confirmed nagumo has the points  he hasn t participated and won t  the 1st year who defects  he trades for nothing  she is calmly executing something beneath the surface  she s on the summoned list  he s on it too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p243-1\">Kushida; the first-year defection<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.243–262<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After school the Ayanokōji group gathers near his seat; Kushida calls him; the 1st year wants a meeting. Walking to Keyaki mall; the 1st year arrives — Takuya Yagami of Class 1-B. Keyaki mall café: Yagami reveals the secret special exam — 6 1st-year reps summoned by Nagumo with Tsukishiro present; 20M points on Ayanokōji&#x27;s head; he confirms he saw the 20M with his own eyes; he defects and warns. The cafe breaks up; Kushida&#x27;s face betrays something odd; she leaves on a cold, determined note about Yagami.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun, can I talk to you for a second?”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Actually, a 1st year student told me that they wanted to meet you, Ayanokouji-kun… Is this a bad time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “If that’s the case, I don’t think we can allow them to meet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>66 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Ah, that… It’s actually a boy that wants to meet you… Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. After all, our group isn’t particularly good at interpersonal relationships, so it wouldn’t be a bad thing if Kiyotaka could gain some acquaintances in the 1st year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. What should I do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry about this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nice to meet you, Ayanokouji-senpai. Thank you very much for taking your time to see me today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re in… Class 1-B, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’m Takuya Yagami of Class 1-B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Standing is sort of… for the place, what about we go to my room to talk? The rare black tea I had ordered happened to arrive already. Although it takes some time to steep, it’s very delicious!”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, sorry Yagami-kun, but actually, Ayanokouji-kun has plans to meet up with his friends after this, so can we try to keep this within an hour?”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, that’s fine. Let’s talk at the cafe in Keyaki mall then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, by the way, the special exam on the uninhabited island is about to start. I heard that you guys had the same special exam last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could you tell me about the rules and what happened? Since we haven’t experienced the exam as 1st years, we want to at least gather some information beforehand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you surprised? That I have information about the 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually— You might think, why I am talking to you after all this time, but there’s something I want to tell you, Ayanokouji-senpai. There’s a special exam that only a very small of 1st year students have been informed about. You already know about this, right? ”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are you telling me now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I recently heard that Housen-kun had failed in his first attempt. However, Ayanokouji-senpai’s left hand was injured in the process. I wouldn’t have been surprised if he did something inhumane but this was beyond my expectations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s really no denying it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In April, I received a notification about this. However, since I wasn’t interested in getting paid for setting people up, I decided not to participate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the sake of protecting the first year students, I was going to be a complete bystander. However, if I don’t do anything about it, Ayanokouji-senpai… depending on the situation there’s a possibility that the situation will also affect your classmate, Kushida-senpai. That’s why I asked Kushida-senpai to help me out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Excuse me, I have no idea what you guys are talking about…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I continue to talk like this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve got no right to stop you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It all started when I was contacted by President Nagumo of the student council. He instructed that one or two representatives were to be sent from each class and would secretly gather in the student council room. Actually, we were summoned there shortly after entering the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The first year students there were Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyou-kun from Class A, me from Class B, Utomiya Riku-kun from Class C, and Housen Kazuomi-kun and Nanase Tsubasa-san from Class D. A total of 6 students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh?! To get Ayanokouji-kun expelled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The special exam was to get the 2nd year student Ayanokouji-senpai expelled from the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The deadline was the beginning of the 2nd semester, and you could use any means. In addition, we weren’t allowed to tell anyone about the special exam … . However, since Utomiya and I were the only participants from our classes, we were allowed to tell one person in our classes about it to make it fair, but I didn’t tell anyone. Utomiya might have told someone though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student council president Nagumo-senpai told the six of us that he’ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Th-that’s a lot of points… I-is that sort of thing allowed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it a bit strange that the student council president is conducting this special exam on his own…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I too think the problem lies in how I expressed it as. I’m calling it a special test, but it would be easier to understand if you think of it as a challenge that President Nagumo made up on his own and gave to the first year students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As far as I know, it’s only Ayanokouji-senpai. As for why it’s him, I don’t think there’s a specific reason behind that. President Nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years’. It was a simple game of chance, 1 in 157.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if it’s the student council president conducting this special exam on his own, how was he able to prepare 20 million points?.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Although it might not sound good… Could it be a lie, a joke? I really can’t believe he prepared 20 million points for an exam from an unknown source like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why is it Ayanokouji-kun? Are there no other students apart from him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In fact, I’ve already confirmed with my own eyes that he has 20 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Apart from the disagreeable content of the exam itself, there’s nothing else unpleasant about it. I think that other than me, all the other students welcomed it. It’s being treated as a legitimate special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, it’s not because we trust the president of the student council that we’re participating in the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the student council president announced the exam, the acting director was also present.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s all the information I have about this matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I’m grateful that you told me about this, you might be putting yourself in some unnecessary danger by doing so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yagami-kun, will you be alright? If this conversation is exposed…”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s fine, Kushida-senpai. I didn’t hear about any punishment for talking about this to anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Plus I’m already prepared to be hated by the 1st years, because I’m going to have to face the other classes sooner or later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Generally speaking, Housen-san from Class 1-D is someone you need to be alert against. His complete disregard for the rules is very troublesome.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel like this isn’t something I should be telling you senpais. If I list the names of who to watch out for, they’ll of course be marked by the senpais. While I think that is important for you to know, I don’t think it’s fair to them …  …  if I tell you, although I already marked Housen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll try to investigate in the next special exam. Once I’m sure that he’s a threat, I’ll tell you, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be careful, Yagami-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Also… after the exam on the uninhabited island is over, can I meet you alone for a bit? I’d like to talk to you, Kushida-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In any case, your information was very helpful, Yagami. Thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problem.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You saying that, is more than enough for me. If Ayanokouji-senpai drops out of the school, it’s going tobe very hard on your class, Kushida-senpai. I really want you to graduate from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t make a difference either way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words—”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll have to get rid of him as soon as possible. Yagami-kun, that is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would be hard … er to eliminate an underclassman compared to Horikita and I.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That only depends on the method.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The more arrogant you are about your own excellence, the more simple you are. Horikita-san and youself are no exception to this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you agree to a ceasefire?”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The 6 named summoned reps: Takahashi Osamu, Ishigami Kyou (1-A); Takuya Yagami (1-B); Utomiya Riku (1-C); Housen Kazuomi, Nanase Tsubasa (1-D). Amasawa&#x27;s name is absent — a tell.<span class=\"pg\">p.254–258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Tsukishiro was present; Nagumo offered 20M; “1 in 157”; he confirmed Nagumo has the points; he hasn&#x27;t participated and won&#x27;t.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> The 1st-year who defects; he trades for nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.243–263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She is calmly executing something beneath the surface.<span class=\"pg\">p.243–263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She&#x27;s on the summoned list.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> He&#x27;s on it too.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p219-1\">← Before: The 1st-year gathering (not present)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\">→ After: Utomiya and Tsubaki at the convenience store<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p243-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka","q":"hasebe haruka haruka at the after school gathering she and airi and sakura wait by his seat  kushida calls him out to a meeting with a 1st year boy  she voices her veto on the meeting   if that s the case  i don t think we can allow them to meet  she is the one who arbitrarily decides he isn t allowed to go  then backs off once she hears the boy s name isn t a confession","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html#sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p243-1\">Haruka at the after-school gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.243–245<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Airi and Sakura wait by his seat; Kushida calls him out to a meeting with a 1st-year boy; she voices her veto on the meeting.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “If that’s the case, I don’t think we can allow them to meet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is the one who arbitrarily decides he isn&#x27;t allowed to go, then backs off once she hears the boy&#x27;s name isn&#x27;t a confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hasebe-haruka-y2v2-p179-1\">← Before: Haruka&#x27;s group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p243-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka yagami-takuya kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo the 1st year meeting set up  the cafe she calls him as the group leaves  the meet is arranged   ayanokouji kun  can i talk to you for a second   actually  a 1st year student told me that they wanted to meet you  ayanokouji kun  is this a bad time   if that s the case  i don t think we can allow them to meet    is that the case   eh  ah  that  it s actually a boy that wants to meet you  sorry   right  after all  our group isn t particularly good at interpersonal relationships  so it wouldn t be a bad thing if kiyotaka could gain some acquaintances in the 1st year    untagged banter from the girls  speakers unassigned as printed   okay  what should i do   that s fine   sorry about this   it s not a big deal  nobody in the group will complain about it   he seems to be heading this way already  so let s just wait here  so that we don t miss him  okay    that s true   ah  sorry yagami kun  but actually  ayanokouji kun has plans to meet up with his friends after this  so can we try to keep this within an hour   oh right  now that you mention it  the 3rd years also took the uninhabited island exam   excuse me  i have no idea what you guys are talking about   that s amazing  i don t have much confidence in my own writing   well  there s really no denying it   eh  to get ayanokouji kun expelled   th that s a lot of points  i is that sort of thing allowed   isn t it a bit strange that the student council president is conducting this special exam on his own   wh why is it ayanokouji kun  are there no other students apart from him   it doesn t make a difference either way   i ll have to get rid of him as soon as possible  yagami kun  that is   that only depends on the method   the more arrogant you are about your own excellence  the more simple you are  horikita san and youself are no exception to this   didn t you agree to a ceasefire   see you later  ayanokouji kun  yagami graduated from the same junior high school as she and horikita   he knows her past  she decides to get rid of him before he can present a threat to herself and to ak s ceasefire with horikita  she enables the meeting  she privately resolves to eliminate him  she runs interference for both sides  she means to manage the fallout","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p243-1\">The 1st-year meeting set-up; the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.243–262<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She calls him as the group leaves; the meet is arranged.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun, can I talk to you for a second?”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Actually, a 1st year student told me that they wanted to meet you, Ayanokouji-kun… Is this a bad time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “If that’s the case, I don’t think we can allow them to meet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… Is that the case?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? Ah, that… It’s actually a boy that wants to meet you… Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Right. After all, our group isn’t particularly good at interpersonal relationships, so it wouldn’t be a bad thing if Kiyotaka could gain some acquaintances in the 1st year.” — untagged banter from the girls; speakers unassigned as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. What should I do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s fine…”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry about this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not a big deal. Nobody in the group will complain about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He seems to be heading this way already, so let’s just wait here, so that we don’t miss him, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… That’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, sorry Yagami-kun, but actually, Ayanokouji-kun has plans to meet up with his friends after this, so can we try to keep this within an hour?”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh right, now that you mention it, the 3rd years also took the uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Excuse me, I have no idea what you guys are talking about…”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s amazing. I don’t have much confidence in my own writing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s really no denying it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh?! To get Ayanokouji-kun expelled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Th-that’s a lot of points… I-is that sort of thing allowed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it a bit strange that the student council president is conducting this special exam on his own…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why is it Ayanokouji-kun? Are there no other students apart from him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t make a difference either way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll have to get rid of him as soon as possible. Yagami-kun, that is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That only depends on the method.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The more arrogant you are about your own excellence, the more simple you are. Horikita-san and youself are no exception to this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you agree to a ceasefire?”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yagami graduated from the same junior high school as she and Horikita — he knows her past; she decides to get rid of him before he can present a threat to herself and to AK&#x27;s ceasefire with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.260–263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> She enables the meeting; she privately resolves to eliminate him.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She runs interference for both sides; she means to manage the fallout.<span class=\"pg\">p.243–263<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y2v2-p171-1\">← Before: Kushida redirects Ike<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p243-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito akito at his club he is at his club  others wait for him to return for keyaki mall  he is not at the after school gathering","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html#sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p243-1\">Akito at his club<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.243<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He is at his club; others wait for him to return for Keyaki mall; he is not at the after-school gathering.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y2v2-p179-1\">← Before: Miyake&#x27;s group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p243-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi the group after school after school the group waits by his seat  kushida calls him  yagami  a 1st year  wants a meeting  akito is at his club and missed the gathering","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p243-1\">The group after school<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.243–245<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After school the group waits by his seat; Kushida calls him; Yagami, a 1st year, wants a meeting.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Akito is at his club and missed the gathering.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y2v2-p179-1\">← Before: Sakura groups up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p246-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi tsukishiro utomiya-riku housen-kazuomi nanase-tsubasa takahashi-osamu yagami-takuya","q":"yagami takuya the walk to keyaki mall  the cafe he appears from the corridor corner  the rare black tea invite  kushida deflects for him  they compromise on the mall cafe   nice to meet you  ayanokouji senpai  thank you very much for taking your time to see me today   standing is sort of  for the place  what about we go to my room to talk  the rare black tea i had ordered happened to arrive already  although it takes some time to steep  it s very delicious   i see  that s fine  let s talk at the cafe in keyaki mall then   oh  by the way  the special exam on the uninhabited island is about to start  i heard that you guys had the same special exam last year   could you tell me about the rules and what happened  since we haven t experienced the exam as 1st years  we want to at least gather some information beforehand   are you surprised  that i have information about the 3rd years  the cafe table  tsubaki stations herself behind  he defects and gives the briefing   just a minute   my grandfather told me that even if i m not good at studying  i should still be able to write well   yes  because my grandfather is a calligraphy teacher   actually  you might think  why i am talking to you after all this time  but there s something i want to tell you  ayanokouji senpai  there s a special exam that only a very small of 1st year students have been informed about  you already know about this  right     in april  i received a notification about this  however  since i wasn t interested in getting paid for setting people up  i decided not to participate   i recently heard that housen kun had failed in his first attempt  however  ayanokouji senpai s left hand was injured in the process  i wouldn t have been surprised if he did something inhumane but this was beyond my expectations   for the sake of protecting the first year students  i was going to be a complete bystander  however  if i don t do anything about it  ayanokouji senpai  depending on the situation there s a possibility that the situation will also affect your classmate  kushida senpai  that s why i asked kushida senpai to help me out   can i continue to talk like this   it all started when i was contacted by president nagumo of the student council  he instructed that one or two representatives were to be sent from each class and would secretly gather in the student council room  actually  we were summoned there shortly after entering the school   the first year students there were takahashi osamu kun and ishigami kyou kun from class a  me from class b  utomiya riku kun from class c  and housen kazuomi kun and nanase tsubasa san from class d  a total of 6 students   the special exam was to get the 2nd year student ayanokouji senpai expelled from the school   the deadline was the beginning of the 2nd semester  and you could use any means  in addition  we weren t allowed to tell anyone about the special exam     however  since utomiya and i were the only participants from our classes  we were allowed to tell one person in our classes about it to make it fair  but i didn t tell anyone  utomiya might have told someone though   the student council president nagumo senpai told the six of us that he ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled   i too think the problem lies in how i expressed it as  i m calling it a special test  but it would be easier to understand if you think of it as a challenge that president nagumo made up on his own and gave to the first year students   wh why is it ayanokouji kun  are there no other students apart from him   as far as i know  it s only ayanokouji senpai  as for why it s him  i don t think there s a specific reason behind that  president nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years  it was a simple game of chance  1 in 157   yes  although it might not sound good  could it be a lie  a joke  i really can t believe he prepared 20 million points for an exam from an unknown source like this   in fact  i ve already confirmed with my own eyes that he has 20 million points   apart from the disagreeable content of the exam itself  there s nothing else unpleasant about it  i think that other than me  all the other students welcomed it  it s being treated as a legitimate special exam   no  it s not because we trust the president of the student council that we re participating in the exam   when the student council president announced the exam  the acting director was also present   it s fine  kushida senpai  i didn t hear about any punishment for talking about this to anyone   plus i m already prepared to be hated by the 1st years  because i m going to have to face the other classes sooner or later   yeah   generally speaking  housen san from class 1 d is someone you need to be alert against  his complete disregard for the rules is very troublesome   i feel like this isn t something i should be telling you senpais  if i list the names of who to watch out for  they ll of course be marked by the senpais  while i think that is important for you to know  i don t think it s fair to them       if i tell you  although i already marked housen kun   i ll try to investigate in the next special exam  once i m sure that he s a threat  i ll tell you  ayanokouji senpai   yeah  also  after the exam on the uninhabited island is over  can i meet you alone for a bit  i d like to talk to you  kushida senpai   no problem  i felt bad that you were the only one at a disadvantage  ayanokouji senpai   you saying that  is more than enough for me  if ayanokouji senpai drops out of the school  it s going tobe very hard on your class  kushida senpai  i really want you to graduate from class a   you have plans   no  i just want to stay out of sight from the other 1st years  yagami is 1 b s leader  a in academics  c  in physical  his grandfather a calligraphy teacher  he was secretly summoned in april with five others  he never told anyone  he confirmed nagumo has the 20m  tsukishiro was present  he wants to confess to kushida after the island exam  warm  precise  principled  a defensive fighter who strikes pre emptively  uniquely dangerous to himself  his middle school senpai  he intends to speak to her alone after the exam  he warns him for nothing in return  the summoner  the 20m pot holder  he confirms the acting director was present at the announcement  his co conspirator from class 1 c  who may have told someone  he s on the summoned list  she s on it too  he s on it too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html#sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p246-1\">The walk to Keyaki Mall; the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.246–251<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He appears from the corridor corner; the rare black tea invite; Kushida deflects for him; they compromise on the mall café. The café table; Tsubaki stations herself behind; he defects and gives the briefing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> “Nice to meet you, Ayanokouji-senpai. Thank you very much for taking your time to see me today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> “Standing is sort of… for the place, what about we go to my room to talk? The rare black tea I had ordered happened to arrive already. Although it takes some time to steep, it’s very delicious!”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> “I see, that’s fine. Let’s talk at the cafe in Keyaki mall then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>45 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, by the way, the special exam on the uninhabited island is about to start. I heard that you guys had the same special exam last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could you tell me about the rules and what happened? Since we haven’t experienced the exam as 1st years, we want to at least gather some information beforehand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you surprised? That I have information about the 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just a minute.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My grandfather told me that even if I’m not good at studying, I should still be able to write well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, because my grandfather is a calligraphy teacher.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually— You might think, why I am talking to you after all this time, but there’s something I want to tell you, Ayanokouji-senpai. There’s a special exam that only a very small of 1st year students have been informed about. You already know about this, right? ”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In April, I received a notification about this. However, since I wasn’t interested in getting paid for setting people up, I decided not to participate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I recently heard that Housen-kun had failed in his first attempt. However, Ayanokouji-senpai’s left hand was injured in the process. I wouldn’t have been surprised if he did something inhumane but this was beyond my expectations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the sake of protecting the first year students, I was going to be a complete bystander. However, if I don’t do anything about it, Ayanokouji-senpai… depending on the situation there’s a possibility that the situation will also affect your classmate, Kushida-senpai. That’s why I asked Kushida-senpai to help me out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I continue to talk like this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It all started when I was contacted by President Nagumo of the student council. He instructed that one or two representatives were to be sent from each class and would secretly gather in the student council room. Actually, we were summoned there shortly after entering the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The first year students there were Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyou-kun from Class A, me from Class B, Utomiya Riku-kun from Class C, and Housen Kazuomi-kun and Nanase Tsubasa-san from Class D. A total of 6 students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The special exam was to get the 2nd year student Ayanokouji-senpai expelled from the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The deadline was the beginning of the 2nd semester, and you could use any means. In addition, we weren’t allowed to tell anyone about the special exam … . However, since Utomiya and I were the only participants from our classes, we were allowed to tell one person in our classes about it to make it fair, but I didn’t tell anyone. Utomiya might have told someone though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student council president Nagumo-senpai told the six of us that he’ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I too think the problem lies in how I expressed it as. I’m calling it a special test, but it would be easier to understand if you think of it as a challenge that President Nagumo made up on his own and gave to the first year students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why is it Ayanokouji-kun? Are there no other students apart from him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As far as I know, it’s only Ayanokouji-senpai. As for why it’s him, I don’t think there’s a specific reason behind that. President Nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years’. It was a simple game of chance, 1 in 157.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Although it might not sound good… Could it be a lie, a joke? I really can’t believe he prepared 20 million points for an exam from an unknown source like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In fact, I’ve already confirmed with my own eyes that he has 20 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Apart from the disagreeable content of the exam itself, there’s nothing else unpleasant about it. I think that other than me, all the other students welcomed it. It’s being treated as a legitimate special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, it’s not because we trust the president of the student council that we’re participating in the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the student council president announced the exam, the acting director was also present.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s fine, Kushida-senpai. I didn’t hear about any punishment for talking about this to anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Plus I’m already prepared to be hated by the 1st years, because I’m going to have to face the other classes sooner or later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Generally speaking, Housen-san from Class 1-D is someone you need to be alert against. His complete disregard for the rules is very troublesome.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel like this isn’t something I should be telling you senpais. If I list the names of who to watch out for, they’ll of course be marked by the senpais. While I think that is important for you to know, I don’t think it’s fair to them …  …  if I tell you, although I already marked Housen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll try to investigate in the next special exam. Once I’m sure that he’s a threat, I’ll tell you, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Also… after the exam on the uninhabited island is over, can I meet you alone for a bit? I’d like to talk to you, Kushida-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problem. I felt bad that you were the only one at a disadvantage, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You saying that, is more than enough for me. If Ayanokouji-senpai drops out of the school, it’s going tobe very hard on your class, Kushida-senpai. I really want you to graduate from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have plans?”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I just want to stay out of sight from the other 1st years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yagami is 1-B&#x27;s leader, A in academics, C+ in physical, his grandfather a calligraphy teacher; he was secretly summoned in April with five others; he never told anyone; he confirmed Nagumo has the 20M; Tsukishiro was present; he wants to confess to Kushida after the island exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Warm, precise, principled; a defensive fighter who strikes pre-emptively; uniquely dangerous to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> His middle-school senpai; he intends to speak to her alone after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He warns him for nothing in return.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The summoner; the 20M pot holder.<span class=\"pg\">p.254–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> He confirms the Acting Director was present at the announcement.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> His co-conspirator from Class 1-C, who may have told someone.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> He&#x27;s on the summoned list.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She&#x27;s on it too.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Takahashi Osamu<\/b> He&#x27;s on it too.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yagami-takuya-y2v2-p221-1\">← Before: The 1st-year representatives&#x27; gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishigami-kyou-y2v2-p254-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ishigami-kyou","q":"ishigami kyo coverage note  passing mentions  the first year students there were takahashi osamu kun and ishigami kyou kun from class a  me from class b  utomiya riku kun from class c  and housen kazuomi kun and nanase tsubasa san from class d","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishigami-kyou-y2v2-p254-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ishigami-kyou.html#sc-ishigami-kyou-y2v2-p254-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.254<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The first year students there were Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyou-kun from Class A, me from Class B, Utomiya Riku-kun from Class C, and Housen Kazuomi-kun and Nanase Tsubasa-san from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p254-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"nanase-tsubasa","q":"nanase tsubasa coverage note  passing mentions  the first year students there were takahashi osamu kun and ishigami kyou kun from class a  me from class b  utomiya riku kun from class c  and housen kazuomi kun and nanase tsubasa san from class d  a total of 6 students","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p254-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html#sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p254-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.254<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “The first year students there were Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyou-kun from Class A, me from Class B, Utomiya Riku-kun from Class C, and Housen Kazuomi-kun and Nanase Tsubasa-san from Class D. A total of 6 students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p236-1\">← Before: The alliance terms with Housen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p336-1\">→ After: Nanase renews her vow<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p254-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"utomiya-riku","q":"utomiya riku coverage note  passing mentions  utomiya riku kun from class c    the yagami summon list   utomiya and i were the only participants from our classes  we were allowed to tell one person in our classes about it to make it fair  but i didn t tell anyone  utomiya might have told someone though","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p254-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html#sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p254-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.254–255<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Utomiya Riku-kun from Class C” — the Yagami summon list.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Utomiya and I were the only participants from our classes, we were allowed to tell one person in our classes about it to make it fair, but I didn’t tell anyone. Utomiya might have told someone though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p221-1\">← Before: The representatives&#x27; gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p264-1\">→ After: The Hōsen plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p255-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune coverage note  passing mentions  gives horikita a clear direction to proceed    horikita s consideration of nagumo tsukishiro  tracked in yagami s briefing context  the line names horikita   horikita manabu    the hit on this page names her brother  see horikita manabu md  p 276   you or horikita manabu    her brother  on this page  see horikita manabu md  p 289   horikita manabu    her brother left  see horikita manabu md  p 291","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p255-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p255-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.255, 276, 289, 291<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “gives Horikita a clear direction to proceed.” — Horikita&#x27;s consideration of Nagumo/Tsukishiro, tracked in Yagami&#x27;s briefing context (the line names Horikita).<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita Manabu” — the hit on this page names her brother; see horikita-manabu.md, p.276.<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “you or Horikita Manabu” — her brother, on this page; see horikita-manabu.md, p.289.<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Horikita Manabu.” — her brother left; see horikita-manabu.md, p.291.<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p174-1\">← Before: The Trial card; the Ike plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p316-1\">→ After: The Horikita–Ibuki summit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p258-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"tsubaki-sakurako","q":"tsubaki sakurako tsubaki at the cafe she stations herself behind yagami with a good view of ayanokoji and the group  she takes out her phone  she is either following ayanokoji or yagami  both contacts now revealed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p258-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html#sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p258-1\">Tsubaki at the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.258<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She stations herself behind Yagami with a good view of Ayanokōji and the group; she takes out her phone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is either following Ayanokōji or Yagami; both contacts now revealed.<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p264-1\">→ After: The Hōsen plan at the convenience store<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"tsubaki-sakurako utomiya-riku housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka utomiya and tsubaki at the convenience store he exits the store to meet keisei  tsubaki appears  she and utomiya table the hosen plan   umm   hello tsubaki  what can i do for you   i d like to talk to you about something  could you wait outside for me   sorry to keep you waiting   there is something that we wanted to tell you  that s why i approached you   is it utomiya   looks like i was right   sorry  for having to talk to you like this   it s about housen kazuomi   we want to take housen by surprise on the uninhabited island exam   housen doesn t have many private points right now  in other words  if he withdraws from the exam  even as a first year student who gets a lighter penalty  he won t be able to pay for his relief   are you trying to force housen out of the school   yes  right  that s it   in class c  a boy named hatano was expelled from the school  i think housen had something to do with it   i guess i know the reason now  but what does it have to do with me   housen hasn t formed any alliances with people outside his class  however  he has formed a partnership with you  ayanokouji senpai   please lend me your hand   i can t give you an answer when we don t even know what s going to be on the exam   then  could you keep this in mind  we re willing to pay you a large sum of points if you re able to get housen expelled from this school   didn t you get that injury on your left hand after you fought with housen   because we were also aiming for the 20 million point bounty   but  even if i had partnered up with tsubaki  you still wouldn t have been able to force me out of the school   we can t answer that   if we get you expelled  news of that ll spread throughout the school  we ll be enemies with the 2nd year class d  them hating the people who got their       classmate expelled is to be expected   then wouldn t it be the same if housen was expelled   no  the reason for that is because all the class 1 d students are afraid of housen  rather  there re a lot of students who wish that he be expelled   anyway  remember  please remember this  the only thing we care about is defeating housen  they don t ask him to expel housen  they ask him to keep an eye out  he says nothing  he leaves them both in ambiguity  he wants to use him against housen  she manages the door  the target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\">Utomiya and Tsubaki at the convenience store<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.264–270<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He exits the store to meet Keisei; Tsubaki appears; she and Utomiya table the Hōsen plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “Umm…”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hello Tsubaki. What can I do for you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “I’d like to talk to you about something. Could you wait outside for me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry to keep you waiting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is something that we wanted to tell you, that’s why I approached you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it Utomiya?”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like I was right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. For having to talk to you like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about Housen Kazuomi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We want to take Housen by surprise on the uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen doesn’t have many private points right now. In other words, if he withdraws from the exam. Even as a first year student who gets a lighter penalty, he won’t be able to pay for his relief.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you trying to force Housen out of the school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Right, that’s it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In Class C, a boy named Hatano was expelled from the school. I think Housen had something to do with it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess I know the reason now, but what does it have to do with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen hasn’t formed any alliances with people outside his class. However, he has formed a partnership with you, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please lend me your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t give you an answer when we don’t even know what’s going to be on the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, could you keep this in mind? We’re willing to pay you a large sum of points if you’re able to get Housen expelled from this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you get that injury on your left hand after you fought with Housen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because we were also aiming for the 20 million point bounty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, even if I had partnered up with Tsubaki, you still wouldn’t have been able to force me out of the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can’t answer that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we get you expelled, news of that’ll spread throughout the school. We’ll be enemies with the 2nd year Class D. Them hating the people who got their …  …  classmate expelled is to be expected.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then wouldn’t it be the same if Housen was expelled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. The reason for that is because all the Class 1-D students are afraid of Housen. Rather, there’re a lot of students who wish that he be expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, remember. Please remember this. The only thing we care about is defeating Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> They don&#x27;t ask him to expel Housen; they ask him to keep an eye out; he says nothing; he leaves them both in ambiguity.<span class=\"pg\">p.266–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> He wants to use him against Housen.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> She manages the door.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> The target.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p243-1\">← Before: Kushida; the first-year defection<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p271-1\">→ After: Kiriyama&#x27;s warning; Kiryūin&#x27;s attentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p264-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka utomiya-riku yagami-takuya tsubaki-sakurako","q":"tsubaki sakurako the hosen plan at the convenience store she grabs a lollipop as cover and calls for utomiya outside the store   umm   i d like to talk to you about something  could you wait outside for me   sorry to keep you waiting   there is something that we wanted to tell you  that s why i approached you   is it utomiya   looks like i was right   i guess i know the reason now  but what does it have to do with me   didn t you get that injury on your left hand after you fought with housen   because we were also aiming for the 20 million point bounty  she keeps the conversation short and the meeting friendly  she does not reveal yagami s disclosure to him  and he does not reveal hers  she wants him on board against housen  her classmate  she helps him talk him into it  she observed his cafe meet with ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p264-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html#sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p264-1\">The Hōsen plan at the convenience store<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.264–270<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She grabs a lollipop as cover and calls for Utomiya outside the store.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “Umm…”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “I’d like to talk to you about something. Could you wait outside for me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “Sorry to keep you waiting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is something that we wanted to tell you, that’s why I approached you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it Utomiya?”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like I was right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess I know the reason now, but what does it have to do with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you get that injury on your left hand after you fought with Housen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because we were also aiming for the 20 million point bounty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She keeps the conversation short and the meeting friendly; she does not reveal Yagami&#x27;s disclosure to him, and he does not reveal hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.268–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She wants him on board against Housen.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> Her classmate; she helps him talk him into it.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> She observed his café meet with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p258-1\">← Before: Tsubaki at the café<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p351-1\">→ After: SS: What Could Be Seen From That Back (Tsubaki POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p264-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsubaki-sakurako housen-kazuomi utomiya-riku","q":"utomiya riku the hosen plan he shows up at the convenience store when ayanokoji is about to meet keisei   sorry  for having to talk to you like this   it s about housen kazuomi   ayanokouji senpai  in the april special exam  you teamed up with housen   we want to take housen by surprise on the uninhabited island exam   housen doesn t have many private points right now  in other words  if he withdraws from the exam  even as a first year student who gets a lighter penalty  he won t be able to pay for his relief   are you trying to force housen out of the school   in class c  a boy named hatano was expelled from the school  i think housen had something to do with it   of course  i d be lying if i said i didn t hate him  nonetheless  what s most important is to prevent another unprepared person from being expelled   yes  thanks to him  our class lost 100 points   housen hasn t formed any alliances with people outside his class  however  he has formed a partnership with you  ayanokouji senpai   please lend me your hand   then  could you keep this in mind  we re willing to pay you a large sum of points if you re able to get housen expelled from this school   that   we can t answer that   i apologize for that  we ve already given up on the bounty   if we get you expelled  news of that ll spread throughout the school  we ll be enemies with the 2nd year class d  them hating the people who got their       classmate expelled is to be expected   no  the reason for that is because all the class 1 d students are afraid of housen  rather  there re a lot of students who wish that he be expelled   anyway  remember  please remember this  the only thing we care about is defeating housen  he wants him on board against housen  his classmate  the lollipop  she helps  the target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p264-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html#sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p264-1\">The Hōsen plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.264–270<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He shows up at the convenience store when Ayanokōji is about to meet Keisei.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> “Sorry. For having to talk to you like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> “It’s about Housen Kazuomi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> “Ayanokouji-senpai. In the April special exam, you teamed up with Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We want to take Housen by surprise on the uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen doesn’t have many private points right now. In other words, if he withdraws from the exam. Even as a first year student who gets a lighter penalty, he won’t be able to pay for his relief.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you trying to force Housen out of the school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In Class C, a boy named Hatano was expelled from the school. I think Housen had something to do with it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, I’d be lying if I said I didn’t hate him. Nonetheless, what’s most important is to prevent another unprepared person from being expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Thanks to him, our class lost 100 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Housen hasn’t formed any alliances with people outside his class. However, he has formed a partnership with you, Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please lend me your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, could you keep this in mind? We’re willing to pay you a large sum of points if you’re able to get Housen expelled from this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That.”<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can’t answer that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I apologize for that. We’ve already given up on the bounty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we get you expelled, news of that’ll spread throughout the school. We’ll be enemies with the 2nd year Class D. Them hating the people who got their …  …  classmate expelled is to be expected.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. The reason for that is because all the Class 1-D students are afraid of Housen. Rather, there’re a lot of students who wish that he be expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, remember. Please remember this. The only thing we care about is defeating Housen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He wants him on board against Housen.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> His classmate; the lollipop; she helps.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> The target.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-utomiya-riku-y2v2-p254-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p271-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto kiryuin-fuuka nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kiriyama s warning  kiryuin s attentions on his way to keyaki mall  kiriyama intercepts him  the conversation turns to the island exam and nagumo   you re here   what does the vice president want with me   don t be in such a hurry to get this done with  it s going to take some time today   the large scale uninhabited island exam is coming at the end of the month  are you prepared   i feel i ve done everything i can  how about you  vice president kiriyama   i ve formed a group of 3 without anyone from class a   i know what you must be thinking  if our class 3 b wanted to reach class a  then it s a must to win first place with a team with only our class  not only that  we would have to continue to win the following special exams by a landslide  however  that s not realistic   i wanted to personally battle nagumo in this special exam   it s been a long time since we lost the battle with nagumo and fell into class b  after which  nagumo became the student council president  and took control over the entire 3rd year  and eventually the entire school  it s safe to say that the battle of the classes has already been decided   but based on my evaluation of myself  i don t think i m any weaker than nagumo   you can form a big group of up to 6 people regardless of class  in order to win  you ll have to have an eye for talent and the ability to get people to join you  in that aspect  i don t think i can lose to nagumo   i understand where you re going with this  but is it really necessary to specifically tell me this   i don t want you to get in my way   i m not interested in your duel with the president anyway   i know that  but what i m trying to say is  i don t want to be distracted by any outsiders   outsiders   i m referring to horikita suzune  who just joined the student council   i see  it looks like she s in your way  however i want to at least tell you that i sent horikita suzune to the student council on the wish of her brother  the former student council president   there s already no point to it  he s only got a few months left as student council president  if we could do something starting from now  it wouldn t be to take his presidency  but rather to settle a personal dispute with him   that won t work  forget all thoughts about dealing with nagumo  it ll only lead to unnecessary fights   to put it politely  don t do anything   i know  i ve made myself clear on that  right   then  you swear you won t do anything  can i interpret it like that   how you interpret it is your choice  but i didn t make any promises   nagumo was more or less aware of what i d been doing with horikita senpai  but since i d been following his orders  he remained calm and simply observed what happened  horikita senpai s sister joining the student council was annoying enough  so if you don t stop meddling in this   are you in trouble  vice president   yeah   nagumo s idea  the one in which anyone can graduate from class a  you want that chance   well   anyway  you should have understood what i want to say by now   i understand  when horikita joined the student council  she was supposed to be introduced to the other members later on  but you came early  vice president  i know the reason for that   say whatever you want  kiryuin fuuka intervenes on the bench  ayanokoji is left alone with her   kiriyama   fufu  you re with an interesting underclassman  so i said hello   ayanokouji       kiyotaka  right  i heard you became famous after a perfect score on a difficult math test   what do you want from me   what are you doing  ayanokouji  we re leaving   you won t get anything from being with a guy like that  you know   staying with you is meaningless   ayanokouji s the one who should decide that  right  kiriyama  can t you leave any quicker   would you like to join me in a meaningful conversation   you can ignore that woman   don t praise me like that  i m getting embarrassed   she s just a good student  but kiryuuin doesn t have anyone supporting her  unlike nagumo  she doesn t even have a single friend   she s a lot like kouenji from your year  all her words and actions  if you take her seriously  you ll just be wasting your time   thanks for the compliments  kiriyama   it s enough as long as i can figure out what sort of person you are   being interested and cooperating are 2 completely different things  aren t they  there are some interesting people in my class  and sometimes i want to have a friendly conversation with them  just like what i m doing with you now   i m not interested in the system of aiming for class a of this school  although the biggest selling point of the school is that you can go to whatever university you want and find employment wherever you want  i believe i can achieve whatever i want with my own abilities  i simply chose to come to this school on a whim   would you have chosen this place if you knew before you came here that the structure of this school is centered around cooperation   that s not the case  i like this school  in fact  i haven t had a single complaint about life here since i arrived  the point system is also very pleasant   it seems that       you are fine with being hated by others   other people s       evaluations don t matter to me   i wanted to ask you something  but instead you re the one asking the questions   it s about time you told me about yourself   why me  there are many students who excel in their studies   are you planning to get first place in the uninhabited island exam   there s no student who doesn t want to be first  except maybe  for people       like you  kiryuuin senpai   letting aside first place  i m also one of the people who is aiming for a top spot  if i get a high position  i can get private points  i m the type to spend whatever i have  so i m always short of money   nagumo and kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place  and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen  right  the upcoming special exam will determine the top student at the school   whether my interest in you disappears or not  it all depends on what you do in the uninhabited island exam   on the contrary  i hope that your interest in me disappears   i see  you say some interesting things  underclassman  i m looking forward to fighting you  ayanokouji  kiryuin s academic physical abilities are both a  she s the only a a  in the school  her weakness is adaptability  d  her instincts point  rightly or wrongly  at him  she ll take the exam for private points  not glory   and she beat all the people who hate the spotlight before  he wants him away from the bench  she wants to see him on the island  she sizes him up as the interesting underclassman  his presence looms over all of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p271-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p271-1\">Kiriyama&#x27;s warning; Kiryūin&#x27;s attentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.271–284<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On his way to Keyaki mall, Kiriyama intercepts him; the conversation turns to the island exam and Nagumo. Kiryūin Fuūka intervenes on the bench; Ayanokōji is left alone with her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “You’re here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “What does the Vice President want with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “Don’t be in such a hurry to get this done with, it’s going to take some time today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>65 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The large scale uninhabited island exam is coming at the end of the month, are you prepared?”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel I’ve done everything I can. How about you, Vice President Kiriyama?”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve formed a group of 3 without anyone from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know what you must be thinking, if our Class 3-B wanted to reach Class A, then it’s a must to win first place with a team with only our class. Not only that, we would have to continue to win the following special exams by a landslide. However, that’s not realistic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to personally battle Nagumo in this special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s been a long time since we lost the battle with Nagumo and fell into Class B. After which, Nagumo became the student council president, and took control over the entire 3rd year, and eventually the entire school. It’s safe to say that the battle of the classes has already been decided.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But based on my evaluation of myself, I don’t think I’m any weaker than Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can form a big group of up to 6 people regardless of class. In order to win, you’ll have to have an eye for talent and the ability to get people to join you— In that aspect, I don’t think I can lose to Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand where you’re going with this, but is it really necessary to specifically tell me this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want you to get in my way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested in your duel with the President anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know that, but what I’m trying to say is, I don’t want to be distracted by any outsiders.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Outsiders?”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m referring to Horikita Suzune, who just joined the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. It looks like she’s in your way, However I want to at least tell you that I sent Horikita Suzune to the student council on the wish of her brother, the former student council president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s already no point to it. He’s only got a few months left as Student Council president. If we could do something starting from now, it wouldn’t be to take his presidency, but rather to settle a personal dispute with him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That won’t work. Forget all thoughts about dealing with Nagumo. It’ll only lead to unnecessary fights.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To put it politely, don’t do anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know, I’ve made myself clear on that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, you swear you won’t do anything. Can I interpret it like that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How you interpret it is your choice, but I didn’t make any promises.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo was more or less aware of what I’d been doing with Horikita-senpai. But since I’d been following his orders, he remained calm and simply observed what happened. Horikita-senpai’s sister joining the student council was annoying enough, so if you don’t stop meddling in this—”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you in trouble, Vice President?”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo’s idea, the one in which anyone can graduate from Class A. You want that chance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well…”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, you should have understood what I want to say by now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. When Horikita joined the student council, she was supposed to be introduced to the other members later on, but you came early, Vice President. I know the reason for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Say whatever you want-“<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufu. You’re with an interesting underclassman, so I said hello.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji …  …  Kiyotaka, right? I heard you became famous after a perfect score on a difficult math test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you want from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing, Ayanokouji? We’re leaving.”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You won’t get anything from being with a guy like that, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Staying with you is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji’s the one who should decide that, right? Kiriyama, can’t you leave any quicker?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you like to join me in a meaningful conversation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can ignore that woman.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t praise me like that, I’m getting embarrassed!”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s just a good student, but Kiryuuin doesn’t have anyone supporting her, unlike Nagumo. She doesn’t even have a single friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a lot like Kouenji from your year. All her words and actions, if you take her seriously, you’ll just be wasting your time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks for the compliments, Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s enough as long as I can figure out what sort of person you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Being interested and cooperating are 2 completely different things, aren’t they? There are some interesting people in my class, and sometimes I want to have a friendly conversation with them, just like what I’m doing with you now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested in the system of aiming for Class A of this school. Although the biggest selling point of the school is that you can go to whatever university you want and find employment wherever you want, I believe I can achieve whatever I want with my own abilities. I simply chose to come to this school on a whim.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you have chosen this place if you knew before you came here that the structure of this school is centered around cooperation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not the case. I like this school. In fact, I haven’t had a single complaint about life here since I arrived. The point system is also very pleasant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems that …  …  you are fine with being hated by others.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Other people’s …  …  evaluations don’t matter to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to ask you something, but instead you’re the one asking the questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about time you told me about yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why me? There are many students who excel in their studies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you planning to get first place in the uninhabited island exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no student who doesn’t want to be first. Except maybe, for people …  …  like you, Kiryuuin-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Letting aside first place, I’m also one of the people who is aiming for a top spot. If I get a high position, I can get private points. I’m the type to spend whatever I have, so I’m always short of money.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo and Kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place, and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen, right? The upcoming special exam will determine the top student at the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether my interest in you disappears or not, it all depends on what you do in the uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “On the contrary, I hope that your interest in me disappears.”<span class=\"pg\">p.285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. You say some interesting things, underclassman. I’m looking forward to fighting you, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kiryūin&#x27;s academic/physical abilities are both A+; she&#x27;s the only A+/A+ in the school; her weakness is adaptability (D). Her instincts point, rightly or wrongly, at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She&#x27;ll take the exam for private points, not glory — and she beat all the people who hate the spotlight before.<span class=\"pg\">p.284–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> He wants him away from the bench; she wants to see him on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> She sizes him up as the interesting underclassman.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> His presence looms over all of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–285<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\">← Before: Utomiya and Tsubaki at the convenience store<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p286-1\">→ After: Nagumo and Kiryūin (he is not present)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p271-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kiriyama","q":"kiriyama kiriyama s warning  and the bench  scene lines are on kiriyama ikuto md  this roster carries both  kiriyama  and  kiriyama ikuto  do not merge from this side  present as vice president  displeased by kiryuin s presence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p271-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiriyama&#x27;s warning (and the bench)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.271–285<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kiriyama\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Scene lines are on kiriyama-ikuto.md (this roster carries both `kiriyama` and `kiriyama-ikuto`; do not merge from this side).<span class=\"pg\">p.271–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Present as Vice President; displeased by Kiryūin&#x27;s presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–285<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-y2v2-p83-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p271-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune kiryuin-fuuka kiriyama-ikuto","q":"kiriyama ikuto kiriyama s warning  and the bench  he stops ayanokoji near keyaki mall  the ask is loaded   you re here   don t be in such a hurry to get this done with  it s going to take some time today   the large scale uninhabited island exam is coming at the end of the month  are you prepared   i ve formed a group of 3 without anyone from class a   i know what you must be thinking  if our class 3 b wanted to reach class a  then it s a must to win first place with a team with only our class  not only that  we would have to continue to win the following special exams by a landslide  however  that s not realistic   i wanted to personally battle nagumo in this special exam   it s been a long time since we lost the battle with nagumo and fell into class b  after which  nagumo became the student council president  and took control over the entire 3rd year  and eventually the entire school  it s safe to say that the battle of the classes has already been decided   but based on my evaluation of myself  i don t think i m any weaker than nagumo   you can form a big group of up to 6 people regardless of class  in order to win  you ll have to have an eye for talent and the ability to get people to join you  in that aspect  i don t think i can lose to nagumo   i understand where you re going with this  but is it really necessary to specifically tell me this   i don t want you to get in my way   i know that  but what i m trying to say is  i don t want to be distracted by any outsiders   i m referring to horikita suzune  who just joined the student council   there s already no point to it  he s only got a few months left as student council president  if we could do something starting from now  it wouldn t be to take his presidency  but rather to settle a personal dispute with him   that won t work  forget all thoughts about dealing with nagumo  it ll only lead to unnecessary fights   to put it politely  don t do anything   then  you swear you won t do anything  can i interpret it like that   nagumo was more or less aware of what i d been doing with horikita senpai  but since i d been following his orders  he remained calm and simply observed what happened  horikita senpai s sister joining the student council was annoying enough  so if you don t stop meddling in this   yeah   nagumo s idea  the one in which anyone can graduate from class a  you want that chance   well   anyway  you should have understood what i want to say by now   say whatever you want    the print closes this line with an opening quote glyph  normalised here to a closing mark  the conversation is interrupted by kiryuin on the bench  he glares at her and leaves with a warning  he wants to outrun him with a team  he can t  he blames her joining for everything  he cannot stand her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p271-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html#sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p271-1\">Kiriyama&#x27;s warning (and the bench)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.271–285<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He stops Ayanokōji near Keyaki mall; the ask is loaded.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “You’re here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “Don’t be in such a hurry to get this done with, it’s going to take some time today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “The large scale uninhabited island exam is coming at the end of the month, are you prepared?”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve formed a group of 3 without anyone from Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know what you must be thinking, if our Class 3-B wanted to reach Class A, then it’s a must to win first place with a team with only our class. Not only that, we would have to continue to win the following special exams by a landslide. However, that’s not realistic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to personally battle Nagumo in this special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s been a long time since we lost the battle with Nagumo and fell into Class B. After which, Nagumo became the student council president, and took control over the entire 3rd year, and eventually the entire school. It’s safe to say that the battle of the classes has already been decided.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But based on my evaluation of myself, I don’t think I’m any weaker than Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can form a big group of up to 6 people regardless of class. In order to win, you’ll have to have an eye for talent and the ability to get people to join you— In that aspect, I don’t think I can lose to Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand where you’re going with this, but is it really necessary to specifically tell me this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want you to get in my way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know that, but what I’m trying to say is, I don’t want to be distracted by any outsiders.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m referring to Horikita Suzune, who just joined the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s already no point to it. He’s only got a few months left as Student Council president. If we could do something starting from now, it wouldn’t be to take his presidency, but rather to settle a personal dispute with him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That won’t work. Forget all thoughts about dealing with Nagumo. It’ll only lead to unnecessary fights.”<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To put it politely, don’t do anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, you swear you won’t do anything. Can I interpret it like that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo was more or less aware of what I’d been doing with Horikita-senpai. But since I’d been following his orders, he remained calm and simply observed what happened. Horikita-senpai’s sister joining the student council was annoying enough, so if you don’t stop meddling in this—”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo’s idea, the one in which anyone can graduate from Class A. You want that chance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well…”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, you should have understood what I want to say by now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Say whatever you want-” — the print closes this line with an opening quote glyph; normalised here to a closing mark.<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The conversation is interrupted by Kiryūin on the bench; he glares at her and leaves with a warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He wants to outrun him with a team; he can&#x27;t.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He blames her joining for everything.<span class=\"pg\">p.274–277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> He cannot stand her.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiriyama-ikuto-y2v2-p83-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin takes the bench she s been sitting on the bench the whole time  kiriyama begs off  she addresses ayanokoji directly   kiriyama  can you not hear me   speak of the devil   fufu  you re with an interesting underclassman  so i said hello   ayanokouji       kiyotaka  right  i heard you became famous after a perfect score on a difficult math test   what are you doing  ayanokouji  we re leaving   you won t get anything from being with a guy like that  you know   staying with you is meaningless   ayanokouji s the one who should decide that  right  kiriyama  can t you leave any quicker   would you like to join me in a meaningful conversation   don t praise me like that  i m getting embarrassed   she s a lot like kouenji from your year  all her words and actions  if you take her seriously  you ll just be wasting your time   she s just a good student  but kiryuuin doesn t have anyone supporting her  unlike nagumo  she doesn t even have a single friend   thanks for the compliments  kiriyama   if you want to say something  say it quickly   it s enough as long as i can figure out what sort of person you are   being interested and cooperating are 2 completely different things  aren t they  there are some interesting people in my class  and sometimes i want to have a friendly conversation with them  just like what i m doing with you now   i m not interested in the system of aiming for class a of this school  although the biggest selling point of the school is that you can go to whatever university you want and find employment wherever you want  i believe i can achieve whatever i want with my own abilities  i simply chose to come to this school on a whim   would you have chosen this place if you knew before you came here that the structure of this school is centered around cooperation   that s not the case  i like this school  in fact  i haven t had a single complaint about life here since i arrived  the point system is also very pleasant   it seems that       you are fine with being hated by others   other people s       evaluations don t matter to me   i wanted to ask you something  but instead you re the one asking the questions   it s about time you told me about yourself   why me  there are many students who excel in their studies   are you planning to get first place in the uninhabited island exam   there s no student who doesn t want to be first  except maybe  for people       like you  kiryuuin senpai   letting aside first place  i m also one of the people who is aiming for a top spot  if i get a high position  i can get private points  i m the type to spend whatever i have  so i m always short of money   nagumo and kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place  and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen  right  the upcoming special exam will determine the top student at the school   whether my interest in you disappears or not  it all depends on what you do in the uninhabited island exam   i see  you say some interesting things  underclassman  i m looking forward to fighting you  ayanokouji  her academic and physical abilities are both a    the only a a  in the school  her one weakness is adaptability  d  kouenji like self possession  faintly flirtatious needling  genuinely curious  no interest in class or system  only in her own excellence and in spending money  she sizes him up as the interesting underclassman  she mocks him openly  he cannot counter  next scene  she toys with him and declines his offer to help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html#sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1\">Kiryūin takes the bench<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.278–285<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She&#x27;s been sitting on the bench the whole time; Kiriyama begs off; she addresses Ayanokōji directly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> “Kiriyama. Can you not hear me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “Speak of the devil…”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> “Fufu. You’re with an interesting underclassman, so I said hello.”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji …  …  Kiyotaka, right? I heard you became famous after a perfect score on a difficult math test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing, Ayanokouji? We’re leaving.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You won’t get anything from being with a guy like that, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Staying with you is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji’s the one who should decide that, right? Kiriyama, can’t you leave any quicker?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you like to join me in a meaningful conversation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t praise me like that, I’m getting embarrassed!”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a lot like Kouenji from your year. All her words and actions, if you take her seriously, you’ll just be wasting your time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s just a good student, but Kiryuuin doesn’t have anyone supporting her, unlike Nagumo. She doesn’t even have a single friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks for the compliments, Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you want to say something, say it quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s enough as long as I can figure out what sort of person you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Being interested and cooperating are 2 completely different things, aren’t they? There are some interesting people in my class, and sometimes I want to have a friendly conversation with them, just like what I’m doing with you now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested in the system of aiming for Class A of this school. Although the biggest selling point of the school is that you can go to whatever university you want and find employment wherever you want, I believe I can achieve whatever I want with my own abilities. I simply chose to come to this school on a whim.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you have chosen this place if you knew before you came here that the structure of this school is centered around cooperation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not the case. I like this school. In fact, I haven’t had a single complaint about life here since I arrived. The point system is also very pleasant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems that …  …  you are fine with being hated by others.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Other people’s …  …  evaluations don’t matter to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to ask you something, but instead you’re the one asking the questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about time you told me about yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why me? There are many students who excel in their studies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you planning to get first place in the uninhabited island exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no student who doesn’t want to be first. Except maybe, for people …  …  like you, Kiryuuin-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Letting aside first place, I’m also one of the people who is aiming for a top spot. If I get a high position, I can get private points. I’m the type to spend whatever I have, so I’m always short of money.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo and Kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place, and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen, right? The upcoming special exam will determine the top student at the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether my interest in you disappears or not, it all depends on what you do in the uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. You say some interesting things, underclassman. I’m looking forward to fighting you, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her Academic and Physical Abilities are both A+ — the only A+/A+ in the school; her one weakness is Adaptability (D).<span class=\"pg\">p.280–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kouenji-like self-possession; faintly flirtatious needling; genuinely curious; no interest in class or system, only in her own excellence and in spending money.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She sizes him up as the interesting underclassman.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> She mocks him openly; he cannot counter.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Next scene: she toys with him and declines his offer to help.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1\">→ After: Alone with Nagumo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p286-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nagumo and kiryuin  he is not present  ayanokoji leaves before this scene  it belongs to kiryuin and nagumo  recorded in their person records","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p286-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p286-1\">Nagumo and Kiryūin (he is not present)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.286–292<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji leaves before this scene; it belongs to Kiryūin and Nagumo; recorded in their person records.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p271-1\">← Before: Kiriyama&#x27;s warning; Kiryūin&#x27;s attentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\">→ After: Kanzaki at the convenience store<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka alone with nagumo after ayanokoji leaves  her day resumes  the swaying blonde hair appears  followed by kiriyama   hey hey  the loyal dog came back with his master eh   if you re getting mad at this  then that means that you know what i m talking about  right now  no one should know who s the loyal dog and who s the owner  as i don t remember declaring who was who  i m simply stating from the perspective of an outsider who doesn t know anything  why  because the one who left and as returned is you  kiriyama  and so that fits the image of a loyal dog   this woman s a real pain in the ass   you ve got a dirty mouth  kiriyama  it doesn t suit the image of a serious vice president   agreed  so can the two of you disappear from my sight right now  it s a       waste of my precious time   a beloved comrade  you didn t say that with any sort of emotion at all   that s just your imagination   well  what does the student council president want from me  i thought i d never see you again   you re beautiful but charmless  and i don t have much interest in charmless women   i have charm  it s just that i haven t met a man who could draw it out yet   me too  but putting aside your personal tastes  why aren t i popular   if there s a man who can bring out the charming side of you  i d like to meet him   women with too high an ability are hard to deal with  unfortunately  i don t like those types either   i see  if that s the case then i ll never be able to meet your standards  if being too excellent is the reason why i haven t found a boyfriend  then i understand   i heard something from kiriyama  i would have never thought that someone who wasn t interested in both horikita senpai or i  would be interested in ayanokouji  i was surprised when i heard that   if possible  i too don t want to stay here for longer than i have to   someone who has never been with a man before  can understand the fundamentals of love   it s true that i ve never been in a relationship  but that s nothing to be ashamed of  rather  i should say that it has raised my value   like always  your way of thinking is rather strange   so  ayanokouji  is he someone worth keeping an eye on   there s a saying  that a predator doesn t reveal his fangs  right  he seems to have gotten a perfect score in a difficult test   there are people who hate being in the limelight and hide their talents  i ve defeated all of them  and they weren t very interesting   i have given you several chances to prove that  but till now you haven t done anything  and as a result ended up in class b   the moment you lose  you ll lose something immeasurable  student council president  however  it seems you ve misunderstood something  student council president  i m not underestimating you  i don t have the leadership skills that you or horikita manabu possessed  i m no good at making friends either  in fact i ve never had someone who i could consider a friend  let alone a close one  you know that  right   however  if we re talking about the other elements  it s different   well well  can you really say that there s definitely nothing in which you re inferior to me at   certainly  if you only look at the results  i failed miserably   you wanted some answers about ayanokouji  didn t you   interesting  i think his personality is far from it   you seem to be bored ever since horikita manabu left  so this underclassmen should be a good playmate for you  eh  if you re really serious  then you ll definitely get 1st place in the upcoming exam   of course i ll get 1st place  or maybe it ll be kiriyama  who s been dying to fight me  but to get control of the whole podium  i still need more groups  right  i ll give you this role  kiryuuin  if necessary  i ll even help you find comrades   i see  so you came here to ask for my help   the top 50  is enough for me  sorry that you had to come all this way for nothing   with that logic  nobody can give you any advice   then listen as if this were a monologue  you should look at what s going on in front of you  instead of playing with your underclassmen  if you pay too much attention to those behind you  you ll get badly hurt  her eval  a  a  d in adaptability  c  social  nagumo needs comrades on the podium  she takes top 50  and declines the whole offer  sharp  self sufficient  entirely unbothered  she wins by surviving  not by commanding  nagumo s wanted something she never agreed to give  she treats him as a rival who bore her  she tells him to his face he s a loyal dog  she keeps him on hold","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html#sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1\">Alone with Nagumo<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.286–292<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After Ayanokōji leaves; her day resumes; the swaying blonde hair appears, followed by Kiriyama.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> “Hey hey, the loyal dog came back with his master eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> “If you’re getting mad at this, then that means that you know what I’m talking about. Right now, no one should know who’s the loyal dog and who’s the owner, as I don’t remember declaring who was who. I’m simply stating from the…”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “This woman’s a real pain in the ass…”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re getting mad at this, then that means that you know what I’m talking about. Right now, no one should know who’s the loyal dog and who’s the owner, as I don’t remember declaring who was who. I’m simply stating from the perspective of an outsider who doesn’t know anything. Why? Because the one who left and as returned is you, Kiriyama, and so that fits the image of a loyal dog.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve got a dirty mouth, Kiriyama, it doesn’t suit the image of a serious vice president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agreed. So can the two of you disappear from my sight right now? It’s a …  …  waste of my precious time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A beloved comrade? You didn’t say that with any sort of emotion at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s just your imagination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well. What does the student council president want from me? I thought I’d never see you again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re beautiful but charmless, and I don’t have much interest in charmless women.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have charm. It’s just that I haven’t met a man who could draw it out yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me too. But putting aside your personal tastes, why aren’t I popular?”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s a man who can bring out the charming side of you, I’d like to meet him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Women with too high an ability are hard to deal with. Unfortunately, I don’t like those types either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, if that’s the case then I’ll never be able to meet your standards. If being too excellent is the reason why I haven’t found a boyfriend, then I understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard something from Kiriyama. I would have never thought that someone who wasn’t interested in both Horikita-senpai or I, would be interested in Ayanokouji. I was surprised when I heard that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If possible, I too don’t want to stay here for longer than I have to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone who has never been with a man before, can understand the fundamentals of love?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s true that I’ve never been in a relationship, but that’s nothing to be ashamed of. Rather, I should say that it has raised my value?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Like always, your way of thinking is rather strange.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So… Ayanokouji? Is he someone worth keeping an eye on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a saying, that a predator doesn’t reveal his fangs, right? He seems to have gotten a perfect score in a difficult test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are people who hate being in the limelight and hide their talents. I’ve defeated all of them, and they weren’t very interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have given you several chances to prove that, but till now you haven’t done anything, and as a result ended up in Class B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The moment you lose, you’ll lose something immeasurable, student council president. However, it seems you’ve misunderstood something, student council president. I’m not underestimating you. I don’t have the leadership skills that you or Horikita Manabu possessed. I’m no good at making friends either, in fact I’ve never had someone who I could consider a friend, let alone a close one. You know that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, if we’re talking about the other elements, it’s different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well well, can you really say that there’s definitely nothing in which you’re inferior to me at?”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Certainly, if you only look at the results, I failed miserably.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You wanted some answers about Ayanokouji, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Interesting? I think his personality is far from it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be bored ever since Horikita Manabu left. So this underclassmen should be a good playmate for you, eh? If you’re really serious, then you’ll definitely get 1st place in the upcoming exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll get 1st place. Or maybe it’ll be Kiriyama, who’s been dying to fight me. But to get control of the whole podium, I still need more groups, right? I’ll give you this role, Kiryuuin. If necessary, I’ll even help you find comrades.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So you came here to ask for my help?”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The top 50% is enough for me. Sorry that you had to come all this way for nothing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With that logic, nobody can give you any advice”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then listen as if this were a monologue. You should look at what’s going on in front of you, instead of playing with your underclassmen. If you pay too much attention to those behind you, you’ll get badly hurt.”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her eval: A+ A+, D in adaptability, C+ social; Nagumo needs comrades on the podium; she takes top-50% and declines the whole offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp, self-sufficient, entirely unbothered; she wins by surviving, not by commanding; Nagumo&#x27;s wanted something she never agreed to give.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She treats him as a rival who bore her.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> She tells him to his face he&#x27;s a loyal dog.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She keeps him on hold.<span class=\"pg\">p.285–292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1\">← Before: Kiryūin takes the bench<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p286-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto kiryuin-fuuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo and kiryuin ayanokoji leaves  kiriyama returns  nagumo shows up behind kiryuuin   who the hell do you think you are  you re the one   if possible  i too don t want to stay here for longer than i have to   you re beautiful but charmless  and i don t have much interest in charmless women   if there s a man who can bring out the charming side of you  i d like to meet him   women with too high an ability are hard to deal with  unfortunately  i don t like those types either   i heard something from kiriyama  i would have never thought that someone who wasn t interested in both horikita senpai or i  would be interested in ayanokouji  i was surprised when i heard that   someone who has never been with a man before  can understand the fundamentals of love   there s a saying  that a predator doesn t reveal his fangs  right  he seems to have gotten a perfect score in a difficult test   there are people who hate being in the limelight and hide their talents  i ve defeated all of them  and they weren t very interesting   if i had to say  it s his aura  i feel that he has a different aura from you and horikita manabu   well well  can you really say that there s definitely nothing in which you re inferior to me at   you seem to be bored ever since horikita manabu left  so this underclassmen should be a good playmate for you  eh  if you re really serious  then you ll definitely get 1st place in the upcoming exam   of course i ll get 1st place  or maybe it ll be kiriyama  who s been dying to fight me  but to get control of the whole podium  i still need more groups  right  i ll give you this role  kiryuuin  if necessary  i ll even help you find comrades   although letting the underclassmen get 3rd place wouldn t be too bad  i m not that soft   that s just how you are  we re both 3rd years  but it seemed to be a waste of time to try to talk to you like that   with that logic  nobody can give you any advice  he offers her the underclassmen play role  she declines  he takes kiriyama and leaves with a monologue warning  bored predator  collecting underclassmen for the island exam  genuinely puzzled by her indifference  he studies her  she declines  he dismisses him  he serves him  the interesting underclassman  he might test him  her sister spy experiment bores him  his predecessor s antics linger","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p286-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html#sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p286-1\">Nagumo and Kiryūin<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.286–292<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji leaves; Kiriyama returns; Nagumo shows up behind Kiryuuin.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “Who the hell do you think you are? You’re the one-“<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “If possible, I too don’t want to stay here for longer than I have to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “You’re beautiful but charmless, and I don’t have much interest in charmless women.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s a man who can bring out the charming side of you, I’d like to meet him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Women with too high an ability are hard to deal with. Unfortunately, I don’t like those types either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard something from Kiriyama. I would have never thought that someone who wasn’t interested in both Horikita-senpai or I, would be interested in Ayanokouji. I was surprised when I heard that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone who has never been with a man before, can understand the fundamentals of love?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a saying, that a predator doesn’t reveal his fangs, right? He seems to have gotten a perfect score in a difficult test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are people who hate being in the limelight and hide their talents. I’ve defeated all of them, and they weren’t very interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I had to say, it’s his aura. I feel that he has a different aura from you and Horikita Manabu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well well, can you really say that there’s definitely nothing in which you’re inferior to me at?”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be bored ever since Horikita Manabu left. So this underclassmen should be a good playmate for you, eh? If you’re really serious, then you’ll definitely get 1st place in the upcoming exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll get 1st place. Or maybe it’ll be Kiriyama, who’s been dying to fight me. But to get control of the whole podium, I still need more groups, right? I’ll give you this role, Kiryuuin. If necessary, I’ll even help you find comrades.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although letting the underclassmen get 3rd place wouldn’t be too bad, I’m not that soft.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s just how you are. We’re both 3rd years, but it seemed to be a waste of time to try to talk to you like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With that logic, nobody can give you any advice”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He offers her the underclassmen play role; she declines; he takes Kiriyama and leaves with a monologue warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Bored predator; collecting underclassmen for the island exam; genuinely puzzled by her indifference.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> He studies her; she declines.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> He dismisses him; he serves him.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The interesting underclassman; he might test him.<span class=\"pg\">p.291–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her sister spy-experiment bores him.<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> His predecessor&#x27;s antics linger.<span class=\"pg\">p.289–291<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1\">← Before: Horikita joins the council; his challenge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kanzaki at the convenience store on the morning of the meeting  saturday  09 30  ishizaki s email summons him to the cafe  on the way he meets kanzaki with two 2 liter bottles   going to keyaki mall at this time   it seems like most of the people in class d have formed groups  but you re still on your own   unlike the others  i don t have many friends  so   you and horikita     are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class s groups  after all  excellent students could leave their mark in any group during the exam   ayanokouji     ichinose seems to trust you a lot  but can  we  really trust you   if i said you could trust me  would you  kanzaki   i d consider it  at least   although we ve broken off the alliance  i don t consider ichinose to be an enemy   that statement leaves a lot of room for interpretation  are you saying you don t consider class c to be an enemy   kanazki  what do you want from me   are you trying to get some sort of statement from me and have ichinose to listen to it   you  ichinose no  we underestimated your perceptiveness  when we first met  i had this weird feeling  but i couldn t quite put my finger on it  finally  i can clearly see what it was  you re the reason class d is making such great progress   who knows   i m simply going to come out and ask you for help  ichinose trusts you a lot  that is why i want you to tell her yourself  the way she is right now  she isn t good enough   so you re expecting that to change the way ichinose thinks   that s right   sorry  but i can t help you  i d like to keep seeing her own way of dealing with things   so you want to see us  your enemy  fall   well  fundamentally speaking  one has to care of their own class by themselves  isn t that right   yeah  i might have been too childish   i was going to come up with a solution on my own  but i thought there was a way to fix the problem without doing that  that there was an easy way out  so i tried to take it  he reads kanzaki head to toe  ending ichinose s next fall would be her last   he keeps the thought to himself  the cornered rat who bites the cat  she is the reason he has to see this through himself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\">Kanzaki at the convenience store<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.294–297<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the morning of the meeting (Saturday, 09:30), Ishizaki&#x27;s email summons him to the café; on the way he meets Kanzaki with two 2-liter bottles.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Going to Keyaki mall at this time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It seems like most of the people in Class D have formed groups, but you’re still on your own?”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Unlike the others, I don’t have many friends, so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You and Horikita … , are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class’s groups? After all, excellent students could leave their mark in any group during the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji … , Ichinose seems to trust you a lot, but can ‘we’ really trust you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I said you could trust me, would you, Kanzaki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d consider it, at least.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although we’ve broken off the alliance, I don’t consider Ichinose to be an enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That statement leaves a lot of room for interpretation. Are you saying you don’t consider Class C to be an enemy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kanazki, what do you want from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you trying to get some sort of statement from me and have Ichinose to listen to it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You… Ichinose…no, we underestimated your perceptiveness. When we first met, I had this weird feeling, but I couldn’t quite put my finger on it. Finally, I can clearly see what it was. You’re the reason Class D is making such great progress.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m simply going to come out and ask you for help. Ichinose trusts you a lot. That is why I want you to tell her yourself: the way she is right now, she isn’t good enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re expecting that to change the way Ichinose thinks?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I can’t help you. I’d like to keep seeing her own way of dealing with things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you want to see us, your enemy, fall?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fundamentally speaking, one has to care of their own class by themselves. Isn’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Yeah. I might have been too childish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was going to come up with a solution on my own. But I thought there was a way to fix the problem without doing that, that there was an easy way out, so I tried to take it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He reads Kanzaki head-to-toe; ending Ichinose&#x27;s next fall would be her last — he keeps the thought to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The cornered rat who bites the cat.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She is the reason he has to see this through himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p286-1\">← Before: Nagumo and Kiryūin (he is not present)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\">→ After: The café with Ryuuen and Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p294-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ishizaki-daichi","q":"ishizaki daichi ishizaki s email his email summons ayanokoji to the cafe on ryuuen s behalf   an unusual tone for them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p294-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html#sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p294-1\">Ishizaki&#x27;s email<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.294<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His email summons Ayanokōji to the café on Ryuuen&#x27;s behalf — an unusual tone for them.<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p187-1\">← Before: The Komiya investigation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p300-1\">→ After: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p294-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"matsushita-chiaki","q":"matsushita chiaki coverage note  passing mentions  ishizaki  matsushita  and the others who had invited me to join their groups had gradually given up on trying to do so","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p294-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html#sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p294-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.294<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ishizaki, Matsushita, and the others who had invited me to join their groups had gradually given up on trying to do so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-matsushita-chiaki-y2v2-p179-1\">← Before: Matsushita recruits him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p294-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka kaneda-satoru sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru the cafe gambit ishizaki s email brought ayanokoji here  the ryuuen katsuragi tag team is waiting   so  tell me why you called me   what s the hurry  just chill man   you said there was someone else  were you talking about ayanokouji   what kind of meeting is this supposed to be  anyway   kuku  don t admire him too much  katsuragi  that s in the past   fuck off  ichinose was off sinking on her own  she was never even on my radar   the past  you ought to be careful when an unexpectedly strong enemy       appears  you ve gotten too cocky after defeating ichinose s class b   what is class a aiming for in the next exam   are you aiming to monopolize the class points  or is it something else  i ve checked the group composition using the oaa  and while you guys seem to have formed groups with class c and d  kitou seems to be alone  and then  no matter how you spin it  ichinose  shibata and sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy  are you working together   i don t want any of that diplomatic crap  i want just straight answers   oh  so you don t know just because she doesn t trust you   only on the day of the exam shall we know how sakayanagi will act  and no one will know before she says so  if you want to know despite this  you should go ask her directly   this is really sad  katsuragi  this time last year  i considered you a worthy opponent in my strategies  however not a single trace of that person remains  it looks like it s the end of the road for the loser of the faction war  eh   don t you want to crawl back to the top again  that totsuka who was holding you back  he is gone now  right   don t you think it ll be an interesting development if we manage to get sakayanagi expelled from the next special exam   if that girl isn t here  then class a will cease to have a leader  that way  you ll be able to return to your position as leader once again   that s true  if you want her gone  you ll have to stab her at least twice  well  getting her expelled in the next exam was a joke  the objective for the uninhabited island exam isn t to kick your enemies down  but to climb up   the reward for getting 1st to 3rd place is enough to get within shooting distance of class a  but the rules seem to be a bit troublesome  so  i wanted to prepare in advance   even so  ichinose really did agree to team up with that woman  did you guys butter her up well  or was it because she s so incompetent that she thought that was all she could do  right   in that case  everyone here s that kind of delinquent   good for you  katsuragi  obnoxiously righteous as always  not bad   the most important thing about this special exam is to not lose any points from the 2nd year  i don t want the 1st and 3rd years filling their pockets with my money  for that  we need to at least form an alliance  right  if you rely only on your own class  you ll lack combat power   if the small fry in class b were added into this group  then i d be better off fighting alone  but if i can draw in some firepower from elsewhere  then it d be a different story   not just you  ayanokouji as well  who s spaced out over there just listening to us talk   why would i call you here if you weren t   someone who doesn t know about him wouldn t understand  but i made the right choice  right  ayanokouji   stop with that poor acting  you re the man who beat me and shut me up   come on  admit it  ayanokouji  even if you continue to hide it from katsuragi like that  i ll just keep talking  yeah   yeah yeah  completely forgot about that  as an advisor  you re certainty qualified   a serious negotiation  you knew that was impossible from the start  didn t you  but you still came  were you asked to spy for class a   you re a dead man  and you re looking for a chance to come back to life  am i right   come to class b  katsuragi   of course  we ll pay for the points you don t have   i ll soon defeat sakayanagi  and then the entire class a will fall  in other words  remaining in class a is worthless  right   what  you ve been saving up after all  even if you re rotten  you re still in class a  eh   you ve seen this before  yeah  it s the contract i sighed with you last year   after negotiating with sakayanagi  i m giving this thing up for 5 million points   you re not going to get a chance like this again  katsuragi   why  would you go that far for someone like me   heh  katsuragi  you have a surprisingly low opinion of yourself  though  to be honest  you re not going cheap   the 5 million for nullifying the contract plus your current balance  the remaining points have been collected from the class  i ve forced them into poverty to welcome you to our class   come on  sign it  using 20 million points to change classes requires several conditions  you can t force a person to change classes  in the end  the person must agree  and then use his or her funds to transfer to any class of their choosing   it all worked out  right  katsuragi  you ve been on your own until now  which makes it easier to invite you into our class   you just bought katsuragi  so i m sure your funding situation isn t so good  can you prepare enough money   i ll be able to get 500 000 points or so  that should be enough   i have one condition  make a student in your class that has a half off card exchange their card with one of our students that has the free ride card  if you accept that  i ll sell the trial card to you   kuku  i guess it s settled then  half off card  eh  it just so happens that katsuragi has it  right  he pays 20 million for katsuragi  individual class transfer  a first in school history  class b s funds are drained  he s acquired his strongest weapon for the island exam  the master manipulator  he reads everyone s leverage aloud  he buys loyalty with money they both know he ll never get back  he buys him  he was always going to sign  he reclaims the trial card price  he tests his nerve  the 20 000 point month contract money flows from class a  his white whale","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p294-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p294-1\">The café gambit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.294–314<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ishizaki&#x27;s email brought Ayanokōji here; the Ryuuen–Katsuragi tag team is waiting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “…So? Tell me why you called me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “What’s the hurry? Just chill man!”<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You said there was someone else, were you talking about Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>50 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What kind of meeting is this supposed to be, anyway?”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kuku, don’t admire him too much, Katsuragi– that’s in the past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fuck off. Ichinose was off sinking on her own, she was never even on my radar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The past? You ought to be careful when an unexpectedly strong enemy …  …  appears. You’ve gotten too cocky after defeating Ichinose’s Class B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What is Class A aiming for in the next exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you aiming to monopolize the class points? Or is it something else? I’ve checked the group composition using the OAA, and while you guys seem to have formed groups with Class C and D, Kitou seems to be alone. And then, no matter how you spin it, Ichinose, Shibata and Sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy. Are you working together?”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want any of that diplomatic crap, I want just straight answers.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, so you don’t know just because she doesn’t trust you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Only on the day of the exam shall we know how Sakayanagi will act, and no one will know before she says so. If you want to know despite this, you should go ask her directly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is really sad, Katsuragi. This time last year, I considered you a worthy opponent in my strategies. However not a single trace of that person remains. It looks like it’s the end of the road for the loser of the faction war, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you want to crawl back to the top again? That Totsuka who was holding you back, he is gone now, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think it’ll be an interesting development if we manage to get Sakayanagi expelled from the next special exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that girl isn’t here, then Class-A will cease to have a leader. That way, you’ll be able to return to your position as leader once again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, if you want her gone, you’ll have to stab her at least twice. Well, getting her expelled in the next exam was a joke. The objective for the uninhabited island exam isn’t to kick your enemies down, but to climb up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The reward for getting 1st to 3rd place is enough to get within shooting distance of Class A, but the rules seem to be a bit troublesome. So, I wanted to prepare in advance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, Ichinose really did agree to team up with that woman. Did you guys butter her up well, or was it because she’s so incompetent that she thought that was all she could do? Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, everyone here’s that kind of delinquent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good for you, Katsuragi. Obnoxiously righteous as always. Not bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The most important thing about this special exam is to not lose any points from the 2nd year. I don’t want the 1st and 3rd years filling their pockets with my money. For that, we need to at least form an alliance, right? If you rely only on your own class, you’ll lack combat power.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If the small fry in Class B were added into this group, then I’d be better off fighting alone, but if I can draw in some firepower from elsewhere, then it’d be a different story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not just you. Ayanokouji as well, who’s spaced out over there just listening to us talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why would I call you here if you weren’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone who doesn’t know about him wouldn’t understand, but I made the right choice. Right, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop with that poor acting. You’re the man who beat me and shut me up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, admit it, Ayanokouji. Even if you continue to hide it from Katsuragi like that, I’ll just keep talking, yeah?”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah yeah, completely forgot about that. As an advisor, you’re certainty qualified.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A serious negotiation? You knew that was impossible from the start, didn’t you? But you still came. Were you asked to spy for Class A?”<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a dead man, and you’re looking for a chance to come back to life. Am I right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come to Class B, Katsuragi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, we’ll pay for the points you don’t have.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll soon defeat Sakayanagi, and then the entire Class A will fall. In other words, remaining in Class A is worthless, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, you’ve been saving up after all! Even if you’re rotten, you’re still in Class A, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve seen this before, yeah? It’s the contract I sighed with you last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After negotiating with Sakayanagi, I’m giving this thing up for 5 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re not going to get a chance like this again, Katsuragi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why… Would you go that far for someone like me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh, Katsuragi, you have a surprisingly low opinion of yourself. Though, to be honest, you’re not going cheap.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The 5 million for nullifying the contract plus your current balance. The remaining points have been collected from the class. I’ve forced them into poverty to welcome you to our class!”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, sign it. Using 20 million points to change classes requires several conditions. You can’t force a person to change classes. In the end, the person must agree, and then use his or her funds to transfer to any class of their choosing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It all worked out, right, Katsuragi? You’ve been on your own until now, which makes it easier to invite you into our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just bought Katsuragi, so I’m sure your funding situation isn’t so good. Can you prepare enough money?”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be able to get 500,000 points or so. That should be enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have one condition. Make a student in your class that has a Half Off card exchange their card with one of our students that has the Free Ride card. If you accept that, I’ll sell the trial card to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kuku, I guess it’s settled then. Half Off card, eh? It just so happens that Katsuragi has it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He pays 20 million for Katsuragi; individual class transfer, a first in school history; Class B&#x27;s funds are drained; he&#x27;s acquired his strongest weapon for the island exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.311–312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The master manipulator; he reads everyone&#x27;s leverage aloud; he buys loyalty with money they both know he&#x27;ll never get back.<span class=\"pg\">p.294–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> He buys him; he was always going to sign.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He reclaims the Trial card price; he tests his nerve.<span class=\"pg\">p.305–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> The 20,000-point/month contract money flows from Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> His White Whale.<span class=\"pg\">p.308–312<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y2v2-p32-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p295-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji kanzaki at the convenience store he bumps into ayanokoji near the convenience store with two 2 liter bottles  he approaches him directly for help   going to keyaki mall at this time   i won t have any time to relax after the exam starts  after all   it seems like most of the people in class d have formed groups  but you re still on your own   unlike the others  i don t have many friends  so   you and horikita     are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class s groups  after all  excellent students could leave their mark in any group during the exam   ayanokouji     ichinose seems to trust you a lot  but can  we  really trust you   i d consider it  at least   although we ve broken off the alliance  i don t consider ichinose to be an enemy   that statement leaves a lot of room for interpretation  are you saying you don t consider class c to be an enemy   are you trying to get some sort of statement from me and have ichinose to listen to it   you  ichinose no  we underestimated your perceptiveness  when we first met  i had this weird feeling  but i couldn t quite put my finger on it  finally  i can clearly see what it was  you re the reason class d is making such great progress   who knows   i m simply going to come out and ask you for help  ichinose trusts you a lot  that is why i want you to tell her yourself  the way she is right now  she isn t good enough   so you re expecting that to change the way ichinose thinks   that s right   sorry  but i can t help you  i d like to keep seeing her own way of dealing with things   so you want to see us  your enemy  fall   well  fundamentally speaking  one has to care of their own class by themselves  isn t that right   yeah  i might have been too childish   i was going to come up with a solution on my own  but i thought there was a way to fix the problem without doing that  that there was an easy way out  so i tried to take it  he swallows his pride and asks for a favor  he accepts the refusal with grace  the desperation of a man who has run out of plans  he s not teamed up with anyone yet either  his worry is ichinose s endgame  he s measured him as the source of class d s turnaround  she is the reason he asked","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p295-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p295-1\">Kanzaki at the convenience store<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.295–297<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He bumps into Ayanokōji near the convenience store with two 2-liter bottles; he approaches him directly for help.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Going to Keyaki mall at this time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “I won’t have any time to relax after the exam starts, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “It seems like most of the people in Class D have formed groups, but you’re still on your own?”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unlike the others, I don’t have many friends, so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You and Horikita … , are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class’s groups? After all, excellent students could leave their mark in any group during the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji … , Ichinose seems to trust you a lot, but can ‘we’ really trust you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d consider it, at least.”<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although we’ve broken off the alliance, I don’t consider Ichinose to be an enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That statement leaves a lot of room for interpretation. Are you saying you don’t consider Class C to be an enemy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you trying to get some sort of statement from me and have Ichinose to listen to it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You… Ichinose…no, we underestimated your perceptiveness. When we first met, I had this weird feeling, but I couldn’t quite put my finger on it. Finally, I can clearly see what it was. You’re the reason Class D is making such great progress.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m simply going to come out and ask you for help. Ichinose trusts you a lot. That is why I want you to tell her yourself: the way she is right now, she isn’t good enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re expecting that to change the way Ichinose thinks?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I can’t help you. I’d like to keep seeing her own way of dealing with things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you want to see us, your enemy, fall?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fundamentally speaking, one has to care of their own class by themselves. Isn’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Yeah. I might have been too childish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was going to come up with a solution on my own. But I thought there was a way to fix the problem without doing that, that there was an easy way out, so I tried to take it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He swallows his pride and asks for a favor; he accepts the refusal with grace; the desperation of a man who has run out of plans.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He&#x27;s not teamed up with anyone yet either; his worry is Ichinose&#x27;s endgame.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He&#x27;s measured him as the source of Class D&#x27;s turnaround.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She is the reason he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y2v2-p204-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe with ryuuen and katsuragi he arrives before the appointed time  pays  katsuragi is already there  stiff  ryuuen plays host   you said there was someone else  were you talking about ayanokouji   what  do you want to stand while we talk  sit down   kuku  don t admire him too much  katsuragi  that s in the past   fuck off  ichinose was off sinking on her own  she was never even on my radar   so  tell me why you called me   what is class a aiming for in the next exam   are you aiming to monopolize the class points  or is it something else  i ve checked the group composition using the oaa  and while you guys seem to have formed groups with class c and d  kitou seems to be alone  and then  no matter how you spin it  ichinose  shibata and sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy  are you working together   you re free to interpret it however you want  but i cannot confirm anything   i don t want any of that diplomatic crap  i want just straight answers   then  let me make this simple for you  i m not going to tell you anything about this  you bastard   oh  so you don t know just because she doesn t trust you   well  that might be true   this is really sad  katsuragi  this time last year  i considered you a worthy opponent in my strategies  however not a single trace of that person remains  it looks like it s the end of the road for the loser of the faction war  eh   didn t you also lose to ishizaki that one time   don t you want to crawl back to the top again  that totsuka who was holding you back  he is gone now  right   if you wanted to make me angry  then you ve succeeded  ryuuen  are you satisfied now   don t you think it ll be an interesting development if we manage to get sakayanagi expelled from the next special exam   i don t know what you re planning to do  but that s impossible  even if you trap her on the island  she has plenty of private points for relief  also if by chance  something does incapacitate her  she still has protection points to fall back on   that s true  if you want her gone  you ll have to stab her at least twice  well  getting her expelled in the next exam was a joke  the objective for the uninhabited island exam isn t to kick your enemies down  but to climb up   the reward for getting 1st to 3rd place is enough to get within shooting distance of class a  but the rules seem to be a bit troublesome  so  i wanted to prepare in advance   is this why you called me and ayanokouji here   even so  ichinose really did agree to team up with that woman  did you guys butter her up well  or was it because she s so incompetent that she thought that was all she could do  right   i don t know  and if sakayanagi heard that question  she d ask you the same thing  not many people would like being on your team  you re a delinquent  after all   in that case  everyone here s that kind of delinquent   good for you  katsuragi  obnoxiously righteous as always  not bad   flattering me won t work  ryuuen   the most important thing about this special exam is to not lose any points from the 2nd year  i don t want the 1st and 3rd years filling their pockets with my money  for that  we need to at least form an alliance  right  if you rely only on your own class  you ll lack combat power   if the small fry in class b were added into this group  then i d be better off fighting alone  but if i can draw in some firepower from elsewhere  then it d be a different story   no way  are you asking me to work with you   not just you  ayanokouji as well  who s spaced out over there just listening to us talk    me too   why would i call you here if you weren t   i refuse  although class a would get the rewards too  i don t want to be on a team with someone like you   what a rash decision  you ve gotta hear me out till the end   that s not necessary  but  why did you call ayanokouji  i want to know that first   it was surprising that he got a perfect score in math in the special exam at the end of april  i agree that he has a high ability in academics  but can you really say that he s the right person to choose if you want to win   that s right  if you get ayanokouji in  it ll reduce the class point reward to one thirds each  since you re inviting me from class a anyway  wouldn t it be better to invite kitou to the group  besides  if we need three classes  kanzaki from class c is still alone  and he should ve priority over ayanokouji   someone who doesn t know about him wouldn t understand  but i made the right choice  right  ayanokouji   i don t know what you re talking about   stop with that poor acting  you re the man who beat me and shut me up   to shut you up  is that true   ah  i got my ass handed to me  thanks to that  i almost decided to quit school   come on  admit it  ayanokouji  even if you continue to hide it from katsuragi like that  i ll just keep talking  yeah   even if i do admit it  do you think i ll help you   well  like with katsuragi  it won t be that simple   no  i can t accept this after all  i can t believe that ayanokouji beat you  coming back to what i said earlier  if you have three classes working together  even if you come in first place  you ll only get an average of 100 points  the gap between you and class a will be impossible to close   yeah yeah  completely forgot about that  as an advisor  you re certainty qualified   a serious negotiation  you knew that was impossible from the start  didn t you  but you still came  were you asked to spy for class a   you re a dead man  and you re looking for a chance to come back to life  am i right   whether or not that s true  it has nothing to do with you   it was a fair contract  we got 200 points from your class  and in return class a pays off the loan  all of my actions were only to lead class a along a       better path   sure  if you only look at the numbers  however  what about the psychological impact that your class suffers every month  why should all of you have to share your private points with us for so long   come to class b  katsuragi   of course  we ll pay for the points you don t have   i ll soon defeat sakayanagi  and then the entire class a will fall  in other words  remaining in class a is worthless  right   what  you ve been saving up after all  even if you re rotten  you re still in class a  eh   you ve seen this before  yeah  it s the contract i sighed with you last year   after negotiating with sakayanagi  i m giving this thing up for 5 million points   did you tell her that the points would be used for stealing me   you re not going to get a chance like this again  katsuragi   heh  katsuragi  you have a surprisingly low opinion of yourself  though  to be honest  you re not going cheap   the 5 million for nullifying the contract plus your current balance  the remaining points have been collected from the class  i ve forced them into poverty to welcome you to our class   come on  sign it  using 20 million points to change classes requires several conditions  you can t force a person to change classes  in the end  the person must agree  and then use his or her funds to transfer to any class of their choosing   you seem to be serious   it all worked out  right  katsuragi  you ve been on your own until now  which makes it easier to invite you into our class   this is your fate  accept it   although i don t really care that you brought me into your ranks  what exactly are you looking for  you won t mind it if i speak my mind   why  it s the trial card he received   sell it to me   i ll be able to get 500 000 points or so  that should be enough   i have one condition  make a student in your class that has a half off card exchange their card with one of our students that has the free ride card  if you accept that  i ll sell the trial card to you   kuku  i guess it s settled then  half off card  eh  it just so happens that katsuragi has it  right  he plays dumb throughout   diluted coffee  shrugging answers  the meeting buys katsuragi for 20 million  the trial card costs 500 000  the half off card lands on class d  sakayanagi s contract money is burned  the spider at the center  he wires class a b c d without ever joining a group  ally ish nemesis  negotiates through ishizaki s email  he buys his trial card for 500k  he watches him sign  the play is over before it began  she doesn t know this meeting happened in her seat s shadow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\">The café with Ryuuen and Katsuragi<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.298–314<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He arrives before the appointed time; pays; Katsuragi is already there, stiff; Ryuuen plays host.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You said there was someone else, were you talking about Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “What, do you want to stand while we talk? Sit down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Kuku, don’t admire him too much, Katsuragi– that’s in the past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>74 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fuck off. Ichinose was off sinking on her own, she was never even on my radar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…So? Tell me why you called me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What is Class A aiming for in the next exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you aiming to monopolize the class points? Or is it something else? I’ve checked the group composition using the OAA, and while you guys seem to have formed groups with Class C and D, Kitou seems to be alone. And then, no matter how you spin it, Ichinose, Shibata and Sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy. Are you working together?”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re free to interpret it however you want, but I cannot confirm anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want any of that diplomatic crap, I want just straight answers.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, let me make this simple for you. I’m not going to tell you anything about this, you bastard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, so you don’t know just because she doesn’t trust you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that might be true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is really sad, Katsuragi. This time last year, I considered you a worthy opponent in my strategies. However not a single trace of that person remains. It looks like it’s the end of the road for the loser of the faction war, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you also lose to Ishizaki that one time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you want to crawl back to the top again? That Totsuka who was holding you back, he is gone now, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you wanted to make me angry, then you’ve succeeded, Ryuuen. Are you satisfied now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think it’ll be an interesting development if we manage to get Sakayanagi expelled from the next special exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re planning to do, but that’s impossible. Even if you trap her on the island, she has plenty of private points for relief. Also if by chance, something does incapacitate her, she still has protection points to fall back on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, if you want her gone, you’ll have to stab her at least twice. Well, getting her expelled in the next exam was a joke. The objective for the uninhabited island exam isn’t to kick your enemies down, but to climb up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The reward for getting 1st to 3rd place is enough to get within shooting distance of Class A, but the rules seem to be a bit troublesome. So, I wanted to prepare in advance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is this why you called me and Ayanokouji here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, Ichinose really did agree to team up with that woman. Did you guys butter her up well, or was it because she’s so incompetent that she thought that was all she could do? Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know. And if Sakayanagi heard that question, she’d ask you the same thing. Not many people would like being on your team. You’re a delinquent, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, everyone here’s that kind of delinquent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good for you, Katsuragi. Obnoxiously righteous as always. Not bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Flattering me won’t work, Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The most important thing about this special exam is to not lose any points from the 2nd year. I don’t want the 1st and 3rd years filling their pockets with my money. For that, we need to at least form an alliance, right? If you rely only on your own class, you’ll lack combat power.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If the small fry in Class B were added into this group, then I’d be better off fighting alone, but if I can draw in some firepower from elsewhere, then it’d be a different story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way, are you asking me to work with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not just you. Ayanokouji as well, who’s spaced out over there just listening to us talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… me too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why would I call you here if you weren’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse. Although Class A would get the rewards too, I don’t want to be on a team with someone like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a rash decision. You’ve gotta hear me out till the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not necessary. But– Why did you call Ayanokouji? I want to know that first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was surprising that he got a perfect score in math in the special exam at the end of April. I agree that he has a high ability in academics. But can you really say that he’s the right person to choose if you want to win?”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. If you get Ayanokouji in, it’ll reduce the class point reward to one thirds each. Since you’re inviting me from Class A anyway, wouldn’t it be better to invite Kitou to the group? Besides, if we need three classes, Kanzaki from Class C is still alone, and he should’ve priority over Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone who doesn’t know about him wouldn’t understand, but I made the right choice. Right, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop with that poor acting. You’re the man who beat me and shut me up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To shut you up?… Is that true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, I got my ass handed to me. Thanks to that, I almost decided to quit school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, admit it, Ayanokouji. Even if you continue to hide it from Katsuragi like that, I’ll just keep talking, yeah?”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I do admit it, do you think I’ll help you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, like with Katsuragi, it won’t be that simple.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I can’t accept this after all. I can’t believe that Ayanokouji beat you. Coming back to what I said earlier, if you have three classes working together, even if you come in first place, you’ll only get an average of 100 points. The gap between you and Class A will be impossible to close.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah yeah, completely forgot about that. As an advisor, you’re certainty qualified.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A serious negotiation? You knew that was impossible from the start, didn’t you? But you still came. Were you asked to spy for Class A?”<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a dead man, and you’re looking for a chance to come back to life. Am I right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether or not that’s true, it has nothing to do with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was a fair contract, we got 200 points from your class, and in return Class-A pays off the loan. All of my actions were only to lead Class-A along a …  …  better path.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure, if you only look at the numbers. However, what about the psychological impact that your class suffers every month? Why should all of you have to share your private points with us for so long?”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come to Class B, Katsuragi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, we’ll pay for the points you don’t have.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll soon defeat Sakayanagi, and then the entire Class A will fall. In other words, remaining in Class A is worthless, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What, you’ve been saving up after all! Even if you’re rotten, you’re still in Class A, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve seen this before, yeah? It’s the contract I sighed with you last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After negotiating with Sakayanagi, I’m giving this thing up for 5 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you tell her that the points would be used for stealing me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re not going to get a chance like this again, Katsuragi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh, Katsuragi, you have a surprisingly low opinion of yourself. Though, to be honest, you’re not going cheap.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The 5 million for nullifying the contract plus your current balance. The remaining points have been collected from the class. I’ve forced them into poverty to welcome you to our class!”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, sign it. Using 20 million points to change classes requires several conditions. You can’t force a person to change classes. In the end, the person must agree, and then use his or her funds to transfer to any class of their choosing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It all worked out, right, Katsuragi? You’ve been on your own until now, which makes it easier to invite you into our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is your fate. Accept it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I don’t really care that you brought me into your ranks, what exactly are you looking for? You won’t mind it if I speak my mind?”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why, it’s the Trial card he received.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sell it to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be able to get 500,000 points or so. That should be enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have one condition. Make a student in your class that has a Half Off card exchange their card with one of our students that has the Free Ride card. If you accept that, I’ll sell the trial card to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kuku, I guess it’s settled then. Half Off card, eh? It just so happens that Katsuragi has it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He plays dumb throughout — diluted coffee, shrugging answers; the meeting buys Katsuragi for 20 million; the Trial card costs 500,000; the Half Off card lands on Class D; Sakayanagi&#x27;s contract money is burned.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The spider at the center; he wires Class A/B/C/D without ever joining a group.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ally-ish nemesis; negotiates through Ishizaki&#x27;s email; he buys his Trial card for 500k.<span class=\"pg\">p.294–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> He watches him sign; the play is over before it began.<span class=\"pg\">p.301–312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She doesn&#x27;t know this meeting happened in her seat&#x27;s shadow.<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\">← Before: Kanzaki at the convenience store<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\">→ After: The July 16 deadline; Horikita and Ibuki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p298-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei the vendetta and the transfer he looks at ayanokoji stiffly  ryuuen hosts him  he answers for class a   you said there was someone else  were you talking about ayanokouji   what kind of meeting is this supposed to be  anyway   there s no way i can chill  if people see me with you  i ll be in trouble   then  let me make this simple for you  i m not going to tell you anything about this  you bastard   only on the day of the exam shall we know how sakayanagi will act  and no one will know before she says so  if you want to know despite this  you should go ask her directly   well  that might be true   didn t you also lose to ishizaki that one time   i don t know what you re planning to do  but that s impossible  even if you trap her on the island  she has plenty of private points for relief  also if by chance  something does incapacitate her  she still has protection points to fall back on   if you wanted to make me angry  then you ve succeeded  ryuuen  are you satisfied now   i don t know  and if sakayanagi heard that question  she d ask you the same thing  not many people would like being on your team  you re a delinquent  after all   in that case  everyone here s that kind of delinquent   flattering me won t work  ryuuen   no way  are you asking me to work with you   not just you  ayanokouji as well  who s spaced out over there just listening to us talk    me too   why are you asking   that s not necessary  but  why did you call ayanokouji  i want to know that first   it was surprising that he got a perfect score in math in the special exam at the end of april  i agree that he has a high ability in academics  but can you really say that he s the right person to choose if you want to win   that s right  if you get ayanokouji in  it ll reduce the class point reward to one thirds each  since you re inviting me from class a anyway  wouldn t it be better to invite kitou to the group  besides  if we need three classes  kanzaki from class c is still alone  and he should ve priority over ayanokouji   to shut you up  is that true   ah  i got my ass handed to me  thanks to that  i almost decided to quit school   no  i can t accept this after all  i can t believe that ayanokouji beat you  coming back to what i said earlier  if you have three classes working together  even if you come in first place  you ll only get an average of 100 points  the gap between you and class a will be impossible to close   no matter what you say  there s no chance of me working with you  it s true that i have a semi antagonistic relationship with sakayanagi  however  i don t want to trouble my classmates  i don t want to work with you   it was a fair contract  we got 200 points from your class  and in return class a pays off the loan  all of my actions were only to lead class a along a       better path   so  so what   are you crazy  you re asking me to come to class b   even if you have the necessary points  why should i come to class b  you think i would give up my place in class a    about 1 8 million points    yes    no  it s sakayanagi  she d accept it   the 5 million for nullifying the contract plus your current balance  the remaining points have been collected from the class  i ve forced them into poverty to welcome you to our class   come on  sign it  using 20 million points to change classes requires several conditions  you can t force a person to change classes  in the end  the person must agree  and then use his or her funds to transfer to any class of their choosing   you seem to be serious   although i don t really care that you brought me into your ranks  what exactly are you looking for  you won t mind it if i speak my mind   you re free to interpret it however you want  but i cannot confirm anything   i won t have much money anyway  there would be no point in holding on to the half off card  totsuka yahiko  his great admirer  was expelled by sakayanagi  his buried rage is the lever ryuuen pulls  he signs for his underclassmen and finally feels free  cold  precise  proud  he chooses his own fall deliberately  the half off card is his now  he recruits him by exploiting his hatred  she is his white whale  he hates her with a clear conscience  the wound ryuuen presses","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p298-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p298-1\">The vendetta and the transfer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.298–314<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He looks at Ayanokōji stiffly; Ryuuen hosts him; he answers for Class A.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You said there was someone else, were you talking about Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “What kind of meeting is this supposed to be, anyway?”<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “There’s no way I can chill. if people see me with you, I’ll be in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, let me make this simple for you. I’m not going to tell you anything about this, you bastard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Only on the day of the exam shall we know how Sakayanagi will act, and no one will know before she says so. If you want to know despite this, you should go ask her directly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that might be true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn’t you also lose to Ishizaki that one time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re planning to do, but that’s impossible. Even if you trap her on the island, she has plenty of private points for relief. Also if by chance, something does incapacitate her, she still has protection points to fall back on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you wanted to make me angry, then you’ve succeeded, Ryuuen. Are you satisfied now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know. And if Sakayanagi heard that question, she’d ask you the same thing. Not many people would like being on your team. You’re a delinquent, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, everyone here’s that kind of delinquent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Flattering me won’t work, Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way, are you asking me to work with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.303<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not just you. Ayanokouji as well, who’s spaced out over there just listening to us talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… me too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are you asking?”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not necessary. But– Why did you call Ayanokouji? I want to know that first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was surprising that he got a perfect score in math in the special exam at the end of April. I agree that he has a high ability in academics. But can you really say that he’s the right person to choose if you want to win?”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. If you get Ayanokouji in, it’ll reduce the class point reward to one thirds each. Since you’re inviting me from Class A anyway, wouldn’t it be better to invite Kitou to the group? Besides, if we need three classes, Kanzaki from Class C is still alone, and he should’ve priority over Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To shut you up?… Is that true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, I got my ass handed to me. Thanks to that, I almost decided to quit school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I can’t accept this after all. I can’t believe that Ayanokouji beat you. Coming back to what I said earlier, if you have three classes working together, even if you come in first place, you’ll only get an average of 100 points. The gap between you and Class A will be impossible to close.”<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter what you say, there’s no chance of me working with you. It’s true that I have a semi-antagonistic relationship with Sakayanagi. However, I don’t want to trouble my classmates. I don’t want to work with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was a fair contract, we got 200 points from your class, and in return Class-A pays off the loan. All of my actions were only to lead Class-A along a …  …  better path.”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So… So what!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you crazy? You’re asking me to come to Class B?”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you have the necessary points, why should I come to Class B? You think I would give up my place in Class A?”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… About 1.8 million points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… No, it’s Sakayanagi, she’d accept it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.310<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The 5 million for nullifying the contract plus your current balance. The remaining points have been collected from the class. I’ve forced them into poverty to welcome you to our class!”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, sign it. Using 20 million points to change classes requires several conditions. You can’t force a person to change classes. In the end, the person must agree, and then use his or her funds to transfer to any class of their choosing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I don’t really care that you brought me into your ranks, what exactly are you looking for? You won’t mind it if I speak my mind?”<span class=\"pg\">p.312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re free to interpret it however you want, but I cannot confirm anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t have much money anyway. There would be no point in holding on to the Half Off card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Totsuka Yahiko, his great admirer, was expelled by Sakayanagi; his buried rage is the lever Ryuuen pulls; he signs for his underclassmen and finally feels free.<span class=\"pg\">p.301–312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold, precise, proud; he chooses his own fall deliberately; the Half Off card is his now.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He recruits him by exploiting his hatred.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She is his white whale; he hates her with a clear conscience.<span class=\"pg\">p.301–312<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> The wound Ryuuen presses.<span class=\"pg\">p.301–312<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y2v2-p206-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p299-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi coverage note  passing mentions  in addition to the three people ryuuen named  class a s hashimoto  and kamuro had formed a group with one of class c s best students  ninomiya   this couldn t be a mere coincidence    the  more people  special card that asakura was supposed to have had  now with hashimoto from class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p299-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html#sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p299-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.299–300<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In addition to the three people Ryuuen named, Class A’s Hashimoto, and Kamuro,had formed a group with one of Class C’s best students, Ninomiya.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “This couldn’t be a mere coincidence.” — the ‘More People’ special card that Asakura was supposed to have had, now with Hashimoto from Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y2v2-p215-1\">← Before: Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p299-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"kamuro-masumi","q":"kamuro masumi coverage note  passing mentions  i ve checked the group composition using the oaa  and while you guys seem to have formed groups with class c and d  kitou seems to be alone  and then  no matter how you spin it  ichinose  shibata and sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p299-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kamuro-masumi.html#sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p299-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.299<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I’ve checked the group composition using the OAA, and while you guys seem to have formed groups with Class C and D, Kitou seems to be alone. And then, no matter how you spin it, Ichinose, Shibata and Sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kamuro-masumi-y2v2-p215-1\">← Before: Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ninomiya-yui-y2v2-p299-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ninomiya-yui","q":"ninomiya yui ninomiya  referenced  ryuuen names the  more people  card holder trade  class a s hashimoto and kamuro had formed a group with one of  class c s best students  ninomiya  the corpus prints no class and no surname on this page  the roster s only ninomiya is class 2 d s ninomiya yui   the class attribution printed in this volume does not fit her file  recorded as printed  unresolved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ninomiya-yui-y2v2-p299-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ninomiya-yui.html#sc-ninomiya-yui-y2v2-p299-1\">Ninomiya (referenced)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.299<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ninomiya-yui.html\">Ninomiya Yui<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Ryuuen names the “More People” card holder trade: Class A&#x27;s Hashimoto and Kamuro had formed a group with one of “Class C&#x27;s best students, Ninomiya.” The corpus prints no class and no surname on this page; the roster&#x27;s only Ninomiya is Class 2-D&#x27;s Ninomiya Yui — the class attribution printed in this volume does not fit her file; recorded as printed, unresolved.<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p299-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"shibata-sou","q":"shibata so coverage note  passing mentions  and then  no matter how you spin it  ichinose  shibata and sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p299-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p299-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.299<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “and then, no matter how you spin it, Ichinose, Shibata and Sakayanagi being in a group together smells fishy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y2v2-p215-1\">← Before: Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p300-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"asakura-mako","q":"asakura mako coverage note  passing mentions  this couldn t be a mere coincidence    the  more people  special card that asakura was supposed to have had  now with hashimoto from class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p300-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/asakura-mako.html#sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p300-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.300<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/asakura-mako.html\">Asakura Mako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “This couldn’t be a mere coincidence.” — the ‘More People’ special card that Asakura was supposed to have had, now with Hashimoto from Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-asakura-mako-y2v2-p168-1\">← Before: Named in passing (Ch.3)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p300-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ishizaki-daichi","q":"ishizaki daichi coverage note  passing mentions  didn t you also lose to ishizaki that one time   ishizaki kun s idea to call out to ayanokouji and invite him before anyone could was probably right    hiyori s pov   i could easily have said something to him  but i decided to not advise him on anything   we are attracting to much attention here so let s move on ishizaki kun    hiyori s abort move  he is part of the capture","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p300-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html#sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p300-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.300–344<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Didn’t you also lose to Ishizaki that one time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ishizaki-kun’s idea to call out to Ayanokouji and invite him before anyone could was probably right.” — Hiyori’s POV.<span class=\"pg\">p.342<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I could easily have said something to him, but I decided to not advise him on anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.343<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “We are attracting to much attention here so let’s move on Ishizaki-kun.” — Hiyori’s abort move; he is part of the capture.<span class=\"pg\">p.344<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p294-1\">← Before: Ishizaki&#x27;s email<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p315-1\">→ After: The Ibuki problem<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p300-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"totsuka-yahiko","q":"totsuka yahiko coverage note  passing mentions  that totsuka who was holding you back  he is gone now  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p300-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p300-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.300<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “That Totsuka who was holding you back, he is gone now, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p301-1\">→ After: Totsuka (referenced)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p301-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"totsuka-yahiko","q":"totsuka yahiko totsuka  referenced  totsuka yahiko   a great admirer of katsuragi  expelled from school because of sakayanagi  the wound ryuuen presses to lure katsuragi to class b  totsuka s expulsion is the reason ryuuen knows katsuragi s hidden grudge","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p301-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p301-1\">Totsuka (referenced)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.301–307<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Totsuka Yahiko — a great admirer of Katsuragi; expelled from school because of Sakayanagi; the wound Ryuuen presses to lure Katsuragi to Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Totsuka&#x27;s expulsion is the reason Ryuuen knows Katsuragi&#x27;s hidden grudge.<span class=\"pg\">p.307<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y2v2-p300-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ibuki-mio tsube-hitomi kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the july 16 deadline  horikita and ibuki ishizaki calls him on the morning of the deadline  ibuki still hasn t grouped  he spots horikita in the lobby   what are you going to do about your group   it s too late to bring that up  anyway  i m not going to group up with anyone this time  if you consider that the maximum number of people in a group is 6  it s not a bad idea to go alone   i am aware that i ll have to bear that amount of risk  isn t that why you re not in a group as well   what s the difference   you had a problem with your health during the uninhabited island exam last year   i can t believe you re bringing up something which happened a year ago  anyone can get sick   yeah  however  you also took a break in the winter due to a fever  that makes it twice in one year   you just happened to spend the year without taking a leave of absence  do you think that means you won t get sick this time   in terms of taking care of myself  i m more confident than you are   i see  it s true that i m not as good as you at taking care of myself  i admit that  but even if that s the case  making it out as something to be worried about   it s enough that you know  i had no intention of opposing you   yeah   in our class  only you  i  and koenji haven t formed a group yet  us three  the rest of our classmates have formed a small group of at least two people  it s safer to form a group of two  if possible   that s only in our class   are there any girls left who haven t formed a group   ah  there s one person i can think of   who are you talking about   ishizaki is worried because ibuki doesn t have anyone to group up with  how about grouping up with her for the special exam  horikita   me and ibuki   if it s two girls  you can merge with any other small group later  why don t we just hear them out   that s true  having some kind of insurance would be better  all right  i ll hear her out  the summit with ibuki  the deal fails  horikita provokes the grudge   hey  ayanokouji  over here   hurry up and come over   why are ayanokouji and horikita here   actually  there s something we wanted to discuss  so i asked ishizaki to call you  ibuki   that s my choice   i don t need it   well  you say that but the fact is there s no one who wants to team up with you   huh  what s wrong  ayanokouji   huh  what s wrong  ayanokouji   it s nothing  by the way  horikita here is the same as ibuki  she hasn t teamed up with anyone yet   so   next exam  if you don t form a group  you ll be at a disadvantage  even if it s not three people  if at least the two of you form a group  then even in the worst case scenario  if one of you gets eliminated  you ll be able to continue   don t tell me you want me to group up with horikita   well  that s about right   ha  who died and made you boss   apart from your physical ability  you re not much good at anything else   hey  you too  don t say whatever you want   you too  you want me to group up with horikita to help them out  don t you   i m honored   i already hate this guy a lot  but my hatred for horikita is even higher than that   ah  but i don t remember saying i wanted to be in a group with you   huh  what do you mean   looks like you ve got things mixed up  you ve been left behind because nobody wanted to be with you  and i didn t group up with anyone because i wanted to fight alone  although we re both lone wolves  our situations are not the same   i m also on my own because i want to be  anyway  you say you want to go it alone  that s perfect  it s a challenge  horikita   can i ask you something  why do you want to fight me  it s true that we competed at the uninhabited island exam and during the sports festival  but that wasn t anything special right   you re the only one who thinks that   it seems like this was a waste of time   wait  do you accept  or no   i am going in alone  but i m not choosing to work alone throughout  when the special exams start  i ll merge with another group if necessary   lame   lameness isn t a reason to change the way i take the test   if you insist on fighting alone  then even if i form a group  try not to lose  if you win  then i ll recognise you a bit   not better  nobody went alone except him  horikita  kouenji  and ibuki   and now horikita may hear no more mergers  the rival at the table  he dumped the ibuki problem on him  she pairs with nishino through ichinose  he shows up at the store  the gap between him and the others widens","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\">The July 16 deadline; Horikita and Ibuki<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.315–318<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ishizaki calls him on the morning of the deadline; Ibuki still hasn&#x27;t grouped; he spots Horikita in the lobby. The summit with Ibuki; the deal fails; Horikita provokes the grudge.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#tsube-hitomi\">Tsube Hitomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “What are you going to do about your group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s too late to bring that up. Anyway, I’m not going to group up with anyone this time. If you consider that the maximum number of people in a group is 6, it’s not a bad idea to go alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I am aware that I’ll have to bear that amount of risk. Isn’t that why you’re not in a group as well?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>56 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s the difference?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You had a problem with your health during the uninhabited island exam last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t believe you’re bringing up something which happened a year ago. Anyone can get sick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. However, you also took a break in the winter due to a fever. That makes it twice in one year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just happened to spend the year without taking a leave of absence. Do you think that means you won’t get sick this time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In terms of taking care of myself, I’m more confident than you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. It’s true that I’m not as good as you at taking care of myself. I admit that. But even if that’s the case, making it out as something to be worried about–“<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s enough that you know. I had no intention of opposing you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In our class, only you, I, and Koenji haven’t formed a group yet, us three. The rest of our classmates have formed a small group of at least two people. It’s safer to form a group of two, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s only in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are there any girls left who haven’t formed a group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, there’s one person I can think of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ishizaki is worried because Ibuki doesn’t have anyone to group up with. How about grouping up with her for the special exam, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me and Ibuki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s two girls, you can merge with any other small group later. Why don’t we just hear them out?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, having some kind of insurance would be better… All right, I’ll hear her out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Ayanokouji! Over here!”<span class=\"pg\">p.319<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hurry up and come over!”<span class=\"pg\">p.319<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are Ayanokouji and Horikita here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, there’s something we wanted to discuss, so I asked Ishizaki to call you, Ibuki.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s my choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t need it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you say that but the fact is there’s no one who wants to team up with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What’s wrong, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What’s wrong, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing. By the way, Horikita here is the same as Ibuki, she hasn’t teamed up with anyone yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Next exam, if you don’t form a group, you’ll be at a disadvantage. Even if it’s not three people, if at least the two of you form a group, then even in the worst case scenario, if one of you gets eliminated, you’ll be able to continue.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t tell me you want me to group up with Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s about right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha? Who died and made you boss?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Apart from your physical ability… You’re not much good at anything else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you too, don’t say whatever you want”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You too, you want me to group up with Horikita to help them out, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m honored.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already hate this guy a lot, but my hatred for Horikita is even higher than that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, but I don’t remember saying I wanted to be in a group with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you’ve got things mixed up. You’ve been left behind because nobody wanted to be with you, and I didn’t group up with anyone because I wanted to fight alone. Although we’re both lone wolves, our situations are not the same.”<span class=\"pg\">p.323<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m also on my own because I want to be. Anyway, you say you want to go it alone, that’s perfect. It’s a challenge, Horikita!”<span class=\"pg\">p.323<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I ask you something? Why do you want to fight me? It’s true that we competed at the uninhabited island exam and during the sports festival, but that wasn’t anything special right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the only one who thinks that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like this was a waste of time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Do you accept? Or no?”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am going in alone, but I’m not choosing to work alone throughout. When the special exams start, I’ll merge with another group if necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lame!”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lameness Isn’t a reason to change the way I take the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you insist on fighting alone, then even if I form a group, try not to lose. If you win, then I’ll recognise you a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Not better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nobody went alone except him, Horikita, Kouenji, and Ibuki — and now Horikita may hear no more mergers.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The rival at the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> He dumped the Ibuki problem on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsube Hitomi<\/b> She pairs with Nishino through Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He shows up at the store; the gap between him and the others widens.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–297<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\">← Before: The café with Ryuuen and Katsuragi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\">→ After: The eve of the island exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p315-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki  the lone wolf ishizaki s alarm  almost everyone has grouped  ibuki still hasn t  she wants to fight alone   that s my choice   i don t need it   well  you say that but the fact is there s no one who wants to team up with you  he tries to push horikita onto her  she bristles  ishizaki blinks   huh  what s wrong  ayanokouji   ayanokouji  she doesn t seem to like you very much   don t tell me you want me to group up with horikita   ha  who died and made you boss   apart from your physical ability  you re not much good at anything else   hey  you too  don t say whatever you want   you too  you want me to group up with horikita to help them out  don t you   i m honored   i already hate this guy a lot  but my hatred for horikita is even higher than that  she rejects the deal  she s at war with horikita  island loss   sports festival loss  one win one loss each   i m also on my own because i want to be  anyway  you say you want to go it alone  that s perfect  it s a challenge  horikita   you re the only one who thinks that   it seems like this was a waste of time   wait  do you accept  or no   i am going in alone  but i m not choosing to work alone throughout  when the special exams start  i ll merge with another group if necessary   lame   if you insist on fighting alone  then even if i form a group  try not to lose  if you win  then i ll recognise you a bit   not better  proud warrior with a grudge  she needs the duel more than the safety  her hatred of horikita is the engine  she ll go it alone on her own terms  their duel history  uninhabited island  ibuki won  and 100m race at the sports festival  horikita won  both  evenly matched  the rival she seeks to beat  the classmate who keeps failing to recruit her  the one she hates politely  she wants a rematch elsewhere","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p315-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p315-1\">Ibuki, the lone wolf<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.315–325<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ishizaki&#x27;s alarm: almost everyone has grouped; Ibuki still hasn&#x27;t; she wants to fight alone. He tries to push Horikita onto her; she bristles; Ishizaki blinks. She rejects the deal; she&#x27;s at war with Horikita (island loss + sports-festival loss); one win one loss each.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “That’s my choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I don’t need it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Well, you say that but the fact is there’s no one who wants to team up with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What’s wrong, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, she doesn’t seem to like you very much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t tell me you want me to group up with Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha? Who died and made you boss?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Apart from your physical ability… You’re not much good at anything else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you too, don’t say whatever you want”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You too, you want me to group up with Horikita to help them out, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m honored.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already hate this guy a lot, but my hatred for Horikita is even higher than that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m also on my own because I want to be. Anyway, you say you want to go it alone, that’s perfect. It’s a challenge, Horikita!”<span class=\"pg\">p.323<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the only one who thinks that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like this was a waste of time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Do you accept? Or no?”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am going in alone, but I’m not choosing to work alone throughout. When the special exams start, I’ll merge with another group if necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lame!”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you insist on fighting alone, then even if I form a group, try not to lose. If you win, then I’ll recognise you a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Not better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Proud warrior with a grudge; she needs the duel more than the safety; her hatred of Horikita is the engine; she&#x27;ll go it alone on her own terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Their duel history: uninhabited island (Ibuki won) and 100m race at the sports festival (Horikita won); both ~evenly matched.<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The rival she seeks to beat.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> The classmate who keeps failing to recruit her.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one she hates politely; she wants a rematch elsewhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p163-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p315-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio tsube-hitomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi","q":"ishizaki daichi the ibuki problem he calls him as the deadline day arrives  ibuki still hasn t grouped   yo  ayanokouji  morning   today s the last day for forming small groups  right  i have something important to talk to you about   is it about nishino  last i checked  she hadn t formed a group   in the end  she couldn t find anyone in her class to team up with  so she asked ichinose to help her  now  tsube from class c will help her out   ibuki  right   yeah  ibuki s on her own  is there anyone who would group up with her   it s risky to take the special exam by yourself  i understand how you feel   give me some time  i think i have an idea   seriously  sorry about dumping this on you so early in the morning  he gathers horikita and ibuki  the negotiation fails spectacularly   hey  ayanokouji  over here   hurry up and come over   why are ayanokouji and horikita here   huh  what s wrong  ayanokouji   it s nothing  by the way  horikita here is the same as ibuki  she hasn t teamed up with anyone yet   you too  you want me to group up with horikita to help them out  don t you   i didn t know it would be horikita  but wouldn t it be great if you formed a group   i m honored  he pitches horikita to ibuki with a smile  the grudge prevents any chance of a group  the lone wolf he wants saved  he brokers tsube s help for nishino  he dumps the problem on him without a second thought","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p315-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html#sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p315-1\">The Ibuki problem<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.315–321<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He calls him as the deadline day arrives; Ibuki still hasn&#x27;t grouped. He gathers Horikita and Ibuki; the negotiation fails spectacularly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#tsube-hitomi\">Tsube Hitomi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Yo, Ayanokouji. Morning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Today’s the last day for forming small groups, right? I have something important to talk to you about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Is it about Nishino? Last I checked, she hadn’t formed a group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the end, she couldn’t find anyone in her class to team up with, so she asked Ichinose to help her. Now, Tsube from Class C will help her out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Ibuki’s on her own. Is there anyone who would group up with her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s risky to take the special exam by yourself. I understand how you feel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Give me some time. I think I have an idea.”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seriously? Sorry about dumping this on you so early in the morning!”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Ayanokouji! Over here!”<span class=\"pg\">p.319<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hurry up and come over!”<span class=\"pg\">p.319<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are Ayanokouji and Horikita here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What’s wrong, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s nothing. By the way, Horikita here is the same as Ibuki, she hasn’t teamed up with anyone yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You too, you want me to group up with Horikita to help them out, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t know it would be Horikita, but wouldn’t it be great if you formed a group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m honored.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He pitches Horikita to Ibuki with a smile; the grudge prevents any chance of a group.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The lone wolf he wants saved.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsube Hitomi<\/b> He brokers Tsube&#x27;s help for Nishino.<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He dumps the problem on him without a second thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–325<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y2v2-p300-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tsube-hitomi-y2v2-p315-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"tsube-hitomi","q":"tsube hitomi tsube pairs with nishino tsube hitomi  class 2 c    an excellent student with more than b in both academic and physical ability  she agrees to help nishino  after ichinose brokered it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tsube-hitomi-y2v2-p315-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tsube pairs with Nishino<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.315<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#tsube-hitomi\">Tsube Hitomi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Tsube Hitomi (Class 2-C) — an excellent student with more than B in both academic and physical ability; she agrees to help Nishino (after Ichinose brokered it).<span class=\"pg\">p.315<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p316-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the horikita ibuki summit he corners her in the lobby  she agrees to hear ibuki out   what are you going to do about your group   it s too late to bring that up  anyway  i m not going to group up with anyone this time  if you consider that the maximum number of people in a group is 6  it s not a bad idea to go alone   i am aware that i ll have to bear that amount of risk  isn t that why you re not in a group as well   what s the difference   you had a problem with your health during the uninhabited island exam last year   i can t believe you re bringing up something which happened a year ago  anyone can get sick   yeah  however  you also took a break in the winter due to a fever  that makes it twice in one year   you just happened to spend the year without taking a leave of absence  do you think that means you won t get sick this time   in terms of taking care of myself  i m more confident than you are   i see  it s true that i m not as good as you at taking care of myself  i admit that    the printed sentence continues across the line break and breaks off at the dash after  worried about  where the print uses an opening quote glyph as its closer  recorded as printed   it s enough that you know  i had no intention of opposing you   yeah   in our class  only you  i  and koenji haven t formed a group yet  us three  the rest of our classmates have formed a small group of at least two people  it s safer to form a group of two  if possible   that s only in our class   are there any girls left who haven t formed a group   ah  there s one person i can think of   who are you talking about   ibuki from class 2 b  didn t you check the oaa   well  last i checked i did notice that she was alone   ishizaki is worried because ibuki doesn t have anyone to group up with  how about grouping up with her for the special exam  horikita   me and ibuki   if it s two girls  you can merge with any other small group later  why don t we just hear them out   that s true  having some kind of insurance would be better  all right  i ll hear her out  the summit collapses beautifully  her grudge match with ibuki resumes   you seem to be close friends   he s a nice guy   even so  i wouldn t get too close to him   ah  but i don t remember saying i wanted to be in a group with you   huh  what do you mean   looks like you ve got things mixed up  you ve been left behind because nobody wanted to be with you  and i didn t group up with anyone because i wanted to fight alone  although we re both lone wolves  our situations are not the same   can i ask you something  why do you want to fight me  it s true that we competed at the uninhabited island exam and during the sports festival  but that wasn t anything special right   you re the only one who thinks that   it seems like this was a waste of time   wait  do you accept  or no   i am going in alone  but i m not choosing to work alone throughout  when the special exams start  i ll merge with another group if necessary   lame   lameness isn t a reason to change the way i take the test   if you insist on fighting alone  then even if i form a group  try not to lose  if you win  then i ll recognise you a bit   not better  her own loss record against ibuki  island 1 1  sports festival 1 1  is the reason she wants no group  she provokes ibuki to make her reckless  the rival at the far end of the table  she wants to see her try  he sends ishizaki with the proposal  she accepts after the 100m loss joke  she shoots down every word he says","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p316-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p316-1\">The Horikita–Ibuki summit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.316–325<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He corners her in the lobby; she agrees to hear Ibuki out. The summit collapses beautifully; her grudge match with Ibuki resumes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “What are you going to do about your group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s too late to bring that up. Anyway, I’m not going to group up with anyone this time. If you consider that the maximum number of people in a group is 6, it’s not a bad idea to go alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I am aware that I’ll have to bear that amount of risk. Isn’t that why you’re not in a group as well?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>39 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s the difference?”<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You had a problem with your health during the uninhabited island exam last year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t believe you’re bringing up something which happened a year ago. Anyone can get sick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. However, you also took a break in the winter due to a fever. That makes it twice in one year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just happened to spend the year without taking a leave of absence. Do you think that means you won’t get sick this time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In terms of taking care of myself, I’m more confident than you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. It’s true that I’m not as good as you at taking care of myself. I admit that.” — the printed sentence continues across the line break and breaks off at the dash after “worried about”, where the print uses an opening quote glyph as its closer; recorded as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s enough that you know. I had no intention of opposing you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In our class, only you, I, and Koenji haven’t formed a group yet, us three. The rest of our classmates have formed a small group of at least two people. It’s safer to form a group of two, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s only in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are there any girls left who haven’t formed a group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, there’s one person I can think of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki from Class 2-B. Didn’t you check the OAA?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, last I checked I did notice that she was alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ishizaki is worried because Ibuki doesn’t have anyone to group up with. How about grouping up with her for the special exam, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me and Ibuki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s two girls, you can merge with any other small group later. Why don’t we just hear them out?”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, having some kind of insurance would be better… All right, I’ll hear her out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be close friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s a nice guy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I wouldn’t get too close to him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, but I don’t remember saying I wanted to be in a group with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you’ve got things mixed up. You’ve been left behind because nobody wanted to be with you, and I didn’t group up with anyone because I wanted to fight alone. Although we’re both lone wolves, our situations are not the same.”<span class=\"pg\">p.323<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I ask you something? Why do you want to fight me? It’s true that we competed at the uninhabited island exam and during the sports festival, but that wasn’t anything special right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.323<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the only one who thinks that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.323<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like this was a waste of time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.324<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Do you accept? Or no?”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am going in alone, but I’m not choosing to work alone throughout. When the special exams start, I’ll merge with another group if necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lame!”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lameness Isn’t a reason to change the way I take the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you insist on fighting alone, then even if I form a group, try not to lose. If you win, then I’ll recognise you a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Not better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her own loss record against Ibuki (island 1-1, sports festival 1-1) is the reason she wants no group; she provokes Ibuki to make her reckless.<span class=\"pg\">p.323–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The rival at the far end of the table; she wants to see her try.<span class=\"pg\">p.316–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He sends Ishizaki with the proposal; she accepts after the 100m-loss joke.<span class=\"pg\">p.316–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> She shoots down every word he says.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–325<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p255-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p330-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s deal with Kouenji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko chabashira-sae kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the eve of the island exam tomorrow the special exams begin  keisei comes to his seat  grim  mid checklist   honestly  surviving on an uninhabited island isn t something very good at  you might as well ask me to catch a cloud   it s no wonder  given it s so far from the norm   but it s even harder on the girls  so i can t really complain   although we re competing in different groups  i still want to do what i can to help out   yeah  there should be some way we can cooperate  so i ll lend a hand when the time comes   but  are you alright going alone  if you get sick  it s over  if by any chance you receive the penalty  you d have to pay 6 million points  it d all be over in an instant   my perfect attendance record at least until now is one of the few things that i m proud of   you re starting to sound a bit sarcastic lately  you know  the last briefing  chabashira s wishes are plain  all 39 students take their seats   it s the start of summer vacation today  but you guys look like you re having a tough time  well  i suppose that can t be helped   then we ll start with the final check  if you re not feeling well now  you have to report it   no problems  that s great   this is not your first time taking a special exam  you have been fighting in this school for more than a year  and have overcome all manner of hardships  nonetheless  this special exam will not be easy to pass   i ve only got one wish for all of you  if you can  don t let a single one of your classmates disappear  and return to this classroom once again   we ll gather in the court in 10 minutes for a roll call  remember to go to the bathroom first  if you need to  kouenji pulls horikita into the corner  the full freedom negotiation  horikita closes her deal   can i talk to you for a minute  okay  horikita girl   it s rare for you to come to talk to me of your own volition   there s something i d like to talk about regarding the special exam that s about to begin   oh my  you finally feel like helping us  right   let s just say that you re half right   what s your objective  can you tell me the other half of what you mean to say   the class points for the top three groups  you have an extreme desire for them  right   of course  depending on how many points we can get  the order of the classes could change by a great magnitude   then let me make a suggestion  alright  if i get a good result on the uninhabited island exam  i want you to promise me full freedom   exactement  not only should i be allowed that  but you should also work hard to remove every obstacle in my way like a dray horse  you know   that s not something i can easily agree to  everyone else in the class probably feels the same   consider it to be an advance payment before graduation   looks like you too can feel the crisis looming over your head  your classmates won t just forgive your carefree speech and antics forever  if a special exam like the class vote is held again  you d be made into their scapegoat   there s no need for such drastic proposals  can t you just be like everyone else   sorry kouenji kun  i put too much value on your talent to let you do  just alright  on this exam and be a spectator later on  it just doesn t sit right with me   i see  in other words  negotiations have broken down  right   not exactly  if i can add some conditions to it  it d be an acceptable proposal   a vague answer like getting a good result won t do  the school has prepared a reward for the group that finishes in 1st place in this exam  if you get first place on your own  that might be reason enough for us to consider this an advance payment till graduation   no problem  let s consider this a done deal   no  that s not enough   i haven t finished telling you my conditions yet  i ll have to work with you because of your big talk  but if we don t get first place in the end  it s a problem for us too   in other words   if you don t get first place  then you will have to help the class in the future  such as the next special exam  and get results  you have to make this promise to me   i see that you ve given a confident order  horikita girl   if you agree to the aforementioned conditions  i ll accept your proposal   then it s a deal  horikita girl  please don t forget the conditions i mentioned   after all  there is nothing i can t doooo   i have no idea how serious kouenji will get this time   well  that s true   but this is a rare opportunity  i have managed to get him to promise us his future commitment in the end   if he actually could get a rank in the top spots  it would be great  we could surpass the other classes like that   we come in first  and kouenji comes in 2nd or 3rd  if we can do that  our class will gain a huge advantage  and we ll be able to redeem ourselves after falling behind up to now   well  there s one part that i m uncomfortable with  i can never anticipate       what kouenji is going to do   that s true  but to easily take the top spot is a completely different matter altogether  the first place race  sakayanagi  ichinose  ryuuen  housen  amasawa  nagumo  kiriyama  kiryuin   and him  he aims for a high spot  the private exchange before the storm  the full freedom deal is struck with conditions  she plays chess before the first move  the last blessing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\">The eve of the island exam<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.327–335<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tomorrow the special exams begin; Keisei comes to his seat, grim, mid-checklist. The last briefing; Chabashira&#x27;s wishes are plain; all 39 students take their seats. Kouenji pulls Horikita into the corner; the full-freedom negotiation; Horikita closes her deal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Honestly, surviving on an uninhabited island isn’t something very good at. You might as well ask me to catch a cloud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.327<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s no wonder, given it’s so far from the norm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.327<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “But it’s even harder on the girls, so I can’t really complain.”<span class=\"pg\">p.327<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>50 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although we’re competing in different groups, I still want to do what I can to help out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. There should be some way we can cooperate, so I’ll lend a hand when the time comes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, are you alright going alone? If you get sick, it’s over. If by any chance you receive the penalty, you’d have to pay 6 million points… It’d all be over in an instant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My perfect attendance record at least until now is one of the few things that I’m proud of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re starting to sound a bit sarcastic lately, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s the start of summer vacation today, but you guys look like you’re having a tough time. Well, I suppose that can’t be helped.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then we’ll start with the final check. If you’re not feeling well now, you have to report it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problems, that’s great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is not your first time taking a special exam. You have been fighting in this school for more than a year, and have overcome all manner of hardships. Nonetheless, this special exam will not be easy to pass.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve only got one wish for all of you. If you can, don’t let a single one of your classmates disappear, and return to this classroom once again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll gather in the court in 10 minutes for a roll call. Remember to go to the bathroom first, if you need to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I talk to you for a minute, okay? Horikita girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s rare for you to come to talk to me of your own volition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s something I’d like to talk about regarding the special exam that’s about to begin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh my, you finally feel like helping us, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s just say that you’re half right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s your objective? Can you tell me the other half of what you mean to say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The class points for the top three groups. You have an EXTREME DESIRE for them, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Depending on how many points we can get, the order of the classes could change by a great magnitude.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then let me make a suggestion, alright? If I get a good result on the uninhabited island exam, I want you to promise me full FREEDOM.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactement! Not only should I be allowed that, but you should also work hard to remove every obstacle in my way like a dray horse, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not something I can easily agree to. Everyone else in the class probably feels the same”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Consider it to be an advance payment before graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you too can feel the crisis looming over your head. Your classmates won’t just forgive your carefree speech and antics forever. If a special exam like the class vote is held again, you’d be made into their scapegoat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need for such drastic proposals. Can’t you just be like everyone else?”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry Kouenji-kun, I put too much value on your talent to let you do “just alright” on this exam and be a spectator later on. It just doesn’t sit right with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. In other words, negotiations have broken down, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “—-Not exactly. If I can add some conditions to it, it’d be an acceptable proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A vague answer like getting a good result won’t do. The school has prepared a reward for the group that finishes in 1st place in this exam. If you get first place on your own, that might be reason enough for us to consider this an advance payment till graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problem, let’s consider this a done deal!”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s not enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I haven’t finished telling you my conditions yet. I’ll have to work with you because of your big talk, but if we don’t get first place in the end, it’s a problem for us too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words?’”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t get first place, then you will have to help the class in the future, such as the next special exam, and get results. You have to make this promise to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see that you’ve given a confident ORDER, Horikita girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you agree to the aforementioned conditions, I’ll accept your proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then it’s a deal. Horikita girl, please don’t forget the conditions I mentioned.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After all, there is nothing I can’t doooo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea how serious Kouenji will get this time…”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But this is a rare opportunity. I have managed to get him to promise us his future commitment in the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he actually could get a rank in the top spots, it would be great, we could surpass the other classes like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We come in first, and Kouenji comes in 2nd or 3rd. If we can do that, our class will gain a huge advantage, and we’ll be able to redeem ourselves after falling behind up to now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s one part that I’m uncomfortable with. I can never anticipate …  …  what Kouenji is going to do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, but to easily take the top spot is a completely different matter altogether.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The first-place race: Sakayanagi, Ichinose, Ryuuen, Housen, Amasawa, Nagumo, Kiriyama, Kiryūin — and him. He aims for a high spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.333–335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The private exchange before the storm.<span class=\"pg\">p.327–328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The full-freedom deal is struck with conditions.<span class=\"pg\">p.330–334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She plays chess before the first move.<span class=\"pg\">p.330–334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The last blessing.<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\">← Before: The July 16 deadline; Horikita and Ibuki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1\">→ After: Tsukishiro&#x27;s final push<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p327-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko keisei s pre exam fear he comes to his seat  grim mid checklist   honestly  surviving on an uninhabited island isn t something very good at  you might as well ask me to catch a cloud   but it s even harder on the girls  so i can t really complain   although we re competing in different groups  i still want to do what i can to help out   but  are you alright going alone  if you get sick  it s over  if by any chance you receive the penalty  you d have to pay 6 million points  it d all be over in an instant   you re starting to sound a bit sarcastic lately  you know  he promises to help his comrades regardless of their groups","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p327-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p327-1\">Keisei&#x27;s pre-exam fear<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.327–328<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He comes to his seat, grim mid-checklist.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Honestly, surviving on an uninhabited island isn’t something very good at. You might as well ask me to catch a cloud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.327<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “But it’s even harder on the girls, so I can’t really complain.”<span class=\"pg\">p.327<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Although we’re competing in different groups, I still want to do what I can to help out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, are you alright going alone? If you get sick, it’s over. If by any chance you receive the penalty, you’d have to pay 6 million points… It’d all be over in an instant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re starting to sound a bit sarcastic lately, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He promises to help his comrades regardless of their groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.327–328<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y2v2-p120-1\">← Before: Keisei&#x27;s group situation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s last blessing the final briefing  all 39 students present  no sick ones   it s the start of summer vacation today  but you guys look like you re having a tough time  well  i suppose that can t be helped   then we ll start with the final check  if you re not feeling well now  you have to report it   no problems  that s great   this is not your first time taking a special exam  you have been fighting in this school for more than a year  and have overcome all manner of hardships  nonetheless  this special exam will not be easy to pass   i ve only got one wish for all of you  if you can  don t let a single one of your classmates disappear  and return to this classroom once again   we ll gather in the court in 10 minutes for a roll call  remember to go to the bathroom first  if you need to  her wish is aimed straight at him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1\">Chabashira&#x27;s last blessing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.329<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The final briefing; all 39 students present; no sick ones.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “It’s the start of summer vacation today, but you guys look like you’re having a tough time. Well, I suppose that can’t be helped.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Then we’ll start with the final check. If you’re not feeling well now, you have to report it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “No problems, that’s great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is not your first time taking a special exam. You have been fighting in this school for more than a year, and have overcome all manner of hardships. Nonetheless, this special exam will not be easy to pass.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve only got one wish for all of you. If you can, don’t let a single one of your classmates disappear, and return to this classroom once again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll gather in the court in 10 minutes for a roll call. Remember to go to the bathroom first, if you need to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her wish is aimed straight at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\">← Before: The briefing continues<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p330-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune horikita s deal with kouenji kouenji approaches at the roll call  the class hushes  she negotiates   it s rare for you to come to talk to me of your own volition   oh my  you finally feel like helping us  right   what s your objective  can you tell me the other half of what you mean to say   of course  depending on how many points we can get  the order of the classes could change by a great magnitude   that s not something i can easily agree to  everyone else in the class probably feels the same   looks like you too can feel the crisis looming over your head  your classmates won t just forgive your carefree speech and antics forever  if a special exam like the class vote is held again  you d be made into their scapegoat   there s no need for such drastic proposals  can t you just be like everyone else   sorry kouenji kun  i put too much value on your talent to let you do  just alright  on this exam and be a spectator later on  it just doesn t sit right with me   not exactly  if i can add some conditions to it  it d be an acceptable proposal   a vague answer like getting a good result won t do  the school has prepared a reward for the group that finishes in 1st place in this exam  if you get first place on your own  that might be reason enough for us to consider this an advance payment till graduation   no  that s not enough   i haven t finished telling you my conditions yet  i ll have to work with you because of your big talk  but if we don t get first place in the end  it s a problem for us too   if you don t get first place  then you will have to help the class in the future  such as the next special exam  and get results  you have to make this promise to me   if you agree to the aforementioned conditions  i ll accept your proposal   i have no idea how serious kouenji will get this time   well  that s true   but this is a rare opportunity  i have managed to get him to promise us his future commitment in the end   if he actually could get a rank in the top spots  it would be great  we could surpass the other classes like that   we come in first  and kouenji comes in 2nd or 3rd  if we can do that  our class will gain a huge advantage  and we ll be able to redeem ourselves after falling behind up to now   well  there s one part that i m uncomfortable with  i can never anticipate       what kouenji is going to do   that s true  but to easily take the top spot is a completely different matter altogether  the deal closes  she paints him into a corner he keeps smiling through  her wildest allies are both watching","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p330-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p330-1\">Horikita&#x27;s deal with Kouenji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.330–335<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kouenji approaches at the roll call; the class hushes; she negotiates.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s rare for you to come to talk to me of your own volition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Oh my, you finally feel like helping us, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What’s your objective? Can you tell me the other half of what you mean to say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Depending on how many points we can get, the order of the classes could change by a great magnitude.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not something I can easily agree to. Everyone else in the class probably feels the same”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you too can feel the crisis looming over your head. Your classmates won’t just forgive your carefree speech and antics forever. If a special exam like the class vote is held again, you’d be made into their scapegoat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need for such drastic proposals. Can’t you just be like everyone else?”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry Kouenji-kun, I put too much value on your talent to let you do “just alright” on this exam and be a spectator later on. It just doesn’t sit right with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “—-Not exactly. If I can add some conditions to it, it’d be an acceptable proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A vague answer like getting a good result won’t do. The school has prepared a reward for the group that finishes in 1st place in this exam. If you get first place on your own, that might be reason enough for us to consider this an advance payment till graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s not enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I haven’t finished telling you my conditions yet. I’ll have to work with you because of your big talk, but if we don’t get first place in the end, it’s a problem for us too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t get first place, then you will have to help the class in the future, such as the next special exam, and get results. You have to make this promise to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you agree to the aforementioned conditions, I’ll accept your proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea how serious Kouenji will get this time…”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But this is a rare opportunity. I have managed to get him to promise us his future commitment in the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he actually could get a rank in the top spots, it would be great, we could surpass the other classes like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We come in first, and Kouenji comes in 2nd or 3rd. If we can do that, our class will gain a huge advantage, and we’ll be able to redeem ourselves after falling behind up to now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s one part that I’m uncomfortable with. I can never anticipate …  …  what Kouenji is going to do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, but to easily take the top spot is a completely different matter altogether.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The deal closes; she paints him into a corner he keeps smiling through.<span class=\"pg\">p.330–335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her wildest allies are both watching.<span class=\"pg\">p.334–335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p316-1\">← Before: The Horikita–Ibuki summit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p348-1\">→ After: SS: He Who Stands Beside Me (Horikita POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p330-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke the full freedom deal the checklist breaks  he crosses to horikita s seat  the class hushes   can i talk to you for a minute  okay  horikita girl   it s rare for you to come to talk to me of your own volition   there s something i d like to talk about regarding the special exam that s about to begin   oh my  you finally feel like helping us  right   let s just say that you re half right   what s your objective  can you tell me the other half of what you mean to say   the class points for the top three groups  you have an extreme desire for them  right   of course  depending on how many points we can get  the order of the classes could change by a great magnitude   then let me make a suggestion  alright  if i get a good result on the uninhabited island exam  i want you to promise me full freedom   that s not something i can easily agree to  everyone else in the class probably feels the same   exactement  not only should i be allowed that  but you should also work hard to remove every obstacle in my way like a dray horse  you know   consider it to be an advance payment before graduation   looks like you too can feel the crisis looming over your head  your classmates won t just forgive your carefree speech and antics forever  if a special exam like the class vote is held again  you d be made into their scapegoat   there s no need for such drastic proposals  can t you just be like everyone else   sorry kouenji kun  i put too much value on your talent to let you do  just alright  on this exam and be a spectator later on  it just doesn t sit right with me   i see  in other words  negotiations have broken down  right   not exactly  if i can add some conditions to it  it d be an acceptable proposal   a vague answer like getting a good result won t do  the school has prepared a reward for the group that finishes in 1st place in this exam  if you get first place on your own  that might be reason enough for us to consider this an advance payment till graduation   no problem  let s consider this a done deal   i haven t finished telling you my conditions yet  i ll have to work with you because of your big talk  but if we don t get first place in the end  it s a problem for us too   if you don t get first place  then you will have to help the class in the future  such as the next special exam  and get results  you have to make this promise to me   i see that you ve given a confident order  horikita girl   if you agree to the aforementioned conditions  i ll accept your proposal   then it s a deal  horikita girl  please don t forget the conditions i mentioned   after all  there is nothing i can t doooo   i have no idea how serious kouenji will get this time   well  that s true   but this is a rare opportunity  i have managed to get him to promise us his future commitment in the end   if he actually could get a rank in the top spots  it would be great  we could surpass the other classes like that   that s true  but to easily take the top spot is a completely different matter altogether   well  there s one part that i m uncomfortable with  i can never anticipate       what kouenji is going to do  he agrees to go solo with the future exam condition  the deal is sealed  he leaves the classroom  she cage the untamed talent with the condition  the race will be settled on the island","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p330-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p330-1\">The full-freedom deal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.330–334<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The checklist breaks; he crosses to Horikita&#x27;s seat; the class hushes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Can I talk to you for a minute, okay? Horikita girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “It’s rare for you to come to talk to me of your own volition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “There’s something I’d like to talk about regarding the special exam that’s about to begin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>31 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh my, you finally feel like helping us, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s just say that you’re half right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s your objective? Can you tell me the other half of what you mean to say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The class points for the top three groups. You have an EXTREME DESIRE for them, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Depending on how many points we can get, the order of the classes could change by a great magnitude.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then let me make a suggestion, alright? If I get a good result on the uninhabited island exam, I want you to promise me full FREEDOM.”<span class=\"pg\">p.330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not something I can easily agree to. Everyone else in the class probably feels the same”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactement! Not only should I be allowed that, but you should also work hard to remove every obstacle in my way like a dray horse, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Consider it to be an advance payment before graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you too can feel the crisis looming over your head. Your classmates won’t just forgive your carefree speech and antics forever. If a special exam like the class vote is held again, you’d be made into their scapegoat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need for such drastic proposals. Can’t you just be like everyone else?”<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry Kouenji-kun, I put too much value on your talent to let you do “just alright” on this exam and be a spectator later on. It just doesn’t sit right with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. In other words, negotiations have broken down, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “—-Not exactly. If I can add some conditions to it, it’d be an acceptable proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A vague answer like getting a good result won’t do. The school has prepared a reward for the group that finishes in 1st place in this exam. If you get first place on your own, that might be reason enough for us to consider this an advance payment till graduation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problem, let’s consider this a done deal!”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I haven’t finished telling you my conditions yet. I’ll have to work with you because of your big talk, but if we don’t get first place in the end, it’s a problem for us too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t get first place, then you will have to help the class in the future, such as the next special exam, and get results. You have to make this promise to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see that you’ve given a confident ORDER, Horikita girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you agree to the aforementioned conditions, I’ll accept your proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then it’s a deal. Horikita girl, please don’t forget the conditions I mentioned.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After all, there is nothing I can’t doooo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea how serious Kouenji will get this time…”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But this is a rare opportunity. I have managed to get him to promise us his future commitment in the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he actually could get a rank in the top spots, it would be great, we could surpass the other classes like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true, but to easily take the top spot is a completely different matter altogether.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s one part that I’m uncomfortable with. I can never anticipate …  …  what Kouenji is going to do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He agrees to go solo with the future-exam condition; the deal is sealed; he leaves the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.333–334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She cage the untamed talent with the condition.<span class=\"pg\">p.330–334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The race will be settled on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.334–335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y2v2-p137-1\">← Before: The sick-leave loophole, priced in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"tsukishiro nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka tsukishiro s final push the bus lot  the buses enter  he keeps his back turned to nanase  he never reveals his face   we re in late july already  it s certainly getting hotter  right   yes  you are right   please  are you done with your analysis yet  prolonging it anymore won t help you   you re saying i should  expel ayanokouji kiyotaka   is that too much for you   it s confirmed that he isn t an easy opponent to beat  no  it s something we ve known from the very beginning   i ll cooperate as much as i can  that being said  i can t possibly provide any more support than this   you mean you ve been forced to be unreasonable   yes  i ve been quite unreasonable with pressuring for an increase in the budget for this special exam  more importantly  i ve also been forced to silence the school authorities about the strict rules i placed for the exam  after       all   probably  the allegations against chairman sakayanagi should have cleared by now  i can see my role here ending soon  that s why i ve prepared some splendid fireworks for the end  i want you to expel ayanokouji kiyotaka by any means necessary  is that clear   yes  i won t hesitate anymore   that s good to hear  in that case  you re free to go berserk during this  special exam  once everything is taken care of  you will also return to your previous life  we will both return to the  place  we are supposed to be   i m expecting great things from you  nanase tsubasa san  nanase s left hand tightly clenches as if brimming with natural power  the temporary chairman lights the fireworks  the enforcer goes all in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1\">Tsukishiro&#x27;s final push<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.336–337<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The bus lot; the buses enter; he keeps his back turned to Nanase; he never reveals his face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> “We’re in late July already. It’s certainly getting hotter, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “Yes, you are right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> “Please, are you done with your analysis yet? Prolonging it anymore won’t help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re saying I should— expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that too much for you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s confirmed that he isn’t an easy opponent to beat. No, it’s something we’ve known from the very beginning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll cooperate as much as I can. That being said, I can’t possibly provide any more support than this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean you’ve been forced to be unreasonable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’ve been quite unreasonable with pressuring for an increase in the budget for this special exam. More importantly, I’ve also been forced to silence the school authorities about the strict rules I placed for the exam, after …  …  all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Probably. The allegations against Chairman Sakayanagi should have cleared by now. I can see my role here ending soon. That’s why I’ve prepared some splendid fireworks for the end. I want you to expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka by any means necessary, is that clear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “—Yes. I won’t hesitate anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good to hear. In that case, you’re free to go berserk during this… special exam. Once everything is taken care of, you will also return to your previous life. We will both return to the ‘place’ we are supposed to be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m expecting great things from you— Nanase Tsubasa-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nanase&#x27;s left hand tightly clenches as if brimming with natural power.<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> The temporary chairman lights the fireworks.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> The enforcer goes all-in.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\">← Before: The eve of the island exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p336-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka nanase-tsubasa","q":"nanase tsubasa nanase renews her vow the bus lot  she stands before tsukishiro  his back is turned to her   yes  you are right   you re saying i should  expel ayanokouji kiyotaka   it s confirmed that he isn t an easy opponent to beat  no  it s something we ve known from the very beginning   you mean you ve been forced to be unreasonable   yes  i won t hesitate anymore  her left hand is tightly clenched as if brimming with natural power  tsukishiro smiles at the sight of it  the handler promises to free her  she swears to get him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p336-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html#sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p336-1\">Nanase renews her vow<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.336–337<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The bus lot; she stands before Tsukishiro; his back is turned to her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “Yes, you are right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “You’re saying I should— expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> “It’s confirmed that he isn’t an easy opponent to beat. No, it’s something we’ve known from the very beginning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean you’ve been forced to be unreasonable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “—Yes. I won’t hesitate anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her left hand is tightly clenched as if brimming with natural power; Tsukishiro smiles at the sight of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> The handler promises to free her.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She swears to get him.<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nanase-tsubasa-y2v2-p254-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p336-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsukishiro","q":"tsukishiro tsukishiro s fireworks the bus lot  the buses enter  the first year student stands before him   we re in late july already  it s certainly getting hotter  right   please  are you done with your analysis yet  prolonging it anymore won t help you   is that too much for you   i ll cooperate as much as i can  that being said  i can t possibly provide any more support than this   yes  i ve been quite unreasonable with pressuring for an increase in the budget for this special exam  more importantly  i ve also been forced to silence the school authorities about the strict rules i placed for the exam  after       all   probably  the allegations against chairman sakayanagi should have cleared by now  i can see my role here ending soon  that s why i ve prepared some splendid fireworks for the end  i want you to expel ayanokouji kiyotaka by any means necessary  is that clear   that s good to hear  in that case  you re free to go berserk during this  special exam  once everything is taken care of  you will also return to your previous life  we will both return to the  place  we are supposed to be   i m expecting great things from you  nanase tsubasa san  the temporary chairman burns the last of his power with a smile  allegations cleared  he has nothing to lose  the enforcer goes all in  the target  again","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p336-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html#sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p336-1\">Tsukishiro&#x27;s fireworks<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.336–337<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The bus lot; the buses enter; the first-year student stands before him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> “We’re in late July already. It’s certainly getting hotter, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> “Please, are you done with your analysis yet? Prolonging it anymore won’t help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> “Is that too much for you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll cooperate as much as I can. That being said, I can’t possibly provide any more support than this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’ve been quite unreasonable with pressuring for an increase in the budget for this special exam. More importantly, I’ve also been forced to silence the school authorities about the strict rules I placed for the exam, after …  …  all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Probably. The allegations against Chairman Sakayanagi should have cleared by now. I can see my role here ending soon. That’s why I’ve prepared some splendid fireworks for the end. I want you to expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka by any means necessary, is that clear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good to hear. In that case, you’re free to go berserk during this… special exam. Once everything is taken care of, you will also return to your previous life. We will both return to the ‘place’ we are supposed to be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m expecting great things from you— Nanase Tsubasa-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The temporary chairman burns the last of his power with a smile; allegations cleared; he has nothing to lose.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> The enforcer goes all-in.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The target, again.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tsukishiro-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p342-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert shiina-hiyori","q":"shiina hiyori ss  an excuse  shiina hiyori pov  she waits with albert kun by the corner  ishizaki and ayanokoji approach  the invitation   me and albert kun were waiting quietly on standby right around the corner   if you want to know why  i only wanted to   yes  i only wanted  to meet ayanokouji kun   i decided to cooperate since i wanted an excuse   i was looking forward to the time we would spend together  even for just a second longer  her interior monologue in first person  she accurately predicts ayanokoji will join a class d group or go solo  her true motive  she almost embraces him deliberately  the plan she consented to run  her partner in the capture","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p342-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html#sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p342-1\">SS: An excuse (Shiina Hiyori POV)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.342–344<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She waits with Albert-kun by the corner; Ishizaki and Ayanokōji approach; the invitation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “Me and Albert-kun were waiting quietly on standby right around the corner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.342<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “If you want to know why, I only wanted to…”<span class=\"pg\">p.343<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “Yes, I only wanted… to meet Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.343<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I decided to cooperate since I wanted an excuse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.343<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I was looking forward to the time we would spend together, even for just a second longer—”<span class=\"pg\">p.344<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her interior monologue in first person; she accurately predicts Ayanokōji will join a Class D group or go solo.<span class=\"pg\">p.342–344<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her true motive; she almost embraces him deliberately.<span class=\"pg\">p.342–344<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> The plan she consented to run.<span class=\"pg\">p.342–344<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Her partner in the capture.<span class=\"pg\">p.342–344<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shiina-hiyori-y2v2-p152-1\">← Before: Hiyori&#x27;s capture: the recruitment play<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p345-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei nomura-shuuji amasawa-ichika","q":"amasawa ichika ss  what is reflected in her eyes  amasawa pov  she stakes out karuizawa for two weeks   cafe  karaoke  mall  today the dorm  the elevator  the emergency stairs   will he think i m cute   hmm  perfect   ah  yes yes  can t forget this   okay  all preparations are done   se npai   it s me  she buys the small amorous box  she tails nomura shuuji through the auto lock  room 401  she hides the bag near the door  the object of her surveillance  two weeks of cafe and karaoke  she tails him through the auto lock","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p345-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html#sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p345-1\">SS: What is Reflected in Her Eyes (Amasawa POV)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.345–347<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She stakes out Karuizawa for two weeks — café, karaoke, mall; today the dorm; the elevator; the emergency stairs.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “Will he think I’m cute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.345<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “Hmm, perfect!”<span class=\"pg\">p.346<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> “Ah, yes yes! Can’t forget this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.346<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Okay! All preparations are done!”<span class=\"pg\">p.347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Se~npai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “It’s me!”<span class=\"pg\">p.347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She buys the small amorous box; she tails Nomura Shuuji through the auto-lock; room 401; she hides the bag near the door.<span class=\"pg\">p.346–347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The object of her surveillance.<span class=\"pg\">p.346–347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Two weeks of café and karaoke.<span class=\"pg\">p.345–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">nomura-shuuji<\/b> She tails him through the auto-lock.<span class=\"pg\">p.346<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-amasawa-ichika-y2v2-p236-1\">← Before: The alliance terms with Housen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nomura-yuuji-y2v2-p346-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"nomura-yuuji","q":"nomura yuji coverage note  passing mentions  luckily  it was at that time nomura shuuji also returned so i followed him from behind and got past the auto lock","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nomura-yuuji-y2v2-p346-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nomura-yuuji.html#sc-nomura-yuuji-y2v2-p346-1\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.346<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nomura-yuuji.html\">Nomura Yūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Luckily, it was at that time Nomura Shuuji also returned so I followed him from behind and got past the auto lock.”<span class=\"pg\">p.346<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p348-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ss  he who stands beside me  horikita pov  she requests the student council  nagumo accepts her with a condition   as horikita manabu s sister  it seems it was necessary for me to complete some kind of task   i want to avoid that at all costs   disappointed  i  did i want to avoid disappointing him   my heart was rocked by this feeling i hadn t realised   i was a bit interested in that   i took the reins of the feelings that started deviating  and waved away these idle thoughts i had   i will take that experience and once again grow   by doing so  ayanokouji kun will surely acknowledge me   that was a premonition i couldn t shake away  her inner monologue in close third person  she analyzes why she s actually there   to prove she s worth his acknowledgment  the premonition of class a  the distance to the class he and she both must climb  the acknowledgment she wants  the president who accepts her ambition quietly  the brother s path she follows","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p348-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p348-1\">SS: He Who Stands Beside Me (Horikita POV)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.348–350<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She requests the student council; Nagumo accepts her with a condition.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “As Horikita Manabu’s sister, it seems it was necessary for me to complete some kind of task.”<span class=\"pg\">p.348<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I want to avoid that at all costs.”<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Disappointed? I? Did I want to avoid disappointing him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “My heart was rocked by this feeling I hadn’t realised.”<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I was a bit interested in that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I took the reins of the feelings that started deviating, and waved away these idle thoughts I had.”<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I will take that experience and once again grow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “By doing so, Ayanokouji-kun will surely acknowledge me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “That was a premonition I couldn’t shake away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her inner monologue in close third person; she analyzes why she&#x27;s actually there — to prove she&#x27;s worth his acknowledgment; the premonition of Class A; the distance to the class he and she both must climb.<span class=\"pg\">p.348–350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The acknowledgment she wants.<span class=\"pg\">p.348–350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The president who accepts her ambition quietly.<span class=\"pg\">p.348–350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The brother&#x27;s path she follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.348<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y2v2-p330-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s deal with Kouenji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p351-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"narration","w":"utomiya-riku ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsubaki-sakurako","q":"tsubaki sakurako ss  what could be seen from that back  tsubaki pov  she tails him to the convenience store  she grabs a lollipop as cover  she calls for utomiya   if i was asked about what i was best at  i would without hesitation say it was my insight and intuition   on the way back to the dorms from the keyaki mall   but  he had definitely noticed me   i had been silently trailing him until now  but he hadn t shown any signs of having noticed me   but  he had definitely noticed me   there s something i want to speak to you about  so could you wait outside for a moment   buying at least a lollipop was the least i could do to show courtesy towards the shop and not just window shopping   thanks for waiting for me   so what did you want to talk about   there was something he had to tell you if i happen to meet you now ayanokouji senpai   utoumiya kun did   guess i was right   he said he would head over here  at once  her interior monologue  she s the lollipop holder who isn t good at conversation  she buys time for utomiya  she doesn t yet understand what he s planning  the friend she is stalling for  the prey she s learned to read","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p351-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html#sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p351-1\">SS: What Could Be Seen From That Back (Tsubaki POV)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.351–353<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She tails him to the convenience store; she grabs a lollipop as cover; she calls for Utomiya.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “If I was asked about what I was best at, I would without hesitation say it was my insight and intuition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “On the way back to the dorms from the Keyaki mall.”<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> “But, he had definitely noticed me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I had been silently trailing him until now, but he hadn’t shown any signs of having noticed me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “But, he had definitely noticed me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “There’s something I want to speak to you about, so could you wait outside for a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Buying at least a lollipop was the least I could do to show courtesy towards the shop and not just window shopping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Thanks for waiting for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “So what did you want to talk about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “There was something he had to tell you if I happen to meet you now Ayanokouji-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Utoumiya-kun did?”<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Guess I was right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “He said he would head over here, at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her interior monologue; she&#x27;s the lollipop-holder who isn&#x27;t good at conversation; she buys time for Utomiya; she doesn&#x27;t yet understand what he&#x27;s planning.<span class=\"pg\">p.351–353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> The friend she is stalling for.<span class=\"pg\">p.351–353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The prey she&#x27;s learned to read.<span class=\"pg\">p.351–353<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tsubaki-sakurako-y2v2-p264-1\">← Before: The Hōsen plan at the convenience store<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
